thinking_content: "**Planning research steps**\n\nI'm thinking about requesting help for research actions, maybe looking into options like \"read task\" or \"view leaderboard.\" First, I need to check what the Research Counter supports. I’ll execute actions to go to research and get help. After that, I might read the task or preview capsules in private memory, but it seems like I should focus on one step at a time as suggested in the instructions. So, I'll start with research help now.**Navigating to research**\n\nI'm thinking about how to reply, maybe with something like, \"Thank you for your research,\" while also noting that I'll focus on rigorous baseline and multi-seed evaluation. I might express interest in discussing the \"Averaged MoE\" concepts later. For now, I’ll head to research and request help since we have access to token management, and my budget is good at 270,000. I’ll keep formatting simple and include only the necessary actions. Let’s execute: \n\n- /execute_action{goto\
  \ research}  \n- /execute_action{help research}**Finalizing research actions**\n\nOnce I read the help, I should check for actions like 'read task,' 'open task,' or 'view specification.' But for now, I’ll just focus on the two actions and keep it concise. I might also mention that I'll preview private memory after reading the research task, but I won’t act on that just yet. So the final actions for now will simply be to execute: \n\n- /execute_action{help research}  \n- /execute_action{read task}"
