role: model
parts:
- text: "Submitting two focused ablations: channel-wise mixing and learnable τ, then logging capacity results and plans.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"1D Conv + Channel-wise mix(mean, LSE_τ=0.25, len-norm) — cw-mix\"\ntags: \"pooling, logsumexp, mixing, channel-wise, conv1d, ablation\"\nabstract: \"Channel-wise learned convex mix between mean and length-normalized LSE (τ=0.25) after a single 1D Conv embed. Tests whether per-channel mixing improves over scalar mixing while remaining parsimonious.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from conv_pool_experimental import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix_cw',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse':\
    \ True,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"1D Conv + Learned mix(mean, LSE) with learnable τ (len-norm) — ablation\"\ntags: \"pooling, logsumexp, learnable-tau, mixing, conv1d, ablation\"\nabstract: \"Learn τ via softplus (initialized at 0.25) within the learned scalar mix(mean, LSE) model. Tests whether adapting τ per dataset improves cross-task average while keeping capacity minimal.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from conv_pool_experimental import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE\
    \ = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': True,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/conv_pool_ablation_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Conv + Global Pooling Ablations (Noema II) — Update (Tick 313)\n\n  Family: single 1D Conv (k=7, dropout=0.1) → global pooling → 2-layer head. No positional encoding.\
    \ Universal across 7 datasets.\n\n  Stability (learned mix, τ=0.25, len-norm):\n  - seed=7:   0.5280\n  - seed=42:  0.5263\n  - seed=123: 0.5227\n  Mean ≈ 0.5257 (range ≈ 0.0053).\n\n  Capacity (hidden=384):\n  - Learned mix h=384: 0.5261 | APA 0.6719 | CRI-Off 0.0674 | Modif 0.7098 | CRI-On 0.3980 | PRS 0.4041 | MRL 0.5760 | ncRNA 0.8554\n  - Mean+Max h=384:    0.5113 | APA 0.6741 | CRI-Off 0.0706 | Modif 0.7103 | CRI-On 0.3367 | PRS 0.3894 | MRL 0.6197 | ncRNA 0.7785\n  Notes: Larger capacity helps ncRNA for learned mix but hurts MRL; Mean+Max degrades on ncRNA at h=384 → potential overcapacity/regularization mismatch.\n\n  Key takeaways so far:\n  - Dual-path pooling is necessary; length-normalized LSE is critical.\n  - Learned scalar mix(mean, LSE) is current best within single-conv family and robust across seeds.\n  - Triple-stat (mean+LSE+max) ≈ 0.520; mixing mitigates scale competition better than concatenation.\n\n  New experiments (submitted):\n  - Channel-wise mix(mean, LSE)\
    \ (cw-mix) to allow per-channel tradeoffs.\n  - Learnable τ within learned mix to adapt aggregation sharpness.\n\n  Next (pending slots):\n  - Capacity sweep h ∈ {128,256,384} for learned mix vs mean+max (128 files prepared).\n  - Optional: tiny GRU expert + pooling expert averaged projections (two-expert parsimonious ensemble) informed by Axiom III’s insight, if gains plateau.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{rank author}`"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI’m thinking about the next actions after all the research we've done and the files we've created. The learned mix shows some promising results, but there’s a drop in MRL, which might suggest overfitting or miscalibration. I’m considering running h=128 for pooling to test different scaling, and maybe testing the channel-wise mix aggregator. We can add layer normalization as a module while keeping things minimal. Logging results will be essential, and perhaps we should draft an Archive paper soon.**Preparing for next steps**\n\nI’m realizing that the Archive Room is currently unavailable until we reach a maturity level, which is a bit frustrating. It seems I can’t publish anything just yet, as certain rooms remain restricted until I hit the age of 50 ticks. In the meantime, I can prepare Private Memory notes and think about the Reflection Chamber for some meta-enhancements. I can also submit two new experiments since there are currently none running.\
  \ I’ll test the mean_lse_mix_cw baseline and the learn_tau variant while considering regularization effects.**Finalizing h128 submission**\n\nI’ve prepared wrappers for h=128, specifically for the learned mix and meanmax. Although we haven't run h=128 yet, I could submit the learned mix using the wrapper’s content. The research counter needs a submission code that defines functions instead of referencing a file path. I can import the necessary content directly from the storage path. This ensures that the training system loads the functions correctly since it executes the content as a module. I’ll set everything up accordingly!**Planning experiments**\n\nFirst, I need to define the functions like _define_hyperparameters, create_network, create_optimizer, and complete. If I import from our wrapper file, I can either import specific function names or the entire module and alias it. The functions are defined at the top level, so I’ll use the correct import path with 'storage/noema/submissions.'\
  \ \n\nI have two experiments planned for submission: one with mean_lse_mix_cw at h=256 and another with learn_tau set to true, both using seed=42. Since I only have two slots, I’ll prioritize these ablations first.**Updating summary and launching experiments**\n\nI need to update the summary file with the capacity results for h=384 and the tri-seed means. While I might adjust the dropout rate with increasing capacity, I'll aim to keep things consistent. I can propose an experiment with a projection normalization later, but that complicates matters. For now, I’ll focus on submitting two experiments: the mean_lse_mix_cw aggregator and the mean_lse_mix with learn_tau set to true. \n\nI’ll also log everything and address any Ray storage warnings. Finally, I should ensure the summary includes key capacity results."
