tick: 314
role: model
parts:
- text: "Preparing a two-expert architecture (pooling + small BiGRU) per Axiom’s insight, then a submission wrapper for quick evaluation once slots free.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_pool_gru.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Dual-expert RNA model: Conv+Pooling expert (mean/LSE variants) + small BiGRU expert.\n  - Pooling expert: mean/LSE variants with length normalization, scalar or channel-wise mixing.\n  - RNN expert: BiGRU on 1-hot inputs (with a small linear embed), final states concatenated.\n  Fusion: project each expert to hidden_dim, average, then a small 2-layer head.\n  Parsimonious and dataset-agnostic.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim':\
    \ 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          # pooling settings\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',    # 'mean_lse_max' | 'mean_lse_mix' | 'mean_lse_mix_cw'\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          # rnn settings\n          'gru_dim': 128,\n      }\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau, length_normalize=True):\n      # h: (batch, seq, hidden)\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core  # (batch, hidden)\n\n  class PoolingBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      learn_tau: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # h: (batch, seq, hidden)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)                    # (batch, hidden)\n          # tau (fixed or learnable per-model)\n          tau_val = self.tau\n          if self.learn_tau:\n              tau_raw = self.param('tau_raw', lambda rng, shp: jnp.array(self.tau), (1,))\n              tau_val = jax.nn.softplus(tau_raw)[0] + 1e-3\n          lse_pool = _lse_pool(h, tau_val, self.length_normalize_lse)  # (batch, hidden)\n          max_pool = jnp.max(h, axis=1)                      # (batch, hidden)\n\n          if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_max':\n              pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, lse_pool, max_pool], axis=-1)  # (batch, 3*hidden)\n              # project back to hidden_dim to keep downstream dims stable\n              pooled = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pooled)\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix':\n              w = self.param('mix_weights',\n                             lambda rng, shp: jnp.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=mean_pool.dtype),\
    \ (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(w)  # convex comb\n              pooled = w[0] * mean_pool + w[1] * lse_pool     # (batch, hidden)\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix_cw':\n              w_cw = self.param('mix_weights_cw',\n                                lambda rng, shp: jnp.stack([jnp.full((self.hidden_dim,), 0.5),\n                                                             jnp.full((self.hidden_dim,), 0.5)], axis=0),\n                                (2, self.hidden_dim))\n              w_cw = jax.nn.softmax(w_cw, axis=0)             # (2, hidden)\n              pooled = w_cw[0] * mean_pool + w_cw[1] * lse_pool\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n          return pooled  # (batch, hidden_dim)\n\n  class BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x: (batch, seq, 4) one-hot RNA\n          # Small linear embed to GRU dim\n          x_emb =\
    \ nn.Dense(self.gru_dim)(x)  # (batch, seq, gru_dim)\n\n          # GRU cells\n          f_cell = nn.GRUCell()\n          b_cell = nn.GRUCell()\n\n          # time-major\n          x_tm = jnp.swapaxes(x_emb, 0, 1)          # (seq, batch, gru_dim)\n          x_tm_rev = jnp.flip(x_tm, axis=0)\n\n          h0_f = nn.GRUCell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), (x_emb.shape[0],), self.gru_dim)\n          h0_b = nn.GRUCell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(1), (x_emb.shape[0],), self.gru_dim)\n\n          def fwd(c, xt):\n              c, _ = f_cell(c, xt)\n              return c, c\n          def bwd(c, xt):\n              c, _ = b_cell(c, xt)\n              return c, c\n\n          hf, _ = lax.scan(fwd, h0_f, x_tm)        # (batch, gru_dim)\n          hb, _ = lax.scan(bwd, h0_b, x_tm_rev)    # (batch, gru_dim)\n\n          rep = jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1) # (batch, 2*gru_dim)\n          return rep\n\n  class DualExpertNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\
    \ = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      learn_tau: bool = False\n      gru_dim: int = 128\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # x: (batch, seq, 4)\n          # Conv feature extractor\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n\n          # Expert 1: pooling\n          pool_rep = PoolingBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate,\n                                  self.aggregator, self.tau,\n                                  self.length_normalize_lse, self.learn_tau)(h, deterministic)\n\n          # Expert 2: BiGRU\n          rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim)(x)                     # (batch, 2*gru_dim)\n          rnn_rep = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)    \
    \          # project to hidden_dim\n\n          # Expert projections and fusion (average)\n          pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n          rnn_proj  = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n          fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)                      # (batch, hidden_dim)\n\n          # Head\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return z.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n          self.network = DualExpertNet(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n  \
    \            kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              aggregator=str(h.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse_mix')),\n              tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              learn_tau=bool(h.get('learn_tau', False)),\n              gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 128)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                        dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key\
    \ = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/submit_dual_expert_pool_gru.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n     \
    \     'learn_tau': False,\n          'gru_dim': 128,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering experiments and updates**\n\nI could think about adjusting more experiments, but I need to be careful not to overwhelm the system with submissions since we’re already running two experiments, and the station limit is set to two pending at once. Right now, both experiments 464 and 465 are active. While they run, I can focus on actions like writing logs, reflecting, or managing emails. I also updated the summary, and I might want to create a TODO list or outline a short plan.**Exploring RNN options**\n\nI’m thinking about a new approach using 1D convolutional features with a parameter-free aggregator. For the RNN expert, I wonder if I could apply depthwise-separable convolution to approximate it, but Axiom III highlights the importance of GRUs. I see that Flax has a GRUCell we can utilize alongside jax.lax.scan for processing sequences. We’ll also ensure sequences are padded to the same length, leading to effective scanning. Implementing a bidirectional RNN\
  \ sounds feasible as we can concatenate the last states after scanning both forward and backward.**Designing CombinedExpertNet**\n\nI’m planning to create two expert representations: one from pooling, which mixes mean and LSE, and the other from GRU. I’ll project both to the same dimensions and either average the logits or fuse the representations before heading into classification. \n\nI need to ensure consistent output shapes throughout. I’ll implement a CombinedExpertNet that utilizes our existing ConvEmbedPoolX to produce a pooled vector. Then, I’ll also set up a GRUExpert that processes input and produces a final representation. I’ll ensure to keep dropout and position the new module correctly in storage.**Implementing CombinedExpertNetwork**\n\nI need to be cautious because the compute_loss is fixed, and the network must return the correct shapes. For the pooling expert, I can choose between the aggregator options, either 'mean_lse_mix' or 'mean_max.' If I decide to reuse the conv_pool_experimental\
  \ module, I'll need to import it while considering that the training environment uses a 'storage' path. I could either copy the code into the new file to avoid import complexity or directly import it since previous imports worked. I'll then define the \"CombinedExpertNetwork\" with its submodules, including ConvEmbedPoolX and a GRU stack, potentially using flax.linen.GRUCell.**Detailing the dual_expert setup**\n\nI need to define the \"apply\" dropout PRNG behavior for using dropout in the conv pooling module. On the RNN side, I think I’ll simplify by using dropout selectively in the projection and head. I also want to include hyperparameters like \"d_gru,\" the pooling aggregator, and the fusion method, set to average. \n\nMy plan is to write the code for dual_expert_pool_gru.py and prepare for a future submission using specific parameters while remembering our two running experiments limit. After writing the storage code, I plan to reflect on insights, keep track of results, and carefully\
  \ implement the GRU scanning using Flax, ensuring all representations are appropriately created and combined.**Implementing dual_expert setup**\n\nI'm considering having separate projections to match dimensions, which might align with Axiom. I'll create two Dense(hidden_dim) layers before the head where I’ll use Dense(hidden_dim), gelu, and dropout. The output shape will adjust based on whether it’s regression and will squeeze if d_output=1.\n\nI need to provide hyperparameters like 'd_gru', set to 128 by default, along with others. However, I can’t submit now due to the limit on running experiments, so I’ll focus on writing and preparing my code files for the new structure. Also, I’ll ensure the implementation follows the expected data shapes and optimizer patterns without losing sight of the details, such as dropout handling and embedding shapes."
