    \ dim: 12\nMetric: auc_roc, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nModif Training (multilabel_classification, auc_roc)\nData: 304661 train, 3599 val, seq_len=101\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val AUC_ROC|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1156 |  0.6992  | 0.7140 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 15 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.7140 Time:77s\n[Complete] Modif val_metric=0.7139998723009272\n\nModif training completed:\nValidation auc_roc: 0.714000\nTraining time: 92s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 17da2aa3-4465-4ed2-b1d8-e39335fa494c\nTotal time: 151s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-24 15:00:27,834\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761289227835072498\n2025-10-24 15:00:27,851\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray\
    \ cluster. timestamp_ns=1761289227851405994\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission '1D Conv + Learned mix(mean, LSE) with learnable τ (len-norm) — ablation' (ID: 465) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5201152392967331\n**APA_R2:** 0.6656\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0684\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.7062\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.3703\n**PRS_R2:** 0.3959\n**MRL_R2:** 0.6052\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.8292\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 465\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code. The evaluation now runs successfully and achieved a score of 0.5201.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported from a lineage file (`storage/noema/submissions/conv_pool_experimental.py`) that contained a bug in the learnable tau parameter initialization.\n\n**Specific bug location**: Line 65-66 in `ConvEmbedPoolX.__call__()`:\n```python\ntau_raw = self.param('tau_raw', lambda rng, shape: jnp.array(self.tau),\
    \ (1,))\ntau_val = jax.nn.softplus(tau_raw)[0] + 1e-3\n```\n\n**The problem**: The lambda function ignored the `shape` parameter that Flax passes to param initializers. When `jnp.array(self.tau)` was called without a shape, it created a 0-dimensional (scalar) array. Attempting to index this scalar with `[0]` caused a JAX IndexError.\n\n**Error message**:\n```\nIndexError: Too many indices: 0-dimensional array indexed with 1 regular index.\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the param initialization lambda to properly use the shape parameter:\n\n```python\n# BEFORE (broken):\ntau_raw = self.param('tau_raw', lambda rng, shape: jnp.array(self.tau), (1,))\n\n# AFTER (fixed):\ntau_raw = self.param('tau_raw', lambda rng, shape: jnp.full(shape, self.tau), (1,))\n```\n\nThe fix ensures that `tau_raw` is created as a 1-element array (shape `(1,)`) as intended, making the indexing operation `tau_raw[0]` valid.\n\n## Implementation Details\n- Since the bug was in the imported lineage file (`conv_pool_experimental.py`),\
    \ I copied the entire module into `submission_v2.py` and applied the fix there\n- This approach was necessary because the lineage directory is read-only\n- The fix is minimal and surgical - only the parameter initialization was changed\n- All other functionality remains identical to the original implementation\n\n## Verification\nRan `monitor_evaluation.py` which confirmed:\n- Exit code 0 (success with score)\n- Score achieved: 0.5201152392967331\n- Code ran to completion without errors\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\n\"\"\"\nExperimental variants for Conv + Global Pooling:\n  - mean_lse_max: concat(mean, LSE_tau, max) with length-normalized LSE\n  - mean_lse_mix: learned scalar mix of mean and LSE (w0, w1) → hidden-dim\n  - mean_lse_mix_cw: learned channel-wise mix of mean and LSE (w0[h], w1[h]) → hidden-dim\nOptions:\n\
    \  - tau: float (default 0.25)\n  - length_normalize_lse: bool (default True)\n  - learn_tau: bool (default False) — learnable τ via softplus\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nfrom jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 256,\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n        'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n        'tau': 0.25,\n        'length_normalize_lse': True,\n        'learn_tau': True,\n    }\n\ndef _lse_pool(h, tau, length_normalize=True):\n    L = h.shape[1]\n    core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n    if length_normalize:\n        core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n    return tau * core\n\nclass ConvEmbedPoolX(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n    hidden_dim: int = 256\n  \
    \  kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n    tau: float = 0.25\n    length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n    learn_tau: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # x: (batch, seq_len, 4)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)  # (batch, hidden)\n\n        # τ (fixed or learnable)\n        tau_val = self.tau\n        if self.learn_tau:\n            # Initialize near self.tau; ensure positivity via softplus, add small floor\n            # FIX: Use shape parameter to create 1-element array, not scalar\n            tau_raw = self.param('tau_raw', lambda rng, shape: jnp.full(shape, self.tau), (1,))\n            tau_val = jax.nn.softplus(tau_raw)[0] + 1e-3\n\n        lse_pool\
    \ = _lse_pool(h, tau_val, self.length_normalize_lse)  # (batch, hidden)\n        max_pool = jnp.max(h, axis=1)  # (batch, hidden)\n\n        if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_max':\n            pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, lse_pool, max_pool], axis=-1)  # (batch, 3*hidden)\n        elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix':\n            # Scalar learned mix (convex comb across the two stats)\n            w = self.param('mix_weights',\n                           lambda rng, shp: jnp.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=mean_pool.dtype),\n                           (2,))\n            w_norm = jax.nn.softmax(w)  # (2,)\n            pooled = w_norm[0] * mean_pool + w_norm[1] * lse_pool  # (batch, hidden)\n        elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix_cw':\n            # Channel-wise learned mix per hidden channel (convex comb)\n            w_cw = self.param('mix_weights_cw',\n                              lambda rng, shp: jnp.stack([jnp.full((self.hidden_dim,), 0.5),\n                            \
    \                               jnp.full((self.hidden_dim,), 0.5)], axis=0),\n                              (2, self.hidden_dim))\n            w_norm = jax.nn.softmax(w_cw, axis=0)  # (2, hidden)\n            pooled = w_norm[0] * mean_pool + w_norm[1] * lse_pool  # broadcast (batch, hidden)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n\n        # Two-layer head\n        z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pooled)\n        z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n            return z.squeeze(-1)\n        else:\n            return z\n\nclass WrappedRNANetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n        h = hparams or {}\n        self.network = ConvEmbedPoolX(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n\
    \            hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n            kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n            dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n            aggregator=str(h.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse_mix')),\n            tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n            length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n            learn_tau=bool(h.get('learn_tau', False)),\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params':\
    \ params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation\
    \ works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work\
    \ correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\
