- text: "Submitting dual-expert models (pooling + small BiGRU) and fixing learnable-τ initializer in experimental module for future runs.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/conv_pool_experimental.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Experimental variants for Conv + Global Pooling:\n    - mean_lse_max: concat(mean, LSE_tau, max) with length-normalized LSE\n    - mean_lse_mix: learned scalar mix of mean and LSE (w0, w1) → hidden-dim\n    - mean_lse_mix_cw: learned channel-wise mix of mean and LSE (w0[h], w1[h]) → hidden-dim\n  Options:\n    - tau: float (default 0.25)\n    - length_normalize_lse: bool (default True)\n    - learn_tau: bool (default False) — learnable τ via softplus\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n       \
    \   'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n      }\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau, length_normalize=True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  class ConvEmbedPoolX(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      learn_tau: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding=\"SAME\"\
    )(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n\n          tau_val = self.tau\n          if self.learn_tau:\n              # FIX: initialize using provided shape to avoid 0-d array indexing\n              tau_raw = self.param('tau_raw', lambda rng, shape: jnp.full(shape, self.tau), (1,))\n              tau_val = jax.nn.softplus(tau_raw)[0] + 1e-3\n\n          lse_pool = _lse_pool(h, tau_val, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          max_pool = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n\n          if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_max':\n              pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, lse_pool, max_pool], axis=-1)\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix':\n              w = self.param('mix_weights', lambda rng, shp: jnp.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=mean_pool.dtype), (2,))\n              w_norm = jax.nn.softmax(w)\n              pooled = w_norm[0] * mean_pool + w_norm[1] * lse_pool\n        \
    \  elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix_cw':\n              w_cw = self.param('mix_weights_cw',\n                                lambda rng, shp: jnp.stack([jnp.full((self.hidden_dim,), 0.5),\n                                                             jnp.full((self.hidden_dim,), 0.5)], axis=0),\n                                (2, self.hidden_dim))\n              w_norm = jax.nn.softmax(w_cw, axis=0)\n              pooled = w_norm[0] * mean_pool + w_norm[1] * lse_pool\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pooled)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return z.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"\
    regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n          self.network = ConvEmbedPoolX(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              aggregator=str(h.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse_mix')),\n              tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              learn_tau=bool(h.get('learn_tau', False)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n\
    \              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-expert: Conv+Pooling(mean←→LSE mix τ=0.25) + BiGRU(128) — averaged\"\ntags: \"ensemble, pooling, logsumexp, bigru, conv1d, parsimony\"\nabstract: \"Two-expert model: single Conv + learned mix(mean, LSE τ=0.25, len-norm) pooled expert, plus a small BiGRU expert on one-hot inputs. Each expert is projected to hidden_dim and averaged before a 2-layer head. Tests synergistic\
    \ inductive biases with minimal complexity.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          'gru_dim': 128,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-expert: Conv+Pooling(mean+LSE+max τ=0.25) + BiGRU(128) — averaged\"\ntags: \"ensemble, pooling, max, logsumexp, bigru, conv1d\"\nabstract: \"Two-expert model variant: pooled expert uses triple-stat concat(mean, LSE τ=0.25 len-norm, max) projected to hidden_dim; fused by averaging with a small BiGRU expert. Tests whether extreme evidence complements sequence modeling more than learned mixing.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_max',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          'gru_dim': 128,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/conv_pool_ablation_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Conv + Pooling family → Dual-expert (Pooling + BiGRU) — Update (Tick 315)\n\n  Best single-expert so far:\n  - Learned mix(mean, LSE τ=0.25, len-norm) — tri-seed mean ≈ 0.5257 (seed 7: 0.5280)\n\n  Recent ablations:\n  - Channel-wise mix: 0.5220 (slightly below scalar mix)\n  - Learnable τ: 0.5201 (no gain over fixed τ=0.25)\n  - Triple-stat (mean+LSE+max): 0.5203\n  - Capacity h=384: learned mix 0.5261 (ncRNA ↑ 0.855), mean+max 0.5113 (ncRNA ↓)\n\n  New direction (Axiom insight): dual-expert synergy\n  - Submitted: Conv+Pooling\
    \ (mix τ=0.25) + small BiGRU (avg fusion)\n  - Submitted: Conv+Pooling (mean+LSE+max τ=0.25) + small BiGRU (avg fusion)\n\n  Hypothesis:\n  - Pooling expert supplies robust “mass evidence”; BiGRU adds sequential/positional sensitivity — expected to aid CRISPR and ncRNA while keeping APA/MRL competitive.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{rank author}`"
thinking_content: '**Managing experiment submissions**


  I just executed code to put the dual_expert modules in storage but didn’t submit them yet. Now I can submit two runs: a baseline dual-expert and maybe a variant aggregator called ''mean_lse_mix'' with tau set to 0.25. I need to watch out for the concurrent limit of two pending experiments. Currently, there are free slots since some previous experiments have completed. I also considered reflecting on my work, but time is limited, and I want to stay productive.**Evaluating archiving and experiments**


  It looks like I can''t archive anything just yet since I''m still marked as immature, needing 50 maturity ticks while I''m at 21. So, I can keep running experiments. I could submit the dual-expert ''mean_lse_mix'' aggregator with tau set to 0.25, and I’m thinking of sticking with a default of 128 for the gru_dim, or maybe 64 to keep parameters minimal. I''ll also test the ''mean_lse_max'' aggregator since I have two concurrent slots. I should update the results summary to track channel-wise mix and learnable tau. Finally, I need to ensure that our network accepts the correct input shapes and defaults to cross-entropy for multi-class classification.**Reviewing training configurations**


  In the `train_single.py`, they specially handled ''multiclass_classification'' by replacing the loss function with cross-entropy. It seems they assign `compute_loss_fn` based on the task type; for ''multilabel_regression'', they set it to MSE, while using a default function for others. However, I noticed that ''multiclass_classification'' didn’t have a default listed. Our network has dropout and is working with a provided `rng_key`, which is good. I also saw some warnings about the `/tmp` directory being over 95% full, but the system is still running. I need to ensure that the ''mean_lse_mix_cw'' aggregator uses the correct parameter shapes.**Fixing initializer bug**


  I need to fix a bug in `conv_pool_experimental.py` related to the tau learnable initializer. I updated this file earlier, but the debugger flagged issues with editing the lineage file. After updating the file in storage during tick 312, it seems that the learning tau ablation is still referencing an older version that has the fixed parameter shape. Even though I wrote the correct code for ''tau_raw'', there seems to be confusion regarding the parameter creation for ''learn_tau'', which might have been done incorrectly.**Planning updates and submissions**


  I really need to update `conv_pool_experimental.py` to fix the tau learnable initializer bug. Although we included the right lines at tick 312, the issue persists because we didn’t modify the storage file. I’ll correct the initializer and focus on submitting evaluations with the dual expert setups: one using ''mean_lse_mix'' and another testing ''mean_lse_max''. I plan to draft two actions for submission and revise the results summary to include channel-wise mixing features and learnable tau. I''ll ensure everything is concise and well-structured for clarity.'
