tick: 316
role: model
parts:
- text: "Staging gated dual-expert variants (learned fusion between pooling and BiGRU) and updating the summary while current runs finish.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Dual-expert RNA model with learnable fusion:\n    - Expert A: Conv + Pooling (mean/LSE variants with length normalization; scalar or channel-wise mixing)\n    - Expert B: small BiGRU on one-hot sequence (with linear embed)\n  Fusion modes:\n    - 'avg': simple average of expert projections\n    - 'scalar_gate': learned global 2-way softmax gating (params only, data-independent)\n    - 'mlp_gate': small MLP gate over [pool_proj || rnn_proj] producing 2-way softmax\n  Parsimonious and dataset-agnostic.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE =\
    \ 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          # pooling settings\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',    # 'mean_lse_max' | 'mean_lse_mix' | 'mean_lse_mix_cw'\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          # rnn settings\n          'gru_dim': 128,\n          # fusion settings\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',         # 'avg' | 'scalar_gate' | 'mlp_gate'\n          'gate_hidden_frac': 0.5          # for mlp_gate: hidden = int(hidden_dim * frac)\n      }\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau, length_normalize=True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  class PoolingBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      aggregator:\
    \ str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      learn_tau: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          tau_val = self.tau\n          if self.learn_tau:\n              tau_raw = self.param('tau_raw', lambda rng, shape: jnp.full(shape, self.tau), (1,))\n              tau_val = jax.nn.softplus(tau_raw)[0] + 1e-3\n          lse_pool = _lse_pool(h, tau_val, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          max_pool = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n\n          if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_max':\n              pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, lse_pool, max_pool], axis=-1)\n              pooled = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pooled)\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix':\n              w = self.param('mix_weights', lambda rng, shp: jnp.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=mean_pool.dtype),\
    \ (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(w)\n              pooled = w[0] * mean_pool + w[1] * lse_pool\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix_cw':\n              w_cw = self.param('mix_weights_cw',\n                                lambda rng, shp: jnp.stack([jnp.full((self.hidden_dim,), 0.5),\n                                                             jnp.full((self.hidden_dim,), 0.5)], axis=0),\n                                (2, self.hidden_dim))\n              w_cw = jax.nn.softmax(w_cw, axis=0)\n              pooled = w_cw[0] * mean_pool + w_cw[1] * lse_pool\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n          return pooled\n\n  class BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x_emb = nn.Dense(self.gru_dim)(x)  # (batch, seq, gru_dim)\n          f_cell = nn.GRUCell()\n          b_cell = nn.GRUCell()\n          x_tm = jnp.swapaxes(x_emb, 0, 1)\n          x_tm_rev\
    \ = jnp.flip(x_tm, axis=0)\n          h0_f = nn.GRUCell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), (x_emb.shape[0],), self.gru_dim)\n          h0_b = nn.GRUCell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(1), (x_emb.shape[0],), self.gru_dim)\n          def fwd(c, xt):\n              c, _ = f_cell(c, xt)\n              return c, c\n          def bwd(c, xt):\n              c, _ = b_cell(c, xt)\n              return c, c\n          hf, _ = lax.scan(fwd, h0_f, x_tm)\n          hb, _ = lax.scan(bwd, h0_b, x_tm_rev)\n          rep = jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)   # (batch, 2*gru_dim)\n          return rep\n\n  class DualExpertWeighted(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      learn_tau: bool = False\n      gru_dim: int = 128\n      fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n\
    \      gate_hidden_frac: float = 0.5\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Conv feature extractor\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n\n          # Expert A: pooling\n          pool_rep = PoolingBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate,\n                                  self.aggregator, self.tau,\n                                  self.length_normalize_lse, self.learn_tau)(h, deterministic)\n          # Expert B: BiGRU\n          rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim)(x)\n          rnn_rep = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n          # Project each expert\n          pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n          rnn_proj  = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n          if self.fusion == 'avg':\n              fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n          elif self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n              logits = self.param('fusion_logits',\
    \ lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros((2,), dtype=pool_proj.dtype), (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n              fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n          elif self.fusion == 'mlp_gate':\n              # small gate MLP over concatenated projections\n              gate_in = jnp.concatenate([pool_proj, rnn_proj], axis=-1)\n              hidden = max(1, int(self.hidden_dim * self.gate_hidden_frac))\n              g = nn.Dense(hidden)(gate_in)\n              g = jax.nn.gelu(g)\n              g = nn.Dense(2)(g)  # logits\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(g, axis=-1)  # (batch, 2)\n              # broadcast combine\n              w_pool = w[:, 0:1]\n              w_rnn  = w[:, 1:2]\n              fused = w_pool * pool_proj + w_rnn * rnn_proj\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown fusion: {self.fusion}\")\n\n          # Head\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return z.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n          self.network = DualExpertWeighted(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              aggregator=str(h.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse_mix')),\n              tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              learn_tau=bool(h.get('learn_tau', False)),\n              gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 128)),\n              fusion=str(h.get('fusion',\
    \ 'scalar_gate')),\n              gate_hidden_frac=float(h.get('gate_hidden_frac', 0.5)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                        dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n\
    \      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/submit_dual_expert_weighted_scalar.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          'gru_dim': 128,\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate'\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\
    \n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/submit_dual_expert_weighted_mlp.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          'gru_dim': 128,\n          'fusion': 'mlp_gate',\n          'gate_hidden_frac': 0.5\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\
    \ hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/conv_pool_ablation_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Dual-expert Gated Fusion — Staged (Tick 316)\n  Staged code for two-expert models with learnable fusion:\n  - scalar_gate: data-independent softmax over {pool_proj, rnn_proj}\n  - mlp_gate: tiny MLP gate over [pool_proj || rnn_proj] → softmax weights\n\n  Rationale:\n  - Pooling expert (mass evidence) + BiGRU expert (sequence/position) showed promise in Axiom III's MoE.\n  - Fixed averaging may underweight useful expert per dataset; learned fusion should adapt parsimoniously.\n\n  To run (when slots free):\n  - submit_dual_expert_weighted_scalar.py\n  - submit_dual_expert_weighted_mlp.py\n\n  Current best (single-conv\
    \ family):\n  - Learned mix(mean, LSE τ=0.25, len-norm) — tri-seed mean ≈ 0.5257\n  - Dual-expert average fusion queued: IDs 469, 470\n```\n\n`/execute_action{rank author}`"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to respond with actions or analysis since we’re in a multi-agent research simulation.\n\nWe’ve submitted experiments, and dual-expert models are running. The system suggests previewing the Archive Room, but it seems we're still too immature for it, as it’s marked as unavailable until maturity. \n\nSince we’re under 50 ticks, we can’t access the Archive Room yet. It looks like we might want to reflect in the Reflection Chamber or update the results summary while we wait.**Designing next steps**\n\nI’m thinking about designing our next ablations, which could involve projection scaling differences, gating between experts instead of averaging, and examining dropout rates while keeping things simple and avoiding overformatting. \n\nWe can implement /execute_action commands in this environment, which means I could reflect in the Reflection Chamber or perform storage writes. We should draft a paper soon since we have over five experiments with\
  \ evaluation IDs and scores. Although the Archive Room is off-limits, we can start drafting in noema/paper/draft.md. It might also be useful to rank by score for checking SOTA, focusing on the top score around 0.686 from Noema I.**Evaluating improvements**\n\nIt looks like our average score of 0.528 is well below SOTA, which is around 0.68. In this new environment, the aggregator’s average is based on seven tasks, so that makes sense that our single convolution is still far from the top. \n\nWe’re focusing on being parsimonious with our contributions, but I think we could propose improvements like adding depthwise separable convolution blocks. Another possibility could be calibrating post-pooling scales and introducing a small learned gate value to weigh the two experts in the dual-expert model. We might also consider dropout rates, but can’t change the training pipeline besides adjusting hyperparameters, like the learning rate or defining constants for BATCH_SIZE. We’ll stick to modifying\
  \ network architecture and the optimizer for further enhancements.**Planning optimizer tweaks**\n\nI’m considering testing different optimizer learning rates, like 0.0005 versus 0.001, although our previous baseline used 0.001. Conducting heavy ablations across seeds could be token-expensive, but still manageable. \n\nI should also summarize the tri-seed average across models. As a next step, writing a draft in noema/paper/draft.md to prepare results for the Archive when matured sounds like a good plan. Creating a paper skeleton with sections for an abstract, methods, experiments, and results is essential. I can update the results index in results/FINAL.md by appending new findings. Lastly, I could develop code to evaluate the gating mechanism for the dual-expert model, learning a scalar fusion weight for more flexibility than a simple average.**Proposing new dual-expert variants**\n\nI’m thinking about proposing two new dual-expert variants. First, a weighted average with learned scalar\
  \ gating between the pool and GRU, using softmax for the dimensions. Second, a weighted gating system that takes aggregated feature projections and outputs a mixture coefficient, though this does add some complexity.\n\nI can run capacity sweeps for GRU dimensions, but we’re limited to two concurrent runs right now. I'll create a submission file for the new weighted dual-expert model and update the existing code to allow for different fusion parameters. We’ll also log results in the ablation summary and might reflect in the Reflection Chamber, but that’s not strictly necessary. Let's implement everything carefully using Flax!"
