parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 317\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 120,194 / 270,000 used (45%)\n- Agent Age: 24 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Dual-expert: Conv+Pooling(mean←→LSE mix τ=0.25) + BiGRU(128) — averaged' (ID: 469) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/b2757607-e97b-4741-907b-b2b7af3f3497/storage/system/main.py\"\
    , line 593, in <module>\n    result = main()\n             ^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/b2757607-e97b-4741-907b-b2b7af3f3497/storage/system/main.py\", line 553, in main\n    validation_success = simple_cpu_validation()\n                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/b2757607-e97b-4741-907b-b2b7af3f3497/storage/system/main.py\", line 415, in simple_cpu_validation\n    params = network.init(key, dummy_input)\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/b2757607-e97b-4741-907b-b2b7af3f3497/storage/noema/submissions/dual_expert_pool_gru.py\", line 178, in init\n    variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/b2757607-e97b-4741-907b-b2b7af3f3497/storage/noema/submissions/dual_expert_pool_gru.py\"\
    , line 141, in __call__\n    rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim)(x)                     # (batch, 2*gru_dim)\n              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/b2757607-e97b-4741-907b-b2b7af3f3497/storage/noema/submissions/dual_expert_pool_gru.py\", line 93, in __call__\n    f_cell = nn.GRUCell()\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/flax/linen/kw_only_dataclasses.py\", line 235, in init_wrapper\n    dataclass_init(self, *args, **kwargs)\nTypeError: GRUCell.__init__() missing 1 required positional argument: 'features'\n--------------------\nFor simplicity, JAX has removed its internal frames from the traceback of the following exception. Set JAX_TRACEBACK_FILTERING=off to include these.\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Dual-expert: Conv+Pooling(mean+LSE+max τ=0.25) + BiGRU(128) — averaged' (ID: 470) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\
    \n**Score:** 0.6206692484130775\n**APA_R2:** 0.8474\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0796\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9228\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.3719\n**PRS_R2:** 0.4699\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8669\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.7862\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 470\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The code has been successfully fixed and is running without errors. The submission is executing the full evaluation pipeline (validation, training, and testing) which takes several minutes to complete.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had **two critical bugs** in the `BiGRUBlock` class imported from `storage/noema/submissions/dual_expert_pool_gru.py`:\n\n### Bug 1: Missing required `features` parameter\n```python\n# WRONG (original code):\nf_cell = nn.GRUCell()\nb_cell = nn.GRUCell()\n```\n**Error**: `TypeError: GRUCell.__init__() missing 1 required positional argument: 'features'`\n\n### Bug 2: Incorrect `initialize_carry` API\
    \ usage\n```python\n# WRONG (original code):\nh0_f = nn.GRUCell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), (x_emb.shape[0],), self.gru_dim)\n```\n**Error**: `TypeError: 'int' object is not subscriptable` - The API expects a shape tuple as the second argument, not separate batch_size and features arguments.\n\n### Bug 3: JAX tracer leak with manual scan\nEven after fixing bugs 1 and 2, using manual `lax.scan` with GRU cells created inside `@nn.compact` caused a tracer leak error because the cells were being captured incorrectly by the scan function.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated **submission_v5.py** with a complete reimplementation of the `BiGRUBlock` using Flax's high-level `nn.RNN` wrapper:\n\n### Fixed Implementation\n```python\nclass BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n    gru_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # x: (batch, seq, 4) one-hot RNA\n        batch_size = x.shape[0]\n\n        # Small linear embed to GRU dim\n        x_emb = nn.Dense(self.gru_dim)(x)  # (batch,\
    \ seq, gru_dim)\n\n        # Use RNN scan for bidirectional processing\n        # Forward GRU\n        f_gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n        hf = f_gru(x_emb)  # (batch, seq, gru_dim), returns all hidden states\n        hf_final = hf[:, -1, :]  # Take last hidden state (batch, gru_dim)\n\n        # Backward GRU\n        x_emb_rev = jnp.flip(x_emb, axis=1)  # Reverse sequence\n        b_gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n        hb = b_gru(x_emb_rev)  # (batch, seq, gru_dim)\n        hb_final = hb[:, -1, :]  # Take last hidden state (batch, gru_dim)\n\n        rep = jnp.concatenate([hf_final, hb_final], axis=-1)  # (batch, 2*gru_dim)\n        return rep\n```\n\n### Key Changes\n1. **Used `nn.RNN` wrapper**: Properly handles the scan loop and state management\n2. **Correct GRUCell instantiation**: Added required `features=self.gru_dim` parameter\n3. **Simplified bidirectional logic**: Flip input sequence for backward pass instead of manual scan\n4. **Extracted\
    \ final states**: Take last hidden state `[:, -1, :]` from the sequence outputs\n\n## Verification\nThe fix was verified by monitoring the evaluation:\n- ✅ Passes initialization phase (network creation)\n- ✅ Passes validation phase (CPU inference test)\n- ✅ Running for 300+ seconds without crashes (full evaluation in progress)\n- ✅ Exit code indicates successful execution\n\nThe evaluation is taking several minutes because it includes:\n1. Simple CPU validation\n2. Full training on multiple RNA datasets\n3. Testing and metric computation\n\n## Recommendation\nThe code is now working correctly. The complete neural network architecture (Conv+Pooling expert + BiGRU expert) is functioning as intended. The agent can use this fixed submission as a reference for future work with bidirectional RNNs in Flax.\n\n## Files Modified\n- **submissions/submission_v5.py** - Complete fixed implementation (no dependencies on buggy lineage code)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files\
    \ in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v5):**\n```python\n\"\"\"\nFixed version: Dual-expert RNA model with corrected BiGRU implementation.\nBugs fixed:\n1. nn.GRUCell() was called without the required 'features' argument\n2. nn.GRUCell.initialize_carry() was called with wrong arguments\n3. Tracer leak fixed by using scan properly with Flax modules\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nfrom jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 256,\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n        'aggregator': 'mean_lse_max',\n        'tau': 0.25,\n        'length_normalize_lse': True,\n        'learn_tau': False,\n        'gru_dim': 128,\n    }\n\ndef _lse_pool(h,\
    \ tau, length_normalize=True):\n    # h: (batch, seq, hidden)\n    L = h.shape[1]\n    core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n    if length_normalize:\n        core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n    return tau * core  # (batch, hidden)\n\nclass PoolingBlock(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n    tau: float = 0.25\n    length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n    learn_tau: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # h: (batch, seq, hidden)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)                    # (batch, hidden)\n        # tau (fixed or learnable per-model)\n        tau_val = self.tau\n        if self.learn_tau:\n            tau_raw = self.param('tau_raw', lambda rng, shp: jnp.array(self.tau), (1,))\n            tau_val = jax.nn.softplus(tau_raw)[0] + 1e-3\n        lse_pool = _lse_pool(h,\
    \ tau_val, self.length_normalize_lse)  # (batch, hidden)\n        max_pool = jnp.max(h, axis=1)                      # (batch, hidden)\n\n        if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_max':\n            pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, lse_pool, max_pool], axis=-1)  # (batch, 3*hidden)\n            # project back to hidden_dim to keep downstream dims stable\n            pooled = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pooled)\n        elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix':\n            w = self.param('mix_weights',\n                           lambda rng, shp: jnp.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=mean_pool.dtype), (2,))\n            w = jax.nn.softmax(w)  # convex comb\n            pooled = w[0] * mean_pool + w[1] * lse_pool     # (batch, hidden)\n        elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix_cw':\n            w_cw = self.param('mix_weights_cw',\n                              lambda rng, shp: jnp.stack([jnp.full((self.hidden_dim,), 0.5),\n                                                           jnp.full((self.hidden_dim,),\
    \ 0.5)], axis=0),\n                              (2, self.hidden_dim))\n            w_cw = jax.nn.softmax(w_cw, axis=0)             # (2, hidden)\n            pooled = w_cw[0] * mean_pool + w_cw[1] * lse_pool\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n        return pooled  # (batch, hidden_dim)\n\nclass BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n    gru_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # x: (batch, seq, 4) one-hot RNA\n        batch_size = x.shape[0]\n\n        # Small linear embed to GRU dim\n        x_emb = nn.Dense(self.gru_dim)(x)  # (batch, seq, gru_dim)\n\n        # Use RNN scan for bidirectional processing\n        # Forward GRU\n        f_gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n        hf = f_gru(x_emb)  # (batch, seq, gru_dim), returns all hidden states\n        hf_final = hf[:, -1, :]  # Take last hidden state (batch, gru_dim)\n\n        # Backward GRU\n        x_emb_rev = jnp.flip(x_emb, axis=1)  # Reverse\
    \ sequence\n        b_gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n        hb = b_gru(x_emb_rev)  # (batch, seq, gru_dim)\n        hb_final = hb[:, -1, :]  # Take last hidden state (batch, gru_dim)\n\n        rep = jnp.concatenate([hf_final, hb_final], axis=-1)  # (batch, 2*gru_dim)\n        return rep\n\nclass DualExpertNet(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n    hidden_dim: int = 256\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n    tau: float = 0.25\n    length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n    learn_tau: bool = False\n    gru_dim: int = 128\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # x: (batch, seq, 4)\n        # Conv feature extractor\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n\n        # Expert 1: pooling\n        pool_rep = PoolingBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate,\n\
    \                                self.aggregator, self.tau,\n                                self.length_normalize_lse, self.learn_tau)(h, deterministic)\n\n        # Expert 2: BiGRU\n        rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim)(x)                     # (batch, 2*gru_dim)\n        rnn_rep = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)              # project to hidden_dim\n\n        # Expert projections and fusion (average)\n        pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n        rnn_proj  = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n        fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)                      # (batch, hidden_dim)\n\n        # Head\n        z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)\n        z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n            return z.squeeze(-1)\n        else:\n            return z\n\nclass WrappedRNANetwork:\n\
    \    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n        h = hparams or {}\n        self.network = DualExpertNet(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n            kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n            dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n            aggregator=str(h.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse_mix')),\n            tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n            length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n            learn_tau=bool(h.get('learn_tau', False)),\n            gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 128)),\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                      dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\
    \n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n\
