parts:
- text: "Excellent progress. The dual-expert model (pooling + BiGRU) with learned mean↔LSE mix set a new best for our lineage at 0.6305. I’ll run tri-seed stability for this variant next.\n\nSubmitting learned-mix dual-expert tri-seed (seeds 7 and 123).\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-expert (avg): Conv+Pooling(mean↔LSE mix τ=0.25 len-norm) + BiGRU(128) — tri-seed (seed=7)\"\ntags: \"ensemble, pooling, logsumexp, bigru, replication, stability\"\nabstract: \"Tri-seed replication for the dual-expert learned mix(mean, LSE τ=0.25 len-norm) + BiGRU. This run uses BASE_SEED=7 to assess stability and variance across datasets.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n    \
    \      'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          'gru_dim': 128,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-expert (avg): Conv+Pooling(mean↔LSE mix τ=0.25 len-norm) + BiGRU(128) — tri-seed (seed=123)\"\ntags: \"ensemble, pooling, logsumexp, bigru, replication, stability\"\nabstract: \"Tri-seed replication for the dual-expert learned mix(mean, LSE τ=0.25 len-norm) + BiGRU. This run uses BASE_SEED=123 to complete stability assessment.\"\
    \ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          'gru_dim': 128,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage\
    \ write noema/results/dual_expert_breakthrough.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Dual-Expert (Pooling + BiGRU) — Stability Plan Update (Tick 319)\n\n  New best (learned mix, seed=42):\n  - 472 — 0.6305 | APA 0.8463 | CRI-Off 0.0869 | Modif 0.9346 | CRI-On 0.4356 | PRS 0.4481 | MRL 0.8697 | ncRNA 0.7923\n\n  Triple-stat results:\n  - 470 (seed=42): 0.6207 (very strong)\n  - 473 (seed=7):  0.5986 (Modif drop to 0.7371 indicates higher variance)\n\n  Actions:\n  - Submitted tri-seed for learned mix (seeds=7,123). After completion, compare variance vs triple-stat.\n  - Next queued (after slots free): gated fusion with learned mix (scalar_gate, mlp_gate) to adaptively weight experts.\n\n  Notes:\n  - Dual-expert consistently boosts APA/MRL/PRS/Modif; learned mix appears more stable than triple-stat across seeds.\n  - Aim: close the remaining gap to lineage SOTA (~0.686) via adaptive fusion and mild capacity tuning (hidden ∈ {192, 320}), while keeping parsimony.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{rank\
    \ author}`"
