tick: 320
role: model
parts:
- text: "Staging adaptive fusion with post-fusion normalization, and documenting the plan in Private Memory. Will submit gated variants once current tri-seed runs complete.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Dual-expert RNA model with learnable fusion and optional post-fusion normalization.\n    - Expert A: Conv + Pooling (mean/LSE variants with length normalization; scalar or channel-wise mixing)\n    - Expert B: small BiGRU on one-hot sequence (with linear embed)\n  Fusion modes:\n    - 'avg': simple average of expert projections\n    - 'scalar_gate': learned global 2-way softmax gating (params only, data-independent)\n    - 'mlp_gate': small MLP gate over [pool_proj || rnn_proj] producing 2-way softmax\n  Optionally apply LayerNorm after fusion to stabilize scales.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  from jax.scipy.special\
    \ import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          # pooling settings\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',    # 'mean_lse_max' | 'mean_lse_mix' | 'mean_lse_mix_cw'\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          # rnn settings\n          'gru_dim': 128,\n          # fusion settings\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',         # 'avg' | 'scalar_gate' | 'mlp_gate'\n          'gate_hidden_frac': 0.5,         # for mlp_gate: hidden = int(hidden_dim * frac)\n          'post_norm': False               # apply LayerNorm after fusion\n      }\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau, length_normalize=True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core\
    \ = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  class PoolingBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      learn_tau: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          tau_val = self.tau\n          if self.learn_tau:\n              tau_raw = self.param('tau_raw', lambda rng, shape: jnp.full(shape, self.tau), (1,))\n              tau_val = jax.nn.softplus(tau_raw)[0] + 1e-3\n          lse_pool = _lse_pool(h, tau_val, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          max_pool = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n\n          if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_max':\n              pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, lse_pool, max_pool], axis=-1)\n              pooled = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pooled)\n\
    \          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix':\n              w = self.param('mix_weights', lambda rng, shp: jnp.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=mean_pool.dtype), (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(w)\n              pooled = w[0] * mean_pool + w[1] * lse_pool\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix_cw':\n              w_cw = self.param('mix_weights_cw',\n                                lambda rng, shp: jnp.stack([jnp.full((self.hidden_dim,), 0.5),\n                                                             jnp.full((self.hidden_dim,), 0.5)], axis=0),\n                                (2, self.hidden_dim))\n              w_cw = jax.nn.softmax(w_cw, axis=0)\n              pooled = w_cw[0] * mean_pool + w_cw[1] * lse_pool\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n          return pooled\n\n  class BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x_emb = nn.Dense(self.gru_dim)(x)\
    \  # (batch, seq, gru_dim)\n          f_gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hf = f_gru(x_emb)              # (batch, seq, gru_dim)\n          hf_final = hf[:, -1, :]\n          x_emb_rev = jnp.flip(x_emb, axis=1)\n          b_gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hb = b_gru(x_emb_rev)\n          hb_final = hb[:, -1, :]\n          return jnp.concatenate([hf_final, hb_final], axis=-1)\n\n  class DualExpertWeighted(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      learn_tau: bool = False\n      gru_dim: int = 128\n      fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n      gate_hidden_frac: float = 0.5\n      post_norm: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Conv features\n\
    \          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n\n          # Experts\n          pool_rep = PoolingBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate,\n                                  self.aggregator, self.tau,\n                                  self.length_normalize_lse, self.learn_tau)(h, deterministic)\n          rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim)(x)\n          rnn_rep = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n          # Projections\n          pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n          rnn_proj  = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n          # Fusion\n          if self.fusion == 'avg':\n              fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n          elif self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n              logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros((2,), dtype=pool_proj.dtype), (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n              fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n\
    \          elif self.fusion == 'mlp_gate':\n              gate_in = jnp.concatenate([pool_proj, rnn_proj], axis=-1)\n              hidden = max(1, int(self.hidden_dim * self.gate_hidden_frac))\n              g = nn.Dense(hidden)(gate_in)\n              g = jax.nn.gelu(g)\n              g = nn.Dense(2)(g)\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(g, axis=-1)\n              fused = w[:, :1] * pool_proj + w[:, 1:] * rnn_proj\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown fusion: {self.fusion}\")\n\n          if self.post_norm:\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n\n          # Head\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return z.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n  \
    \    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n          self.network = DualExpertWeighted(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              aggregator=str(h.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse_mix')),\n              tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              learn_tau=bool(h.get('learn_tau', False)),\n              gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 128)),\n              fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n              gate_hidden_frac=float(h.get('gate_hidden_frac', 0.5)),\n              post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', False)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key\
    \ = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                        dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/submit_dual_expert_weighted_scalar_mix_postnorm.py}`\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          'gru_dim': 128,\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n\
    \      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/submit_dual_expert_weighted_mlp_mix_postnorm.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          'gru_dim': 128,\n          'fusion': 'mlp_gate',\n          'gate_hidden_frac': 0.5,\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:\
    \ float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-Expert Breakthrough: Pooling + BiGRU — Results and Next Steps\"\nabstract: \"Summary of experiments leading to a new lineage-best (0.6305) with a parsimonious two-expert model; stability plan, fusion ablations, and capacity considerations.\"\ncontent: |\n  Key results:\n  - 472 (dual-expert, learned mix, seed=42): 0.6305 | APA 0.8463 | CRI-Off 0.0869 | Modif 0.9346 | CRI-On 0.4356 | PRS 0.4481 | MRL 0.8697 | ncRNA 0.7923\n  - 470 (dual-expert, triple-stat, seed=42): 0.6207 (strong across APA/MRL/Modif/PRS)\n  - 473 (dual-expert, triple-stat, seed=7): 0.5986 (Modif dropped to 0.7371 → higher variance)\n  - Single-expert best (learned mix): ~0.526 (tri-seed\
    \ mean)\n  - Channel-wise mix and learnable τ did not help in single-expert.\n  - Capacity (h=384) helped ncRNA but hurt MRL in single-expert; dual-expert mitigates with strong MRL.\n\n  Diagnosis:\n  - Complementary inductive biases (mass evidence via pooling + sequence/position via BiGRU) explain broad gains.\n  - Triple-stat pooling can be volatile on Modif; learned mix appears more stable (pending tri-seeds).\n\n  In flight / staged:\n  - Running: dual-expert learned mix tri-seeds (seeds 7, 123).\n  - Staged (awaiting slots): gated fusion (scalar and MLP) with post-fusion LayerNorm, aggregator=learned mix.\n  - Staged: tri-seed triple-stat seed=123; compare stability to learned mix.\n  - If gains plateau: small capacity sweep (hidden ∈ {192, 320}) under dual-expert learned mix.\n\n  Paper outline (draft later):\n  - Motivation: parsimony + universality; pitfalls of single-stat pooling.\n  - Method: dual-expert (Conv+Pooling) + (BiGRU) with simple fusion; ablations (mix vs max vs\
    \ triple-stat; seeds; gating; capacity).\n  - Results: aggregate and per-dataset trends; stability; compute/time budget.\n  - Takeaways: simple deterministic ensembles of diverse inductive biases outperform single-expert baselines on multi-dataset RNA.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{rank author}`"
thinking_content: '**Analyzing next steps**


  I need to decide on our next actions and message about our progress. We''ve made a major breakthrough with dual-expert pooling and BiGRU, scoring 0.6305, which is our new best for lineage but still below the SOTA at around 0.686 (from Noema I results). We have tri-seed runs for the learned-mix dual-expert with seeds 7 and 123 running, and other experiments are completed but can’t submit gated fusion variants just yet. I’ll focus on preparing and updating the summary now.**Planning next experiments**


  Next, when slots become available, I plan to run the scalar gate with the mean LSE mix aggregator, as well as the MLP gate. I also want to tri-seed the triple-stat experiment with seed 123, which is already staged. It might be helpful to store the scripts and adjust hyperparameters for capacity, like hidden dimensions of 320 or 192, to find the best fit. I should remain cautious about capacity since MRL soared precariously high at 0.8697. Reflecting in the Reflection Chamber seems like a good idea to gather insights too!**Clarifying reflection actions**


  I''m feeling a bit unclear about what steps to take regarding the reflection room. We haven''t looked up help for it yet, but research operations might be an option. I also considered writing a paper in private memory, but it seems the Archive Room is unavailable for now, requiring maturity. Since we’re at 27 ticks and need 50 for access, I can still document in private memory. Writing a capsule there to keep records might be beneficial while noting that we can''t publish just yet.**Proposing next steps**


  I think we should evaluate the gating variants after tri-seed runs and try capacity settings for hidden dimensions of 192 and 320 for the learned mix. Adding fusion gating and normalizing the fused vector could be beneficial, especially with the new "fusion" setup. We can introduce a post-fusion LayerNorm as well, even though the spec doesn''t allow editing the training loop. While keeping everything minimal, we should stage an update for the dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted to include the post_norm parameter. But with two existing submissions, we can''t submit any more right now, so we’ll need to prioritize our actions.**Outlining action steps**


  I’m planning to write additional wrappers and update the summary, plus note insights in the Reflection Room. The steps include updating the storage write to the weighted module to add optional LayerNorm for better gating stability. I''ll prepare for capacity sweeps for the learned-mix dual-expert setup and document results in private memory. Sending an email to Axiom III about our breakthrough could be nice but must be token-efficient. Finally, I’ll create a capsule in private memory with all relevant details, while ensuring we don’t submit any new runs since two are pending.'
