tick: 321
role: model
parts:
- text: "The learned-mix dual-expert set a new best (0.6305), but seed=7 shows instability (MRL early-stopped at 0.615). I’ll test adaptive fusion with post-fusion normalization to stabilize across seeds.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-expert (scalar gate + post-norm): mix(mean,LSE τ=0.25) + BiGRU(128)\"\ntags: \"ensemble, gating, layernorm, pooling, logsumexp, bigru\"\nabstract: \"Learned scalar gating between pooled expert and BiGRU projection with post-fusion LayerNorm. Aggregator uses learned mix(mean, length-normalized LSE, τ=0.25). Tests whether adaptive fusion and scale normalization improve stability and average score.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        \
    \  'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          'gru_dim': 128,\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-expert (MLP gate + post-norm): mix(mean,LSE τ=0.25) + BiGRU(128)\"\ntags: \"ensemble, gating, mlp, layernorm, pooling, bigru\"\nabstract: \"Tiny MLP gate over concat(projections) with softmax weights and\
    \ post-fusion LayerNorm. Aggregator uses learned mix(mean, length-normalized LSE, τ=0.25). Tests data-dependent fusion for stability and average score.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          'gru_dim': 128,\n          'fusion': 'mlp_gate',\n          'gate_hidden_frac': 0.5,\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float\
    \ = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_breakthrough.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Dual-Expert (Pooling + BiGRU) — Stability observations (Tick 321)\n  Learned mix (avg fusion):\n  - seed=42: 0.6305 | APA 0.8463 | CRI-Off 0.0869 | Modif 0.9346 | CRI-On 0.4356 | PRS 0.4481 | MRL 0.8697 | ncRNA 0.7923\n  - seed=123: 0.6256 | APA 0.8526 | CRI-Off 0.0881 | Modif 0.9258 | CRI-On 0.4196 | PRS 0.4408 | MRL 0.8771 | ncRNA 0.7754\n  - seed=7:   0.5768 | APA 0.8476 | CRI-Off 0.0837 | Modif 0.8577 | CRI-On 0.4011 | PRS 0.4494 | MRL 0.6152 | ncRNA 0.7831\n  Observation: seed=7 underperforms due to MRL early stop (0.615), while other seeds reach ~0.87 R2. Hypothesis: fusion scale mismatch or seed interaction with dropout led to suboptimal convergence\
