thinking_content: '**Planning evaluation actions**


  I’m figuring out our next steps with two ongoing evaluations, 477 and 478. We’ve had tri-seed results: seed 42 is at 0.6305, seed 123 at 0.6256, and seed 7 at 0.5768. I want to improve stability, so we submitted gating with post-norm for seed 42. However, we can''t publish in the Archive Room yet since it''s unavailable until maturity at 50 ticks. Right now, we’re at 29 ticks, so I’ll prepare a draft in Private Memory. Plus, I should check the Noema I Archive for the state of the art, noting we''re still behind.**Exploring model adjustments**


  I’m considering ways to improve the BiGRU model''s capacity by increasing hidden dimensions or adjusting dropout to avoid early stopping due to MRL. I could also explore adding LayerNorm, although gating with post-norm might help too. A learning rate schedule could be beneficial as well since the default uses optax adamw at 0.001. The training logs indicate unexpectedly high scores, but I''m puzzled why the average remains at 0.63 despite such good results. My calculations confirm the consistency of the average across various tasks, which is interesting.**Planning model improvements**


  It seems Noema I''s top score of around 0.686 is significantly higher than our best of 0.6305. I''m thinking about how we might reach a mid 0.65 by adjusting gating or the aggregator triple-stat. Our earlier triple-stat with seed 42 was 0.6207, and we haven''t run gating for that yet, but we''re currently working on gated mixes. I also want to check storage system defaults for training loops and plan next experiments, like using post-norm gating and experimenting with model dimensions and dropout rates. We should be mindful of token usage; I''m aware we''re at 167k out of 270k.**Continuing research actions**


  It looks like the user didn''t have a specific request, so I want to keep moving forward with research actions. I’m thinking about whether to write to Public Memory or the Archive, but Public Memory is restricted until it matures. Private Memory is a good option, though. I noticed that Research Counter only shows Noema I results right now, displaying the top score of 0.686. Our score of 0.630 isn’t visible since it seems to be filtered out. I guess Page 2 might show it, but that''s not essential.**Designing additional wrappers**


  I’m thinking about implementing a small ablation with the dual-expert learned mix, adjusting dropout to 0.08 to see if it helps with the MRL issue on seed 7. Another idea is to use post-norm averaging without gating, as we already have gating and post-norm. I could easily test the ''avg with post_norm'' setup. We can design wrappers for different dropout levels and GRU sizes, creating two for dropout at 0.08 and GRU dimension at 160. We won’t submit yet because we have two runs ongoing, but I can start writing files now and update the summary. I''ll also consider sending a note to Axiom III about training stability. Lastly, I need to wrap up my final actions!'
