- text: "Submitting tri-seed replication for the current best model (scalar gate + post-norm, BiGRU=160) to assess stability.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-expert (scalar gate + post-norm, BiGRU=160) — tri-seed (seed=7)\"\ntags: \"ensemble, gating, layernorm, pooling, bigru, stability\"\nabstract: \"Tri-seed replication of the best model: scalar-gated fusion with post-fusion LayerNorm between pooled learned mix(mean, len-norm LSE τ=0.25) and BiGRU hidden=160. This run uses BASE_SEED=7.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse':\
    \ True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-expert (scalar gate + post-norm, BiGRU=160) — tri-seed (seed=123)\"\ntags: \"ensemble, gating, layernorm, pooling, bigru, stability\"\nabstract: \"Tri-seed replication of the best model: scalar-gated fusion with post-fusion LayerNorm between pooled learned mix(mean, len-norm LSE τ=0.25) and BiGRU hidden=160. This run uses BASE_SEED=123.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n\
    \  from dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage\
    \ write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  eval_id,model,seed,score,APA,CRI-Off,Modif,CRI-On,PRS,MRL,ncRNA\n  485,scalar_gate+postnorm mix+BiGRU160,42,0.6388,0.8536,0.0888,0.9241,0.3895,0.5336,0.8732,0.8092\n  477,scalar_gate+postnorm mix+BiGRU128,42,0.6372,0.8506,0.0845,0.9173,0.3877,0.5153,0.8852,0.8200\n  481,scalar_gate+postnorm mix+BiGRU128,123,0.6182,0.8500,0.0788,0.7927,0.3620,0.5244,0.8858,0.8338\n  480,scalar_gate+postnorm mix+BiGRU128,7,0.6214,0.8489,0.0796,0.8779,0.3895,0.4559,0.8843,0.8138\n  472,avg mix+BiGRU128,42,0.6305,0.8463,0.0869,0.9346,0.4356,0.4481,0.8697,0.7923\n  475,avg mix+BiGRU128,123,0.6256,0.8526,0.0881,0.9258,0.4196,0.4408,0.8771,0.7754\n  474,avg mix+BiGRU128,7,0.5768,0.8476,0.0837,0.8577,0.4011,0.4494,0.6152,0.7831\n```"
