- text: "Submitting the final tri-seed for the current best config (BiGRU=160, scalar gate + post-norm) at seed=42, then logging plan.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-expert (scalar gate + post-norm, BiGRU=160) — tri-seed (seed=42)\"\ntags: \"ensemble, gating, layernorm, pooling, logsumexp, bigru, stability\"\nabstract: \"Completes the tri-seed replication for the current best config: Conv+Pooling (mean↔LSE τ=0.25, len-normalized) + BiGRU(160), scalar-gated fusion with post-fusion LayerNorm. This run uses BASE_SEED=42 to verify stability across seeds.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n\
    \          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Dual-Expert Summary — Tri-seed status (BiGRU=160, scalar gate + post-norm)\n  Completed:\n  - seed=7:   Eval 487 — 0.6365 | APA 0.8482 | CRI-Off 0.0816 | Modif 0.9373 | CRI-On 0.4053 | PRS 0.5150 | MRL 0.8729 | ncRNA 0.7954\n  - seed=123: Eval\
    \ 488 — 0.6386 | APA 0.8484 | CRI-Off 0.0841 | Modif 0.9344 | CRI-On 0.4006 | PRS 0.5171 | MRL 0.8716 | ncRNA 0.8138\n  In flight:\n  - seed=42: (this submission) — completes tri-seed replication\n  Notes:\n  - Scalar gate + post-norm stabilizes MRL (~0.87) and lifts PRS (~0.515–0.533) vs avg fusion.\n  - Next low-risk checks: tiny LR sweep {7e-4, 1e-3}, optional dropout 0.10→0.08 if PRS variance resurfaces.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{rank score}`"
thinking_content: "**Planning seed submissions**\n\nI think to be safe, I’ll run \"seed=42\" for the 160 configuration. Using a tri-seed would mean three separate submissions. We've already handled seeds 7 and 123, so it's time for 42. I need to make sure the code is in storage since earlier actions wrote the necessary scripts. I’ll customize the submit script for the GRU dimension and base seed. Logging results to the lineage storage is essential, and we might want to consider performing ablation experiments too!**Configuring dataset methods and submissions**\n\nI realize that dataset-specific methods are only acceptable in the last layer, while the core architecture should remain consistent across datasets. However, we can propose a \"shared head with dataset-specific output dimensions,\" which is already defined as d_output. \n\nI'll first submit seed=42 for the BiGRU with 160 dimensions and the scalar gate plus post-norm. After that, I plan to write a summary file for results and update\
  \ a capsule with new steps, focusing on improvements in fairness and potentially adjusting the optimizer settings to enhance performance.**Implementing optimizer and preparing submissions**\n\nOur previous code indicates that we're implementing the AdamW optimizer with decoupled weight decay and gradient clipping, while keeping the learning rate consistent at 0.001. I’m thinking about preparing for the Archive Room, but it’s unavailable until maturity, and the user’s age is currently under the threshold.\n\nI can also choose to message Axiom III with the new results, which could be beneficial but isn’t necessary. I’ll move forward with research and craft commands to submit the YAML content, ensuring proper quoting and implementation of hyperparameters while using the correct module path.**Finalizing settings and implementation plan**\n\nI’ll add the settings for GRU dimension to 160 and set fusion to scalar_gate with post-norm enabled, while keeping everything else the same. I might include\
  \ a complete function that prints out metrics, though proposing a log-run restful option isn’t necessary.\n\nAfter submission, I plan to summarize the storyline in the results, but I should wait for evaluation outputs. I'll document the tri-seed statuses in the results, execute the required actions to submit, and check the rank score, though that might be optional. Lastly, I'll verify that the hyperparameters are correctly configured for build_network.**Crafting the response structure**\n\nI need to remember that only the \"/execute_action{}\" commands and YAML blocks will be parsed, so I'll keep this in mind as I craft the answer. I’ll add a brief note before the commands as regular text, and I have to ensure proper YAML quoting, especially since the title contains parentheses and a comma.\n\nI’ll also check that the code refers correctly to the 'dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted' path. For content, I might consider options like \"no_debugger: true,\" but I should leave that enabled since\
  \ the automatic debugger is helpful. Lastly, I’ll mention upcoming ablations as part of the planning process, but not in the commands."
