tick: 336
role: model
parts:
- text: "Learnings: k=11 boosts ncRNA (0.8646) but drops PRS; τ=0.20 doesn’t help. Re-attempting learnable τ (now that the queue is free) and probing k=9 as a middle ground.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-expert (scalar gate + post-norm, BiGRU=160) — learnable LSE τ (init 0.25) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"ensemble, gating, layernorm, pooling, logsumexp, bigru\"\nabstract: \"Enable learnable LSE temperature (global; init τ=0.25) within the mean↔LSE mix to let the model calibrate pooling sharpness. Baseline: scalar-gated dual-expert with BiGRU=160 and post-fusion LayerNorm.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator':\
    \ 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,           # init\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': True,     # learn temperature\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-expert (scalar gate + post-norm, BiGRU=160) — kernel_size=9 — seed=42\"\ntags: \"ensemble, gating, layernorm, bigru, pooling, kernel-size\"\nabstract: \"Middle-ground kernel to trade off motif span vs PRS stability: conv k=9 with otherwise identical dual-expert setup.\
    \ Tests whether it preserves PRS while improving ncRNA/APA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 9,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset');\
    \ vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update (Tick 336)\n  Recent ablations:\n  - k=11 (Eval 499): 0.6425 | APA 0.8474 | CRI-Off 0.0852 | Modif 0.9223 | CRI-On 0.4000 | PRS 0.4998 | MRL 0.8785 | ncRNA 0.8646 (↑). Trade-off: ncRNA↑, PRS↓.\n  - τ=0.20 (Eval 500): 0.6357 | APA 0.8451 | CRI-Off 0.0819 | Modif 0.8931 | CRI-On 0.4067 | PRS 0.5154 | MRL 0.8784 | ncRNA 0.8292. Not better than τ=0.25.\n  - RC(train+eval) (Eval 495): 0.6427; near-best but not an improvement (APA↑, PRS slightly↓). RC eval-only catastrophic—orientation-specific labels.\n\n  Best so far:\n  - Tri-seed scalar-gated BiGRU=160, k=7: 492 (seed=42) — 0.6446 | APA 0.8459 | CRI-Off 0.0625 | Modif 0.9448 | CRI-On 0.3938 | PRS 0.5514 | MRL 0.8873 | ncRNA 0.8262.\n\n  In flight:\n  - Learnable τ (init 0.25).\n  - k=9 middle-ground.\n\n  Next if needed:\n  - Pre-fusion per-expert\
    \ scale norm (tiny LayerNorm per expert before gating) to stabilize PRS/CRI. Tri-seed any win.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing model performance**\n\nI noticed that a learning rate of 1e-3 seems good, especially since LR 7e-4 harmed PRS significantly. The RC eval-only is catastrophic and orientation-specific, but the train+eval improved APA to 0.8583 while maintaining PRS. Now, I'm thinking about trying a learnable tau variant that could find a suitable value, possibly around 0.22. We also want to explore adding pre-fusion per-expert LayerNorm, which might help with projection scales and reduce PRS variance. But will our base code support this 'pre_norm'? That’s a good question!**Considering code updates and requirements**\n\nEarlier, it was noted in a summary that \"Gated fusion + post-norm\" was mentioned, but there wasn't a reference to \"pre-norm.\" The updates I’m considering require a code change since we already utilized post-pool scale calibration. I can update the module 'dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted.py' to include optional per-expert LayerNorm, which is manageable. However,\
  \ I need to ensure that the code stays compliant with allowed functions. Also, we have to meet the archive paper requirement of at least five experiments, but maturity hasn’t reached the necessary 50 ticks.**Preparing for submission**\n\nWe can't publish until we reach 50 ticks, and we're currently at 43. The next step involves reattempting the submission of the learnable tau and possibly the pre-norm gating variant. The concurrency limit is at 2, and since we have no running experiments, I can submit both now. However, I need to update the 'dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted.py' module to add pre-norm. I should be cautious about overwriting this module since it could impact future training, but previous evaluations are complete, so it should be manageable.**Testing pre-norm support**\n\nI don’t think we need to rewrite the code if it already supports 'pre_norm,' but it's unclear if it does. We previously confirmed support for 'post_norm,' so I should test the 'pre_norm' parameter to ensure\
  \ robustness. If it doesn't work, I could propose using only 'post_norm.' I’ll submit the learnable tau and wait for results. Meanwhile, I’m considering the Reflection Chamber to gain perspective, but I wonder about its specific actions. It's also a good idea to note reflections in Private Memory, along with calibrating PRS using small adjustments.**Updating and submitting results**\n\nI need to update the summary file with the latest results for submissions 499 and 500, noting that kernel 11 improved ncRNA but hurt PRS. A learnable tau variant should be submitted first, followed by an optional pre-norm gating variant if the code supports it. Since we might overwrite existing module code, I want to check if 'dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted.py' supports 'pre_norm'. To be safe, I’ll focus on submitting just the learnable tau variant now, considering other incremental changes like adjusting dropout rates or kernel size later. Before submitting, I’ll read the module to confirm support.**Finalizing\
  \ submission actions**\n\nI need to summarize the results: submission 499 improved ncRNA to 0.8646 while 500 didn’t help. I’ll resubmit the learnable tau variant with the appropriate YAML code referencing the same module settings. Since the concurrency limit is 2, I can submit both the learnable tau and the kernel size of 9. \n\nI’ll update the results file summary and consider minor adjustments while being mindful of token usage. Now, I'll proceed with the following actions:\n\n- Submit learnable tau.\n- Submit kernel size 9.\n- Update storage with a summary. \n- Possibly share results in Private Memory."
