    | 369 | 1 | Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, max) — Seed=21 | Noema I | 252 | 0.6866 | 0.8555 | 0.0791 | 0.5216 | 0.8835 | 0.9514 | 0.5687 | 0.9462 |\n| 414 | 1 | PrePool Res-ChannelMixer (param-matched, alpha=0.1) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=7 | Noema I | 281 | 0.6861 | 0.8582 | 0.0620 | 0.5215 | 0.8861 | 0.9514 | 0.5725 | 0.9508 |\n| 246 | 1 | Replication: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — length-normalized (seed=7) | Noema I | 150 | 0.6859 | 0.8541 | 0.0814 | 0.5276 | 0.8816 | 0.9515 | 0.5572 | 0.9477 |\n| 200 | 1 | DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) | Noema I | 122 | 0.6843 | 0.8598 | 0.0726 | 0.5039 | 0.8830 | 0.9514 | 0.5612 | 0.9585 |\n| 396 | 1 | PrePool Res-ChannelMixer (param-matched) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=42 | Noema I | 272 | 0.6835 | 0.8573 | 0.0725 | 0.4893 | 0.8971 | 0.9511 | 0.5652 | 0.9523 |\n| 400 | 1 | Control (param-matched head=192, no mixer) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=42 | Noema I | 275 | 0.6831 | 0.8570\
    \ | 0.0772 | 0.5017 | 0.8817 | 0.9523 | 0.5545 | 0.9569 |\n| 203 | 1 | DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) — Seed=123 | Noema I | 124 | 0.6830 | 0.8589 | 0.0783 | 0.5039 | 0.8779 | 0.9512 | 0.5584 | 0.9523 |\n| 167 | 1 | Replication: Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM (No-PE) — Seed=7 | Noema I | 98 | 0.6828 | 0.8613 | 0.0752 | 0.5090 | 0.8999 | 0.9492 | 0.5638 | 0.9215 |\n| 178 | 1 | Replication: DSConv Hybrid Mean+Max (No-PE) — Seed=123 | Noema I | 104 | 0.6820 | 0.8588 | 0.0795 | 0.4981 | 0.8832 | 0.9502 | 0.5553 | 0.9492 |\n| 175 | 1 | Replication: DSConv Hybrid Mean+Max (No-PE) — Seed=42 | Noema I | 102 | 0.6819 | 0.8577 | 0.0782 | 0.4948 | 0.8792 | 0.9517 | 0.5611 | 0.9508 |\n\nPage 1 of 19 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-19, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**noema/submissions/dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted.py:**\n\
    ```\n\"\"\"\nDual-expert RNA model with learnable fusion and optional post-fusion normalization.\n  - Expert A: Conv + Pooling (mean/LSE variants with length normalization; scalar or channel-wise mixing)\n  - Expert B: small BiGRU on one-hot sequence (with linear embed)\nFusion modes:\n  - 'avg': simple average of expert projections\n  - 'scalar_gate': learned global 2-way softmax gating (params only, data-independent)\n  - 'mlp_gate': small MLP gate over [pool_proj || rnn_proj] producing 2-way softmax\nOptionally apply LayerNorm after fusion to stabilize scales.\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nfrom jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 256,\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n        # pooling settings\n        'aggregator':\
    \ 'mean_lse_mix',    # 'mean_lse_max' | 'mean_lse_mix' | 'mean_lse_mix_cw'\n        'tau': 0.25,\n        'length_normalize_lse': True,\n        'learn_tau': False,\n        # rnn settings\n        'gru_dim': 128,\n        # fusion settings\n        'fusion': 'scalar_gate',         # 'avg' | 'scalar_gate' | 'mlp_gate'\n        'gate_hidden_frac': 0.5,         # for mlp_gate: hidden = int(hidden_dim * frac)\n        'post_norm': False               # apply LayerNorm after fusion\n    }\n\ndef _lse_pool(h, tau, length_normalize=True):\n    L = h.shape[1]\n    core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n    if length_normalize:\n        core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n    return tau * core\n\nclass PoolingBlock(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n    tau: float = 0.25\n    length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n    learn_tau: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n   \
    \     h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n        tau_val = self.tau\n        if self.learn_tau:\n            tau_raw = self.param('tau_raw', lambda rng, shape: jnp.full(shape, self.tau), (1,))\n            tau_val = jax.nn.softplus(tau_raw)[0] + 1e-3\n        lse_pool = _lse_pool(h, tau_val, self.length_normalize_lse)\n        max_pool = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n\n        if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_max':\n            pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, lse_pool, max_pool], axis=-1)\n            pooled = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pooled)\n        elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix':\n            w = self.param('mix_weights', lambda rng, shp: jnp.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=mean_pool.dtype), (2,))\n            w = jax.nn.softmax(w)\n            pooled = w[0] * mean_pool + w[1] * lse_pool\n        elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix_cw':\n            w_cw = self.param('mix_weights_cw',\n                    \
    \          lambda rng, shp: jnp.stack([jnp.full((self.hidden_dim,), 0.5),\n                                                           jnp.full((self.hidden_dim,), 0.5)], axis=0),\n                              (2, self.hidden_dim))\n            w_cw = jax.nn.softmax(w_cw, axis=0)\n            pooled = w_cw[0] * mean_pool + w_cw[1] * lse_pool\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n        return pooled\n\nclass BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n    gru_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        x_emb = nn.Dense(self.gru_dim)(x)  # (batch, seq, gru_dim)\n        f_gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n        hf = f_gru(x_emb)              # (batch, seq, gru_dim)\n        hf_final = hf[:, -1, :]\n        x_emb_rev = jnp.flip(x_emb, axis=1)\n        b_gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n        hb = b_gru(x_emb_rev)\n        hb_final = hb[:, -1, :]\n        return jnp.concatenate([hf_final, hb_final],\
    \ axis=-1)\n\nclass DualExpertWeighted(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n    hidden_dim: int = 256\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n    tau: float = 0.25\n    length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n    learn_tau: bool = False\n    gru_dim: int = 128\n    fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n    gate_hidden_frac: float = 0.5\n    post_norm: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # Conv features\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n\n        # Experts\n        pool_rep = PoolingBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate,\n                                self.aggregator, self.tau,\n                                self.length_normalize_lse, self.learn_tau)(h, deterministic)\n        rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim)(x)\n        rnn_rep = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\
    \n        # Projections\n        pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n        rnn_proj  = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n        # Fusion\n        if self.fusion == 'avg':\n            fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n        elif self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n            logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros((2,), dtype=pool_proj.dtype), (2,))\n            w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n            fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n        elif self.fusion == 'mlp_gate':\n            gate_in = jnp.concatenate([pool_proj, rnn_proj], axis=-1)\n            hidden = max(1, int(self.hidden_dim * self.gate_hidden_frac))\n            g = nn.Dense(hidden)(gate_in)\n            g = jax.nn.gelu(g)\n            g = nn.Dense(2)(g)\n            w = jax.nn.softmax(g, axis=-1)\n            fused = w[:, :1] * pool_proj + w[:, 1:] * rnn_proj\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown fusion: {self.fusion}\")\n\n        if self.post_norm:\n\
    \            fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n\n        # Head\n        z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)\n        z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n            return z.squeeze(-1)\n        else:\n            return z\n\nclass WrappedRNANetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n        h = hparams or {}\n        self.network = DualExpertWeighted(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n            kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n            dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n            aggregator=str(h.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse_mix')),\n            tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n            length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse',\
    \ True)),\n            learn_tau=bool(h.get('learn_tau', False)),\n            gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 128)),\n            fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n            gate_hidden_frac=float(h.get('gate_hidden_frac', 0.5)),\n            post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', False)),\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                      dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef build_network(d_output,\
    \ task_type, hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n\n```\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #21. Your message ID is Noema_private_21-4.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 21 | Tri-seed complete (0.6446); Next: LR sweep and RC invariance | Noema II | Tick 331 | 271 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 20 | Dual-Expert Breakthrough: Pooling + BiGRU — Results and Next Steps | Noema II | Tick 320 | 224 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 19 | Final Handoff — What Matters and Where to Look (Tick 290) | Noema I | Tick 290 | 154 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 18 | Stability Atlas\
    \ wrap + monitor plan (Tick 269) | Noema I | Tick 269 | 113 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 17 | Plan — Tri-seed replication of Veritas II ID 365 (Tick 258) | Noema I | Tick 258 | 71 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 16 | MoE-Gumbel replication plan and provisional findings (Tick 237) | Noema I | Tick 237 | 107 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 15 | Replication plan for Axiom II Gumbel-gated hybrid (Tick 222) | Noema I | Tick 222 | 78 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 14 | Unified invariance audit + pooling calibration outcomes (Tick 212) | Noema I | Tick 212 | 157 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 13 | Next Directions (low-risk pivots) — Tick 146 | Noema I | Tick 146 | 224 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 12 | Handoff Snapshot — Tick 135 | Noema I | Tick 135 | 163 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
