role: model
parts:
- text: "Good news: k=11 lifted ncRNA substantially but hurt PRS; τ=0.20 didn’t help; learnable τ regressed due to ncRNA collapse. While pre-expert LN runs (505/506), I need to correct a file write (previous write failed in Private Memory). Rewriting the prenorm file in Research Counter now and logging results.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted_prenorm.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Dual-expert RNA model with learnable fusion and optional pre-/post-fusion normalization.\n    - Expert A: Conv + Pooling (mean/LSE variants with length normalization; scalar or channel-wise mixing)\n    - Expert B: small BiGRU on one-hot sequence (with linear embed)\n  Fusion modes:\n    - 'avg': simple average of expert projections\n    - 'scalar_gate': learned global 2-way softmax gating (params only, data-independent)\n    - 'mlp_gate': small MLP gate over [pool_proj || rnn_proj] producing 2-way softmax\n  Options:\n    - pre_expert_norm: LayerNorm each\
    \ expert projection prior to fusion (scale calibration)\n    - post_norm: LayerNorm after fusion\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n      'learning_rate': 0.001,\n      'hidden_dim': 256,\n      'kernel_size': 7,\n      'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n      # pooling settings\n      'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',    # 'mean_lse_max' | 'mean_lse_mix' | 'mean_lse_mix_cw'\n      'tau': 0.25,\n      'length_normalize_lse': True,\n      'learn_tau': False,\n      # rnn settings\n      'gru_dim': 128,\n      # fusion settings\n      'fusion': 'scalar_gate',         # 'avg' | 'scalar_gate' | 'mlp_gate'\n      'gate_hidden_frac': 0.5,         # for mlp_gate: hidden = int(hidden_dim * frac)\n      'pre_expert_norm': False,        # NEW: per-expert LayerNorm\
    \ before fusion\n      'post_norm': False               # LayerNorm after fusion\n    }\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau, length_normalize=True):\n    L = h.shape[1]\n    core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n    if length_normalize:\n      core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n    return tau * core\n\n  class PoolingBlock(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n    tau: float = 0.25\n    length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n    learn_tau: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n      h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n      mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n      tau_val = self.tau\n      if self.learn_tau:\n        tau_raw = self.param('tau_raw', lambda rng, shape: jnp.full(shape, self.tau), (1,))\n        tau_val = jax.nn.softplus(tau_raw)[0] + 1e-3\n      lse_pool = _lse_pool(h, tau_val, self.length_normalize_lse)\n      max_pool = jnp.max(h,\
    \ axis=1)\n\n      if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_max':\n        pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, lse_pool, max_pool], axis=-1)\n        pooled = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pooled)\n      elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix':\n        w = self.param('mix_weights', lambda rng, shp: jnp.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=mean_pool.dtype), (2,))\n        w = jax.nn.softmax(w)\n        pooled = w[0] * mean_pool + w[1] * lse_pool\n      elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix_cw':\n        w_cw = self.param('mix_weights_cw',\n                          lambda rng, shp: jnp.stack([jnp.full((self.hidden_dim,), 0.5),\n                                                       jnp.full((self.hidden_dim,), 0.5)], axis=0),\n                          (2, self.hidden_dim))\n        w_cw = jax.nn.softmax(w_cw, axis=0)\n        pooled = w_cw[0] * mean_pool + w_cw[1] * lse_pool\n      else:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n      return pooled\n\n  class BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n\
    \    gru_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n      x_emb = nn.Dense(self.gru_dim)(x)  # (batch, seq, gru_dim)\n      f_gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n      hf = f_gru(x_emb)              # (batch, seq, gru_dim)\n      hf_final = hf[:, -1, :]\n      x_emb_rev = jnp.flip(x_emb, axis=1)\n      b_gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n      hb = b_gru(x_emb_rev)\n      hb_final = hb[:, -1, :]\n      return jnp.concatenate([hf_final, hb_final], axis=-1)\n\n  class DualExpertWeighted(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n    hidden_dim: int = 256\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n    tau: float = 0.25\n    length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n    learn_tau: bool = False\n    gru_dim: int = 128\n    fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n    gate_hidden_frac: float = 0.5\n    pre_expert_norm: bool = False\n    post_norm: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n   \
    \ def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n      # Conv features\n      h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n      h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n\n      # Experts\n      pool_rep = PoolingBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate,\n                              self.aggregator, self.tau,\n                              self.length_normalize_lse, self.learn_tau)(h, deterministic)\n      rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim)(x)\n      rnn_rep = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n      # Projections\n      pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n      rnn_proj  = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n      # Pre-expert normalization (per-expert)\n      if self.pre_expert_norm:\n        pool_proj = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(pool_proj)\n        rnn_proj  = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(rnn_proj)\n\n      # Fusion\n      if self.fusion == 'avg':\n        fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n      elif self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n\
    \        logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros((2,), dtype=pool_proj.dtype), (2,))\n        w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n        fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n      elif self.fusion == 'mlp_gate':\n        gate_in = jnp.concatenate([pool_proj, rnn_proj], axis=-1)\n        hidden = max(1, int(self.hidden_dim * self.gate_hidden_frac))\n        g = nn.Dense(hidden)(gate_in)\n        g = jax.nn.gelu(g)\n        g = nn.Dense(2)(g)\n        w = jax.nn.softmax(g, axis=-1)\n        fused = w[:, :1] * pool_proj + w[:, 1:] * rnn_proj\n      else:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Unknown fusion: {self.fusion}\")\n\n      if self.post_norm:\n        fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n\n      # Head\n      z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)\n      z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n      z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n      z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n      if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n  \
    \      return z.squeeze(-1)\n      else:\n        return z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n      h = hparams or {}\n      self.network = DualExpertWeighted(\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n        kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n        dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n        aggregator=str(h.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse_mix')),\n        tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n        length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n        learn_tau=bool(h.get('learn_tau', False)),\n        gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 128)),\n        fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n        gate_hidden_frac=float(h.get('gate_hidden_frac', 0.5)),\n        pre_expert_norm=bool(h.get('pre_expert_norm', False)),\n        post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', False)),\n      )\n\n    def init(self,\
    \ rng_key, dummy_input):\n      params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n      variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                    dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n      return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n      if deterministic:\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n      else:\n        if rng_key is None:\n          rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n\
    \  # Update (Tick 339)\n  New results:\n  - k=9 (Eval 504): 0.6183 | APA 0.8468 | CRI-Off 0.0874 | Modif 0.8238 | CRI-On 0.3771 | PRS 0.4668 | MRL 0.8782 | ncRNA 0.8477 (ncRNA ok; Modif/PRS regressed).\n  - Learnable τ (Eval 503): 0.6123 | APA 0.8494 | CRI-Off 0.0839 | Modif 0.8719 | CRI-On 0.4044 | PRS 0.5446 | MRL 0.8797 | ncRNA 0.6523 (ncRNA collapsed).\n  - k=11 (Eval 499): 0.6425 | APA 0.8474 | CRI-Off 0.0852 | Modif 0.9223 | CRI-On 0.4000 | PRS 0.4998 | MRL 0.8785 | ncRNA 0.8646 (trade-off: ncRNA↑, PRS↓).\n\n  Best so far (tri-seed): 492 (seed=42) — 0.6446 | APA 0.8459 | CRI-Off 0.0625 | Modif 0.9448 | CRI-On 0.3938 | PRS 0.5514 | MRL 0.8873 | ncRNA 0.8262.\n\n  In flight:\n  - 505: Pre-expert LN + post-norm (BiGRU=160, k=7).\n  - 506: Same + grad clip=1.0.\n\n  Notes:\n  - RC train+eval (495) near-best; eval-only RC averaging invalid (orientation-specific).\n  - Kernel >7 boosts ncRNA but tends to hurt PRS/Modif; τ=0.25 remains preferable to τ=0.20.\n  - Hypothesis: calibration\
    \ (pre-expert LN) + post-norm should stabilize fusion and may lift PRS/Spearman without sacrificing Modif/ncRNA.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{rank author}`"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating training approaches**


  I''m thinking about label smoothing for classification tasks, especially in multi-label setups. There’s a mix with logistic scaling; however, the loss functions are hardcoded and unchangeable, though we can still calibrate outputs. I also consider adding dropout or a bias to ensure weights don’t saturate. Gradient clipping is important too, and it’s being handled properly. While we wait for results, I might update our plans or check evaluations sorted by author.**Planning action steps**


  I’m thinking about using the `/execute_action{rank author}` command to change the sort order in the Research Counter, which will help me monitor our results more effectively. It seems like a good approach! I can also run `/execute_action{preview all}` to see the latest 100 entries, but I need to be mindful as it can get token heavy. I want to log results in the summary file and prepare for the next experiment, focusing on pre-expert LN without post-norm.**Testing variants and planning**


  I’m considering a variant with gradient clipping while testing the impact of having post-norm on or off. Since post-norm previously yielded the best results, I wonder if using both pre-expert LN and post-norm can be excessive. I think toggling post-norm off to see its effect could be useful. However, it seems that keeping both or even just using pre-expert norm without post-norm might be redundant. For now, I should check our ranking and add a note to Private Memory, but waiting might be wiser.**Clarifying storage actions**


  I need to ensure compliance regarding our actions in the Private Memory Room. It seems the earlier attempt to execute "storage write" didn’t go through because the action isn''t supported there. Oddly, I had a prior storage write that worked. Confusingly, even though I got an error in the Private Memory Room, submissions were made using the same file. I wonder how it passed validation if the file hadn’t been written. This needs further investigation!**Addressing file writing issues**


  I realize that the latest outputs indicate a problem with the file not being read during simple CPU validation. Submissions using "dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted_prenorm" were queued, but the storage write in the Private Memory Room wasn''t recognized. This means the necessary file hasn’t been created. I need to write the file again in the Research Counter to ensure it exists for evaluation import. I''ll also document the results for 503 and 504 and make sure to update my plans in Private Memory about the file writing location issue. Time to execute the correct storage write!**Preparing final actions**


  It''s a bit lengthy, but I can embed the necessary actions again. First, I''ll rank the author to check our submissions. I want to write an updated results summary in storage, but maybe adding a note to Private Memory isn’t necessary. I’m also considering using ''page_size 30'' for better visibility. Since we’re in the Research Counter, I’ll make sure to execute the storage write appropriately. The content of ‘dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted_prenorm.py’ is long, but I''ll include it again. Time to produce my final actions!'
