parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 340\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 100,567 / 270,000 used (37%)\n- Agent Age: 47 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Dual-expert (scalar gate) + Pre-expert LN + Post-norm + grad-clip=1.0 — BiGRU=160, k=7 — seed=42' (ID: 506) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6393503324221391\n**APA_R2:** 0.8452\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0841\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9474\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4056\n**PRS_R2:** 0.4354\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8762\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.8815\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 506\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the import error by creating a complete implementation with pre-expert normalization\
    \ support.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission tried to import `dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted_prenorm` module which did not exist in the agent's lineage directory. The submission's hyperparameters included `'pre_expert_norm': True`, indicating the agent wanted a version of the dual-expert model that applies LayerNorm before the pooling expert processes the convolved features.\n\nThe error was:\n```\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted_prenorm'\n```\n\nThe agent had `dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted.py` in their lineage, but it didn't support the `pre_expert_norm` parameter.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v2.py` with a complete implementation that:\n\n1. **Added Pre-Expert Normalization Support**: Extended the `DualExpertWeighted` class to `DualExpertWeightedPrenorm` with a `pre_expert_norm` parameter that applies `nn.LayerNorm` to the convolved features before passing them to the pooling expert.\n\n2. **Preserved All Other Functionality**: Maintained\
    \ all the original features:\n   - Dual-expert architecture (Conv+Pooling expert A, BiGRU expert B)\n   - Multiple pooling aggregators (mean_lse_mix, mean_lse_mix_cw, mean_lse_max)\n   - Fusion modes (avg, scalar_gate, mlp_gate)\n   - Post-fusion normalization support\n   - Length-normalized LSE pooling\n\n3. **Matched Requested Hyperparameters**: The fix supports all the hyperparameters the agent specified:\n   - `hidden_dim: 256`\n   - `kernel_size: 7`\n   - `gru_dim: 160`\n   - `fusion: 'scalar_gate'`\n   - `pre_expert_norm: True` ✓ (newly supported)\n   - `post_norm: True` ✓\n   - `grad_clip: 1.0` (via custom optimizer)\n\n4. **Implementation Details**:\n   ```python\n   # Optional pre-expert normalization\n   if self.pre_expert_norm:\n       h_norm = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n   else:\n       h_norm = h\n\n   # Experts operate on normalized features\n   pool_rep = PoolingBlock(...)(h_norm, deterministic)\n   ```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success:\n- Exit\
    \ code: 0 (SUCCESS)\n- Code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- No runtime errors or exceptions\n\nThe submission is now executing the full training pipeline with the pre-expert normalization architecture as intended.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\n\"\"\"\nDual-expert RNA model with learnable fusion, optional pre-expert normalization, and post-fusion normalization.\n  - Expert A: Conv + Pooling (mean/LSE variants with length normalization; scalar or channel-wise mixing)\n  - Expert B: small BiGRU on one-hot sequence (with linear embed)\nFusion modes:\n  - 'avg': simple average of expert projections\n  - 'scalar_gate': learned global 2-way softmax gating (params only, data-independent)\n  - 'mlp_gate': small MLP gate over [pool_proj || rnn_proj] producing 2-way softmax\nOptionally apply LayerNorm before experts\
    \ (pre_expert_norm) and after fusion (post_norm) to stabilize scales.\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nfrom jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 256,\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n        'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n        'tau': 0.25,\n        'length_normalize_lse': True,\n        'learn_tau': False,\n        'gru_dim': 160,\n        'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n        'pre_expert_norm': True,\n        'post_norm': True,\n        'grad_clip': 1.0\n    }\n\ndef _lse_pool(h, tau, length_normalize=True):\n    L = h.shape[1]\n    core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n    if length_normalize:\n        core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n    return tau * core\n\nclass PoolingBlock(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim:\
    \ int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n    tau: float = 0.25\n    length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n    learn_tau: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n        tau_val = self.tau\n        if self.learn_tau:\n            tau_raw = self.param('tau_raw', lambda rng, shape: jnp.full(shape, self.tau), (1,))\n            tau_val = jax.nn.softplus(tau_raw)[0] + 1e-3\n        lse_pool = _lse_pool(h, tau_val, self.length_normalize_lse)\n        max_pool = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n\n        if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_max':\n            pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, lse_pool, max_pool], axis=-1)\n            pooled = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pooled)\n        elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix':\n            w = self.param('mix_weights', lambda rng, shp: jnp.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=mean_pool.dtype),\
    \ (2,))\n            w = jax.nn.softmax(w)\n            pooled = w[0] * mean_pool + w[1] * lse_pool\n        elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix_cw':\n            w_cw = self.param('mix_weights_cw',\n                              lambda rng, shp: jnp.stack([jnp.full((self.hidden_dim,), 0.5),\n                                                           jnp.full((self.hidden_dim,), 0.5)], axis=0),\n                              (2, self.hidden_dim))\n            w_cw = jax.nn.softmax(w_cw, axis=0)\n            pooled = w_cw[0] * mean_pool + w_cw[1] * lse_pool\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n        return pooled\n\nclass BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n    gru_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        x_emb = nn.Dense(self.gru_dim)(x)  # (batch, seq, gru_dim)\n        f_gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n        hf = f_gru(x_emb)              # (batch, seq, gru_dim)\n        hf_final = hf[:, -1, :]\n\
    \        x_emb_rev = jnp.flip(x_emb, axis=1)\n        b_gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n        hb = b_gru(x_emb_rev)\n        hb_final = hb[:, -1, :]\n        return jnp.concatenate([hf_final, hb_final], axis=-1)\n\nclass DualExpertWeightedPrenorm(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n    hidden_dim: int = 256\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n    tau: float = 0.25\n    length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n    learn_tau: bool = False\n    gru_dim: int = 128\n    fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n    gate_hidden_frac: float = 0.5\n    pre_expert_norm: bool = False\n    post_norm: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # Conv features\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n\n        # Optional pre-expert normalization\n        if self.pre_expert_norm:\n\
    \            h_norm = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n        else:\n            h_norm = h\n\n        # Experts\n        pool_rep = PoolingBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate,\n                                self.aggregator, self.tau,\n                                self.length_normalize_lse, self.learn_tau)(h_norm, deterministic)\n        rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim)(x)\n        rnn_rep = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n        # Projections\n        pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n        rnn_proj  = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n        # Fusion\n        if self.fusion == 'avg':\n            fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n        elif self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n            logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros((2,), dtype=pool_proj.dtype), (2,))\n            w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n            fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n        elif self.fusion == 'mlp_gate':\n            gate_in\
    \ = jnp.concatenate([pool_proj, rnn_proj], axis=-1)\n            hidden = max(1, int(self.hidden_dim * self.gate_hidden_frac))\n            g = nn.Dense(hidden)(gate_in)\n            g = jax.nn.gelu(g)\n            g = nn.Dense(2)(g)\n            w = jax.nn.softmax(g, axis=-1)\n            fused = w[:, :1] * pool_proj + w[:, 1:] * rnn_proj\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown fusion: {self.fusion}\")\n\n        if self.post_norm:\n            fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n\n        # Head\n        z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)\n        z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n            return z.squeeze(-1)\n        else:\n            return z\n\nclass WrappedRNANetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n        h =\
    \ hparams or {}\n        self.network = DualExpertWeightedPrenorm(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n            kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n            dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n            aggregator=str(h.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse_mix')),\n            tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n            length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n            learn_tau=bool(h.get('learn_tau', False)),\n            gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 128)),\n            fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n            gate_hidden_frac=float(h.get('gate_hidden_frac', 0.5)),\n            pre_expert_norm=bool(h.get('pre_expert_norm', False)),\n            post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', False)),\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params':\
    \ params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                      dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    # Add global-norm clipping before AdamW\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On\
