role: model
parts:
- text: "Submitting two targeted probes to recover PRS while keeping strong ncRNA/Modif: (1) base best + grad clip; (2) avg fusion with pre-expert LN.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-expert (scalar gate + post-norm) + grad-clip=1.0 — BiGRU=160, k=7 — seed=42\"\ntags: \"ensemble, gating, layernorm, optimization, bigru, pooling\"\nabstract: \"Base best config with global-norm gradient clipping (1.0) added to the optimizer to stabilize training and recover PRS while retaining ncRNA/Modif gains.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse':\
    \ True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-expert (avg) + Pre-expert LN + Post-norm — BiGRU=160, k=7 — seed=42\"\ntags: \"ensemble, averaging, layernorm, prenorm, bigru, pooling\"\nabstract: \"Switch fusion to equal averaging with per-expert pre-LN and post-fusion LN to equalize expert scales, aiming to improve PRS stability while keeping strong\
    \ ncRNA/Modif.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted_prenorm import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'learn_tau': False,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'fusion': 'avg',\n          'pre_expert_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')}\
    \ val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update (Tick 340)\n  New: Probing PRS recovery while preserving ncRNA/Modif.\n  - Submitted base best + grad-clip=1.0 (scalar gate + post-norm, BiGRU=160, k=7).\n  - Submitted avg fusion + pre-expert LN + post-norm (BiGRU=160, k=7).\n  Rationale: 506 showed big ncRNA/Modif gains but PRS dropped; clipping may stabilize PRS. Avg fusion with LN may balance experts without over-weighting one branch.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Testing fusion parameters**\n\nI'm planning to test initial parameters like setting fusion to 'avg', with pre_expert_norm and post_norm enabled, using BiGRU 160. I might also try reverting to the base best model while adding k=11 for boosting ncRNA, although it dropped PRS significantly in earlier tests so that's risky. Another idea is to introduce a 'scalar_gate' with a slight L2 penalty, but that seems complicated. Instead, maybe calibrating expert outputs sizes with learned scalar scales could work, but that requires new code.**Evaluating scalar impact on PRS**\n\nI'm considering adding two scalars, 'alpha_pool' and 'alpha_rnn', to pool_proj and rnn_proj before gating. This might help balance PRS, but since 'pre_expert_norm' already normalizes, I'm not sure it will make a difference. The recent results show a PRS of 0.435, which is a decrease. It could be due to pre-expert LN affecting the conv features negatively. I'll think about removing pre_expert_norm and testing\
  \ grad clipping at 1.0 with the original code. I want to propose two new configurations that incorporate these changes.**Exploring optimizer configurations**\n\nI'm allowed to create an optimizer using base build_network from dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted with specific parameters: post_norm set to True and no pre_expert_norm. I noticed that fusion set to 'avg' with both pre_expert_norm and post_norm likely negatively impacted PRS, so I might reconsider that setup. Testing 'mlp_gate' with pre_expert_norm and post_norm seems unnecessary since it previously underperformed. Instead, tuning dropout might be more promising, though using 0.10 again since 0.08 dropped PRS significantly. I also saw that CRI options had similar results, not a huge boost.**Managing configurations and tokens**\n\nI need to keep an eye on token usage—I'm at 100k and 37% used, which is good. I should also plan to update my Private Memory and consider the Reflection Chamber for some introspection, as suggested. My plan\
  \ involves submitting the base configuration of dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted with BiGRU 160, post_norm True, and scalar gate while applying grad clipping at 1.0 to stabilize PRS near 0.5514. I’ll test ‘avg’ fusion with pre-expert LN for potential recovery but note the risks. After submission, I'll summarize results and update memory. Also, I’ll prepare to prune tokens soon since I have a few ticks left.**Crafting YAML submissions**\n\nSince we've just pruned, there’s no need to do that again; I'm at 100k tokens, 37% used. It’s time to prepare YAML for submissions. \n\nFirst, for the base with grad clip, I’ll import 'dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted' and override the default optimizer to add grad clipping. The hyperparameters will be set as needed. Then, for the second submission, I’ll use the 'avg' fusion from 'dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted_prenorm' file. \n\nI’ll make sure both submissions are entered, ensuring correct YAML formatting. After submitting, I'll update the summary file and\
  \ possibly reflect in private memory afterwards."
