tick: 341
role: model
parts:
- text: "Preparing a multi-τ pooling variant to target PRS/CRISPR while keeping parsimony; documenting paper outline and plan while current runs finish.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_pool_gru_multitau.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Dual-expert RNA model with multi-τ LSE pooling mix.\n    - Expert A: Conv -> global pooling with learned mix over {mean, LSE(τ_i)} for τ_i in tau_list\n    - Expert B: small BiGRU on one-hot sequence\n  Fusion: 'avg' | 'scalar_gate' | 'mlp_gate'\n  Normalization: optional post-fusion LayerNorm; optional pre-expert per-projection LayerNorm.\n  Goal: capture variable motif scales with a parsimonious, dataset-agnostic pooling.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n    \
    \  'learning_rate': 0.001,\n      'hidden_dim': 256,\n      'kernel_size': 7,\n      'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n      # pooling\n      'aggregator': 'mean_lse_multi_mix',   # 'mean_lse_multi_mix' | 'mean_lse_multi_mix_cw'\n      'tau_list': [0.125, 0.25, 0.5],\n      'length_normalize_lse': True,\n      # rnn\n      'gru_dim': 160,\n      # fusion\n      'fusion': 'scalar_gate',              # 'avg' | 'scalar_gate' | 'mlp_gate'\n      'gate_hidden_frac': 0.5,\n      # norms\n      'pre_expert_norm': False,\n      'post_norm': True\n    }\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau, length_normalize=True):\n    L = h.shape[1]\n    core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n    if length_normalize:\n      core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n    return tau * core\n\n  class PoolingBlockMultiTau(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_multi_mix\"\n    tau_list: Sequence[float] = (0.125, 0.25, 0.5)\n    length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n\n    @nn.compact\n\
    \    def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n      h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n      mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)  # (B, C)\n      lse_pools = [ _lse_pool(h, float(t), self.length_normalize_lse) for t in self.tau_list ]  # each (B, C)\n      comps = [mean_pool] + lse_pools\n      K = len(comps)\n\n      if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_multi_mix':\n        w = self.param('mix_w', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros((K,)), (K,))\n        w = jax.nn.softmax(w)  # (K,)\n        pooled = sum(w[i] * comps[i] for i in range(K))\n      elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_multi_mix_cw':\n        w_cw = self.param('mix_w_cw', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros((K, self.hidden_dim)), (K, self.hidden_dim))\n        w_cw = jax.nn.softmax(w_cw, axis=0)  # (K, C)\n        pooled = sum(w_cw[i] * comps[i] for i in range(K))\n      else:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n      return pooled  # (B, C)\n\n  class BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n\
    \    gru_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n      x_emb = nn.Dense(self.gru_dim)(x)\n      f = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n      hf = f(x_emb)[:, -1, :]\n      b = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n      hb = b(jnp.flip(x_emb, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n      return jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)\n\n  class DualExpertMultiTau(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n    hidden_dim: int = 256\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_multi_mix\"\n    tau_list: Sequence[float] = (0.125, 0.25, 0.5)\n    length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n    gru_dim: int = 160\n    fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n    gate_hidden_frac: float = 0.5\n    pre_expert_norm: bool = False\n    post_norm: bool = True\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n      # Conv features\n      h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding=\"\
    SAME\")(x)\n      h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n\n      # Experts\n      pool_rep = PoolingBlockMultiTau(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate,\n                                      self.aggregator, self.tau_list,\n                                      self.length_normalize_lse)(h, deterministic)\n      rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim)(x)\n      rnn_rep = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n      # Projections\n      pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n      rnn_proj  = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n      if self.pre_expert_norm:\n        pool_proj = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(pool_proj)\n        rnn_proj  = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(rnn_proj)\n\n      # Fusion\n      if self.fusion == 'avg':\n        fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n      elif self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n        logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros((2,), dtype=pool_proj.dtype), (2,))\n        w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n        fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n\
    \      elif self.fusion == 'mlp_gate':\n        gate_in = jnp.concatenate([pool_proj, rnn_proj], axis=-1)\n        hidden = max(1, int(self.hidden_dim * self.gate_hidden_frac))\n        g = nn.Dense(hidden)(gate_in); g = jax.nn.gelu(g); g = nn.Dense(2)(g)\n        w = jax.nn.softmax(g, axis=-1)\n        fused = w[:, :1] * pool_proj + w[:, 1:] * rnn_proj\n      else:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Unknown fusion: {self.fusion}\")\n\n      if self.post_norm:\n        fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n\n      z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)\n      z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n      z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n      z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n      return z.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n      h = hparams or {}\n      self.network = DualExpertMultiTau(\n        d_output=d_output,\n\
    \        task_type=task_type,\n        hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n        kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n        dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n        aggregator=str(h.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse_multi_mix')),\n        tau_list=tuple(h.get('tau_list', [0.125, 0.25, 0.5])),\n        length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n        gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n        fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n        gate_hidden_frac=float(h.get('gate_hidden_frac', 0.5)),\n        pre_expert_norm=bool(h.get('pre_expert_norm', False)),\n        post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', True)),\n      )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n      params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n      variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                    dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n      return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params,\
    \ x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n      if deterministic:\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n      else:\n        if rng_key is None:\n          rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/paper/draft_outline_tick341.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Title: Calibrated Dual-Expert for RNA: Conv+Pooling (mean↔multi-τ LSE) + BiGRU with Simple Gating\n\n  Abstract (50-80w):\n  We study a parsimonious dual-expert RNA model combining a single 1D conv + global pooling (mean↔LSE mix) with a small BiGRU, fused by scalar gating and layer normalization.\
    \ Across seven datasets, simple calibration (post-norm, optional grad clip) yields strong ncRNA/Modif while preserving MRL/APA, and multi-τ pooling targets PRS/CRISPR. We provide extensive ablations and stability analyses.\n\n  Methods:\n  - Expert A: conv(h=256,k=7), global pooling: mean↔LSE(τ) learned mix; length-normalized LSE; optional multi-τ {0.125,0.25,0.5}\n  - Expert B: BiGRU(160) on one-hot; last-state concat; linear projection\n  - Fusion: avg / scalar gate / MLP gate; post-fusion LayerNorm; optional pre-expert LN; optimizer AdamW; optional global-norm clip\n  - No pretraining or external data; same core across datasets\n\n  Key Results (eval IDs):\n  - Best tri-seed (scalar gate + post-norm, k=7, BiGRU=160): 492 (seed=42) 0.6446 | Modif 0.9448 | PRS 0.5514 | MRL 0.8873 | ncRNA 0.8262\n  - RC (train+eval): 495 — 0.6427 (APA↑; PRS slightly↓)\n  - k=11: 499 — 0.6425 (ncRNA 0.8646↑; PRS 0.4998↓)\n  - Pre-expert LN + post-norm + clip: 506 — 0.6394 (Modif 0.9474, ncRNA 0.8815;\
    \ PRS 0.4354↓)\n  - LR 7e-4: 494 — 0.6183 (PRS 0.415↓)\n\n  Ablations:\n  - τ=0.25 > τ=0.20; learnable τ regressed via ncRNA collapse\n  - RC eval-only invalid (orientation-specific)\n  - Wider conv kernels boost ncRNA but trade PRS/Modif\n  - MLP gate underperformed scalar; post-norm essential\n\n  Next:\n  - Evaluate multi-τ pooling mix; if positive, tri-seed + small sweep on tau_list\n  - Prepare archive submission after maturity (≥ tick 50)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 341 update:\n  - 506 (pre-expert LN + post-norm + clip) = 0.6394: ncRNA 0.8815 & Modif 0.9474 strong, but PRS 0.4354 (down from 0.551).\n  - To target PRS/CRISPR without sacrificing Modif/ncRNA, coded a generic multi-τ pooling (mean + LSE at {0.125,0.25,0.5} with learned mix). Plan to test on base scalar-gated config after 509/510 finish.\n  - Paper outline drafted (draft_outline_tick341.md). After maturity, prepare archive manuscript with\
    \ ≥5 evals, ablations, and stability.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning and reflection**\n\nI think a good plan is to use the Reflection Chamber to look at the big picture for my paper and refine the tri-seed with modifications. I need to prepare code for the dataset-specific final head, while keeping in mind the constraint about not using dataset-specific methods. It seems like I should also prepare a concise paper for Archive later, focusing on \"Dual-Expert Calibration\" with required experiments. While I can't submit too soon, I can draft and clean up storage along the way. I'll check the rank score to see our place in the SOTA.**Evaluating SOTA progress**\n\nLooking at our best score of 0.6446, it’s clear we're not surpassing the state of the art (SOTA). I’m considering a pivot since the earlier SOTA used DSConv architectures, and those yielded scores around 0.68. Our dual-expert model hasn't hit that mark, so deeper modifications might be necessary. I also think it could be worthwhile to calibrate gating weights to be more\
  \ data-dependent while avoiding extremes, possibly using constraints like vector norms before gating. But since we can't add new losses, maybe we can manipulate gating behavior through dropout or parametrize mixing weights instead.**Exploring gating and calibration**\n\nI’m thinking about using weight normalization on fusion logits to create softer gating. Since we can't add any new loss functions, I can initialize the gating logits to zero since that’s already done. However, I noticed that using an MLP gate led to decreased performance. Maybe we could implement gating as a mixture with a learned scalar between 0.3 and 0.7, but that might change the network structure. \n\nAnother improvement could involve post-pool calibration with Feature-wise Linear Modulation (FiLM) constants, but that's dataset-specific. Instead, I might try applying LayerNorm to expert outputs and the fused features, while adding a residual connection to keep the fused vector intact. But then again, that approach\
  \ is quite similar to averaging.**Evaluating aggregation and planning**\n\nI’m considering that for CRISPR and PRS tasks, we might need a sharper aggregator for pooling. We tested with tau 0.20, but the PRS improved only to 0.515, which is a drop from the best 0.551 we had. It seems that the gating with pre-norm plus gradient clipping led to a further drop to 0.435 on PRS. \n\nWe should also consider dropout rates since reducing it to 0.08 didn’t help much either. A good plan would be to prepare to write in Private Memory, aiming for publication shortly after maturity, likely around tick 343.**Summarizing results and planning actions**\n\nI need to create a results summary document and a basic \"submission.py\" for the best tri-seed to re-run seeds 7 and 123 with updated configurations. I noticed that pre-norm and gradient clipping led to a decrease in PRS scores. I should ensure our storage code reflects our desired pre-expert normalization and note differences. While waiting for results,\
  \ it's good to prepare the tri-seed for baseline 492 and plan for future reflections and submissions. We might consider various aggregator strategies to improve PRS and stay aligned with our goals.**Planning code implementation and reflections**\n\nI should write actions to update storage and prepare for submissions. First, I'll create a new module called 'dual_expert_pool_gru_multitau.py' to implement a multi-τ aggregator for pooling. Then, I'll prepare a draft outline for the paper summarizing key evaluations. After writing the files, I’ll update Private Memory with insights from the results. Although I want to reflect in the Reflection Chamber, it might be more productive to focus on these coding tasks first. I’ll keep actions concise and implement clarity in my code."
