parts:
- text: "Submitting multi-τ pooling variants to target PRS/CRISPR while preserving Modif/ncRNA.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-expert (scalar gate + post-norm) — multi-τ pooling {0.125,0.25,0.5} — BiGRU=160, k=7 — seed=42\"\ntags: \"multi-tau, pooling, logsumexp, ensemble, gating, bigru\"\nabstract: \"Adds a parsimonious multi-τ pooling mix (mean + LSE at τ∈{0.125,0.25,0.5}) to the Conv+Pooling expert with scalar-gated fusion and post-fusion LayerNorm. Hypothesis: variable sharpness captures motif-scale diversity, improving PRS/CRISPR without harming Modif/ncRNA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru_multitau import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate':\
    \ 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_multi_mix',\n          'tau_list': [0.125, 0.25, 0.5],\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'pre_expert_norm': False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-expert (scalar gate + post-norm) + grad-clip=1.0 — multi-τ pooling — BiGRU=160, k=7 — seed=42\"\ntags: \"multi-tau, pooling, optimization, ensemble, gating, bigru\"\nabstract: \"Same multi-τ setup, with global-norm gradient clipping (1.0) added to the optimizer to stabilize\
    \ training and potentially improve PRS/CRISPR while keeping Modif/ncRNA strong.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_pool_gru_multitau import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_multi_mix',\n          'tau_list': [0.125, 0.25, 0.5],\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'pre_expert_norm': False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update (Tick 342)\n  New results:\n  - 509 (base best + grad-clip=1.0): 0.6420 | APA 0.8421 | CRI-Off 0.0868 | Modif 0.9480 | CRI-On 0.4034 | PRS 0.5129 | MRL 0.8793 | ncRNA 0.8215.\n  - 510 (avg + pre-LN + post-norm): 0.6335 | APA 0.8504 | CRI-Off 0.0807 | Modif 0.9126 | CRI-On 0.3960 | PRS 0.5083 | MRL 0.8791 | ncRNA 0.8077.\n  Best remains 492 (tri-seed scalar-gated, k=7): 0.6446 with PRS 0.5514.\n  \n  In flight:\n  - Multi-τ pooling (mean + LSE τ∈{0.125,0.25,0.5}) with scalar gate + post-norm — with and without grad clip — to target PRS/CRISPR without sacrificing Modif/ncRNA.\n  \n  Notes:\n  - Clipping helped recover PRS vs pre-LN variant; scalar gate superior to avg for our setup. τ=0.25 still strong;\
    \ broader τ mix may capture motif-scale diversity beneficial for PRS/CRISPR.\n```"
