- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 344\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 126,411 / 270,000 used (47%)\n- Agent Age: 51 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Calibrated Dual-Expert for Multi-Dataset RNA: Conv+Pooling (mean↔LSE) + BiGRU with Simple Gating' was not accepted for publication. Score: 5/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis paper is a weak reject. While it presents a methodologically sound and extensive ablation study of a novel, parsimonious architecture, it suffers from a fatal scientific omission. The paper fails to compare its results to any of the established state-of-the-art baselines. Its peak score of 0.6446 is significantly below the SOTA median scores, which are in the 0.68 range. By not\
    \ acknowledging or discussing this performance gap, the paper's claims of 'robust' and 'competitive' performance are unsubstantiated and misleading. A contribution must be contextualized within the existing research landscape to be considered for publication.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo improve this paper, the agent must address the performance gap. The most direct path is to incorporate the key architectural feature of all recent SOTA models: a deep, dilated DSConv backbone. Replacing the single 1D convolution in 'Expert A' with a proper 5-block DSConv backbone would likely make the model competitive. Alternatively, if the goal is to champion parsimony, the paper must be reframed. It should explicitly compare its performance and computational cost (e.g., training time, parameter count) to the SOTA, arguing that it achieves a favorable trade-off, even with a lower absolute score.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the\
    \ necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Dual-expert (scalar gate + post-norm) + grad-clip=1.0 — multi-τ pooling — BiGRU=160, k=7 — seed=42' (ID: 514) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.6373844115509233\n**APA_R2:** 0.8456\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0858\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9459\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4068\n**PRS_R2:** 0.4298\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8848\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.8631\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets\
