role: model
parts:
- text: "Reviewer feedback acknowledged. I’ll implement the suggested DSConv backbone for Expert A, run two evaluations, and then revise the paper with SOTA comparisons and discussion of trade-offs.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_pool_gru.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Dual-expert RNA model with a DSConv backbone in Expert A + global pooling (mean↔LSE mix) and a BiGRU Expert B.\n  Fusion via scalar gate; post-fusion LayerNorm. Universal across datasets.\n\n  Expert A:\n    - Input embed conv -> 5 DSConv residual blocks with dilations [1,2,4,8,16]\n    - DSConv block: depthwise-separable conv (dilated DWConv + PWConv) + GELU + residual\n    - Global pooling: learned mix(mean, LSE τ=0.25) with length normalization\n\n  Expert B:\n    - BiGRU(160) over one-hot sequence; final states concatenated and projected\n\n  Fusion:\n    - Scalar gate (2-way softmax over expert projections)\n    - Optional post-fusion\
    \ LayerNorm\n\n  Notes:\n    - No pretraining or external data. Same core method across datasets.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          # pooling\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          # rnn\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          # DSConv\n          'ds_dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          # fusion/norms\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau, length_normalize=True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n\
    \          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  class PoolingBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          lse_pool = _lse_pool(h, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix':\n              w = self.param('mix_w', lambda rng, shp: jnp.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=mean_pool.dtype), (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(w)\n              pooled = w[0] * mean_pool + w[1] * lse_pool\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n          return pooled\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size:\
    \ int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          # Depthwise dilated conv\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          # Pointwise conv\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,))(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Initial embedding to hidden_dim\n       \
    \   h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  class BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x_emb = nn.Dense(self.gru_dim)(x)\n          f = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hf = f(x_emb)[:, -1, :]\n          b = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hb = b(jnp.flip(x_emb, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n          return jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)\n\n  class DualExpertDSConv(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse:\
    \ bool = True\n      gru_dim: int = 160\n      fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n      post_norm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Expert A: DSConv backbone -> pooling\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          pool_rep = PoolingBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate, self.aggregator, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)(h, deterministic)\n          # Expert B: BiGRU\n          rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim)(x)\n          rnn_rep = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n          # Projections\n          pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n          rnn_proj  = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n          # Fusion\n          if self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n              logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros((2,), dtype=pool_proj.dtype), (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n\
    \              fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n          elif self.fusion == 'avg':\n              fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown fusion: {self.fusion}\")\n          if self.post_norm:\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n          # Head\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused); z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return z.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n          self.network = DualExpertDSConv(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size',\
    \ 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(h.get('ds_dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              aggregator=str(h.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse_mix')),\n              tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n              fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n              post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', True)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n             \
    \ if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-expert (DSConv Expert A) + mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU(160), scalar gate + post-norm — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, logsumexp, bigru, gating, layernorm\"\nabstract: \"Expert A uses a 5-block dilated DSConv backbone (dilations=[1,2,4,8,16]) before global pooling (learned mix of mean and length-normalized LSE, τ=0.25). Expert B is BiGRU(160). Scalar-gated fusion + post-fusion LayerNorm. Tests SOTA-aligned backbone within our dual-expert framework.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n\
    \  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_pool_gru import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n\
    ```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-expert (DSConv Expert A) + mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU(160), scalar gate + post-norm + grad-clip=1.0 — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, logsumexp, bigru, gating, layernorm, optimization\"\nabstract: \"Same DSConv dual-expert config with global-norm gradient clipping (1.0) added to the optimizer to stabilize PRS/CRISPR while retaining strong Modif/ncRNA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_pool_gru import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n    \
    \      'post_norm': True,\n          'grad_clip': 1.0\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 21}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 344 — Reviewer feedback response and plan:\n  - Paper rejected: lacked SOTA context; suggested DSConv backbone. Action: implemented DSConv Expert A (5 dilated blocks) within dual-expert; submitted base and +clip runs.\n  - Multi-τ pooling did not improve PRS (513/514). Best remains 492 (0.6446).\n  - Next: if DSConv improves ≥0.66,\
    \ tri-seed + full SOTA comparison (scores, params, wall time). Else, reframe paper emphasizing parsimony vs SOTA cost with explicit gap.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Revising the plan for Expert A**\n\nI need to adjust our approach and incorporate a DSConv backbone for Expert A. Our lineage storage might already have the necessary DSConv code. I’ve seen that DSConv has shown some state-of-the-art results in Noema, with top entries around 0.6866. The review suggests we add a 5-block DSConv to Expert A, which could improve beyond our current base of 0.6446 while maintaining compatibility across datasets. It’s also essential to include SOTA results in our comparisons.**Planning immediate actions**\n\nI need to revise the paper to include SOTA baseline comparisons, possibly framing them as trade-offs. Reviewers want us to focus on DSConv to stay competitive, so it might help to run at least one DSConv variant to demonstrate improved scores. I’ll implement the DSConv backbone in Expert A using our existing lineage code. We need to check the contents to ensure compatibility. Afterwards, I’ll create a submission file where Expert A uses\
  \ DSConv stacks before pooling while keeping the scalar gate and setting specific training hyperparameters.**Outlining actions for submission**\n\nI’ll define the network according to the allowed functions and shapes before submitting the evaluation. Next, I need to revise the paper to include SOTA comparisons, highlighting the balance between compute and performance, especially if we’re still below SOTA. It might be a good idea to discuss high-level concepts with others in Public Memory, though it’s not necessary. I’ve used 122,919 tokens out of 270K, so that's okay. \n\nI’ll focus on reading DSConv modules, writing new submission code for the DSConv-based dual-expert, and submitting runs, keeping in mind the two-at-a-time limit.**Planning the DSConv implementation**\n\nI think I need to reframe our approach to prioritize parsimony in computation costs while incorporating DSConv. I’ll be implementing the code for the dual_expert_dsconv_pool_gru.py in noema/submissions. It’s crucial that\
  \ the code compiles without any external dependencies and fits within allowed time limits. \n\nI’ll define the DSConvBlock using depthwise and pointwise convolutions, then stack five of them with specified rates. After the convolution stack, I’ll apply the pooling method. For Expert B, I’ll keep the BiGRU as is. Finally, I’ll submit the code once everything is in place.**Preparing to implement DSConv**\n\nI need to write the code for the dual_expert_dsconv_pool_gru.py and submit two experiments: one with DSConv expert plus scalar gate, and the second with grad clip at 1.0 while considering a tau of 0.25 for pooling. Adjusting the kernel size to 7 for DSConv sounds good.\n\nI'll define the DSConvBlock class and ensure the right parameters are passed for kernel size. After implementing this, I'll update private memory notes about reviewer feedback and our plan, but I need to wait to revise the paper until we see results that indicate improvement. It’s not urgent to prune token usage since\
  \ it’s currently at 47%. Let's proceed with the commands as laid out."
