parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 346\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 137,137 / 270,000 used (51%)\n- Agent Age: 53 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Dual-expert (DSConv Expert A) + mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU(160), scalar gate + post-norm + grad-clip=1.0 — seed=42' (ID: 518) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File\
    \ \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/2c90c43b-c914-4511-baa8-2bea1f6ed2b3/storage/system/main.py\", line 593, in <module>\n    result = main()\n             ^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/2c90c43b-c914-4511-baa8-2bea1f6ed2b3/storage/system/main.py\", line 553, in main\n    validation_success = simple_cpu_validation()\n                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/2c90c43b-c914-4511-baa8-2bea1f6ed2b3/storage/system/main.py\", line 415, in simple_cpu_validation\n    params = network.init(key, dummy_input)\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/2c90c43b-c914-4511-baa8-2bea1f6ed2b3/storage/noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_pool_gru.py\", line 187, in init\n    variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\
    \ dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/2c90c43b-c914-4511-baa8-2bea1f6ed2b3/storage/noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_pool_gru.py\", line 142, in __call__\n    h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/2c90c43b-c914-4511-baa8-2bea1f6ed2b3/storage/noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_pool_gru.py\", line 111, in __call__\n    h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/2c90c43b-c914-4511-baa8-2bea1f6ed2b3/storage/noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_pool_gru.py\"\
    , line 87, in __call__\n    x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/flax/linen/kw_only_dataclasses.py\", line 235, in init_wrapper\n    dataclass_init(self, *args, **kwargs)\nTypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'\n--------------------\nFor simplicity, JAX has removed its internal frames from the traceback of the following exception. Set JAX_TRACEBACK_FILTERING=off to include these.\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Dual-expert (DSConv Expert A) + mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU(160), scalar gate + post-norm — seed=42' (ID: 517) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6673839767223287\n**APA_R2:** 0.8526\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0838\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9506\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4069\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5556\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8807\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9415\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\
    \n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 517\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The submission was fixed and is now running without crashes. The code executed for over 300 seconds without errors, indicating the fix resolved the issue.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported a function `build_network` from `storage/noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_pool_gru.py`, which contained a bug in the `DSConvBlock` class. The bug was a Flax API incompatibility:\n\n**Line 90 of dual_expert_dsconv_pool_gru.py:**\n```python\nx = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n            dilation=(self.dilation,),  # INCORRECT parameter name\n            padding='SAME')(x)\n```\n\nThe error message was:\n```\nTypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'\n```\n\nThis occurred because newer versions of Flax use `kernel_dilation` instead of `dilation` as the parameter name\
    \ for the Conv layer.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` which:\n\n1. **Copied and fixed the buggy classes** from the lineage file:\n   - `DSConvBlock` - Changed `dilation=(self.dilation,)` to `kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,)` at line 87\n   - `DSConvBackbone` - Uses the fixed `DSConvBlock`\n   - `DualExpertDSConv` - Uses the fixed `DSConvBackbone`\n   - `WrappedRNANetwork` - Uses the fixed `DualExpertDSConv`\n\n2. **Kept working imports**: Imported the remaining helper functions that didn't need fixes:\n   - `_lse_pool`\n   - `PoolingBlock`\n   - `BiGRUBlock`\n   - `create_optimizer`\n\n3. **Maintained all functionality**: The fix only changed the parameter name, preserving all the original model architecture and hyperparameters.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed successful execution:\n- Exit code: 0 (SUCCESS)\n- Runtime: 300+ seconds without crashes\n- Status: Code running as expected\n\nThe fix successfully resolved the Flax API incompatibility\
    \ issue, allowing the dual-expert DSConv model to initialize and execute properly.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n# Import most functions from the lineage file, but we'll define DSConvBlock locally to fix the bug\nfrom dual_expert_dsconv_pool_gru import (\n    build_network,\n    create_optimizer as make_optimizer,\n    _define_hyperparameters,\n    _lse_pool,\n    PoolingBlock,\n    DSConvBackbone,\n    BiGRUBlock,\n    DualExpertDSConv,\n    WrappedRNANetwork\n)\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n# Fixed DSConvBlock with kernel_dilation instead of dilation\nclass DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n\
    \    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        residual = x\n        # Depthwise dilated conv - FIXED: using kernel_dilation instead of dilation\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                    kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                    feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),  # FIXED: was dilation, now kernel_dilation\n                    padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        # Pointwise conv\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,))(x)\n        x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n        return residual + x\n\n# Override DSConvBackbone to use our fixed DSConvBlock\nclass DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilations: tuple\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # Initial embedding\
    \ to hidden_dim\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding='SAME')(x)\n        h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n        for d in self.dilations:\n            h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n        return h\n\n# Override DualExpertDSConv to use our fixed DSConvBackbone\nclass DualExpertDSConv(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n    hidden_dim: int = 256\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    ds_dilations: tuple = (1,2,4,8,16)\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n    tau: float = 0.25\n    length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n    gru_dim: int = 160\n    fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n    post_norm: bool = True\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # Expert A: DSConv backbone -> pooling\n        h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n \
    \       pool_rep = PoolingBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate, self.aggregator, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)(h, deterministic)\n        # Expert B: BiGRU\n        rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim)(x)\n        rnn_rep = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n        # Projections\n        pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n        rnn_proj  = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n        # Fusion\n        if self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n            logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros((2,), dtype=pool_proj.dtype), (2,))\n            w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n            fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n        elif self.fusion == 'avg':\n            fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown fusion: {self.fusion}\")\n        if self.post_norm:\n            fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n        # Head\n        z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused); z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n\
    \        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n        return z.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else z\n\n# Override WrappedRNANetwork to use our fixed DualExpertDSConv\nclass WrappedRNANetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams=None):\n        from jax import random\n        h = hparams or {}\n        self.network = DualExpertDSConv(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n            kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n            ds_dilations=tuple(h.get('ds_dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n            dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n            aggregator=str(h.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse_mix')),\n            tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n            length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n            gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim',\
    \ 160)),\n            fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n            post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', True)),\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        from jax import random\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        from jax import random\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 256,\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n        'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n        'tau': 0.25,\n        'length_normalize_lse': True,\n        'gru_dim': 160,\n        'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n        'post_norm': True\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting\
    \ APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA\
    \ network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0\
    \ min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0133 |  0.3469  | 0.3549 \n 20  | 0.0120 |  0.3746  | 0.3851 \n 30  | 0.0124 |  0.3874  | 0.4069 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 32 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4069 Time:27s\n[Complete] CRI-On val_metric=0.40686186966262944\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.406862\nTraining time: 38s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\
