- text: "Tri-seed DSConv dual-expert mean ≈ 0.6668 (IDs 517/521/522). Proceeding to get parameter counts and retry clipped DSConv (now that dilation API is fixed), then I’ll revise the paper with SOTA comparisons.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv dual-expert — parameter count (test only)\"\ntags: \"dsconv, parameters, analysis\"\nabstract: \"Runs test() to report parameter counts for the DSConv dual-expert (ID 517 config) across representative heads—no training.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  import dsconv_paramcount_submit as pc\n\n  def test():\n      return pc.test()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-expert (DSConv Expert A) + mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU(160), scalar gate + post-norm + grad-clip=1.0 — seed=42 (retry)\"\ntags: \"dsconv, gating, layernorm, optimization, bigru, pooling\"\nabstract: \"Retry DSConv dual-expert with global-norm gradient clipping (1.0) after fixing kernel_dilation\
    \ API. Tests whether clipping improves PRS/CRI stability.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_pool_gru import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n\
    \      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update (Tick 348)\n  DSConv Expert A + mean↔LSE(τ=0.25,len-norm) + BiGRU(160), scalar gate + post-LN — Tri-seed:\n  - 517 (seed=42): 0.6674 | APA 0.8526 | CRI-Off 0.0838 | Modif 0.9506 | CRI-On 0.4069 | PRS 0.5556 | MRL 0.8807 | ncRNA 0.9415.\n  - 521 (seed=7):  0.6679 | APA 0.8532 | CRI-Off 0.0884 | Modif 0.9493 | CRI-On 0.4192 | PRS 0.5521 | MRL 0.8826 | ncRNA 0.9308.\n  - 522 (seed=123):0.6650 | APA 0.8510 | CRI-Off 0.0837 | Modif 0.9509 | CRI-On 0.4042 | PRS 0.5517 | MRL 0.8917 | ncRNA 0.9215.\n  Mean ≈ 0.6668 (gap to SOTA 0.6866 ≈ 0.0198). Largest remaining gap is CRI-On Spearman (~0.41 vs ~0.52 in SOTA).\n\n  Actions:\n  - Submitted parameter-count test for DSConv dual-expert (no training).\n  - Retrying DSConv + grad-clip=1.0\
    \ (seed=42) after kernel_dilation fix to probe PRS/CRI stability.\n\n  Next:\n  - Use param counts and tri-seed mean to revise paper with explicit SOTA table (IDs 369/328/365) and trade-off analysis (params, wall-time).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning paper submission**\n\nI’m considering adding compute and parameter counts to support our paper. To get numeric values, I’ll run the dsconv_paramcount_submit function to submit to research. The test function will run but won’t train, and while the score won’t matter, it’s fine. After submission, we’ll prepare a revision paper in Archive Room, including a concise SOTA table and referencing evaluation IDs, coverage, and parameter counts. This will help us focus on the DSConv results versus SOTA.**Preparing for submission**\n\nI need to execute some actions right now. First, I'll submit the parameter count using the dsconv_paramcount_submit file, found in storage/noema/submissions. I can use the command `/execute_action{submit 1}` with the title \"param count.\" To make the test function callable in the submission, I have to ensure it's defined correctly.\n\nAfter we receive a response, we can proceed to write a revised Archive submission. The reviewer suggested\
  \ we can resubmit immediately, so I’ll prepare the new archive capsule, including a placeholder for parameter counts.**Deciding on submission timing**\n\nThe test will run soon, so I plan to submit the archive after obtaining the parameter counts. However, I'm wondering if it's better to publish later with all the numbers included. The system emphasizes focusing on verifiable claims supported by experimental data, which makes me think it might be wise to wait a tick for those counts before resubmitting. \n\nIn the meantime, I can create a note in Private Memory or draft the revision for a new content file. So, for now, I'll submit the param count test and update the results summary.**Analyzing performance metrics**\n\nI’m thinking about proposing a small improvement to the CRI-Off or PRS. The current PRS value is around 0.5556, while the SOTA table shows it at approximately 0.5687, which isn’t too far off. The main gap is with the overall performance and specifically the APA metrics, where\
  \ we have 0.853 compared to SOTA's 0.8555. \n\nThe larger gap appears in Spearman CRI-On, which stands at about 0.41 for us versus around 0.52 in SOTA. This significant difference of about 0.10 could impact the overall average score, which is 0.667 for us against SOTA’s top score of roughly 0.686. Major architectural changes might be challenging, but small augmentations like kernel expansion or bidirectional gating could help address this in the future while maintaining simplicity.**Scheduling submission actions**\n\nIn this turn, I need to submit the param count test, and then update the results summary with the tri-seed mean and gap. Once the test is complete, we can resubmit the archive. I’ll ensure to include the necessary YAML and confirm quoting. \n\nFor the tri-seed mean, I calculate it as 0.6668 with four decimal places. I also want to propose another attempt with DSConv and grad clipping since we fixed kernel dilation. Although it's not absolutely necessary, it could improve PRS.\
  \ We'll submit both the param count test and the clipped DSConv with seed 42. I’ll create the actions accordingly."
