tick: 349
role: model
parts:
- text: "Submitting a revised archive paper with explicit SOTA context, tri-seed results, and parameter counts; noting in-flight clipped-DSConv run.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Near-SOTA with <1M Params: DSConv Dual-Expert (mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU) with Scalar Gating\"\nabstract: |\n  We revise our prior dual-expert RNA model by replacing the single 1D conv in Expert A with a 5-block dilated DSConv backbone (dilations=[1,2,4,8,16]). The architecture remains parsimonious: Expert A uses a learned mix of mean and length-normalized LSE pooling (τ=0.25); Expert B is a small BiGRU(160). Fusion is via a scalar gate with post-fusion LayerNorm. Across seven datasets, tri-seed mean reaches 0.6668 with ~0.93–0.933M parameters, narrowing the SOTA gap to ~0.02 (SOTA ≈0.6866). We include full ablations, parameter counts, and wall-time, and release code/configs for reproducibility.\ncontent: |\n  1) Method (Universal across datasets, no pretraining\
    \ or external data)\n  - Inputs: one-hot RNA (B, L, 4); no positional encodings.\n  - Expert A (Backbone + Pooling):\n    • DSConv backbone: 5 residual blocks with dilations [1, 2, 4, 8, 16].\n    • Each block: depthwise (kernel_dilation) + pointwise conv + GELU + residual.\n    • Global pooling: learned mix of mean and LogSumExp (LSE, τ=0.25), length-normalized.\n  - Expert B (Order-sensitive branch): BiGRU(160), final-state concat → linear projection.\n  - Fusion and Head:\n    • Scalar gate (2-way softmax) over expert projections; post-fusion LayerNorm.\n    • 2-layer head → dataset-specific output (regression, multilabel regression/classification, multiclass).\n  - Optimizer and Training:\n    • AdamW (lr=1e-3, wd=1e-2), batch size=64, early stopping (patience=10), max 100 epochs/dataset.\n\n  2) Results and SOTA Context (Research Counter IDs; higher is better)\n  - SOTA references (top examples):\n    • 369 (Noema I): 0.6866\n    • 328 (Axiom II): 0.6863\n    • 365 (Veritas II):\
    \ 0.6862\n  - Our DSConv Dual-Expert (scalar gate + post-LN), tri-seed:\n    • 517 (seed=42): 0.6674 | APA 0.8526 | CRI-Off 0.0838 | Modif 0.9506 | CRI-On 0.4069 | PRS 0.5556 | MRL 0.8807 | ncRNA 0.9415\n    • 521 (seed=7):  0.6679 | APA 0.8532 | CRI-Off 0.0884 | Modif 0.9493 | CRI-On 0.4192 | PRS 0.5521 | MRL 0.8826 | ncRNA 0.9308\n    • 522 (seed=123):0.6650 | APA 0.8510 | CRI-Off 0.0837 | Modif 0.9509 | CRI-On 0.4042 | PRS 0.5517 | MRL 0.8917 | ncRNA 0.9215\n  - Tri-seed mean ≈ 0.6668 (gap to 0.6866 ≈ 0.0198). Notably strong classification (ncRNA up to 0.9415; Modif up to 0.9506–0.9509) and solid PRS/MRL, with CRI-On still the largest remaining gap (~0.41 vs ~0.52 in top SOTA).\n\n  3) Model Size and Wall-Time\n  - Parameter counts (test() run, ID 524):\n    • regression(d_out=1): 930,085\n    • multilabel_regression(d_out=3): 930,599\n    • multilabel_classification(d_out=12): 932,912\n    • multiclass_classification(d_out=13): 933,169\n    Param range across heads: ~0.93M to ~0.933M.\n\
    \  - Wall-time: end-to-end multi-dataset total ~32 minutes for ID 517 (within system limits; dataset trials run in parallel).\n\n  4) Ablations and Negative Results\n  - Pooling and Calibration:\n    • Learned mix(mean, LSE τ=0.25, length-normalized) > mean-only and τ=0.20. Length normalization is critical.\n    • Multi-τ pooling (τ∈{0.125,0.25,0.5}) did not improve mean score or PRS (e.g., 513: 0.6342; 514: 0.6374).\n  - Fusion:\n    • Scalar gate > average > MLP gate (MLP underperformed).\n  - RC Invariance:\n    • Eval-only RC averaging is invalid for orientation-specific labels (catastrophic drop in 497).\n    • Train+eval RC averaging can help APA but is not a consistent win across tasks.\n  - Learnable τ (global) caused ncRNA instability (503: 0.6123).\n  - Prior single-conv dual-expert peaked at 0.6446; DSConv backbone closed ~50% of the prior gap to SOTA.\n\n  5) Reproducibility\n  - Code (lineage storage):\n    • DSConv dual-expert: storage/noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_pool_gru.py\n\
    \    • Base dual-expert (single conv): storage/noema/submissions/dual_expert_pool_gru_weighted.py\n    • Parameter count script: storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_paramcount_submit.py (test-only)\n  - Hyperparameters set in _define_hyperparameters(); BASE_SEED, BATCH_SIZE constants defined per submission.\n  - All referenced evaluation IDs are reproducible via Research Counter.\n\n  6) Discussion and Outlook\n  - This DSConv dual-expert achieves near-SOTA performance with <1M parameters and a simple training recipe, offering a favorable accuracy-parameter trade-off.\n  - Remaining gap is concentrated in CRI-On Spearman; we hypothesize that longer-range motif aggregation or light cross-channel calibration (e.g., per-block channel-wise reweighting) may help without large complexity increases.\n  - In-flight: DSConv + global-norm gradient clipping (ID 525) to probe PRS/CRI stability. If gains hold, we will tri-seed and update this report.\n\n  7) Summary\n  - A compact, universal DSConv\
    \ dual-expert model reaches tri-seed mean 0.6668 with ~0.93M parameters, narrowing the SOTA gap to ~0.02 and providing strong classification/regression balance with straightforward reproducibility.\n```"
