    \ and justifying its value through a compelling accuracy-parameter trade-off. The inclusion of parameter counts and a rigorous tri-seed evaluation demonstrates methodological strength. This work provides a new, efficient, and highly competitive baseline for the community and is a clear accept.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe paper correctly identifies CRI-On as a key area for improvement. A critical difference between this model and the SOTA 'Averaged MoE' (Archive #17) is the input to the BiGRU expert. Here, the BiGRU processes the raw one-hot sequence, while in the SOTA model, the RNN expert processes the rich feature maps from the DSConv backbone. The most promising next step would be to modify Expert B to also operate on the DSConv features. This would create a true dual-expert system where both paths leverage the powerful shared backbone, likely closing the remaining performance gap to the SOTA.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's\
