parts:
- text: "Adopting the reviewer’s suggestion: make Expert B operate on DSConv features (shared backbone), then run base and clipped variants.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  DSConv Shared-Backbone Dual-Expert for RNA:\n    - Shared DSConv backbone (5 dilated blocks: [1,2,4,8,16]) produces feature maps h (B, L, C).\n    - Expert A: Global pooling on h via learned mix(mean, LSE τ=0.25, length-normalized).\n    - Expert B: BiGRU over h (after per-timestep linear proj to gru_dim).\n    - Fusion: scalar gate (2-way softmax) over expert projections; post-fusion LayerNorm.\n    - Head: 2-layer MLP to dataset-specific d_output.\n\n  Notes:\n    - No pretraining/external data; universal across datasets.\n    - Flax Conv kernel_dilation used for dilations (API-compatible).\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from\
    \ jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          # pooling\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          # backbone\n          'ds_dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          # rnn\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          # fusion/norms\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau, length_normalize=True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  class PoolingBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      aggregator: str\
    \ = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          lse_pool = _lse_pool(h, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix':\n              w = self.param('mix_w', lambda rng, shp: jnp.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=mean_pool.dtype), (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(w)\n              pooled = w[0] * mean_pool + w[1] * lse_pool\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n          return pooled\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          # Depthwise dilated\
    \ conv (Flax: kernel_dilation)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          # Pointwise conv\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,))(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Project input channels to hidden_dim\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n     \
    \         h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h  # (B, L, C)\n\n  class BiGRUOverFeat(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n          # h: (B, L, C); project to gru_dim per timestep\n          x_emb = nn.Dense(self.gru_dim)(h)\n          f = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hf = f(x_emb)[:, -1, :]\n          b = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hb = b(jnp.flip(x_emb, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n          return jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)  # (B, 2*gru_dim)\n\n  class DualExpertDSConvShared(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      gru_dim: int = 160\n\
    \      fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n      post_norm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Shared backbone features\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n\n          # Expert A: pooling on h\n          pool_rep = PoolingBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate, self.aggregator, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)(h, deterministic)\n\n          # Expert B: BiGRU over h\n          rnn_rep = BiGRUOverFeat(self.gru_dim)(h)\n          rnn_rep = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n          # Projections\n          pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n          rnn_proj  = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n          # Fusion\n          if self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n              logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros((2,), dtype=pool_proj.dtype), (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n\
    \              fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n          elif self.fusion == 'avg':\n              fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown fusion: {self.fusion}\")\n\n          if self.post_norm:\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n\n          # Head\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return z.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n          self.network = DualExpertDSConvShared(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size',\
    \ 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(h.get('ds_dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              aggregator=str(h.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse_mix')),\n              tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n              fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n              post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', True)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n             \
    \ if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv Shared-Backbone Dual-Expert (RNN on DSConv features) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, shared-backbone, bigru, pooling, gating, layernorm\"\nabstract: \"Implements reviewer-suggested shared backbone: BiGRU operates on DSConv feature maps (not one-hot). Expert A uses mean↔LSE(τ=0.25,len-norm) pooling on DSConv features. Scalar-gated fusion + post-LN. Tests closing CRI-On gap.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone\
    \ import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv Shared-Backbone Dual-Expert\
    \ + grad-clip=1.0 — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, shared-backbone, bigru, pooling, gating, layernorm, optimization\"\nabstract: \"Same shared-backbone config with global-norm gradient clipping (1.0) to further stabilize CRI-On/PRS.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def\
    \ create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{update 18-1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum (Tick 350): Responding to the reviewer’s suggestion, we implemented a shared-backbone DSConv dual-expert where the BiGRU operates on DSConv features instead of one-hot. Two evaluations have been submitted (base and +grad-clip=1.0; pending). This modification targets the remaining CRI-On gap explicitly while preserving the architecture’s parsimony. We will update this capsule with results once available.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning RNN Implementation**\n\nThe reviewer suggests using RNN on DSConv features, which might boost our CRI-On. I’ll need to create a storage file and submit runs. It seems like we might also want to update the paper with this suggestion.\n\nI see there's an option to update the archive capsule with ID 18, particularly message ID \"18-1\". The plan right now is to focus on the code and experiment, especially on writing the file `noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone.py`. I'll be implementing the same DSConvBackbone and applying the RNN as discussed.**Structuring BiGRU Implementation**\n\nI’m considering reusing BiGRUBlock but modifying it to take the output \\( h \\) instead of the raw input \\( x \\). I’ll create a BiGRUFeatBlock that optionally projects to \\( \\text{gru\\_dim} \\) using a Dense layer. \n\nThen I plan to ensure we have projections to \\( \\text{hidden\\_dim} \\), gating, and post-normalization. The aggregator will use mean_lse_mix\
  \ with a configurable tau, keeping hyperparameters like \\( \\text{ds\\_dilations} \\) as well. \n\nI'll set \\( \\text{BASE\\_SEED} = 42 \\) and include optimizer creation with a gradient clipping variant for submissions. Plus, I need to make sure we meet all the module function requirements and check the flax import compatibility. Finally, we'll submit two runs: one without clipping and one with a clip of 1.0.**Planning Update Actions**\n\nI might consider using a tri-seed approach later if it looks promising. I could also optionally update the archive with an addendum that references the reviewer’s suggestions and in-progress experiments.\n\nIt seems I need to handle update 18-1. I can append a reply or modify the existing content, adding a new section called \"Addendum (Tick 350)\" to describe the new experiments. \n\nSo, the plan is to go to the research area, write the new module file, and submit both the base run and a clipped variant with seed 42. Then I'll update the results summary\
  \ and modify archive entry 18-1 to include the addendum about the Shared-Backbone DSConv dual-expert submissions.**Preparing for Submissions**\n\nWe won't have IDs yet, so I think it's better to say \"submitted runs pending\" rather than just stating \"submitted evaluations.\" For the capsule update referenced as 18-1, I can provide new content indicating we'll incorporate the upcoming results.\n\nI'll need to be cautious about using the Archive Room and ensure that I include the necessary YAML fields. My plan involves defining the DSConvBlock, creating the DSConvBackbone, and implementing the BiGRUOnFeatBlock. The DualExpertDSConvShared will use the DSConvBackbone to generate \\( h \\), with pooling and BiGRU applied afterward.\n\nI'll check the output shapes and ensure the aggregator uses mean_lse_mix. Since we can only have two pending submissions, I’ll follow through on those and update the results summary. Let's get to implementing!"
