tick: 352
role: model
parts:
- text: "Shared-backbone looks promising: clipped variant reached 0.6751 with CRI-On 0.4924. I’ll tri-seed the clipped shared-backbone and log param counts for the shared model, then update the paper addendum.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv Shared-Backbone Dual-Expert + grad-clip=1.0 — tri-seed (seed=7)\"\ntags: \"dsconv, shared-backbone, bigru, pooling, gating, layernorm\"\nabstract: \"Tri-seed replication of the shared-backbone dual-expert where BiGRU runs on DSConv features; scalar gate + post-LN; global-norm grad-clip=1.0. This run uses BASE_SEED=7 to assess stability.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n\
    \          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv Shared-Backbone Dual-Expert + grad-clip=1.0 — tri-seed (seed=123)\"\ntags: \"dsconv, shared-backbone, bigru, pooling, gating, layernorm\"\nabstract: \"Tri-seed replication (seed=123) of the shared-backbone\
    \ dual-expert where BiGRU runs on DSConv features; scalar gate + post-LN; global-norm grad-clip=1.0.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Param count: DSConv Shared-Backbone Dual-Expert (test only)\"\ntags: \"dsconv, shared-backbone, parameters, analysis\"\nabstract: \"Runs test() to report parameter counts for the shared-backbone dual-expert across representative heads. No training.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone import build_network\n\n  def _count_params(params_tree):\n      leaves = jax.tree_util.tree_leaves(params_tree)\n      return sum(int(x.size) for x in leaves)\n\n  def _init_and_count(d_output, task_type):\n      hparams = {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n        \
    \  'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n      net = build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams)\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      dummy = jnp.zeros((2, 186, 4), dtype=jnp.float32)\n      params = net.init(key, dummy)\n      return _count_params(params)\n\n  def test():\n      counts = {}\n      counts['regression(d_output=1)'] = _init_and_count(1, 'regression')\n      counts['multilabel_regression(d_output=3)'] = _init_and_count(3, 'multilabel_regression')\n      counts['multilabel_classification(d_output=12)'] = _init_and_count(12, 'multilabel_classification')\n      counts['multiclass_classification(d_output=13)'] = _init_and_count(13, 'multiclass_classification')\n      print(\"Shared-backbone param counts:\")\n      for k,v in counts.items():\n          print(f\"  {k}: {v:,}\
    \ params\")\n      print(f\"Param range: {min(counts.values()):,} to {max(counts.values()):,}\")\n      return counts\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update (Tick 352)\n  Shared-backbone DSConv dual-expert (BiGRU on DSConv features), scalar gate + post-LN:\n  - 527 (base, seed=42): 0.6663 | CRI-On 0.4515 | PRS 0.5433 | MRL 0.8964 | ncRNA 0.8923.\n  - 528 (clip=1.0, seed=42): 0.6751 | CRI-On 0.4924 | PRS 0.5542 | MRL 0.8947 | ncRNA 0.8985.\n  Notes:\n  - Shared-backbone lifts CRI-On substantially (to ~0.49 with clipping) and MRL remains strong; slight ncRNA drop vs earlier non-shared (0.94→~0.90).\n  - Tri-seed (clip) submitted: seeds {7, 123}. Next: summarize mean/variance and compare to SOTA rows (IDs 369/328/365).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{update 18-1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum (Tick 352): Shared-backbone DSConv dual-expert results:\n  - Base (ID 527): 0.6663 (CRI-On 0.4515).\n\
    \  - +Grad-clip=1.0 (ID 528): 0.6751 (CRI-On 0.4924), narrowing SOTA gap to ~0.0115.\n  We have queued tri-seeds for the clipped shared-backbone and will update with the averaged score and parameter counts for the shared model. Preliminary observation: CRI-On and MRL improve with shared features; ncRNA slightly decreases (~0.90). We will explore light per-expert projection calibration if needed, while keeping the method parsimonious.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating next steps in token management**\n\nI'm working in the Token Management Room after a recent pruning, and I've got some new results. The DSConv shared-backbone base shows promising metrics but still falls behind the state of the art (SOTA). Key improvements like CRI-On and others are notable, but the ncRNA drop is something to consider. For next steps, I think tri-seed replication for stability confirmation is essential. Maybe adjusting dropout or training will help recapture that ncRNA accuracy. I'm curious about the reasons for the decline!**Exploring RNN adjustments**\n\nI'm considering whether the RNN's operation on features might be weakening the classification head's strength. I think we could try adding a simple calibration or reweighting per block, but I'd like to minimize any risks. Post-fusion layer normalization is an idea, and per-expert projection normalization before fusion could help equalize scales. We should also run tri-seed for 528 to publish\
  \ our results table. I'm aiming for an average close to SOTA, updating our archive with new results while noting the CRI-On improvement!**Planning architecture adjustments**\n\nI need to run a parameter count for the new architecture. It seems we didn't create a test script for this yet, so I plan to adapt the existing dsconv_paramcount_submit.py to import relevant files. I'm also considering producing a tri-seed CSV summary of lineage results. One more tweak could be increasing the gru_dim to 192 to boost CRI-On while managing ncRNA, but that will raise the parameter count. \n\nI’ll proceed stepwise with the necessary submissions to keep everything organized!**Preparing for concise submissions**\n\nI want to ensure our messages stay concise according to the desired verbosity. We're re-submitting the new code \"submit_shared_backbone_clip_seed7\" along with seed 123 and confirming that the optimizer includes clipping. I’ll write the submission content to import from our shared files accordingly.\
  \ \n\nThere's also a thought to add a per-expert pre-projection LayerNorm for better scaling, but I'll hold off on code changes for now. Dropping dropout to 0.08 seems tempting to boost classification, but I’m hesitant since it hurt PRS before. Let’s stick with 0.10 and focus on tri-seed.**Generating action plan**\n\nI’m laying out the next steps clearly: I need to go to research and submit tri-seeds 7 and 123 using clipping. Then, I'll write a results summary to update with ID 527 and 528, along with the planned tri-seeds. After updating archive 18-1 to report improvements, I want to mention both the CRI-On improvement and the changes to MRL.\n\nIt's essential to avoid oversharing, and I’ll keep the tags limited to six. I also plan to run a param count test for the shared-backbone model. Let’s finalize and implement this all in YAML format!"
