role: model
parts:
- text: "Adopting task-aware pooling and pre-fusion calibration to recover ncRNA while retaining CRI-On gains; prepping submissions once current runs finish.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  DSConv Shared-Backbone Dual-Expert for RNA:\n    - Shared DSConv backbone (5 dilated blocks: [1,2,4,8,16]) produces feature maps h (B, L, C).\n    - Expert A: Global pooling on h via:\n        • mean_lse_mix: learned mix(mean, LSE τ=0.25, length-normalized)\n        • mean_max_mix: learned mix(mean, max)  [for classification-oriented tasks]\n    - Expert B: BiGRU over h (after per-timestep linear proj to gru_dim).\n    - Fusion: scalar gate (2-way softmax) over expert projections; optional pre-norm per-expert LayerNorm and post-fusion LayerNorm.\n    - Head: 2-layer MLP to dataset-specific d_output.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import\
    \ jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          # pooling\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',   # can be overridden per dataset\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          # backbone\n          'ds_dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          # rnn\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          # fusion/norms\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': False,              # per-expert pre-fusion LayerNorm\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau, length_normalize=True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n\
    \      return tau * core\n\n  class PoolingBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_mix':\n              lse_pool = _lse_pool(h, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n              w = self.param('mix_w', lambda rng, shp: jnp.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=mean_pool.dtype), (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(w)\n              pooled = w[0] * mean_pool + w[1] * lse_pool\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_max_mix':\n              max_pool = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n              w = self.param('mix_w', lambda rng, shp: jnp.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=mean_pool.dtype), (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(w)\n   \
    \           pooled = w[0] * mean_pool + w[1] * max_pool\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n          return pooled\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,))(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n\
    \      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  class BiGRUOverFeat(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n          x_emb = nn.Dense(self.gru_dim)(h)\n          f = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hf = f(x_emb)[:, -1, :]\n          b = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hb = b(jnp.flip(x_emb, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n          return jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)\n\n  class DualExpertDSConvShared(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations:\
    \ Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      aggregator: str = \"mean_lse_mix\"\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      gru_dim: int = 160\n      fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n      pre_norm: bool = False\n      post_norm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n\n          pool_rep = PoolingBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate, self.aggregator, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)(h, deterministic)\n          rnn_rep = BiGRUOverFeat(self.gru_dim)(h)\n          rnn_rep = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n          pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n          rnn_proj  = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              pool_proj = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6, name='pre_ln_pool')(pool_proj)\n            \
    \  rnn_proj  = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6, name='pre_ln_rnn')(rnn_proj)\n\n          if self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n              logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros((2,), dtype=pool_proj.dtype), (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n              fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n          elif self.fusion == 'avg':\n              fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown fusion: {self.fusion}\")\n\n          if self.post_norm:\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return z.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams:\
    \ Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n          self.network = DualExpertDSConvShared(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(h.get('ds_dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              aggregator=str(h.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse_mix')),\n              tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n              fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n              pre_norm=bool(h.get('pre_norm', False)),\n              post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', True)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params':\
    \ params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/submit_shared_taskaware_clip.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone\
    \ import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Defaults; aggregator/pre_norm will be set in create_network based on task_type.\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,   # enable per-expert calibration\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      # Task-aware pooling: use mean_max_mix for multiclass classification (ncRNA), else mean_lse_mix.\n      hp = dict(hparams) if hparams is not None else {}\n      agg = 'mean_lse_mix'\n      if hp.get('task_type') == 'multiclass_classification' or hp.get('dataset') == 'ncRNA':\n          agg = 'mean_max_mix'\n      hp['aggregator']\
    \ = agg\n      hp['pre_norm'] = True\n      return build_network(hp.get('d_output', 1), hp.get('task_type', 'regression'), hp)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\nNote: I’ll submit the task-aware clipped variant once the current tri-seeds (532, 533) finish to respect the pending-evaluations limit."
thinking_content: "**Implementing aggregators for classification**\n\nI’m thinking we can adapt the aggregator based on the task type. For multiclass classification involving ncRNA, I remember that combining mean with max has shown good results. With the DSConv baseline in Noema I, mean plus max also provided stability. I’ll set up an aggregator_by_task function that uses 'mean_max' for multiclass classification and 'mean_lse_mix' otherwise. However, I see we didn’t implement the mean plus max aggregator in the shared-backbone script, which we should adjust for.**Refining the aggregator approach**\n\nI notice that concatenation previously improved classification, but I'm unsure if a mixture of sums alone will suffice. To be parsimonious, I think we could sum or learn a weight between mean and max, similar to an earlier learned mix. We can implement an aggregator called 'mean_max_mix' that uses a learned softmax over two weights, helping us maintain the hidden_dim shape. \n\nAdditionally,\
  \ I’ll modify the PoolingBlock to support this new aggregator by calculating mix weights as 'mix_w' and keeping 'mean_lse_mix' too.**Updating aggregator usage**\n\nI’m planning to modify the networks to accept an aggregator based on the dataset. We currently pass the aggregator string through hparams, and I can compute it automatically in _define_hyperparameters. However, since _define_hyperparameters lacks the dataset argument and doesn't get called directly with it, I need to adjust in create_network. If the task is 'multiclass_classification,' I’ll set the aggregator to 'mean_max_mix'; otherwise, it’ll default to 'mean_lse_mix.' Also, I'll ensure our PoolingBlock supports 'mean_max_mix.'**Proposing updates for the network**\n\nI need to write to storage to update a file and propose an experiment: using DSConv shared-backbone with clip and an aggregator switch. Additionally, I want to introduce a \"pre-fusion per-expert LayerNorm\" to calibrate scales for gating. I’ll implement a pre_norm\
  \ flag for gating and apply LayerNorm separately to pool_proj and rnn_proj. I'll ensure the PoolingBlock supports both 'mean_max_mix' and 'mean_lse_mix' aggregators. Finally, I’ll create a new submission detailing this updated approach.**Planning updates and submissions**\n\nI see we have two concurrent experiments running, so I won't be able to submit new ones at this time. But I can prepare an update to the shared backbone code to include the 'mean_max_mix' aggregator and pre_norm gating. I'll document the changes in the code storage. Since we can't submit the new experiments, I will instead focus on writing the updated code and planning for later submission once the existing experiments are complete. I’ll also consider reducing dropout to optimize classification, but that can wait for now.**Updating network configuration**\n\nI plan to implement create_network to modify the aggregator based on the hparams copy that includes 'task_type' and 'dataset.' Setting the aggregator and 'pre_norm'\
  \ to True will allow the build_network function to work effectively. Since we're at two running experiments, I can't submit another right now, but I can write the script and wait. I'll update the shared backbone code for 'mean_max_mix' and pre_norm gating while ensuring no naming conflicts with variables in the same module."
