parts:
- text: "Shared-backbone clipped tri-seed mean ≈ 0.6711; task-aware runs (IDs 535, 536) are in queue. I’ll stage a seed=123 task-aware submit and a shared-backbone param-count test to dispatch as soon as slots free.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/submit_shared_taskaware_clip_seed123.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from submit_shared_taskaware_clip import _define_hyperparameters, create_network, complete\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      # Mirror clip=1.0 config\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/shared_paramcount_submit.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys, jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n\
    \  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone import build_network\n\n  def _count_params(tree):\n      leaves = jax.tree_util.tree_leaves(tree)\n      return sum(int(x.size) for x in leaves)\n\n  def _init_and_count(d_output, task_type):\n      hparams = {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n      net = build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams)\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      dummy = jnp.zeros((2, 186, 4), dtype=jnp.float32)\n      params = net.init(key, dummy)\n      return _count_params(params)\n\n  def test():\n      counts = {\n        'regression(d_output=1)': _init_and_count(1, 'regression'),\n        'multilabel_regression(d_output=3)':\
    \ _init_and_count(3, 'multilabel_regression'),\n        'multilabel_classification(d_output=12)': _init_and_count(12, 'multilabel_classification'),\n        'multiclass_classification(d_output=13)': _init_and_count(13, 'multiclass_classification'),\n      }\n      print(\"Shared-backbone param counts:\")\n      for k,v in counts.items():\n          print(f\"  {k}: {v:,} params\")\n      print(f\"Param range: {min(counts.values()):,} to {max(counts.values()):,}\")\n      return counts\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update (Tick 355)\n  Shared-backbone + clip tri-seed (complete):\n  - 528 (seed=42): 0.6751 | CRI-On 0.4924 | PRS 0.5542 | MRL 0.8947 | ncRNA 0.8985.\n  - 532 (seed=7):  0.6671 | CRI-On 0.4559 | PRS 0.5460 | MRL 0.8918 | ncRNA 0.8908.\n  - 533 (seed=123):0.6712 | CRI-On 0.4751 | PRS 0.5522 | MRL 0.8935 | ncRNA 0.9031.\n  Mean ≈ 0.6711 (gap to SOTA 0.6866 ≈ 0.0155).\n\n  In-flight:\n  - Task-aware pooling\
    \ + pre-norm + clip=1.0 (IDs 535, 536). Seed=123 staged for immediate submit when queue frees (submit_shared_taskaware_clip_seed123.py).\n  - Shared-backbone param-count test staged (shared_paramcount_submit.py).\n  Goal: recover ncRNA while preserving CRI-On gains; then report updated mean and param counts in archive addendum.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Updating evaluation progress**\n\nI’m in the Archive Room, and two recent evaluations are running. One evaluation, the shared-backbone clipped tri-seed, yields a mean of about 0.6711. I’ve also submitted task-aware pooling with pre-norm seeds 42 and 7, which are queued as 535 and 536, and tick 355 shows they’re running now. The next steps involve waiting for results and potentially submitting additional parameters for the shared backbone. There are a few other considerations to address as well.**Planning next steps**\n\nI’m considering submitting a parameter count test for the shared backbone after the queue clears, but running jobs 535 and 536 are currently filling both slots. I’ve already prepared the test script titled \"Param count: DSConv Shared-Backbone Dual-Expert (test only)\" but haven’t submitted it yet. \n\nAdditionally, I might prune tokens since the cooldown from the last prune at tick 351 has now matured, allowing for another can be performed. I also need\
  \ to think about updating the archive addendum, but I’ll wait until I have the results.**Planning next actions**\n\nI’m thinking of logging a summary to the results file since that seems important right now. I could propose several next actions. One option is to store a script for the parameter count submission since we haven’t saved a dedicated one before. I might also prepare a tri-seed for later use and schedule it once the current tasks finish. Additionally, I could commit a summary of the results, but I’ve just updated that. Lastly, I should consider minimal modifications for tuning pre-norm or capacity.**Proposing action steps**\n\nI’m looking at the current action allowances, and it seems we can issue multiple execute_action commands in a single turn. First, I’ll suggest checking the rank score page at the Research Counter since I'm in the Archive.\n\nNext, I plan to create a submission script called 'submit_shared_taskaware_clip_seed123.py', but I could also just use the existing\
  \ 'submit_shared_taskaware_clip.py' with a constant base seed. The pending queue is full right now, so I’ll save the code in a file with BASE_SEED=123 for submission later without running it yet.**Creating submission scripts**\n\nI need to create a parameter count test script for the shared backbone and plan to submit it later. Although I earlier created 'Param count: DSConv Shared-Backbone Dual-Expert (test only)', I should store it as 'noema/submissions/shared_paramcount_submit.py'.\n\nNext, I’ll quickly summarize the tri-seed results and outline our plan: I’ll store the seed=123 submission file and the parameter count test, but there won't be any further submissions since the queue is full. I'll also include some execute_action commands to maintain clarity. \n\nMy first steps will be to go to research, store the required files, and possibly update the results summary. Then, I’ll prepare the code for 'submit_shared_taskaware_clip_seed123.py' to replicate 'submit_shared_taskaware_clip.py'\
  \ with BASE_SEED=123, along with 'shared_paramcount_submit.py' for the shared backbone. Given that the token budget is at a safe level, I think I’m on the right track!"
