parts:
- text: "Tri-seed task-aware shared-backbone mean ≈ 0.6729 (gap ~0.0137). CRI-On peaks at 0.5050 (seed=123). Pre-norm OFF improved ncRNA on seed=42 (0.8615 → 0.8754) with similar CRI-On. I’ll run pre-norm OFF for seeds 7 and 123, then report param counts and update the paper.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Shared-backbone DSConv dual-expert (task-aware pooling, pre-norm=OFF, clip=1.0) — seed=7\"\ntags: \"dsconv, shared-backbone, task-aware, pooling, gating\"\nabstract: \"Ablation to test pre-fusion LN removal across seeds: task-aware pooling (mean_max_mix for ncRNA; mean_lse_mix otherwise); pre-norm OFF; grad-clip=1.0. BASE_SEED=7.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n   \
    \       'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',  # overridden for ncRNA\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': False,  # ablation\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      hp = dict(hparams) if hparams is not None else {}\n      agg = 'mean_lse_mix'\n      if hp.get('task_type') == 'multiclass_classification' or hp.get('dataset') == 'ncRNA':\n          agg = 'mean_max_mix'\n      hp['aggregator'] = agg\n      hp['pre_norm'] = False\n      return build_network(hp.get('d_output', 1), hp.get('task_type', 'regression'), hp)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params,\
    \ opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Shared-backbone DSConv dual-expert (task-aware pooling, pre-norm=OFF, clip=1.0) — seed=123\"\ntags: \"dsconv, shared-backbone, task-aware, pooling, gating\"\nabstract: \"Ablation to test pre-fusion LN removal across seeds: task-aware pooling (mean_max_mix for ncRNA; mean_lse_mix otherwise); pre-norm OFF; grad-clip=1.0. BASE_SEED=123.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',  # overridden for ncRNA\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse':\
    \ True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': False,  # ablation\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      hp = dict(hparams) if hparams is not None else {}\n      agg = 'mean_lse_mix'\n      if hp.get('task_type') == 'multiclass_classification' or hp.get('dataset') == 'ncRNA':\n          agg = 'mean_max_mix'\n      hp['aggregator'] = agg\n      hp['pre_norm'] = False\n      return build_network(hp.get('d_output', 1), hp.get('task_type', 'regression'), hp)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update (Tick 358)\n  Task-aware shared-backbone (pre-norm ON) — Tri-seed:\n  - 535 (seed=42): 0.6681 | CRI-On 0.4841 | PRS 0.5562 | MRL 0.8933 | ncRNA 0.8615\n  - 536 (seed=7):  0.6757 | CRI-On 0.4861 | PRS 0.5537 | MRL 0.8895 | ncRNA 0.9185\n  - 539 (seed=123):0.6751 | CRI-On 0.5050 | PRS 0.5551 | MRL 0.8873 | ncRNA 0.8923\n  Mean ≈ 0.6729 (SOTA 0.6866 gap ≈ 0.0137). CRI-On peak 0.5050 (seed=123).\n\n  Pre-norm OFF (seed=42) ablation:\n  - 540: 0.6677 | CRI-On 0.4798 | PRS 0.5481 | MRL 0.8895 | ncRNA 0.8754\n  Note: Pre-norm OFF improved ncRNA for seed=42 vs pre-norm ON (0.8754 vs 0.8615) with minor CRI-On change. Replications (seeds 7, 123) submitted to assess mean impact.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{update 18-1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum (Tick 358): Task-aware shared-backbone tri-seed mean = 0.6729 (IDs 535/536/539), closing the gap to ~0.0137 from SOTA (0.6866). CRI-On improved up to 0.5050 (seed=123). \n  We observed\
    \ that turning OFF per-expert pre-LN increased ncRNA for seed=42 (0.8615 → 0.8754) with minimal CRI-On change; tri-seed pre-norm OFF is now running (seeds 7, 123) to confirm generality. \n  Next we will finalize the default config (task-aware pooling, clip=1.0, shared backbone; pre-norm ON or OFF based on tri-seed), report shared-backbone parameter counts, and update the accuracy–parameter trade-off table.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing results**\n\nI need to respond based on the station environment and focus on the Archive Room while reviewing the updated paper. I've received results for task-aware seed 123, scoring 0.67506 with a CRI-On of 0.5050, which is excellent. The pre-norm OFF for seed 42 shows some improvements too. While the CRI-On score slightly decreased, the ncRNA improved. The tri-seed mean calculation appears close to bridging the state-of-the-art gap, which is promising!**Examining experiment status**\n\nThe message says that there are no current running experiments. The last ticks, 539 and 540, have both been evaluated, leaving our queue open. Our last plan included testing a shared-backbone parameter count. We can submit that evaluation, update the archive addendum with those numbers, and potentially propose a final default config of shared-backbone with task-aware pooling and pre-norm disabled. While pre-norm off improved ncRNA for seed 42, I think we should schedule tests\
  \ for additional seeds while managing our evaluation limits.**Planning experiment submissions**\n\nCurrently, it’s free to submit pre-norm off for seeds 7 and 123. I can run a parameter count test as well, though I see that test mode doesn't block. Even if it shows \"Evaluation failed: Test mode - no scoring,\" it still takes an evaluation slot. I think we should queue the two seeds and then run the parameter count test afterward. We've used about 50% of our tokens, and I want to update the results summary with CRI-On improvements. Including gating regularization or weight smoothing feels out of scope for now.**Planning next actions**\n\nI need to produce a series of actions: go to research; submit pre-norm off for seeds 7 and 123; submit the shared parameter count test; and update the results summary. I'll also revise the archive addendum with the tri-seed mean for task-aware pre-norm on and note the preliminary effects of pre-norm off on seed 42, while stating the pending tri-seed for\
  \ pre-norm off. Though we're at 134k tokens used out of 270k, pruning conversation isn't urgent. Now, let's calculate the exact tri-seed mean: it averages to about 0.6729, with CRI-On averaging around 0.4917.**Crafting action summary**\n\nI see that CRI-On has improved to 0.5050, getting closer to the state-of-the-art CRI-On of about 0.52. Now, I need to outline a series of actions: \n\n1. Go to research.\n2. Submit pre-norm off for seed 7, creating a wrapper to set BASE_SEED=7 if needed. \n3. Submit pre-norm off for seed 123 similarly. \n4. Submit the parameter count test afterwards, but since that uses a slot and produces no scoring, I'll prioritize the two pre-norm off seeds first. \n\nFinally, I will write updates to the results summary and update the archive addendum. The SOTA gap computation is also noted as 0.0137."
