role: model
parts:
- text: "Submitting two low-risk improvements on the frozen default: cosine warmup-decay learning rate and a small dropout increase.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Shared-backbone default + cosine warmup–decay LR (pre-LN, clip=1.0) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, shared-backbone, lr-schedule, cosine, gating, optimization\"\nabstract: \"Frozen default with cosine warmup–decay LR schedule: warmup 2k steps to base LR, cosine decay over 50k steps to 0.1×. Tests if LR scheduling closes residual gap without changing params.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,       # peak LR for schedule\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',\
    \  # overridden for ncRNA\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      hp = dict(hparams) if hparams is not None else {}\n      agg = 'mean_lse_mix'\n      if hp.get('task_type') == 'multiclass_classification' or hp.get('dataset') == 'ncRNA':\n          agg = 'mean_max_mix'\n      hp['aggregator'] = agg\n      return build_network(hp.get('d_output', 1), hp.get('task_type', 'regression'), hp)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      warmup_steps = 2000\n      decay_steps = 50000\n      schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n          init_value=0.0,\n          peak_value=learning_rate,\n          warmup_steps=warmup_steps,\n          decay_steps=decay_steps,\n          end_value=learning_rate * 0.1\n      )\n      return optax.chain(\n\
    \          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=schedule, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Shared-backbone default + dropout=0.12 (pre-LN, clip=1.0) — seed=123\"\ntags: \"dsconv, shared-backbone, regularization, dropout, gating, pooling\"\nabstract: \"Frozen default with slightly stronger regularization (dropout 0.12). Tests generalization across tasks without changing parameters.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate':\
    \ 0.12,         # increased from 0.10\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_mix',  # overridden for ncRNA\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      hp = dict(hparams) if hparams is not None else {}\n      agg = 'mean_lse_mix'\n      if hp.get('task_type') == 'multiclass_classification' or hp.get('dataset') == 'ncRNA':\n          agg = 'mean_max_mix'\n      hp['aggregator'] = agg\n      return build_network(hp.get('d_output', 1), hp.get('task_type', 'regression'), hp)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset');\
    \ vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update (Tick 364)\n  Frozen default (<1M params) probes to close residual gap:\n  - Cosine warmup–decay LR schedule (warmup 2k → peak LR; decay 50k steps → 0.1×) — seed=42 submitted.\n  - Dropout +0.02 (0.12) — seed=123 submitted.\n\n  Default reference: task-aware pooling (ncRNA: mean_max_mix; others: mean_lse_mix), scalar gate, pre-LN per expert + post-LN, clip=1.0, BiGRU=160, h=256. Tri-seed mean 0.6729; CRI-On peak 0.5050.\n  Goal: improve mean without increasing params; track per-dataset shifts (APA/MRL/PRS/CRI-On/ncRNA/Modif) to attribute gains to schedule vs regularization.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning experiments**\n\nI need to figure out our next steps in the Archive Room. Thankfully, there are no obstacles reported. The agent has finished the default configuration and added some notes. The earlier suggestions included tuning the learning rate schedule using cosine decay and dropout adjustments. \n\nNow, I should consider proposing two new experiments at the Research Counter. One involves creating a cosine decay schedule using the optax framework, ensuring it fits well with our training setup.**Adapting learning rates and dropout**\n\nI need to set up a learning rate schedule since create_optimizer expects a float by default. I can ignore that argument and build a function using a base learning rate. The training loop should pass this learning rate to optax.adamw. To achieve this, I'll use optax's cosine decay schedule.\n\nFor dropout, I can vary the dropout rate between 0.10 and 0.12. Since the system allows two concurrent submissions, I can submit both\
  \ the learning rate schedule and the dropout sweep together. Plus, maybe improving the gating for initial weights would be beneficial!**Updating learning rate settings**\n\nWe’ve concluded to stick with the default values, but I also need to update the results document. I can combine the learning rate (LR) schedule with the existing settings. For clarity, I’ll implement new submission code that specifies the 'lr_schedule' as 'cosine_warmup', leading to a warmup implementation.\n\nHowever, I don't have the total_steps figured out. I could estimate this based on the maximum epochs and the training set size, but getting the dataset size isn’t easy. I might explore using a cosine decay restart schedule, but without accurate step counts, this could affect the schedule duration.**Configuring the training schedule**\n\nIn the training loop, I use optimizer.step for each batch. I can implement a learning rate schedule with a large decay_steps, like 10,000 or 20,000. Although training might end\
  \ earlier, the schedule will stay in its initial region. A simple option would be to use an exponential decay schedule, such as optax.cosine_decay_schedule, which would decrease to 10% over 20,000 steps.\n\nBut unknown step counts may vary by dataset. For the largest dataset with a BATCH_SIZE of 64, the steps per epoch would be about 2,273. I'm estimating that with 30 minutes of training, early stopping might take around 20-30 epochs, totaling roughly 45,000-68,000 steps, so I’ll settle on 50,000 for decay_steps and use a warmup of around 2,000 steps. I can define this schedule in create_optimizer while ignoring the float 'learning_rate' parameter.**Preparing experiment submissions**\n\nI can reduce the dropout to 0.08 to potentially improve results, but that previously hurt performance in the scalar gate non-shared config. For the shared-backbone, it might be different and safe to test. I should use dual seeds: one run at dropout 0.12 to enhance classification performance.\n\nI’ll draft\
  \ two YAML submissions now. The first will focus on a cosine warmup-decay learning rate with seed 42, including necessary imports and optimizations. The second submission will adjust dropout to 0.12 with seed 123. Once that’s done, I also need to log results and possibly note insights later."
