role: model
parts:
- text: "Reading Logos II’s enriched pooling paper, then implementing enriched pooling (mean, max, LSE, std) with channel-wise learned mix and submitting two runs (h=256 and h=192).\n\n`/execute_action{read 20}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_enriched.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Dual-expert with shared DSConv backbone and enriched pooling:\n  - Shared DSConv (5 blocks, dilations [1,2,4,8,16])\n  - Enriched pooling stats over sequence: mean, max, LSE(τ), std; channel-wise learned softmax mix (minimal params)\n  - Expert A: Enriched pooled DSConv features\n  - Expert B: BiGRU(=gru_dim) on DSConv features (bidirectional), projected to hidden_dim\n  - Fusion: scalar gate (softmax over 2 experts), optional pre/post LayerNorm\n  - Defaults: dropout=0.10, τ=0.25 with length normalization, clip handled in submit file\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy\
    \ as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau=0.25, length_normalize=True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = x\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          # depthwise dilated conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME')(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n\
    \          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          # pointwise conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # 1x1 embedding to hidden_dim\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          return h  # (B, L, H)\n\n  class EnrichedPooling(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      pre_norm: bool = False  # apply\
    \ LN before pooling\n      eps: float = 1e-6\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # h: (B, L, H)\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)            # (B, H)\n          lse_pool  = _lse_pool(h, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)  # (B, H)\n          max_pool  = jnp.max(h, axis=1)             # (B, H)\n          var_pool  = jnp.var(h, axis=1)\n          std_pool  = jnp.sqrt(var_pool + self.eps)  # (B, H)\n          stats = jnp.stack([mean_pool, lse_pool, max_pool, std_pool], axis=-1)  # (B, H, 4)\n\n          # Channel-wise learned mix over 4 stats (softmax on last dim)\n          logits = self.param('mix_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (self.hidden_dim, 4))\n          w = jax.nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)  # (H, 4)\n          w = jnp.expand_dims(w, axis=0)      \
    \ # (1, H, 4)\n          mixed = jnp.sum(stats * w, axis=-1)  # (B, H)\n          return mixed\n\n  class BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim: int\n      pre_norm: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x: (B, L, H)\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(x)\n          f = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hf = f(x)[:, -1, :]\n          b = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hb = b(jnp.flip(x, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n          return jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)  # (B, 2*gru_dim)\n\n  class DualExpertSharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      gru_dim: int = 160\n      fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n      pre_norm: bool\
    \ = True     # per-expert prenorm and backbone prenorm\n      post_norm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Shared backbone over one-hot input\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(x, deterministic)\n\n          # Expert A: Enriched pooling on DSConv features\n          pool_rep = EnrichedPooling(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n\n          # Expert B: BiGRU on DSConv features\n          rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim, self.pre_norm)(h)\n          rnn_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n          # Fusion\n          if self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n              logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n              fused\
    \ = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n          elif self.fusion == 'avg':\n              fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown fusion: {self.fusion}\")\n\n          if self.post_norm:\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n\n          # Head\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused); z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return z.squeeze(-1)\n          return z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n          self.network = DualExpertSharedBackbone(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size',\
    \ 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(h.get('ds_dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n              fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n              pre_norm=bool(h.get('pre_norm', True)),\n              post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', True)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is\
    \ None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Shared-backbone DSConv + Enriched Pooling (mean/max/LSE/std cw-mix), scalar gate, pre/post-LN — h=256 — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, enriched-pooling, cw-mix, gating, shared-backbone, parsimonious\"\nabstract: \"Adds enriched pooling with channel-wise learned mix over mean, max, LSE(τ=0.25 len-norm), and std on the shared DSConv backbone. BiGRU(160) expert and scalar-gated fusion retained. Tests if richer yet minimal pooling closes the gap without >1M params.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n\
    \  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_enriched import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n\
    \      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Shared-backbone DSConv + Enriched Pooling cw-mix — width=192 (param-reduced), seed=123\"\ntags: \"dsconv, enriched-pooling, parameter-reduction, cw-mix, shared-backbone\"\nabstract: \"Parameter-reduced variant: hidden_dim=192 with enriched pooling cw-mix and BiGRU(160). Tests if enriched pooling enables near-SOTA performance with fewer parameters.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_enriched import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 192,             # reduced width\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n    \
    \      'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/enriched_pooling_plan.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 367 — Enriched Pooling Plan\n  - Implemented enriched pooling over DSConv features with channel-wise learned mix of {mean, max, LSE(τ=0.25 len-norm), std}; minimal params (~4*H logits).\n  - Submitted:\n    • h=256, seed=42 (enriched cw-mix, clip=1.0) — goal: close gap\
    \ to ~0.686.\n    • h=192, seed=123 (param-reduced) — goal: high score/parameter efficiency.\n  - Next (if positive): tri-seed both, compare param counts vs performance; integrate into archive addendum with updated trade-off table.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating pooling techniques**\n\nI’m thinking about ideas like enriched pooling and parameter reduction. There might be alternatives, such as using mean, standard deviation, and max for pooling or channel attention. We could explore these concepts more or make comparisons. Should we run tri-seed for dropout of 0.12? One seed was slightly negative, so we don't want to waste compute. It might be interesting to test balanced dropout by dataset, but we need to be cautious with the rules around dataset-specific methods.**Considering parameter reduction**\n\nI’m exploring parameter reduction, thinking about decreasing hidden_dim from 256 to 192 to keep performance while improving parameter efficiency and possibly regularization. This could help us match similar scores, especially since we have a powerful DSConv. \n\nWhile others achieved a score of 0.6822 with reduced width and enriched pooling, our current score is 0.6729. It seems our architecture is nearly competitive.\
  \ Maybe adding variance or second-order features before pooling could help close the gap. Alternatively, adjusting gating per dataset is worth considering.**Evaluating architecture adaptations**\n\nI’m considering the limitations on dataset-specific methods; while core architecture should remain consistent across datasets, we can condition aggregator selection by task type, which serves as final head adaptation. However, adding dataset-specific gating might be questionable. \n\nI could explore ideas like \"conditional dropout per head,\" as seen in SOTA examples, but varying dropout rates may also conflict with uniformity across tasks. If the training code uses a hardcoded dropout rate, I might just stick with that. Alternatively, adding residual pre-activation or layer scaling to DSConv blocks might help stabilize things while maintaining simplicity.**Exploring training techniques**\n\nI’m considering \"LayerScale\" or \"skip-init\" to help scale the residual branch, which might improve\
  \ CRI-On during training. However, I'm aware that typical DSConv doesn’t include positional encoding, and adding something like phase-shift data augmentation isn’t allowed. \n\nI also noted that improvements in Spearman scores correlate with gating and GRU capacity. We reached an improvement of 0.505 with pre-LN ON, but SOTA is around 0.568. Perhaps using \"multi-branch pooling features\" or \"averaged MoE\" could help close the gap, as seen in Axiom III's score of 0.6849.**Implementing enriched pooling**\n\nI’m considering treating the pooling aggregator as a combination of mean, log-sum-exp (LSE), and max to create an enriched triple-stat approach. In our previous attempts, we saw mixed results, but using enriched pooling could help with the DSConv setup. I’m thinking about implementing \"Enriched Pooling (EPool)\" that captures these stats along channels with a small projection impact.\n\nMaintaining architecture uniformity across datasets is critical. I also aim to keep parameters\
  \ under 1M while exploring the implementation of a gating mechanism for better results with minimal overhead. I'll also investigate prior publications for insights to refine this further.**Updating pooling aggregators**\n\nI need to decide on the pooling aggregator for ncRNA compared to others. While we previously used 'mean_max_mix' specifically for ncRNA, I'm thinking it might be better to unify across tasks with 'enriched_cw_mix' to maintain fairness and consistency. I want to avoid changing aggregators between datasets. Although mean_max previously performed well for classification tasks, using 'enriched_cw_mix' could enhance flexibility.\n\nI’ll proceed to write a new file for our updated module and ensure we’re sticking to our parameter limits. I'll also prepare for submissions, considering testing with different widths and configurations later on.**Implementing BiGRU and Pooling**\n\nI’m taking a previous pattern to implement the `BiGRUBlock` using a GRU cell, so it processes input\
  \ via both forward and backward passes while concatenating the results. Next, I'll work on the `enriched_cw_mix` aggregator that computes various pooling statistics: mean, logsumexp (LSE), max, and standard deviation. \n\nAfter constructing the aggregated vector, I plan to set up two test runs: one with hidden dimensions of 256 and another reduced to 192, which will cut down on parameters. I'll ensure to input this into the right storage path and follow with submitting evaluations. Plus, I'll read relevant archives for additional context before finalizing everything."
