- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 369\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 110,661 / 270,000 used (41%)\n- Agent Age: 76 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Shared-backbone DSConv + Enriched Pooling cw-mix — width=192 (param-reduced), seed=123' (ID: 559) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/f87ce83d-fab4-49f2-9b15-df677ae39bea/storage/system/main.py\"\
    , line 593, in <module>\n    result = main()\n             ^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/f87ce83d-fab4-49f2-9b15-df677ae39bea/storage/system/main.py\", line 553, in main\n    validation_success = simple_cpu_validation()\n                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/f87ce83d-fab4-49f2-9b15-df677ae39bea/storage/system/main.py\", line 415, in simple_cpu_validation\n    params = network.init(key, dummy_input)\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/f87ce83d-fab4-49f2-9b15-df677ae39bea/storage/noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_enriched.py\", line 177, in init\n    variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n\
    \  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/f87ce83d-fab4-49f2-9b15-df677ae39bea/storage/noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_enriched.py\", line 125, in __call__\n    h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(x, deterministic)\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/f87ce83d-fab4-49f2-9b15-df677ae39bea/storage/noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_enriched.py\", line 62, in __call__\n    h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/f87ce83d-fab4-49f2-9b15-df677ae39bea/storage/noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_enriched.py\"\
    , line 38, in __call__\n    h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/flax/linen/kw_only_dataclasses.py\", line 235, in init_wrapper\n    dataclass_init(self, *args, **kwargs)\nTypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'\n--------------------\nFor simplicity, JAX has removed its internal frames from the traceback of the following exception. Set JAX_TRACEBACK_FILTERING=off to include these.\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Shared-backbone DSConv + Enriched Pooling (mean/max/LSE/std cw-mix), scalar gate, pre/post-LN — h=256 — seed=42' (ID: 558) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6729584296891199\n**APA_R2:** 0.8572\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0752\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9497\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4853\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5466\n**MRL_R2:** 0.9013\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.8954\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets\
    \ successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 558\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the Flax Conv parameter error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code in the lineage file `storage/noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_enriched.py` had a bug in the `DSConvBlock` class at line 38-42.\n\nThe code was using `dilation=(self.dilation,)` as a parameter to `nn.Conv()`, but the correct Flax parameter name is `kernel_dilation`, not `dilation`.\n\n**Error message:**\n```\nTypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'\n```\n\nThis is a simple API mismatch - the Flax `nn.Conv` layer expects `kernel_dilation` for dilated convolutions, not `dilation`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nSince the bug was in an imported lineage file that cannot be modified, I copied the affected classes into `submissions/submission_v2.py` and fixed them:\n\n1. **Fixed `DSConvBlock.__call__` method (line 38-42):**\n   - Changed: `dilation=(self.dilation,)`\n\
    \   - To: `kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,)`\n\n2. **Copied and fixed dependent classes:**\n   - `DSConvBlock` - Contains the actual bug fix\n   - `DSConvBackbone` - Uses the fixed `DSConvBlock`\n   - `DualExpertSharedBackbone` - Uses the fixed `DSConvBackbone`\n   - `WrappedRNANetworkFixed` - Uses the fixed `DualExpertSharedBackbone`\n\n3. **Kept working imports:**\n   - Still imported `_lse_pool`, `EnrichedPooling`, and `BiGRUBlock` from the lineage file as they work correctly\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed the fix was successful:\n- Code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n- No syntax or runtime errors in the execution\n\n## Technical Notes\nThis is a common issue when working with Flax/JAX APIs. The parameter naming conventions are:\n- `kernel_dilation` - Dilation rate for the convolution kernel\n- `input_dilation` - Dilation rate for the input (transposed convolution)\n\nThe fix was minimal and surgical - only the parameter name needed\
    \ to be corrected. The logic and architecture remain unchanged.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys, optax\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n# Import everything EXCEPT DSConvBlock and DSConvBackbone which have bugs\nfrom dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_enriched import (\n    _lse_pool, EnrichedPooling, BiGRUBlock, DualExpertSharedBackbone as OriginalDualExpertSharedBackbone,\n    WrappedRNANetwork, create_optimizer as _create_optimizer\n)\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Sequence\n\n# Fixed DSConvBlock with correct parameter name: kernel_dilation instead of dilation\nclass DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    pre_norm: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self,\
    \ x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        h = x\n        if self.pre_norm:\n            h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n        # depthwise dilated conv - FIX: use kernel_dilation instead of dilation\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                    kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                    feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),  # FIXED: was dilation=(self.dilation,)\n                    padding='SAME')(h)\n        h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        # pointwise conv\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n        return x + h\n\n# Fixed DSConvBackbone that uses the fixed DSConvBlock\nclass DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilations: Sequence[int]\n    dropout_rate: float\n    pre_norm: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self,\
    \ x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # 1x1 embedding to hidden_dim\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding='SAME')(x)\n        for d in self.dilations:\n            h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n        return h  # (B, L, H)\n\n# Fixed DualExpertSharedBackbone that uses the fixed DSConvBackbone\nclass DualExpertSharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n    hidden_dim: int = 256\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    tau: float = 0.25\n    length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n    gru_dim: int = 160\n    fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n    pre_norm: bool = True\n    post_norm: bool = True\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # Shared backbone over one-hot input - use fixed DSConvBackbone\n        h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim,\
    \ self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(x, deterministic)\n\n        # Expert A: Enriched pooling on DSConv features\n        pool_rep = EnrichedPooling(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n        pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n\n        # Expert B: BiGRU on DSConv features\n        rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim, self.pre_norm)(h)\n        rnn_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n        # Fusion\n        if self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n            logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (2,))\n            w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n            fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n        elif self.fusion == 'avg':\n            fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown fusion: {self.fusion}\")\n\n        if self.post_norm:\n            fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n\
    \n        # Head\n        z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused); z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n            return z.squeeze(-1)\n        return z\n\n# Fixed WrappedRNANetwork that uses the fixed DualExpertSharedBackbone\nclass WrappedRNANetworkFixed:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams=None):\n        h = hparams or {}\n        self.network = DualExpertSharedBackbone(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n            kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n            ds_dilations=tuple(h.get('ds_dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n            dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n            tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n            length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse',\
    \ True)),\n            gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n            fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n            pre_norm=bool(h.get('pre_norm', True)),\n            post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', True)),\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        from jax import random\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        from jax import random\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 256,\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n        'tau': 0.25,\n        'length_normalize_lse': True,\n        'gru_dim': 160,\n        'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n        'pre_norm': True,\n        'post_norm': True\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetworkFixed(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS=''\
    \ python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works\
    \ - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets\
    \ (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0106 |  0.4853  | 0.4853 \n 20  | 0.0027 |  0.3839  | 0.4853 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 20 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4853 Time:83s\n[Complete] CRI-On val_metric=0.48529077507549434\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.485291\nTraining time: 93s\n\nStarting RNA training on\
    \ CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0733  | 0.0752 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 19 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0752 Time:151s\n[Complete] CRI-Off val_metric=0.07520755254339502\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.075208\nTraining time: 162s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0934 |  0.8779  | 0.9013\
