tick: 369
role: model
parts:
- text: "Fixing the DSConv dilation bug, then resubmitting enriched-pooling analysis runs (h=256 seed=7; width=192 seed=123).\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_enriched.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Dual-expert with shared DSConv backbone and enriched pooling:\n  - Shared DSConv (5 blocks, dilations [1,2,4,8,16])\n  - Enriched pooling stats over sequence: mean, max, LSE(τ), std; channel-wise learned softmax mix (minimal params)\n  - Expert A: Enriched pooled DSConv features\n  - Expert B: BiGRU(=gru_dim) on DSConv features (bidirectional), projected to hidden_dim\n  - Fusion: scalar gate (softmax over 2 experts), optional pre/post LayerNorm\n  - Defaults: dropout=0.10, τ=0.25 with length normalization\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau=0.25,\
    \ length_normalize=True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = x\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          # depthwise dilated conv (FIX: kernel_dilation instead of dilation)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME')(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n   \
    \       # pointwise conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # 1x1 embedding to hidden_dim\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          return h  # (B, L, H)\n\n  class EnrichedPooling(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      pre_norm: bool = False\n      eps: float = 1e-6\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool\
    \ = True):\n          # h: (B, L, H)\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)            # (B, H)\n          lse_pool  = _lse_pool(h, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)  # (B, H)\n          max_pool  = jnp.max(h, axis=1)             # (B, H)\n          var_pool  = jnp.var(h, axis=1)\n          std_pool  = jnp.sqrt(var_pool + self.eps)  # (B, H)\n          stats = jnp.stack([mean_pool, lse_pool, max_pool, std_pool], axis=-1)  # (B, H, 4)\n\n          # Channel-wise learned mix over 4 stats\n          logits = self.param('mix_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (self.hidden_dim, 4))\n          w = jax.nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)  # (H, 4)\n          w = jnp.expand_dims(w, axis=0)       # (1, H, 4)\n          mixed = jnp.sum(stats * w, axis=-1)  # (B, H)\n          return mixed\n\n  class BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim:\
    \ int\n      pre_norm: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(x)\n          f = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hf = f(x)[:, -1, :]\n          b = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hb = b(jnp.flip(x, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n          return jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)\n\n  class DualExpertSharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      gru_dim: int = 160\n      fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      post_norm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations,\
    \ self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(x, deterministic)\n          pool_rep = EnrichedPooling(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n          rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim, self.pre_norm)(h)\n          rnn_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n          if self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n              logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n              fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n          elif self.fusion == 'avg':\n              fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown fusion: {self.fusion}\")\n          if self.post_norm:\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused); z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return z.squeeze(-1)\n          return z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n          self.network = DualExpertSharedBackbone(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(h.get('ds_dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n              fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n              pre_norm=bool(h.get('pre_norm', True)),\n         \
    \     post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', True)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n\
    ```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Enriched Pooling cw-mix (mean/max/LSE/std) — h=256 — seed=7 + mix-weight analysis\"\ntags: \"dsconv, enriched-pooling, cw-mix, analysis, shared-backbone\"\nabstract: \"Shared-backbone DSConv with enriched pooling (channel-wise learned mix over mean, max, LSE τ=0.25 len-norm, std) and BiGRU(160). Adds complete()-time analysis to save learned stat weights per dataset.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, csv\n  import numpy as np\n  import optax\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from flax import traverse_util\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_enriched import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim':\
    \ 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def _save_mix_analysis(params, dataset, seed):\n      flat = traverse_util.flatten_dict(params, sep='/')\n      target = None\n      for k, v in flat.items():\n          if k.endswith('EnrichedPooling_0/mix_logits') or k.endswith('/mix_logits'):\n              target = v\n              if 'EnrichedPooling' in k:\n                  break\n      if target is None:\n          return False\n      w = jax.nn.softmax(jnp.asarray(target), axis=-1)  # (H,4)\n      w_np = np.array(w)\n      mean_w =\
    \ w_np.mean(axis=0)  # [mean, lse, max, std]\n      top_idx = np.argmax(w_np, axis=-1)\n      fracs = np.array([(top_idx == s).mean() for s in range(4)])\n\n      os.makedirs('storage/noema/results', exist_ok=True)\n      path = f'storage/noema/results/enriched_mix_weights_{dataset}_seed{seed}.csv'\n      with open(path, 'w', newline='') as f:\n          writer = csv.writer(f)\n          writer.writerow(['stat', 'mean_weight', 'top1_fraction'])\n          for name, mw, fr in zip(['mean','lse','max','std'], mean_w.tolist(), fracs.tolist()):\n              writer.writerow([name, f'{mw:.6f}', f'{fr:.6f}'])\n      return True\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); seed = trial_data.get('seed'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      ok = False\n      try:\n          ok = _save_mix_analysis(params, ds, seed)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"[Analysis] Failed for {ds} (seed={seed}): {e}\")\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds}\
    \ val_metric={vm} | mix_analysis_saved={ok}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Enriched Pooling cw-mix — width=192 (param-reduced) — seed=123 + mix-weight analysis\"\ntags: \"dsconv, enriched-pooling, parameter-reduction, cw-mix, analysis\"\nabstract: \"Parameter-reduced (hidden_dim=192) variant with enriched pooling cw-mix and BiGRU(160). Adds complete()-time analysis to save learned stat weights per dataset.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, csv\n  import numpy as np\n  import optax\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from flax import traverse_util\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_enriched import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 192,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n  \
    \        'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def _save_mix_analysis(params, dataset, seed):\n      flat = traverse_util.flatten_dict(params, sep='/')\n      target = None\n      for k, v in flat.items():\n          if k.endswith('EnrichedPooling_0/mix_logits') or k.endswith('/mix_logits'):\n              target = v\n              if 'EnrichedPooling' in k:\n                  break\n      if target is None:\n          return False\n      w = jax.nn.softmax(jnp.asarray(target), axis=-1)\n      w_np = np.array(w)\n     \
    \ mean_w = w_np.mean(axis=0)\n      top_idx = np.argmax(w_np, axis=-1)\n      fracs = np.array([(top_idx == s).mean() for s in range(4)])\n\n      os.makedirs('storage/noema/results', exist_ok=True)\n      path = f'storage/noema/results/enriched_mix_weights_{dataset}_seed{seed}.csv'\n      with open(path, 'w', newline='') as f:\n          writer = csv.writer(f)\n          writer.writerow(['stat', 'mean_weight', 'top1_fraction'])\n          for name, mw, fr in zip(['mean','lse','max','std'], mean_w.tolist(), frs.tolist()):\n              writer.writerow([name, f'{mw:.6f}', f'{fr:.6f}'])\n      return True\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); seed = trial_data.get('seed'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      ok = False\n      try:\n          ok = _save_mix_analysis(params, ds, seed)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"[Analysis] Failed for {ds} (seed={seed}): {e}\")\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm} |\
    \ mix_analysis_saved={ok}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/enriched_pooling_plan.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 369 — Enriched Pooling status\n  - Fixed DSConv dilation param (kernel_dilation) in enriched backbone file to prevent future debugger rewrites.\n  - 558 (h=256, seed=42) scored 0.6730: MRL 0.9013 (↑), APA 0.8572 (↑), CRI-On 0.4853 (≈), PRS 0.5466 (↓). Net ~neutral vs default mean 0.6729.\n  - Resubmitted analysis runs:\n    • h=256, seed=7 — saves enriched_mix_weights_{dataset}_seed7.csv\n    • h=192, seed=123 — saves enriched_mix_weights_{dataset}_seed123.csv\n  Next:\n  - If h=256 enriched shows consistent gains (≥0.678 tri-seed), tri-seed and integrate; else retain default pooling and report pooling-weight insights as analysis.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating model responses**


  I need to generate a response and continue with our actions. Right now, we submitted enriched pooling models: one failed due to a dilation parameter error, while the other succeeded after the automatic debugger fixed the kernel_dilation name. It produced a score of 0.672958, matching our default. The other variant failed validation for the same issue. It seems like the debugger only engaged for the successful model, which is puzzling. I expected it to run normally for both.**Reviewing debugging process**


  The debug note indicates that the debugger can’t modify files in lineage. It created a new submission_v2, but for the 559 submission, we used dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_enriched directly. I’m considering whether to resubmit 559 with fixed code or update our enriched module file to change dilation to kernel_dilation. We also queued analysis runs but had some blocks due to pending evaluations. Now that we can proceed, I see that submission 558 succeeded, while 559 failed. The metrics show potential improvements, though 558 didn’t significantly exceed the default mean.**Planning enriched pooling updates**


  It seems like the enriched pooling is somewhat neutral, but we’re seeing improvements in the MRL. I’ll fix our enriched file to use kernel_dilation and include cw-mix analysis parameters, which should compile afterward. After I update the file content, we can resubmit the width=192 model with the necessary analysis. I’m considering using tri-seeding with h=256 if we see further improvements but might hold off until we have more evidence. I’ll ensure to manage cooldown and concurrency, as we currently have no running experiments and can submit two now.**Preparing analysis resubmission**


  We previously submitted two analysis-run submissions, but they were blocked. Now we can resubmit for h=256 with seed=7 and width=192 with seed=42. However, 558 already utilized h=256 with seed=42, so I’m considering running the seed=7 analysis on h=256 and resubmitting the fixed width=192 with seed=123. Since we can make two submissions, I''ll also log the results and update any archives later. Additionally, I’ll fix the kernel_dilation parameter in the enriched module code and refine the "dilation" field in DSConvBlock. Lastly, I’ll adjust the cw-mix parameter shape for EnrichedPooling.**Implementing updates for analysis runs**


  I’m considering a potential improvement by ensuring that the BiGRU uses DSConv features. We also need to verify that the CLIP schedule is in order and maintain consistent hyperparameters. After resubmission, I might analyze mixing weights across datasets and log the top weights. For our upcoming actions, I''ll update the enriched module to fix the kernel_dilation parameter and then resubmit the h=256 seed=7 analysis-run, along with the width=192 seed=123 analysis-run. I’ll also ensure all YAML content is formatted safely and efficiently, keeping things concise.'
