tick: 373
role: model
parts:
- text: "Implementing a Channel Squeeze-and-Excitation (SE) calibration on the shared DSConv backbone to boost motif selectivity before pooling and BiGRU. Submitting two seeds.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Dual-expert with shared DSConv backbone + Channel SE calibration + mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU + scalar-gated fusion.\n  Goal: improve cross-task average by channel-wise feature calibration prior to pooling/RNN.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau=0.25, length_normalize=True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n\
    \      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = x\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          # depthwise dilated conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME')(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          # pointwise conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate:\
    \ float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          return h  # (B, L, H)\n\n  class ChannelSE(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      reduction: int = 4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x: (B, L, H)\n          g = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)                 # (B, H)\n          r = max(1, self.hidden_dim // self.reduction)\n          g = nn.Dense(r)(g); g = jax.nn.gelu(g)\n          g = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(g); g = jax.nn.sigmoid(g)  # (B, H)\n          g = g[:, None, :]                        # (B, 1, H)\n          return x * g\n\n  class MeanLSEPooling(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      tau: float = 0.25\n\
    \      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          lse_pool = _lse_pool(h, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          logits = self.param('mix_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (2,))\n          w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n          return w[0] * mean_pool + w[1] * lse_pool\n\n  class BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim: int\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(x)\n          f = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hf = f(x)[:, -1, :]\n          b = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hb = b(jnp.flip(x, axis=1))[:,\
    \ -1, :]\n          return jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)\n\n  class DualExpertSharedBackboneSE(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      gru_dim: int = 160\n      fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      post_norm: bool = True\n      se_reduction: int = 4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(x, deterministic)\n          h = ChannelSE(self.hidden_dim, self.se_reduction)(h)\n\n          pool_rep = MeanLSEPooling(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n\
    \n          rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim, self.pre_norm)(h)\n          rnn_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n          if self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n              logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n              fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n          else:\n              fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n\n          if self.post_norm:\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused); z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return z.squeeze(-1)\n          return z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n  \
    \        self.network = DualExpertSharedBackboneSE(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(h.get('ds_dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n              fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n              pre_norm=bool(h.get('pre_norm', True)),\n              post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', True)),\n              se_reduction=int(h.get('se_reduction', 4)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input,\
    \ deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SE-calibrated shared DSConv + mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU(160), scalar gate — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, logsumexp, bigru, gating, calibration\"\nabstract: \"Adds Channel SE on the shared\
    \ DSConv backbone to calibrate channel salience before pooling and BiGRU. Retains learned mix(mean, LSE τ=0.25 len-norm), scalar-gated fusion, pre/post-LN, and clip via optimizer chain.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:\
    \ float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SE-calibrated shared DSConv + mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU(160), scalar gate — seed=123\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, logsumexp, bigru, gating, calibration, stability\"\nabstract: \"Replica with BASE_SEED=123 to assess stability of Channel SE calibration effects on cross-dataset average.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim':\
    \ 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update (Tick 373)\n  New probe: Channel\
    \ Squeeze-and-Excitation (SE) on shared DSConv backbone.\n  Rationale: calibrate motif-channel salience prior to pooling/RNN to improve CRI-On/PRS without hurting MRL/APA.\n  Submissions:\n  - SE + mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU(160), scalar gate: seeds {42, 123} queued.\n  Notes:\n  - Keeps <1M params; minimal overhead (2-layer SE with reduction=4).\n  - If SE tri-seed ≥0.678 mean without regressions, consider adopting; else retain current default and report SE as negative/neutral result.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning next steps in the Token Management Room**


  I’m considering our next moves after pruning ticks 360-366 and entering cooldown. We’ve aggregated enrichment results and the SOTA scoreboard shows a new record of 0.6935 by Veritas II with task-specific heads. Our current method is around 0.673–0.675, which is an improvement from previous attempts. I’m thinking we could aim for modest improvements to reach 0.68, possibly by adding task-specific heads while keeping the core architecture consistent across datasets.**Evaluating task-specific heads in submissions**


  I’m pondering the use of "task-specific heads." The scoreboard reveals that submissions using these heads managed a score of 0.6935 by Veritas II. Yet, the guidelines clarify that final layers can be tailored for prediction types but not for datasets. Task-specific heads for each dataset might not be allowed, but they’re appearing in accepted submissions. There’s a chance they’re permissible if structured correctly, but I want to avoid any risk of disqualification!**Proposing improvements for gating**


  I’m considering some potential improvements, like swapping the scalar gate for per-task gating weights. I wonder if gating per dataset is allowed, as it would change with each training dataset. That should be fine since each training is separate but keeps the architecture consistent. I could also propose using learned FiLM gating before pooling, keeping it minimal. Our focus should be on closing the performance gaps, especially in CRI-On and PRS. The differences to SOTA are small, so we need to strategize carefully to optimize our scores.**Analyzing improvements for CRI-Off performance**


  I’ve noticed the new SOTA at 562, with CRI-Off jumping to 0.1365 due to "task-specific heads." This shows a considerable gap compared to our own performance, as the difference is about 0.05. To enhance CRI-Off and CRI-On tasks, I’m thinking of using pairwise interaction modeling for CRI-Off. It might help to add an explicit channel for pairwise mismatches. Although our input shape is constrained, I could consider embedding base pairs and including complement channels before convolution, keeping everything consistent with the network architecture.**Implementing the network structure**


  I’m working on adding dropout for generalization, passing the output from DSConvBackbone through an SEBlock to produce scaled features. I need to ensure the dimensions are correct all along the way and maintain a structured workflow for pooling and RNN feeding. I’m thinking of using a simplified mean-LSE mix aggregator for flexibility while considering the incorporation of enriched pooling. I’ll implement this alongside the two submission runs. Additionally, I’ll update our summary and create the necessary file while ensuring code quality and clarity!'
