tick: 374
role: model
parts:
- text: "Preparing a boundary-agnostic bi-window pooling variant to target CRI-Off while remaining universal. Staging code and plan (will submit after SE runs 569/570 finish).\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_biwindow.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Dual-expert with shared DSConv backbone + Bi-Window mean↔LSE cw-mix pooling + BiGRU + scalar-gated fusion.\n  Universal design: split sequence into equal halves for pooling on all datasets (no dataset-specific logic).\n  Goal: improve CRI-Off via half-wise pooling while preserving APA/MRL; keep <1M params.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau=0.25, length_normalize=True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L,\
    \ dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = x\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME')(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n     \
    \ dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          return h  # (B, L, H)\n\n  class BiWindowPooling(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # h: (B, L, H)\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          L = h.shape[1]\n          mid = jnp.maximum(L // 2, 1)\n          h1 = h[:, :mid, :]\n          h2 = h[:, mid:, :] if mid < L else h[:,\
    \ :mid, :]  # fallback to avoid empty\n          m1 = jnp.mean(h1, axis=1); l1 = _lse_pool(h1, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          m2 = jnp.mean(h2, axis=1); l2 = _lse_pool(h2, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          stats = jnp.stack([m1, l1, m2, l2], axis=-1)  # (B, H, 4)\n          logits = self.param('mix_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (self.hidden_dim, 4))\n          w = jax.nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)  # (H, 4)\n          w = jnp.expand_dims(w, axis=0)       # (1, H, 4)\n          mixed = jnp.sum(stats * w, axis=-1)  # (B, H)\n          return mixed\n\n  class BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim: int\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(x)\n          f = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hf = f(x)[:, -1, :]\n          b = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hb = b(jnp.flip(x, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n\
    \          return jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)\n\n  class DualExpertSharedBackboneBiWindow(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      gru_dim: int = 160\n      fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      post_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(x, deterministic)\n          pool_rep = BiWindowPooling(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n          rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim, self.pre_norm)(h)\n          rnn_proj\
    \ = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n          if self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n              logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n              fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n          else:\n              fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n          if self.post_norm:\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused); z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return z.squeeze(-1)\n          return z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n          self.network = DualExpertSharedBackboneBiWindow(\n              d_output=d_output,\n\
    \              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(h.get('ds_dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n              fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n              pre_norm=bool(h.get('pre_norm', True)),\n              post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', True)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n\
    \              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/biwindow_plan.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 374 — Bi-Window Pooling Plan\n  Motivation: CRI-Off gap (our ~0.08 vs best 0.1365) likely benefits from modeling interactions across concatenated halves. To stay dataset-agnostic, apply equal-halves pooling on all datasets.\n  Method: After shared DSConv, split sequence at L//2 and compute mean & LSE(τ=0.25,len-norm) per half; channel-wise\
    \ softmax mix over [mean1,lse1,mean2,lse2]; fuse with BiGRU via scalar gate; clip=1.0.\n  Next: Submit seeds {42,123} when SE runs (569/570) finish. Success criterion: ≥0.678 average without regressions; specifically target CRI-Off ↑ while keeping APA/MRL high and ncRNA stable.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering results aggregation**\n\nI’m thinking about creating a results aggregator for best-of and preparing the next steps. If SE doesn’t improve, I might propose using \"pairwise gated interaction for concatenation segments.\" It seems we can't determine boundaries just from the code, especially since dataset lengths vary. For instance, I see that for CRI-Off, the sequence length is 46, likely split in half at 23. Implementing a \"boundary-aware convolution\" could involve adding gating for cross-boundary pairs, computing features, and pooling stats separately for each half.**Exploring dataset-specific methods**\n\nI realize I need to be cautious about dataset-specific logic. The codex warns against using methods tailored to just one dataset, like CRI-Off, which would go against the rules. Instead, I might propose a \"two-window pooling\" approach that applies to all datasets. This could help CRI-Off without negatively affecting others. I think, \"bi-window enriched\
  \ pooling\" could compute stats for each half separately and consider cross-differences. It may also benefit CRI-On! We can implement this while ensuring it works across all datasets. Plus, we already have some solutions running, so I should prepare for submission now.**Managing tokens and pooling strategies**\n\nI need to keep track of tokens and possibly make some private memory notes while planning. I also want to connect this to \"task-aware pooling.\" The tri-seeds 535/536/539 with pre-LN ON improved CRI-On to 0.5050, which is better than the current SOTA for Veritas II at 0.4910. Our focus should be on improving CRI-Off since our current performance is 0.08 compared to SOTA's 0.1365. So implementing a universal \"bi-window pooling\" could help. After the DSConv backbone, I’d compute four statistics per half and consider using gating weights to minimize parameters.**Simplifying stats computation**\n\nI think we can simplify our approach by calculating the mean and LSE for both halves\
  \ and then combining them using learned per-channel mixing. For each channel, I’d produce weights based on four stats, using shapes like (H, 4*2). Each half will yield two stats (mean and LSE), and optionally I can include max and std, which would mean 4 or 8 dimensions per channel for mixing. However, to keep it minimal, I’ll stick to just the mean and LSE, resulting in 4 dimensions. I want to implement a \"bi-window mean + LSE channel-wise mix\" variant with a scalar gate.**Planning implementation steps**\n\nI'm setting tau to 0.25 for length normalization and plan to manage concurrent tasks. I want to write a submission file for the dual expert model with a DSConv backbone and BiWindowPooling that integrates a channel-wise mix from calculated means and LSEs. Right now, I'll write this code but hold off on submissions since we're hitting our limit with two concurrent tasks running. \n\nI'll also log our plans and prepare to clean up a bug in our analysis variant without rushing. Overall,\
  \ I'll focus on code preparation over submission right now, then craft a final brief message."
