tick: 375
role: model
parts:
- text: "Submitting the bi-window pooling variant (seeds 42, 123), then logging SE results and the new plan.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Shared-backbone DSConv + Bi-Window mean/LSE cw-mix + BiGRU(160), scalar gate — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, bi-window, logsumexp, bigru, gating\"\nabstract: \"Bi-window pooling splits the DSConv features into equal halves and computes mean and LSE(τ=0.25, len-norm) per half with channel-wise learned soft mix over [mean1,lse1,mean2,lse2]. Fused with BiGRU via scalar gate. Universal across datasets; aims to improve CRI-Off while keeping APA/MRL strong.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_biwindow import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n  \
    \        'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Shared-backbone DSConv + Bi-Window mean/LSE cw-mix + BiGRU(160), scalar gate — seed=123\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, bi-window, logsumexp, bigru, gating\"\n\
    abstract: \"Replication of bi-window pooling with BASE_SEED=123 to assess stability. Universal equal-halves pooling; channel-wise learned soft mix over [mean1,lse1,mean2,lse2].\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_biwindow import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return\
    \ optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update (Tick 375)\n  Channel SE calibration (shared backbone) results:\n  - 569 (seed=42): 0.6756 | APA 0.8556 | CRI-Off 0.0798 | Modif 0.9500 | CRI-On 0.5034 | PRS 0.5545 | MRL 0.8968 | ncRNA 0.8892\n  - 570 (seed=123): 0.6727 | APA 0.8587 | CRI-Off 0.0806 | Modif 0.9504 | CRI-On 0.4806 | PRS 0.5579 | MRL 0.8959 | ncRNA 0.8846\n  Observations:\n  - SE improves CRI-On (peak 0.5034) and PRS (~0.556), maintains APA/MRL strong; average ~0.674 (↑ vs 0.6729 baseline).\n  Next step:\n  - Submitted Bi-Window pooling (IDs pending): equal-halves mean/LSE cw-mix to target CRI-Off while\
    \ preserving APA/MRL. Criteria: ≥0.678 avg and CRI-Off ↑ without regressions. If positive, tri-seed and consider adoption; else record as negative/neutral.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Preparing for code review**\n\nI need to think about potential issues, like missing the path to a module—we used sys.path for that earlier, and we included build_network. It's important to ensure that this file defines build_network. The create_optimizer function uses optax, so I'll need to import optax in the submission code too. Also, I'll summarize the SE results in 'dual_expert_summary.md' carefully. Titles may have special characters like \"↔\", but to be safe, I might use ASCII versions instead. Quoting in YAML is recommended, so I’ll do that. Finally, I'll ensure to submit for seeds 42 and 123, limiting it to two submissions maximum.**Crafting submission scripts**\n\nI need to create content for my submission scripts, similar to what I've done before. I'll start by importing sys and optax, then add the storage path for submissions. I'll import build_network from the shared backbone file. \n\nNext, I’ll define BASE_SEED and a dictionary for _define_hyperparameters.\
  \ Additionally, I’ll outline the create_network and create_optimizer functions, using clip and adamw. It's essential to print validation metrics too. While I might consider implementing 'analysis saving', it’s not necessary right now. I should avoid extra runs and quickly update the Archive addendum—keeping it minimal is wise."
