parts:
- text: "Bi-Window failed due to JAX dynamic slicing. I’ll fix the mid-split to use static Python ints, then resubmit both seeds.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_biwindow.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Dual-expert with shared DSConv backbone + Bi-Window mean↔LSE cw-mix pooling + BiGRU + scalar-gated fusion.\n  Universal design: split sequence into equal halves for pooling on all datasets (no dataset-specific logic).\n  Goal: improve CRI-Off via half-wise pooling while preserving APA/MRL; keep <1M params.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau=0.25, length_normalize=True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L,\
    \ dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = x\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME')(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n     \
    \ dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          return h  # (B, L, H)\n\n  class BiWindowPooling(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # h: (B, L, H)\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          # Use static Python ints for slicing to satisfy JAX jit constraints\n          L = h.shape[1]\n          mid = L // 2\n          if mid\
    \ < 1:\n              mid = 1\n          h1 = h[:, :mid, :]\n          h2 = h[:, mid:, :] if mid < L else h[:, :mid, :]\n\n          m1 = jnp.mean(h1, axis=1); l1 = _lse_pool(h1, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          m2 = jnp.mean(h2, axis=1); l2 = _lse_pool(h2, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          stats = jnp.stack([m1, l1, m2, l2], axis=-1)  # (B, H, 4)\n\n          logits = self.param('mix_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (self.hidden_dim, 4))\n          w = jax.nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)  # (H, 4)\n          w = jnp.expand_dims(w, axis=0)       # (1, H, 4)\n          mixed = jnp.sum(stats * w, axis=-1)  # (B, H)\n          return mixed\n\n  class BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim: int\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(x)\n          f = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hf = f(x)[:, -1, :]\n          b = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n\
    \          hb = b(jnp.flip(x, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n          return jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)\n\n  class DualExpertSharedBackboneBiWindow(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      gru_dim: int = 160\n      fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      post_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(x, deterministic)\n          pool_rep = BiWindowPooling(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n          rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim,\
    \ self.pre_norm)(h)\n          rnn_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n          if self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n              logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n              fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n          else:\n              fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n          if self.post_norm:\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused); z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return z.squeeze(-1)\n          return z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n          self.network = DualExpertSharedBackboneBiWindow(\n\
    \              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(h.get('ds_dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n              fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n              pre_norm=bool(h.get('pre_norm', True)),\n              post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', True)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True,\
    \ rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Shared-backbone DSConv + Bi-Window mean/LSE cw-mix + BiGRU(160), scalar gate — seed=42 (fixed static split)\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, bi-window, logsumexp, bigru, gating\"\nabstract: \"Fix JAX dynamic-slice by using static Python-int mid for equal-halves pooling. Channel-wise soft mix over [mean1,lse1,mean2,lse2], fused with\
    \ BiGRU via scalar gate.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_biwindow import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params,\
    \ opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Shared-backbone DSConv + Bi-Window mean/LSE cw-mix + BiGRU(160), scalar gate — seed=123 (fixed static split)\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, bi-window, logsumexp, bigru, gating\"\nabstract: \"Fixed static mid split for equal-halves pooling to satisfy JAX jit. Replication with BASE_SEED=123.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_biwindow import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion':\
    \ 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/biwindow_plan.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 377 — Bi-Window fix + resubmission\n  - Root cause: JAX dynamic slice with jnp-derived mid; fix: compute mid via Python ints from h.shape[1] (static) and slice with static indices.\n  - Resubmitted seeds {42,123}. Success criteria unchanged: ≥0.678 average with CRI-Off ↑, no APA/MRL regressions. If neutral/negative,\
    \ record and proceed with SE default and alternate universal splits (quarters or even/odd) if needed.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating sequence lengths**\n\nI'm thinking that `slice_size` should actually be a static integer to handle variable lengths across batches, since the `seq_len` is static known per dataset, like `max_seq_len`. If we pad to a fixed length, `L` would also be static. But there's an error indicating `L` is dynamic. It seems that JAX can return abstract shape dimensions. To avoid the issue, maybe I should predefine `mid` using `h.shape[1]` where `nn.static_slice` is applied.**Fixing the slicing issue**\n\nI'm considering another approach: splitting into two fixed windows using slicing with a constant index of 0. I can utilize `jax.lax.slice` with endpoints that depend on `L`, which I can compute using `h.shape[1]`. In Flax under JIT, `x.shape` returns static shape constants. The issue seems to stem from `L = h.shape[1]` and how `mid` is calculated. To resolve it, I can compute `mid` directly as an integer, ensuring static slicing works properly. Using Python math, I can\
  \ set `mid = (h.shape[1] // 2)` and ensure it’s at least 1.**Updating the code for mid computation**\n\nI think we need to update `dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_biwindow.py` to calculate `mid` as a Python integer: `L = h.shape[1]; mid = max(1, L // 2)`, avoiding any `jnp.*` operations. Slicing with a static `mid` should work fine. The second path uses `h2`, and for odd `L`, the second window will have a length of `L - mid`. After this fix, we should resubmit with seeds. Additionally, we can implement a dynamic fix using `lax.dynamic_slice` if necessary, but sticking with the static approach is simpler. We'll make sure `h.shape[1]` is an integer for consistency.**Implementing robust code**\n\nI'm planning to write more robust code for the `BiWindowPooling` class. First, I'll set `L = h.shape[1]`. If `L` isn't an integer, I'll compute `mid` by casting `L` to an integer with `int(L)` since JAX might return a variable type here. Then, I will define `mid` as `max(1, L // 2)`. I'll also\
  \ ensure that `h1` and `h2` are sliced correctly. Finally, I’ll update the storage write to fix the code and note that I’ll resubmit both seeds while logging this fix for clarity.**Finalizing code adjustments and commands**\n\nIn JAX, dimension shapes are static at compile time, which is good for safety, but I could also consider dynamic slicing using `jnp.split`. However, since it requires static indices, maybe I should stick with static integers instead to avoid risks. I want to fix the code using static values for `L` and `mid`, then proceed with commands like executing actions, writing updates to the storage, and resubmitting both seeds. We’ll also generate the YAML and note the bug fix in the results summary. \n\nI'll structure the commands!"
