parts:
- text: "Bi-Window fix submitted. Preparing an interleaved even/odd pooling variant (static slices, safe for JAX) to target CRI-Off while remaining universal. I’ll stage code and a plan, and submit after 576/577 complete.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_evenodd.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Dual-expert with shared DSConv backbone + Even/Odd mean↔LSE cw-mix pooling + BiGRU + scalar-gated fusion.\n  Universal design: split DSConv features into even/odd positions; compute mean and LSE(τ=0.25, len-norm) per stream;\n  channel-wise learned soft mix over [mean_even, lse_even, mean_odd, lse_odd]. Safe for JAX (static slices).\n  Goal: improve CRI-Off while preserving APA/MRL; keep <1M params.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau=0.25, length_normalize=True):\n\
    \      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = x\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME')(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n         \
    \ return x + h\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          return h  # (B, L, H)\n\n  class EvenOddPooling(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # h: (B, L, H)\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n   \
    \       L = h.shape[1]  # static Python int\n          if L == 1:\n              he = h  # only even stream exists; mirror for odd to avoid empty slice\n              ho = h\n          else:\n              he = h[:, 0::2, :]\n              ho = h[:, 1::2, :]\n\n          me = jnp.mean(he, axis=1); le = _lse_pool(he, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          mo = jnp.mean(ho, axis=1); lo = _lse_pool(ho, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n\n          stats = jnp.stack([me, le, mo, lo], axis=-1)  # (B, H, 4)\n          logits = self.param('mix_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (self.hidden_dim, 4))\n          w = jax.nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)  # (H, 4)\n          w = jnp.expand_dims(w, axis=0)       # (1, H, 4)\n          mixed = jnp.sum(stats * w, axis=-1)  # (B, H)\n          return mixed\n\n  class BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim: int\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              x\
    \ = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(x)\n          f = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hf = f(x)[:, -1, :]\n          b = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hb = b(jnp.flip(x, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n          return jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)\n\n  class DualExpertSharedBackboneEvenOdd(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      gru_dim: int = 160\n      fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      post_norm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(x, deterministic)\n          pool_rep = EvenOddPooling(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate,\
    \ self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n          rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim, self.pre_norm)(h)\n          rnn_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n          if self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n              logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n              fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n          else:\n              fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n\n          if self.post_norm:\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused); z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return z.squeeze(-1)\n          return z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n\
    \      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n          self.network = DualExpertSharedBackboneEvenOdd(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(h.get('ds_dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n              fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n              pre_norm=bool(h.get('pre_norm', True)),\n              post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', True)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params':\
    \ params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/evenodd_plan.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 378 — Even/Odd Pooling Plan\n  Motivation: CRI-Off benefits from modeling cross-position interactions. Even/odd interleaving\
    \ is universal and static-slice safe for JAX, avoiding dynamic index issues.\n  Method: After shared DSConv, split by parity: h[:,0::2,:], h[:,1::2,:]; compute mean+LSE(τ=0.25,len-norm) per stream; channel-wise soft mix over [mean_even,lse_even,mean_odd,lse_odd]; fuse with BiGRU via scalar gate; clip=1.0.\n  Status: Code staged. Will submit seeds {42,123} after Bi-Window fixed runs (576/577) finish. Adoption criteria as before: ≥0.678 avg with CRI-Off ↑ and no APA/MRL regressions; otherwise record as neutral/negative and keep SE default.\n```\n\nIf you prefer, I can also tri-seed the SE-calibrated default to lock stability once current runs complete."
thinking_content: '**Considering JAX slicing strategies**


  I need to be careful to avoid dynamic indexing in JAX by using h[:, ::2, :] and h[:, 1::2, :]. It’s essential to include code to handle cases when L is 1 or odd, as the odd slice could end up empty. I should implement checks since applying jnp.mean on empty results could cause errors. If the second slice has zero length, I’ll fallback to an equal slice. I guess I need to ensure safe computations for both even and odd lengths.**Handling JIT in JAX**


  I’m noticing that handling shapes inside JIT requires them to be static and not dependent on values. The shape for h[:, 1::2, :] needs to be determined at compile time, and if L is 1, that could result in a zero-length dimension. Since JAX needs static dimensions known at compile time, I can''t perform operations like mean on a size 0 slice without running into NaNs or errors. Instead, I should define pooling operations based on whether L is even or odd. I may need to pad a zero row if necessary for the odd case.**Determining slice behavior based on L**


  I’m examining the variable L, which comes from the shape of h. I can set L = h.shape[1]. If L is even, I can define an odd slice using h[:, 1::2, :]. For odd lengths, since L could be at least 1, I’ll ensure that it yields a floor value with at least one element. If L equals 1, I can duplicate values from the even slice instead and create constant branches in my Python code at initialization. This way, I can avoid empty slices and prepare my code properly.'
