parts:
- text: "Bi-Window shows a single-seed peak (0.6788) but not stable; proceeding with Even/Odd pooling submissions and tri-seeding SE to lock stability.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Shared-backbone DSConv + Even/Odd mean/LSE cw-mix + BiGRU(160), scalar gate — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, even-odd, logsumexp, bigru, gating\"\nabstract: \"Even/Odd interleaved pooling: split DSConv features by parity and compute mean and LSE(τ=0.25, len-norm) per stream with channel-wise learned soft mix over [mean_even, lse_even, mean_odd, lse_odd]. Fused with BiGRU via scalar gate. Universal and JAX-safe; targets CRI-Off while preserving APA/MRL.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_evenodd import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n\
    \          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Shared-backbone DSConv + Even/Odd mean/LSE cw-mix + BiGRU(160), scalar gate — seed=123\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, even-odd, logsumexp, bigru, gating, stability\"\
    \nabstract: \"Replication of Even/Odd interleaved pooling (seed=123) to assess stability. Universal design with channel-wise learned soft mix and scalar-gated fusion.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_evenodd import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n\
    \          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SE-calibrated shared DSConv + mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU(160), scalar gate — tri-seed (seed=7)\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, logsumexp, bigru, gating\"\nabstract: \"Tri-seed completion for SE-calibrated shared-backbone model to lock stability. Prior seeds: 42=0.6756, 123=0.6727. This run uses BASE_SEED=7.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size':\
    \ 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update (Tick 379)\n  Bi-Window pooling (equal halves):\n  - 576 (seed=42):\
    \ 0.6788 | APA 0.8628 | CRI-Off 0.0781 | Modif 0.9510 | CRI-On 0.5177 | PRS 0.5515 | MRL 0.8940 | ncRNA 0.8969\n  - 577 (seed=123): 0.6681 | APA 0.8574 | CRI-Off 0.0757 | Modif 0.9509 | CRI-On 0.4459 | PRS 0.5615 | MRL 0.8974 | ncRNA 0.8877\n  Observation: single-seed peak ≥0.678 but not stable; CRI-Off unchanged (~0.076–0.078).\n\n  Actions:\n  - Submitted Even/Odd interleaved pooling (channel-wise soft mix over {mean_even, lse_even, mean_odd, lse_odd}) — seeds {42,123} — to target CRI-Off while staying universal and JAX-safe.\n  - Tri-seeding SE-calibrated default (seed=7) to lock stability (prior: 42=0.6756, 123=0.6727).\n\n  Decision logic:\n  - Prefer SE-calibrated shared backbone as default unless an alternative pooling achieves ≥0.678 tri-seed mean without regressions and shows consistent CRI-Off gains.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning model submissions**\n\nI'm considering ways to improve our gating approach, like proposing a stronger gating MLP or keeping the scalar gate. I think even/odd pooling could benefit the CRI-Off and I'm planning to submit seeds. It sounds good to include gradient clipping and run a tri-seed with seed=7. I want to implement tiny On-Off dropout as an augmentation but can't change the training loop. \n\nI'll focus on submitting the even/odd pooling seeds and ensure everything is stored correctly. Let's make it happen!**Organizing submissions and plans**\n\nI’m planning to submit the even/odd pooling seeds, 42 and 123, and use our earlier created SE tri-seed submission code with seed=7. I also want to update the summary file with the bi-window results and consider logging a possible acceptance plan. If the even/odd approach doesn't improve CRI-Off, we might pivot to \"SE default\" as our final design.\n\nI’ll submit the YAML for seed 42 first and then proceed with\
  \ 123 and the tri-seed. Finally, I need to write updates in the dual_expert_summary. Let’s get started!**Finalizing actions**\n\nI'm contemplating whether we should compute a new \"best average\" orientation, but I think it's not essential right now. Instead, I want to focus on crafting a final message that lists our actions sequentially. I need to ensure that each `/execute_action` command appears on its own line, and I'll follow up with the necessary YAML if needed. \n\nLet's move forward and get this organized! Clearly laying things out should help make everything easier to follow."
