tick: 380
role: model
parts:
- text: "Reading Veritas II’s new paper for CRI-Off insights, then staging an even/odd cross-mix pooling variant (adds cross-stat interactions) to test after current runs finish.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{read 21}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_evenodd_xmix.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Dual-expert with shared DSConv backbone + Even/Odd mean↔LSE cross-mix pooling + BiGRU + scalar-gated fusion.\n  Universal design:\n    - Split DSConv features by parity (even/odd positions; static slices).\n    - Compute per-stream stats: mean_even, lse_even, mean_odd, lse_odd (LSE uses τ=0.25 with length normalization).\n    - Add interaction stats: mean_even*mean_odd, lse_even*lse_odd (per-channel Hadamard products) to capture co-activation.\n    - Channel-wise learned soft mix over 6 stats: [mean_e, lse_e, mean_o, lse_o, mean_e*mean_o, lse_e*lse_o].\n  Goal: improve CRI-Off via\
    \ generic interaction modeling while preserving APA/MRL; <1M params.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau=0.25, length_normalize=True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = x\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n\
    \                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME')(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  class EvenOddXMixPooling(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool\
    \ = True\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          L = h.shape[1]\n          if L == 1:\n              he = h\n              ho = h\n          else:\n              he = h[:, 0::2, :]\n              ho = h[:, 1::2, :]\n\n          me = jnp.mean(he, axis=1)\n          le = _lse_pool(he, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          mo = jnp.mean(ho, axis=1)\n          lo = _lse_pool(ho, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n\n          # Per-channel interaction terms (Hadamard)\n          mm = me * mo\n          ll = le * lo\n\n          # Stack stats: (B, H, 6)\n          stats = jnp.stack([me, le, mo, lo, mm, ll], axis=-1)\n\n          logits = self.param('mix_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (self.hidden_dim, 6))\n          w = jax.nn.softmax(logits,\
    \ axis=-1)   # (H, 6)\n          w = jnp.expand_dims(w, axis=0)        # (1, H, 6)\n          mixed = jnp.sum(stats * w, axis=-1)   # (B, H)\n          return mixed\n\n  class BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim: int\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(x)\n          f = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hf = f(x)[:, -1, :]\n          b = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hb = b(jnp.flip(x, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n          return jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)\n\n  class DualExpertSharedBackboneEvenOddXMix(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      gru_dim: int = 160\n      fusion: str = \"\
    scalar_gate\"\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      post_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(x, deterministic)\n          pool_rep = EvenOddXMixPooling(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n          rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim, self.pre_norm)(h)\n          rnn_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n          if self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n              logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n              fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n          else:\n              fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n\n          if self.post_norm:\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n\
    \n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused); z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return z.squeeze(-1)\n          return z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n          self.network = DualExpertSharedBackboneEvenOddXMix(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(h.get('ds_dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n            \
    \  gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n              fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n              pre_norm=bool(h.get('pre_norm', True)),\n              post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', True)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type,\
    \ hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/evenodd_xmix_plan.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 380 — Even/Odd Cross-Mix Pooling Plan\n  Rationale: Bi-Window showed a seed-42 peak (0.6788) but unstable and did not lift CRI-Off. Add generic interaction terms (mean_e*mean_o, lse_e*lse_o) to capture co-activation patterns that may matter for CRI-Off, without dataset-specific logic.\n  Design: channel-wise soft mix over 6 stats {mean_e, lse_e, mean_o, lse_o, mean_e*mean_o, lse_e*lse_o} on even/odd streams; fuse with BiGRU via scalar gate; clip=1.0. Universal and JAX-safe.\n  Next: Submit seeds {42,123} after current Even/Odd runs (580/581) complete and SE tri-seed(7) is in queue; adopt only if ≥0.678 tri-seed mean with no regressions and clear CRI-Off lift; else keep SE default and report as neutral/negative.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Continuing with experiments**\n\nI need to keep moving forward with our actions. Right now, experiments 580 and 581 (Even/Odd pooling seeds 42 & 123) are running. We had a submission issue with SE tri-seed (seed=7) due to concurrency, so I’ll have to wait until those finish. The results so far show Bi-Window seed 42 at 0.6788, which is close to SOTA but still not quite there, and seed 123 dropped to 0.6681, indicating instability.**Exploring task-specific heads**\n\nTo achieve our goals, I need to consider using task-specific heads. However, the system notes warn against \"dataset-specific methods\" for architecture. They do allow variations by type, like regression and classification. This raises questions: can we use task-specific prediction heads across datasets without violating those rules? The baseline suggests they used dataset-specific heads, but the spec indicates that the core architecture is the same across datasets. It's a bit convoluted, but I need to figure\
  \ out what is permissible here.**Navigating dataset specifics**\n\nThe spec warns against \"no dataset-specific methods,\" so I want to play it safe. I think we should avoid using dataset-specific logic in pooling but could explore options like an \"auxiliary contrastive head\" or \"pairwise difference head\" for CRI-Off since it's based on sgRNA-target concatenation. However, this might be too specific if it uses specific pairs. Alternatively, I can consider methods like \"cross-correlation\" or \"lag-1 differencing\" for pooling. For now, I need to plan our next steps in the Station.**Planning actions and insights**\n\nI’m considering whether to set a rank score to view the scoreboard, but it's not critical. I definitely need to outline specific actions: possibly starting with a summary file for the even/odd plan. We have to be patient and wait for results. There's that new Veritas II archive #21 that could offer insights, especially about the recent announcement on \"Global SOTA & Record\
  \ CRI-Off.\" I think we should read that to see how their CRI-Off improved. Then we can plan our modifications.**Planning next steps and code**\n\nI want to be careful not to go overboard with the code. First, I think we should read archive #21, then stage a \"cross-correlation pooling\" variant. I need to keep that YAML quoting rule in mind, but our content is already simple. So, here’s the plan: \n\n1. Read archive #21 to gather insights.\n2. Update the plan file.\n3. Stage code for \"CrossCorr pooling,\" but don’t submit until current runs are done. I can implement pooling that captures four stats and manage dimensions efficiently. \n\nI’ll also create code for `EvenOddXMixPooling` and finish the immediate actions!"
