parts:
- text: "Implementing task-type-specific prediction heads on the SE-calibrated shared backbone to close the gap and target CRI-Off, then submitting two seeds.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_taskheads.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Dual-expert with shared DSConv backbone + Channel SE + mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU + scalar-gated fusion\n  + task-type-specific prediction heads (small MLP per task type).\n\n  Compliant design: shared feature extractor across datasets; only the final heads are specialized by task_type,\n  as permitted by the spec. Goal: improve overall average and CRI-Off, inspired by Veritas II's task-specific heads.\n\n  Heads:\n    - regression (APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL): Dense(HH) -> GELU -> Dropout -> Dense(1)\n    - multilabel_regression (PRS): Dense(HH) -> GELU -> Dropout -> Dense(3)\n    - multilabel_classification (Modif): Dense(HH) -> GELU -> Dropout -> Dense(12)\n \
    \   - multiclass_classification (ncRNA): Dense(HH) -> GELU -> Dropout -> Dense(13)\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  # ===== Utilities =====\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau=0.25, length_normalize=True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  # ===== Backbone Blocks =====\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = x\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          # Depthwise dilated conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n\
    \                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME')(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          # Pointwise conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          return h  # (B,\
    \ L, H)\n\n  class ChannelSE(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      reduction: int = 4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x: (B, L, H)\n          g = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)                 # (B, H)\n          rd = max(1, self.hidden_dim // self.reduction)\n          g = nn.Dense(rd)(g); g = jax.nn.gelu(g)\n          g = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(g); g = jax.nn.sigmoid(g)  # (B, H)\n          g = g[:, None, :]\n          return x * g\n\n  class MeanLSEPooling(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          lse_pool = _lse_pool(h, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n\
    \          logits = self.param('mix_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (2,))\n          w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n          return w[0] * mean_pool + w[1] * lse_pool\n\n  class BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim: int\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(x)\n          f = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hf = f(x)[:, -1, :]\n          b = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hb = b(jnp.flip(x, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n          return jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)\n\n  # ===== Full Network with Task-Specific Heads =====\n  class DualExpertSETaskHeads(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n\
    \      gru_dim: int = 160\n      fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      post_norm: bool = True\n      se_reduction: int = 4\n      head_hidden: int = 128   # small MLP head size\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Shared feature extractor\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(x, deterministic)\n          h = ChannelSE(self.hidden_dim, self.se_reduction)(h)\n\n          pool_rep = MeanLSEPooling(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n\n          rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim, self.pre_norm)(h)\n          rnn_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n          # Fusion\n          if self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n              logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp),\
    \ (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n              fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n          else:\n              fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n\n          if self.post_norm:\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n\n          # Task-type-specific head (small MLP)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(fused); z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n          # Shape compliance\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return z.squeeze(-1)\n          return z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n          self.network = DualExpertSETaskHeads(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n\
    \              kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(h.get('ds_dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n              fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n              pre_norm=bool(h.get('pre_norm', True)),\n              post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', True)),\n              se_reduction=int(h.get('se_reduction', 4)),\n              head_hidden=int(h.get('head_hidden', 128)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n\
    \          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SE-calibrated shared DSConv + mean↔LSE + BiGRU + task-type heads (HH=128) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, bigru, gating, task-heads\"\nabstract: \"Adds small task-type-specific prediction heads (Dense(128)→GELU→Dropout→Dense(d_out)) on top of the SE-calibrated dual-expert. Shared features remain universal; only heads\
    \ specialize by task type. Tests whether output-level specialization lifts avg and CRI-Off.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_taskheads import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4,\n          'head_hidden': 128\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n      \
    \    optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SE-calibrated shared DSConv + mean↔LSE + BiGRU + task-type heads (HH=128) — seed=123\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, bigru, gating, task-heads\"\nabstract: \"Replication with BASE_SEED=123 to assess stability of task-type heads atop SE-calibrated dual-expert.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_taskheads import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n\
    \          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4,\n          'head_hidden': 128\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update (Tick 381)\n  Even/Odd pooling:\n  - 580 (seed=42): 0.6741 | CRI-Off 0.0885\
    \ | CRI-On 0.4635 | MRL 0.8971 | APA 0.8611 | ncRNA 0.9015\n  - 581 (seed=123): 0.6710 | CRI-Off 0.0807 | CRI-On 0.4646 | MRL 0.9017 | APA 0.8596 | ncRNA 0.8923\n  → Slight CRI-Off lift in seed=42, but average remains <0.678 and unstable.\n\n  New direction (inspired by Archive #21):\n  - Implemented task-type-specific prediction heads atop SE-calibrated shared DSConv + mean↔LSE + BiGRU + scalar gate (HH=128).\n  - Submitted seeds {42,123}. Target: close gap toward 0.6935 SOTA; prioritize CRI-Off without hurting APA/MRL.\n  - If promising, add seed=7 to tri-seed and perform small head_hidden sweep {96,128,160} for trade-off.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Analyzing architecture for tasks**


  I’m thinking that the core architecture should be adaptable for all sequence-level tasks, but the final layers need to tailor to each prediction type. This allows for task-type-specific heads, like how Veritas architecture implemented them. There’s a suggestion that we might adopt task-type heads since specifications permit final layers customization, which could help close the performance gap. So, I’m planning to focus on implementing specialized heads in our architecture for better results.**Implementing task-specific heads**


  I’m considering using a head per task type with a small MLP structure like Dense(128)->GELU->Dropout->Dense(d_output), similar to what Veritas does. To move forward, I should create a new submission using the current default features: shared backbone DSConv, SE, mean↔LSE pooling, BiGRU, and scalar gate. I’ll implement a create_network function that outputs hidden representations but ensure it produces predictions based on task type through its heads. I also need to make sure we stay under 1M parameters.**Adjusting parameters for efficiency**


  I’m looking at the parameter count using DSConv and BiGRU; it’s about 0.971M. Adding a 128-dimensional head will increase it slightly, but I want to keep it under 1.02M, so maybe I should reduce the hidden_dim from 256 to 224. However, I could also proceed with 256 and maintain under 1.1M. I plan to implement a module that shapes Dense(d_output) based on each dataset, using task_type to direct if/elif logic. I’ll set dropout to 0.1 and call it "dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_taskheads.py."**Planning seed submissions**


  I need to submit at least one run with seed=42, but right now, we aren''t running any experiments. However, we''ve completed the even/odd evaluations successfully. Since the system might limit us to two concurrent evaluations and we don''t have any running, I can submit two seeds: 42 and either 7 or 123. I''ll go with 42 first, then move to 7 or 123. It seems more promising to stick with these initial seeds for task-specific heads rather than my previous tri-seed attempt that failed.**Organizing submission tasks**


  I’ve created "evenodd_xmix," but I’ll hold off on submitting that to maintain concurrency for task-specific heads. For my next steps, I’ll create a file named ''dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_taskheads.py.'' This will combine components like DSConv, SE, pooling, BiGRU, and specialized heads for each task type.


  I’ll also submit evaluations with seeds 42 and 123 while ensuring to document everything. Additionally, I’ll implement a small MLP head and manage the output shapes accordingly for classification and regression tasks. Finally, I’ll draft the code and ensure proper storage and summaries.'
