thinking_content: "**Managing token usage and submissions**\n\nI see that the token budget is at 170k of 270k used, so it’s not too high, but we could prune to save some. We should probably set up logging and update the summary file. I need to plan for tri-seed SE submission, which previously failed due to concurrency limits. Currently, I have experiments 585 and 584 running, and since the limit allows only two concurrent submissions, I can’t submit more until they finish. I can stage code or write a plan in the meantime.**Updating memory and considering improvements**\n\nI need to update private memory decision points and add new moves to the archive addendum. Also, I might store the code for the even-odd cross mix since we’ve completed that. I should check results for earlier even-odd, noting that CRI-Off improved to 0.0885 for seed 42, which is a bit better than 0.08, but still behind the global SOTA of 0.1365. Our architecture likely can't match that without specialized heads. I'm considering\
  \ adding training schedules or dropout improvements to enhance our results.**Documenting results and managing tokens**\n\nNow, I need to document the results. At tick 382, I can propose pruning older logs again to manage tokens. I’m cautious about the token management cooldown; it was previously set at 4 ticks after tick 372. Since we're at 382, I think I can prune again. I should check if I can prune 367-370, but 367 was a heavy tick because it involved reading Logos II and submitting enriched runs. I’ll create summary blocks for ticks 367-370 and 371-373, ensuring to include key metrics without being too concise.**Summarizing results and proposing actions**\n\nI’ve documented the results, noting specifics for various ticks: 558 at 0.6730, 563 at 0.6689, and so on, with an aggregator created. It looks good overall. I should finalize updating the 'dual_expert_summary.md' since that's already done. Now, I’m considering writing a mail to Veritas II to praise the results and ask for guidance\
  \ on head hidden choices, dropout, gating, and stabilizing CRI-Off variability. It’s optional, though. I'll plan to tri-seed the SE with head specialization once current runs complete and propose pruning tokens for ticks 367-370 and 371-373 while summarizing the results.**Planning actions and managing tokens**\n\nMy next steps include several actions. I plan to run seed=7 for SE task-heads after the current runs and potentially implement new code for 'task-type head hidden sweep' and 'head dropout variant.' I'll stage an evaluation to compute parameter counts and create a script for that. I also need to update the archive addendum with our steps, but we'll stick to performing actions via /execute_action. \n\nI’ll issue commands for token management pruning on ticks 367-373, summarizing results for those ranges, and ensure I provide thorough but precise details.**Finalizing results and commands**\n\nI’ve saved the aggregator's mix weights and the script. For the SE calibration, I got the\
  \ results: 569 at 0.6756 and 570 at 0.6727, with various metrics like CRI-On and PRS. For the Bi-Window fix and resubmission, I found results for ticks 576 and 577; however, since 576 is newly fixed and arrived at tick 379, it's outside the prune range of 367-373, so I won't include it in the prune. I'll mention the re-submission in my final message, including necessary commands."
