tick: 383
role: model
parts:
- text: "SE task-heads improved stability but didn’t lift CRI-Off. I’ll test SE + Even/Odd cross-mix pooling (adds interaction stats) on two seeds.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_evenodd_xmix.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Shared DSConv backbone + Channel SE + Even/Odd cross-mix pooling + BiGRU + scalar-gated fusion.\n  Universal, <1M params. Even/Odd pooling computes per-stream stats (mean, LSE τ=0.25 len-norm) and\n  interaction terms (mean_e*mean_o, lse_e*lse_o), with channel-wise soft mix over 6 stats.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau=0.25, length_normalize=True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L,\
    \ dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = x\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME')(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n     \
    \ dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          return h  # (B, L, H)\n\n  class ChannelSE(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      reduction: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          g = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)                 # (B, H)\n          rd = max(1, self.hidden_dim // self.reduction)\n          g = nn.Dense(rd)(g); g = jax.nn.gelu(g)\n          g = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(g); g = jax.nn.sigmoid(g)  # (B, H)\n          return x * g[:, None, :]\n\n  class EvenOddXMixPooling(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      pre_norm: bool =\
    \ True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          L = h.shape[1]\n          if L == 1:\n              he = h; ho = h\n          else:\n              he = h[:, 0::2, :]\n              ho = h[:, 1::2, :]\n          me = jnp.mean(he, axis=1)\n          le = _lse_pool(he, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          mo = jnp.mean(ho, axis=1)\n          lo = _lse_pool(ho, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          mm = me * mo\n          ll = le * lo\n          stats = jnp.stack([me, le, mo, lo, mm, ll], axis=-1)  # (B, H, 6)\n          logits = self.param('mix_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (self.hidden_dim, 6))\n          w = jax.nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)   # (H, 6)\n          w = jnp.expand_dims(w, axis=0)        # (1, H, 6)\n          return jnp.sum(stats * w, axis=-1)\
    \    # (B, H)\n\n  class BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim: int\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(x)\n          f = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hf = f(x)[:, -1, :]\n          b = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hb = b(jnp.flip(x, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n          return jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)\n\n  class DualExpertSEEvenOddXMix(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      gru_dim: int = 160\n      fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      post_norm: bool = True\n      se_reduction: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic:\
    \ bool = True):\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(x, deterministic)\n          h = ChannelSE(self.hidden_dim, self.se_reduction)(h)\n          pool_rep = EvenOddXMixPooling(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n          rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim, self.pre_norm)(h)\n          rnn_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n          if self.fusion == 'scalar_gate':\n              logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (2,))\n              w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n              fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n          else:\n              fused = 0.5 * (pool_proj + rnn_proj)\n          if self.post_norm:\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused); z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n\
    \          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return z.squeeze(-1)\n          return z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n          self.network = DualExpertSEEvenOddXMix(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(h.get('ds_dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n              fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n\
    \              pre_norm=bool(h.get('pre_norm', True)),\n              post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', True)),\n              se_reduction=int(h.get('se_reduction', 4)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:\
    \ float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SE + Even/Odd cross-mix pooling + BiGRU(160), scalar gate — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, even-odd, bigru, gating\"\nabstract: \"Adds Channel SE and even/odd cross-mix pooling (mean/LSE per stream + interaction terms) to the shared DSConv backbone, fused with BiGRU via scalar gate. Tests CRI-Off improvements while preserving APA/MRL; universal and <1M params.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_evenodd_xmix import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim':\
    \ 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SE + Even/Odd cross-mix pooling + BiGRU(160), scalar gate — seed=123\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, even-odd, bigru, gating, stability\"\nabstract: \"Replication of Channel SE + even/odd cross-mix pooling to assess stability\
    \ and CRI-Off impact.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_evenodd_xmix import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n\
    \      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update (Tick 383)\n  Task-type heads atop SE shared backbone:\n  - 584 (seed=42): 0.6750 | CRI-Off 0.0745 | CRI-On 0.4824 | MRL 0.9040 | APA 0.8596 | Modif 0.9499 | ncRNA 0.8985\n  - 585 (seed=123): 0.6728 | CRI-Off 0.0809 | CRI-On 0.4790 | MRL 0.8951 | APA 0.8581 | Modif 0.9492 | ncRNA 0.8923\n  Takeaway: stable and solid, but CRI-Off not lifted; average ~0.674 consistent with SE-only.\n\n  New submissions:\n  - SE + Even/Odd cross-mix pooling (mean_e, lse_e, mean_o, lse_o, mean_e*mean_o, lse_e*lse_o) with scalar-gated BiGRU — seeds {42,123}.\n  Goal: lift CRI-Off without harming APA/MRL; retain universality and <1M params. Adoption requires ≥0.678 mean with clear CRI-Off gains; else keep SE default.\n\
    ```"
thinking_content: "**Deciding priority for submissions**\n\nI’m considering our priorities for experiments. We have to balance submitting the evenodd_xmix variant seeds 42 and 123, alongside the SE tri-seed 7. Since we can only submit two at a time, I think we should start with either submitting SE tri-seed first for stability or go for the two evenodd_xmix experiments. I’m leaning toward submitting evenodd_xmix seeds 42 and 123 first. Let's also remember to log the results afterward!**Preparing the submission**\n\nI’m in the Token Management Room, and I need to submit my research using a specific file: noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_evenodd_xmix.py. I'll import that file and utilize the optimizer clip chain as I've done before. I want to ensure the parameters align with previous submissions, keeping hidden_dim at 256, kernel_size at 7, and so on. I notice evenodd_xmix doesn’t include SE, but I’m wondering if we should incorporate it since the earlier variant had good\
  \ results with SE. It’s something to think about!**Modifying the xmix code**\n\nI’m considering quickly modifying the xmix code to include Channel SE for potentially better performance. Although I’ve already written the code without SE in storage, I could create a new file, 'evenodd_xmix_se.py'. Testing the baseline without SE might be okay to target CRI-Off since SE improved CRI-On instead. However, it could be advantageous to add SE to better align with our average target. I’ll go ahead and implement \"dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_evenodd_xmix.py\" and submit seeds 42 and 123!**Staying compliant with submission**\n\nI need to ensure we stay compliant within the station by only implementing allowed functions. I’ll proceed to submit seeds 42 and 123 for se_evenodd_xmix, which should help us achieve better averages. Although computing the parameter count would be nice, it’s not necessary right now. I’ll adjust the log message to summarize our new plan and update the results summary.\
  \ I’m crafting the commands needed, being careful of the concurrency limit while integrating ChannelSE into our new code.**Creating YAML for submission**\n\nI need to ensure that I'm producing the correct YAML content for the code, focusing on proper Flax LNN usage since we previously used RNN without issues. I'll include components like DSConvBackbone, ChannelSE block, and EvenOddXMixPooling. The code structure will be:  \n- `h = DSConvBackbone(...)`  \n- `h = ChannelSE(...)(h)`  \n- `pool_rep = EvenOddXMixPooling(...)(h)`  \n- `rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(...)(h)`  \nI'll incorporate the gating, LayerNorm, and head structure as before while keeping our previous optimizer settings. I’ll also update the \"dual_expert_summary.md\" with task-head results and the plan."
