role: model
parts:
- text: "Submitting the SE-calibrated shared DSConv + motif-detector + task-type heads model for two seeds, then logging plan and expectations.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SE-shared DSConv + mean↔LSE + BiGRU + Motif(k=5,max) + task-type heads — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, bigru, motif, task-heads\"\nabstract: \"Adds a lightweight motif-detector expert (Conv1D k=5 → global max) to SE-calibrated shared DSConv features with mean↔LSE pooling and BiGRU. Three-way scalar-gated fusion; small task-type-specific heads (Dense(128)→GELU→Dropout→Dense(d_out)). Tests CRI-Off lift and average gains while remaining universal and <1M params.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_se_motif_taskheads import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size':\
    \ 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4,\n          'head_hidden': 128,\n          'motif_dim': 128,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SE-shared DSConv + mean↔LSE + BiGRU + Motif(k=5,max) + task-type heads — seed=123\"\ntags: \"\
    dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, bigru, motif, task-heads, stability\"\nabstract: \"Replication of the SE-calibrated shared DSConv + motif-detector + task-type heads model with BASE_SEED=123 to assess stability and CRI-Off impact.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_se_motif_taskheads import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4,\n          'head_hidden': 128,\n          'motif_dim': 128,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type',\
    \ 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update (Tick 385)\n  Even/Odd cross-mix (with SE):\n  - 589 (seed=42): 0.6725 | CRI-Off 0.0738 | CRI-On 0.4915 | PRS 0.5468 | MRL 0.8993 | APA 0.8506 | Modif 0.9506 | ncRNA 0.8954\n  - 590 (seed=123): 0.6759 | CRI-Off 0.0799 | CRI-On 0.4892 | PRS 0.5508 | MRL 0.8972 | APA 0.8581 | Modif 0.9500 | ncRNA 0.9062\n  Takeaway: solid averages (~0.674–0.676), CRI-On good, CRI-Off unchanged (~0.074–0.080). \n\n  New submissions:\n  - SE-shared DSConv + mean↔LSE + BiGRU + Motif(k=5,max) + task-type\
    \ heads (HH=128), scalar 3-way fusion — seeds {42,123}.\n  Goal: lift CRI-Off and overall average while maintaining APA/MRL; universal design and <1M params. If ≥0.678 with clear CRI-Off gains, proceed to tri-seed and minor sweeps (head_hidden {96,128,160}, motif_dim {96,128}); else document as neutral/negative and retain SE default.\n```"
