tick: 386
role: model
parts:
- text: "Staging a mean+max pooling variant of the SE+Motif+Task-Heads model to align with top SOTA pooling, then will submit after current runs (592/593) finish.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_se_motif_taskheads_meanmax.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Shared DSConv backbone + Channel SE + mean+max pooling + BiGRU + Motif(k=5) expert\n  + scalar-gated fusion + small task-type-specific heads.\n\n  Rationale: Top SOTA baselines use mean+max pooling on DSConv features. We combine this with the\n  lightweight motif detector and task-type heads while keeping <1M params and full universality.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  # ===== Backbone Blocks =====\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n     \
    \ @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = x\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          # Depthwise dilated conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME')(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          # Pointwise conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\
    \ kernel_size=(1,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          return h  # (B, L, H)\n\n  class ChannelSE(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      reduction: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          g = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)                   # (B, H)\n          rd = max(1, self.hidden_dim // self.reduction)\n          g = nn.Dense(rd)(g); g = jax.nn.gelu(g)\n          g = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(g); g = jax.nn.sigmoid(g)  # (B, H)\n          return x * g[:, None, :]\n\n  class MeanMaxPooling(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)          # (B, H)\n          max_pool  = jnp.max(h, axis=1)           # (B, H)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, max_pool], axis=-1)  # (B, 2H)\n          fused = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)                  # project back to H\n          return fused\n\n  class BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim: int\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(x)\n          f = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hf = f(x)[:, -1, :]\n          b = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hb = b(jnp.flip(x, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n          return jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)\n\n  class MotifExpert(nn.Module):\n      feat_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.feat_dim, kernel_size=(5,),\
    \ padding='SAME')(x)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = jnp.max(h, axis=1)  # (B, feat_dim)\n          return h\n\n  class DualExpertSEMotifTaskHeadsMeanMax(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      gru_dim: int = 160\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      post_norm: bool = True\n      se_reduction: int = 4\n      head_hidden: int = 128\n      motif_dim: int = 128\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Shared DSConv + SE\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(x, deterministic)\n          h = ChannelSE(self.hidden_dim, self.se_reduction)(h)\n\n          # Expert A: mean+max pooled DSConv features\
    \ (projected to H)\n          pool_proj = MeanMaxPooling(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n\n          # Expert B: BiGRU on DSConv features\n          rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim, self.pre_norm)(h)\n          rnn_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n          # Expert C: Motif detector on raw one-hot\n          motif_rep = MotifExpert(self.motif_dim, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          motif_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(motif_rep)\n\n          # Scalar-softmax fusion over 3 experts\n          logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (3,))\n          w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n          fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj + w[2] * motif_proj\n\n          if self.post_norm:\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n\n          # Task-type-specific head (small MLP)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(fused); z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return z.squeeze(-1)\n          return z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n          self.network = DualExpertSEMotifTaskHeadsMeanMax(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(h.get('ds_dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n              pre_norm=bool(h.get('pre_norm', True)),\n              post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', True)),\n              se_reduction=int(h.get('se_reduction', 4)),\n              head_hidden=int(h.get('head_hidden',\
    \ 128)),\n              motif_dim=int(h.get('motif_dim', 128)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n\
    ```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/meanmax_motif_plan.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 386 — Mean+Max Pooling Variant Plan\n  Motivation: Align pooled DSConv features with strongest SOTA (mean+max), while retaining SE, Motif(k=5), BiGRU, scalar 3-way fusion, and task-type heads. Expectation: improved APA/MRL/ncRNA without hurting PRS; potential CRI-Off lift via motif path + heads.\n  Next: Submit seeds {42,123} once motif-taskheads runs (592/593) complete. Adoption criterion: ≥0.678 mean with no regressions and CRI-Off ↑ vs SE-only; else document as neutral/negative and keep SE default.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Exploring model improvements**\n\nI’m considering several approaches to enhance the model. Adding gradient clipping is already set at 1.0, and dropout is established at 0.1. For data augmentation, I believe using techniques like reverse complement is tricky for RNA one-hot sequences since it might not apply across tasks. I'm evaluating the idea of pre-LN and post-LN calibrations we’ve tested. Finally, I wonder about K-mer embedding using a 1D convolution inside the network, but I can’t modify the data loader.**Planning experiment updates**\n\nI’m considering how we’re currently using convolutional layers. Since two runs are ongoing, I can’t submit more at the moment, but I can stage the next code for an aggregator variant. I could also update Archive Room #18 with new findings, although we probably won’t need that until we have motif results. I noted that we can compute plans if the motif lifts, like tri-seed and capacity sweeps. I’ll document the new results summary\
  \ for the even/odd cross-mix runs, which is already included. Lastly, I’ll prepare the code for the mean+max aggregator within the motif model variant.**Designing network adjustments**\n\nI’m looking at many earlier state-of-the-art models, which used concatenation and doubled dimensions for heads. However, since the network spec returns final predictions, I can design accordingly. I plan to implement a code file called \"dual_expert_dsconv_se_motif_taskheads_meanmax.py,\" customizing the pooling aggregator to use mean+max concatenation into a Dense layer. I might also stage a variant for sum gating versus concatenation. \n\nNext, I’ll write the new code content and update the results document with the mean-max plan. Then, I might go to the archive to acknowledge results so far, ensuring to keep tokens in check.**Preparing code and plans**\n\nI’m focusing on creating actionable steps for the upcoming work. First, I’ll stage the code and plan. I will write the file \"dual_expert_dsconv_se_motif_taskheads_meanmax.py\"\
  \ with the mean+max aggregator into the storage. Next, I'll log the submission plan in \"meanmax_motif_plan.md\" for when slots are available, since two runs are currently active. \n\nI’ll define classes similar to earlier but with a new pooling block called 'MeanMaxPooling,' which will concatenate the mean and max before returning a Dense layer to hidden_dim. Let's finalize the commands for this process."
