- text: "Submitting the mean+max pooling variant with motif path and task-type heads (seeds 42, 123), then logging plan and expectations.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: SE-shared DSConv + mean+max pooling + BiGRU + Motif(k=5,max) + task-type heads — seed=42\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, mean-max, motif, task-heads\"\nabstract: \"Align pooled DSConv features with SOTA (mean+max) while retaining Channel SE, BiGRU, a lightweight motif-detector expert (k=5→global max), scalar 3-way fusion, and small task-type heads. Tests average gains and CRI-Off lift under a universal <1M design.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_se_motif_taskheads_meanmax import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n      \
    \    'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4,\n          'head_hidden': 128,\n          'motif_dim': 128,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: SE-shared DSConv + mean+max pooling + BiGRU + Motif(k=5,max) + task-type heads — seed=123\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, mean-max, motif, task-heads, stability\"\nabstract: \"Replication (seed=123)\
    \ of SE+mean+max DSConv features with BiGRU and motif expert; scalar 3-way fusion; task-type heads. Assesses stability and CRI-Off impact under universal <1M design.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_se_motif_taskheads_meanmax import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4,\n          'head_hidden': 128,\n          'motif_dim': 128,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n    \
    \      optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update (Tick 387)\n  Motif + task-type heads (mean↔LSE pooled DSConv):\n  - 592 (seed=42): 0.6733 | CRI-Off 0.0816 | CRI-On 0.4805 | PRS 0.5563 | MRL 0.8983 | APA 0.8558 | Modif 0.9495 | ncRNA 0.8908\n  - 593 (seed=123): 0.6739 | CRI-Off 0.0799 | CRI-On 0.4722 | PRS 0.5530 | MRL 0.9012 | APA 0.8606 | Modif 0.9517 | ncRNA 0.8985\n  Takeaway: Stable ~0.674 avg with strong MRL/APA/PRS; CRI-Off unchanged (~0.08).\n\n  New runs queued:\n  - SE-shared DSConv + mean+max pooling + BiGRU + Motif(k=5,max) + task-type heads — seeds {42,123}.\n  Goal: align pooling with strongest SOTA while retaining motif\
    \ + heads; adoption if ≥0.678 mean without regressions and with CRI-Off ↑ vs SE-only; else record as neutral/negative.\n```"
