tick: 388
role: model
parts:
- text: "Preparing a concat-fusion variant matching the strongest SOTA pattern (mean+max DSConv pooled features concatenated with a motif path), plus task-type heads. I’ll stage the code and plan; will submit after 596/597 finish.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_se_motif_taskheads_concat.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Shared DSConv backbone + Channel SE + Dual-Path pooled features (mean & max) + Motif(k=5,max) path\n  → concatenate [mean, max, motif] (3H) → LayerNorm → small task-type head.\n  Universal across datasets; <1M params. No BiGRU in this variant to align with SOTA concat design.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = x\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME')(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n\
    \              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          return h  # (B, L, H)\n\n  class ChannelSE(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      reduction: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          g = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)  # (B, H)\n          rd = max(1, self.hidden_dim // self.reduction)\n          g = nn.Dense(rd)(g); g = jax.nn.gelu(g)\n          g = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(g); g = jax.nn.sigmoid(g)\n          return x * g[:, None, :]\n\n  class MotifExpert(nn.Module):\n      feat_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # x: (B, L, 4)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.feat_dim, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return jnp.max(h, axis=1)  # (B, feat_dim)\n\n  class DSConvSEMotifConcatHeads(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_output: int\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      post_norm: bool = True\n      se_reduction: int = 4\n      head_hidden: int = 128\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Shared DSConv + SE → H\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(x, deterministic)\n          h = ChannelSE(self.hidden_dim, self.se_reduction)(h)\n\n          # Dual-path pooled features (no projection): mean, max → H each\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)   # (B, H)\n          max_pool  = jnp.max(h, axis=1)    # (B, H)\n\n          # Motif path on raw one-hot (projected to H via Conv feat_dim=H internally)\n          motif = MotifExpert(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)  # (B,\
    \ H)\n\n          # Concat to 3H and normalize\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, max_pool, motif], axis=-1)  # (B, 3H)\n          if self.post_norm:\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n\n          # Small task-type-specific head\n          z = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(fused); z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return z.squeeze(-1)\n          return z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n          self.network = DSConvSEMotifConcatHeads(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(h.get('ds_dilations',\
    \ [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              pre_norm=bool(h.get('pre_norm', True)),\n              post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', True)),\n              se_reduction=int(h.get('se_reduction', 4)),\n              head_hidden=int(h.get('head_hidden', 128)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output,\
    \ task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/concat_motif_plan.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 388 — Concat Motif + Mean/Max DSConv + Task-Type Heads (no BiGRU)\n  Rationale: Veritas II’s SOTA uses concatenation of mean+max DSConv pooled features with a motif path, then small task-type heads. Our prior gating and added BiGRU may have diluted this effect. This variant mirrors the SOTA fusion: concat [mean, max, motif] → LN → small head; universal and <1M.\n  Next: Submit seeds {42,123} after mean+max + motif + heads (596/597) complete. Adoption criterion: ≥0.678 mean with no regressions and CRI-Off ↑ vs SE-only; else log as neutral/negative and keep SE default.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Designing feature representation**\n\nI’m working on a design involving means and maximums from the DSConv features, taking both without projection. The next step is getting motif representation through Conv1D, producing global max results for 3H channels. I’ll fuse features by concatenating mean, max, and motif before applying layer normalization and passing them through a task-specific head. \n\nAlso, I need to implement the code, define dropout options, and add gradient clipping. It’s important to stage the plan properly! Additionally, I’m considering a tri-seed for SE-only later on.**Crafting actions for implementation**\n\nI’m planning to write a new submission file that implements a concatenation variant. However, I won’t submit it just yet since runs 596 and 597 are still pending. The system indicates we can't submit more than two concurrent experiments, so I'll hold off for now. \n\nI might also prepare to prune token history, but since the cooldown might have\
  \ ended, it’s not necessary right away. I’ll focus on writing the code carefully, ensuring to implement the necessary functions, like defining hyperparameters and creating the network and optimizer. Finally, I’ll stage everything and draft a result summarization plan.**Implementing the motif path correction**\n\nI'm considering how to correct the motif path so it processes the raw one-hot input x correctly. So, I'll go ahead and implement that in the code. I need to remember to write a new file and make a note in the storage plan. I'll be careful with YAML quoting since the code content uses triple quotes. Once I have that sorted out, I can proceed without any issues!"
