tick: 389
role: model
parts:
- text: "Submitting the concat-fusion variant (mean+max DSConv pooled + motif path, no BiGRU) with task-type heads for two seeds, then logging updates.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SE-shared DSConv + concat[mean,max,motif] + task-type heads — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, mean-max, motif, task-heads\"\nabstract: \"Concatenate DSConv pooled mean+max with a lightweight motif path (Conv1D k=5→global max), apply LayerNorm, then small task-type heads. Universal <1M params; mirrors SOTA fusion without BiGRU. Tests CRI-Off and average gains.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_se_motif_taskheads_concat import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'pre_norm': True,\n  \
    \        'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4,\n          'head_hidden': 128,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n                         optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SE-shared DSConv + concat[mean,max,motif] + task-type heads — seed=123\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, mean-max, motif, task-heads, stability\"\nabstract: \"Replication of concat fusion (mean+max DSConv + motif) with task-type heads, BASE_SEED=123. Universal <1M params; target CRI-Off lift and improved average.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys,\
    \ optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_se_motif_taskheads_concat import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4,\n          'head_hidden': 128,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n                         optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage\
    \ write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update (Tick 389)\n  Mean+max DSConv + BiGRU + Motif + heads:\n  - 596 (seed=42): 0.6659 | CRI-Off 0.0815 | CRI-On 0.4624 | PRS 0.5603 | MRL 0.8995 | APA 0.8602 | Modif 0.9500 | ncRNA 0.8477 (drop)\n  - 597 (seed=123): 0.6737 | CRI-Off 0.0848 | CRI-On 0.5068 | PRS 0.5583 | MRL 0.8911 | APA 0.8539 | Modif 0.9503 | ncRNA 0.8708\n  Takeaway: Adding BiGRU to mean+max+motif hurt stability (ncRNA drop, seed=42). CRI-Off still ~0.08–0.085.\n\n  New runs:\n  - Concat fusion (no BiGRU): concat[mean, max, motif] → LN → small task-type head — seeds {42,123}. Mirrors SOTA fusion more closely.\n  Adoption criterion: ≥0.678 mean with no major regressions and a CRI-Off increase vs SE-only (~0.08). If neutral/negative, retain SE-calibrated shared backbone as default and record as negative.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating model performance**


  I''ve noticed that the CRI-Off pattern stays around 0.08 while SOTA achieves 0.1365 using task-specific heads and a dual-path motif approach. Our task-type heads didn''t improve CRI-Off, and adding the motif path didn’t help either. It might be because of their "dual-path conv motif detector" combined with other techniques. They also didn''t use a BiGRU path but instead implemented specific gating. Now that tasks 596/597 are done, we can submit seeds for our concat variant. Let’s move forward!**Planning submission details**


  I need to make sure that our code correctly uses the appropriate output dimensions for each dataset and head. The DSConvSEMotifConcatHeads function seems to be doing well, as it returns a shape that matches the output dimensions. However, we didn''t include optimizer creation with clipping, so I''ll add the optax.clip_by_global_norm chain in our submission code. We also need to update the results summary and plan further. If things go well, I might implement a tri-seed, and otherwise, I''ll revert to the SE default. Let''s prepare for two submissions, defining the necessary YAML content and hyperparameters.**Organizing submission tasks**


  I need to ensure that the optimizer includes clipping and that I’m fully printing out the validation metrics. After that, I''ll write the outcomes from tasks 596 and 597 to the results summary log, noting that we are submitting the concat variant. It''s good to remember our earlier attempts at using a tri-seed for the SE default, although concurrency issues prevented us from resubmitting. For now, I''ll focus on submitting the concat variant seeds, being careful with YAML formatting for titles to avoid any issues. Let’s get this all assembled!'
