parts:
- text: "Concat fusion raised ncRNA/APA but cratered CRI-Off (~0.05–0.065). Reverting to the stronger SE + task-heads as default and completing tri-seed; also probing smaller head (96) for concat to test bias–variance.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SE-calibrated shared DSConv + mean↔LSE + BiGRU + task-type heads (HH=128) — tri-seed (seed=7)\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, bigru, task-heads, stability\"\nabstract: \"Completes tri-seed for the stable SE-calibrated shared-backbone model with task-type heads. Prior seeds: 42=0.6750 (CRI-Off 0.0745), 123=0.6728 (CRI-Off 0.0809). This run uses BASE_SEED=7.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_taskheads import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate':\
    \ 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4,\n          'head_hidden': 128\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SE-shared DSConv + concat[mean,max,motif] + task-type heads — head_hidden=96 (seed=42)\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation,\
    \ pooling, mean-max, motif, task-heads\"\nabstract: \"Bias–variance probe for concat fusion: reduce task head width to 96 to test stability and CRI-Off sensitivity. Universal, <1M params.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_se_motif_taskheads_concat import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4,\n          'head_hidden': 96\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n           \
    \              optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update (Tick 391)\n  Concat[mean,max,motif] + heads (no BiGRU):\n  - 601 (seed=42): 0.6767 | CRI-Off 0.0525 | CRI-On 0.4893 | PRS 0.5641 | MRL 0.8844 | APA 0.8580 | Modif 0.9506 | ncRNA 0.9385\n  - 602 (seed=123): 0.6760 | CRI-Off 0.0648 | CRI-On 0.4666 | PRS 0.5635 | MRL 0.8858 | APA 0.8575 | Modif 0.9507 | ncRNA 0.9431\n  Takeaway: Classification tasks (ncRNA) strong, but CRI-Off severely degraded versus SE-only (~0.08). MRL notably lower.\n\n  Actions:\n  - Submitted SE + task-heads tri-seed (seed=7) to lock a stable default (~0.674 avg; CRI-Off ~0.08).\n  - Submitted concat fusion head sweep (head_hidden=96, seed=42) to test bias–variance\
    \ on CRI-Off and stability.\n\n  Next:\n  - If concat remains CRI-Off-limited, abandon concat as default and retain SE-calibrated shared backbone + task-type heads.\n  - Consider regression-head-only tweaks (head_hidden_reg, pre-head LN) in a follow-up module, keeping per-task-type legality and <1M params.\n```"
