tick: 392
role: model
parts:
- text: "Concat boosted ncRNA/APA but hurt CRI-Off. I’ll stage a targeted head-only adjustment for regression tasks (larger head for regression, smaller for classification; pre-head LayerNorm) on the strong SE + task-heads backbone, then finalize an archive addendum. I’ll submit after 604/605 finish.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_taskheads_typed.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  SE-calibrated shared DSConv + mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU + task-type heads (typed widths).\n  Universal backbone; only the small heads differ by task_type (allowed by spec).\n  Goal: lift CRI-Off (regression mapping) while keeping APA/MRL strong, with <1M params.\n\n  Head widths (default):\n    - regression (APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL): 160\n    - multilabel_regression (PRS): 128\n    - multilabel_classification (Modif): 128\n    - multiclass_classification (ncRNA): 96\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy\
    \ as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  # ===== Utilities =====\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau=0.25, length_normalize=True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = x\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME')(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n\
    \          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          return h  # (B, L, H)\n\n  class ChannelSE(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      reduction: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          g = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          rd = max(1, self.hidden_dim // self.reduction)\n          g = nn.Dense(rd)(g); g = jax.nn.gelu(g)\n\
    \          g = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(g); g = jax.nn.sigmoid(g)\n          return x * g[:, None, :]\n\n  class MeanLSEPooling(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic: bool = True):\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          lse_pool = _lse_pool(h, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          logits = self.param('mix_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (2,))\n          w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n          return w[0] * mean_pool + w[1] * lse_pool\n\n  class BiGRUBlock(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim: int\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          if self.pre_norm:\n              x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(x)\n\
    \          f = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hf = f(x)[:, -1, :]\n          b = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hb = b(jnp.flip(x, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n          return jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)\n\n  class DualExpertSETaskHeadsTyped(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      gru_dim: int = 160\n      fusion: str = \"scalar_gate\"\n      pre_norm: bool = True\n      post_norm: bool = True\n      se_reduction: int = 4\n      head_hidden_map: Dict[str, int] = None  # per-task head widths\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Shared: DSConv + SE\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate,\
    \ self.pre_norm)(x, deterministic)\n          h = ChannelSE(self.hidden_dim, self.se_reduction)(h)\n\n          # Experts: pooled DSConv + BiGRU on DSConv\n          pool_rep = MeanLSEPooling(self.hidden_dim, self.dropout_rate, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse, self.pre_norm)(h, deterministic)\n          pool_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(pool_rep)\n          rnn_rep = BiGRUBlock(self.gru_dim, self.pre_norm)(h)\n          rnn_proj = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(rnn_rep)\n\n          # Scalar-gated fusion (2-way)\n          logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros(shp), (2,))\n          w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n          fused = w[0] * pool_proj + w[1] * rnn_proj\n          if self.post_norm:\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n\n          # Task-type head width mapping (defaults)\n          default_map = {\n              \"regression\": 160,\n              \"multilabel_regression\": 128,\n              \"multilabel_classification\":\
    \ 128,\n              \"multiclass_classification\": 96,\n          }\n          head_map = self.head_hidden_map or default_map\n          hh = int(head_map.get(self.task_type, 128))\n\n          # Small task-type head with pre-head LN\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(hh)(z); z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return z.squeeze(-1)\n          return z\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          h = hparams or {}\n          head_map = h.get('head_hidden_map', None)\n          self.network = DualExpertSETaskHeadsTyped(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(h.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(h.get('kernel_size',\
    \ 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(h.get('ds_dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(h.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              tau=float(h.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(h.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              gru_dim=int(h.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n              fusion=str(h.get('fusion', 'scalar_gate')),\n              pre_norm=bool(h.get('pre_norm', True)),\n              post_norm=bool(h.get('post_norm', True)),\n              se_reduction=int(h.get('se_reduction', 4)),\n              head_hidden_map=head_map,\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params':\
    \ params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/typed_heads_plan.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 392 — Typed Task Heads Plan (SE backbone)\n  Motivation: CRI-Off remains ~0.08 with SE + heads; concat/Gated variants harm CRI-Off. Hypothesis: CRI-Off benefits from a slightly larger regression head, while classification heads can be smaller to reduce overfit.\n  Design: SE-calibrated shared DSConv + mean↔LSE + BiGRU + typed heads (regression 160, PRS 128, Modif 128, ncRNA\
    \ 96), with pre-head LayerNorm.\n  Next: Submit seeds {42,123} when 604/605 finish; adopt if ≥0.678 average with CRI-Off ↑ and no major regressions; otherwise retain SE+heads (HH=128) as default and report neutral/negative.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{update 18-1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum (Tick 392): Stability and CRI-Off findings.\n  - SE calibration with small task-type heads yields a stable ~0.674 average (peak CRI-On ~0.503) with strong APA/MRL/PRS; CRI-Off ~0.08.\n  - Bi-Window pooling gave a single-seed 0.6788 but did not lift CRI-Off consistently; average (~0.672–0.676) remains below SOTA.\n  - Even/Odd pooling and cross-mix maintained averages but did not improve CRI-Off.\n  - Concat[mean,max,motif] (no BiGRU) mirrors strong SOTA patterns and boosts ncRNA/APA, but cratered CRI-Off (0.05–0.065) and slightly lowered MRL, highlighting an output-mapping mismatch.\n  Decision: retain SE-calibrated shared DSConv + mean↔LSE + BiGRU + task-type\
    \ heads as default (<1M params; universal). We are testing typed head widths (larger regression head; smaller classification heads) with pre-head LayerNorm to target CRI-Off without harming stability.\n  We provide full negative-result logs to guide future work; our code remains compliant and universal, with no dataset-specific branches beyond allowed task-type heads.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Proposing CRI-Off improvements**\n\nI'm thinking about specialized modifications for regression tasks in CRI-Off. This would include changing the structure of task-specific heads and adding pairwise interaction terms. I need to ensure compliance within the training system, as it can only use allowed functions. We can adapt head width based on task type. I might also consider variations such as adjusting hidden sizes for regression heads and adding a residual linear skip or feature calibration. Keeping complexity minimal is important. Additionally, I may suggest learning rate differences, though the optimizer currently supports only one rate.**Planning a new variant submission**\n\nI'm considering submitting a new variant that incorporates an SE-calibrated shared DSConv, along with mean↔LSE and BiGRU, and task-type heads. The regression head would have a hidden size of 160 and a pre-head LayerNorm, while the classification head would be smaller at 96 to help reduce overfitting.\
  \ I’ll stage the code for this variant and apply logic in create_network to customize head sizes based on task type. Since we currently have two pending runs (604 and 605), we can only queue more submissions after those finish.**Staging the code and planning updates**\n\nI should stage the code but hold off on submission for now. I'll write down our plans and log them while considering an update to the Archive to summarize negative results for potential publication contributions. There was a previous paper accepted regarding the DSConv Dual-Expert with Scalar Gating. We can update the addendum to include SE calibration and negative results. For the last user query regarding the system info, I plan to write a new submission module with per-task heads and a hidden map, keeping it simple and effective.**Implementing updates and staging code**\n\nI'm planning to implement a weighted formula for our approach, where we'll use a parameter 'reg_head_skip' in hyperparameters to control skip scaling.\
  \ Keeping things stable is important, so I think applying LayerNorm is a simpler choice. \n\nI’ll stage the code file and update the results summary document with our plan. We might also consider updating item 18 in the Archive. \n\nFor token management, we're at 67% usage, which is fine. I’ll prepare the actions to stage and mention them accordingly, adhering to the interface requirements.**Updating references and crafting actions**\n\nI need to reference the ID '18-1' for our updates, particularly to highlight the CRI-On improvements and negative results. It’s important to ensure our code uses allowed functions with Python and Flax imports, just like before. \n\nI’ll define our task-specific head patterns with a mapping for head sizes. For regression, I'll set it at 160, while multilabel regression and classification will be at 128, and multiclass classification at 96. Pre-head LayerNorm will be applied consistently across all tasks, including dropout rates. I’ll make sure to deliver\
  \ these actions as planned without submitting until the current pending tasks finish."
