tick: 393
role: model
parts:
- text: "Submitting typed task-head widths atop the SE-calibrated shared backbone to target CRI-Off while maintaining stability, then logging results.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SE-shared DSConv + mean↔LSE + BiGRU + typed task heads (reg=160, cls=96–128) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, bigru, task-heads, typed-heads\"\nabstract: \"SE-calibrated shared DSConv with mean↔LSE pooling and BiGRU, plus typed small heads: regression=160 (APA/CRI-Off/CRI-On/MRL), PRS=128, Modif=128, ncRNA=96. Pre-head LayerNorm. Goal: lift CRI-Off mapping while preserving stability (<1M params, universal).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_taskheads_typed import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n     \
    \     'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4,\n          'head_hidden_map': {\n              'regression': 160,\n              'multilabel_regression': 128,\n              'multilabel_classification': 128,\n              'multiclass_classification': 96\n          }\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n                         optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n\
    \      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SE-shared DSConv + mean↔LSE + BiGRU + typed task heads (reg=160, cls=96–128) — seed=123\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, bigru, task-heads, typed-heads\"\nabstract: \"Replication (seed=123) of typed task-heads atop SE-calibrated shared backbone. Regression head widened to 160; classification heads reduced (ncRNA=96) to curb overfit. Universal, <1M params.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_taskheads_typed import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n\
    \          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4,\n          'head_hidden_map': {\n              'regression': 160,\n              'multilabel_regression': 128,\n              'multilabel_classification': 128,\n              'multiclass_classification': 96\n          }\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n                         optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/dual_expert_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Update (Tick 393)\n  Tri-seed\
    \ completed for SE + task-type heads (HH=128):\n  - 584 (seed=42): 0.6750 | CRI-Off 0.0745 | CRI-On 0.4824 | PRS 0.5563 | MRL 0.9040 | APA 0.8596 | Modif 0.9499 | ncRNA 0.8985\n  - 585 (seed=123): 0.6728 | CRI-Off 0.0809 | CRI-On 0.4790 | PRS 0.5551 | MRL 0.8951 | APA 0.8581 | Modif 0.9492 | ncRNA 0.8923\n  - 604 (seed=7):  0.6758 | CRI-Off 0.0796 | CRI-On 0.4737 | PRS 0.5610 | MRL 0.8963 | APA 0.8609 | Modif 0.9501 | ncRNA 0.9092\n  → Tri-seed mean ≈ 0.6745; CRI-Off ~0.078–0.081. Stable default.\n\n  Concat[mean,max,motif] + heads (no BiGRU):\n  - 601 (seed=42): 0.6767 | CRI-Off 0.0525 | MRL 0.8844 | APA 0.8580 | ncRNA 0.9385\n  - 602 (seed=123): 0.6760 | CRI-Off 0.0648 | MRL 0.8858 | APA 0.8575 | ncRNA 0.9431\n  Head=96 (seed=42):\n  - 605: 0.6695 | CRI-Off 0.0440 | ncRNA 0.9492 (↑), but CRI-Off severely degraded. \n  → Conclusion: concat boosts ncRNA/APA but consistently harms CRI-Off and MRL.\n\n  New submissions:\n  - Typed task-head widths on SE backbone (reg=160; PRS/Modif=128;\
    \ ncRNA=96), pre-head LN — seeds {42,123}. Goal: improve regression mapping for CRI-Off without destabilizing classification metrics.\n```"
