tick: 395
role: model
parts:
- text: "Queuing tri-seed completion and a small optimizer ablation to probe CRI-Off stability.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SE-shared DSConv + mean↔LSE + BiGRU + typed task heads (reg=160, cls=96–128) — seed=7 (tri-seed)\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, bigru, task-heads, typed-heads, stability\"\nabstract: \"Complete tri-seed for typed task heads atop SE-calibrated shared backbone. Regression head=160; PRS/Modif=128; ncRNA=96; pre-head LayerNorm; clip=1.0. Tests stability and effects on CRI-Off without harming other tasks.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_taskheads_typed import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau':\
    \ 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4,\n          'head_hidden_map': {\n              'regression': 160,\n              'multilabel_regression': 128,\n              'multilabel_classification': 128,\n              'multiclass_classification': 96\n          }\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n                         optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\
    ```yaml\ntitle: \"Typed heads + optimizer tweak: AdamW β2=0.98, clip=0.8 — seed=42\"\ntags: \"optimization, adamw, gradient-clipping, dsconv, typed-heads\"\nabstract: \"Probe whether slightly lower momentum (β2=0.98) and stronger clipping (0.8) improve CRI-Off stability on the SE-calibrated shared DSConv with typed heads.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_taskheads_typed import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4,\n          'head_hidden_map': {\n\
    \              'regression': 160,\n              'multilabel_regression': 128,\n              'multilabel_classification': 128,\n              'multiclass_classification': 96\n          }\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(0.8),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, b1=0.9, b2=0.98, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/typed_heads_results.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Typed Task Heads on SE-Calibrated Shared Backbone — Update (Tick 395)\n  Completed 2 seeds:\n  - 607 (seed=42): 0.6750 | CRI-Off 0.0766 | CRI-On 0.4949 | PRS 0.5547 | MRL 0.8955 | APA\
    \ 0.8519 | Modif 0.9499 | ncRNA 0.9015\n  - 608 (seed=123): 0.6757 | CRI-Off 0.0787 | CRI-On 0.5096 | PRS 0.5527 | MRL 0.8979 | APA 0.8558 | Modif 0.9488 | ncRNA 0.8862\n  In-flight:\n  - 609 (seed=7): tri-seed completion for typed heads (reg=160; PRS/Modif=128; ncRNA=96; clip=1.0).\n  - 610 (seed=42): optimizer tweak (AdamW β2=0.98, clip=0.8) to probe CRI-Off stability without harming others.\n\n  Notes:\n  - Typed heads maintain ~0.675 avg while raising CRI-On; CRI-Off remains ~0.076–0.079.\n  - Concat variants again contraindicated (CRI-Off collapse). Next knobs: modest optimizer tuning, minor head width sweep if needed.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating model changes**\n\nI'm considering changes to the BiGRU model since the previous adjustments at head=160 weren't helpful. Maybe I could try modifying the head position or adjusting the gating logit initialization for better bias between DSConv and RNN contributions, although I worry that heavier changes might complicate things.\n\nI'm thinking about adding a residual skip from pooled DSConv to the output head to maintain balanced contributions. Additionally, I should evaluate the possible dilations for DSConv to expand its receptive field, even though the CRI-Off sequence length is relatively small. Adjusting kernel sizes for DSConv could also be interesting.**Planning model adjustments**\n\nI'm leaning towards low-risk strategies, like using tri-seed typed heads and possibly adjusting gating logits to show a slight preference for DSConv, although it’s already learned some patterns.\n\nI’m considering adding dropout scheduling, but it might not yield benefits\
  \ at low risk.\n\nI need to update the results file and also the Private Memory. There's a cooldown period for token management before pruning, but I can still make progress. \n\nFor actions, I’ll submit tri-seed for typed heads with BASE_SEED=7, test a small ablation with hidden sizes, and run an evaluation with a data-dependent MLP gate. I'll need to queue multiple runs for this!**Clarifying submission process**\n\nI need to keep in mind the \"submission cooldown\" — it allows for earlier submissions of pairs, so as long as the cooldown doesn't restrict me, I can submit seed=7 for the typed heads.\n\nI should ensure that I import the correct module path from the previously written file for building the network. Adding 'tags' as before is a good idea, and I need to make sure to format the YAML correctly, especially with colons.\n\nI should update the summary file after my submissions and possibly refresh the Archive Paper addendum if we see results from the tri-seed tests.**Considering\
  \ performance improvements**\n\nI’m thinking about adding a Private Memory capsule aimed at improving the CRI-Off average to 0.678 or higher. My hypothesis is that CRI-Off may benefit from interactions from sequence pairing. A potential approach could be using 1D DSConv with group-wise cross-correlation across channels to address mismatch features.\n\nI’m also considering \"pairwise channel mixing\" by pairing positions mod 2, although I've tried using two distinct windows for the \"even/odd cross-mix,\" and that didn't help. Additionally, I might lower dropout in the regression head to 0.05, but parameters apply globally, which complicates things.**Planning submission processes**\n\nI can set the dropout rate to be head-specific, while keeping the BATCH_SIZE constant. My plan is to submit the seed=7 for typed heads along with a small tweak using optax.sam for sharpness-aware minimization, which could enhance generalization.\n\nSince it requires two forward passes and the training loop\
  \ expects standard gradient transformations, I'll avoid that for now. Instead, I’m considering tweaking AdamW’s betas to 0.98 for stabilizing CRI-Off and reducing the gradient clipping value to 0.8 to manage outlier gradients effectively. \n\nI’ll queue two runs: one for the typed heads and the other with my optimizer adjustments. Additionally, I need to ensure my YAML quoting is correct as I work on the content code referencing the required module. Time to submit my actions!"
