parts:
- text: "Proceeding with two low-risk probes to improve CRI-Off without sacrificing average: widen regression head and increase SE reduction.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Typed heads: widen regression head (HH_reg=192) on SE-shared DSConv + mean↔LSE + BiGRU — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, bigru, task-heads, optimization\"\nabstract: \"Regression head widened to 192 to improve CRI-Off mapping on the SE-calibrated shared DSConv + mean↔LSE + BiGRU backbone with typed heads; others unchanged (PRS/Modif=128, ncRNA=96). Tests if extra capacity lifts CRI-Off without harming average.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_taskheads_typed import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size':\
    \ 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4,\n          'head_hidden_map': {\n              'regression': 192,\n              'multilabel_regression': 128,\n              'multilabel_classification': 128,\n              'multiclass_classification': 96\n          }\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n                         optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"\
    [Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Typed heads: stronger SE reduction (reduction=8) on SE-shared DSConv + mean↔LSE + BiGRU — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, bigru, task-heads, regularization\"\nabstract: \"Increase SE reduction to 8 (stronger regularization) on the shared DSConv backbone with typed heads (reg=160; PRS/Modif=128; ncRNA=96). Tests if lighter channel re-scaling improves CRI-Off stability without hurting others.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_taskheads_typed import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'ds_dilations':\
    \ [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 8,\n          'head_hidden_map': {\n              'regression': 160,\n              'multilabel_regression': 128,\n              'multilabel_classification': 128,\n              'multiclass_classification': 96\n          }\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n                         optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/typed_heads_results.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Typed Task\
    \ Heads — Tri-seed and Optimizer Probe (Tick 397)\n  Tri-seed typed heads (reg=160; PRS/Modif=128; ncRNA=96; clip=1.0):\n  - 607 (seed=42): 0.6750 | CRI-Off 0.0766 | CRI-On 0.4949 | PRS 0.5547 | MRL 0.8955 | APA 0.8519 | Modif 0.9499 | ncRNA 0.9015\n  - 608 (seed=123): 0.6757 | CRI-Off 0.0787 | CRI-On 0.5096 | PRS 0.5527 | MRL 0.8979 | APA 0.8558 | Modif 0.9488 | ncRNA 0.8862\n  - 612 (seed=7):  0.6755 | CRI-Off 0.0760 | CRI-On 0.5126 | PRS 0.5496 | MRL 0.8918 | APA 0.8605 | Modif 0.9503 | ncRNA 0.8877\n  → Tri-seed mean ≈ 0.6754; consistent CRI-On ↑ vs SE-only; CRI-Off ~0.076–0.079.\n\n  Optimizer tweak (AdamW β2=0.98, clip=0.8):\n  - 613 (seed=42): 0.6745 | CRI-Off 0.0820 | CRI-On 0.5008 | PRS 0.5596 | MRL 0.8896 | APA 0.8553 | Modif 0.9492 | ncRNA 0.8846\n  → Trade-off: CRI-Off ↑ to 0.082 but avg ↓ ~0.0009; MRL/ncRNA slightly down; PRS ↑.\n\n  Next probes (submitted):\n  - HH_reg=192 (seed=42) to lift CRI-Off without regularization side-effects.\n  - SE reduction=8 (seed=42) to test\
    \ gentler channel scaling and stability.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Exploring architecture adjustments**


  I''m considering another potential variant for my model. Maybe I should add a small dropout in the regression head or adjust its hidden width to strengthen mapping. Previously, BiGRU 192 didn''t show improvements, but it could be worth testing reg=192 this time. I''m also contemplating different pooling methods for targeted tasks while maintaining the core architecture. Additionally, adjusting the SE reduction ratio to 8 might help with generalization. Let''s keep exploring these possibilities!**Planning ablation experiments**


  I think we should run two small ablation tests: set SE reduction to 8 and regression head width to 192, both using the default settings of clip=1.0 and AdamW with b2=0.999. Now, I remember that the earlier default was AdamW with b1=0.9. I also want to consider testing gradient centralization or a strongly clipped value to keep improvements. We need to update our results file and maybe jot down next steps in Private Memory. Let''s plan on submitting new experiments!**Submitting actions with updates**


  We''re planning to submit two separate actions: one with typed heads set to reg=192 and the other with reg=160 while applying SE reduction=8. I think we should use seed=42 for both to keep them comparable. There''s been some confusion about submission cooldowns, but since we’re at tick 397, it seems like we may be good to go. I also want to log the updated typed heads results from the tri-seed stats and note the effects of the optimizer tweak.**Preparing for Archive update**


  I’m considering going to the Archive to reply with an Addendum update after finishing the tri-seed tests. It seems I''ve just updated last tick, so I can provide the tri-seed results and comments. I need to respond in a chat format and ensure to process any /execute_action commands clearly. I’ll draft my actions, starting with research and then submitting the reg=192 typed heads and the se_reduction=8 typed heads. I''ll also maintain the default settings for the optimizer. Let’s keep it efficient!**Finalizing storage updates**


  I’m going to write the results to the typed_heads_results.md file, including the tri-seed numbers and the optimizer ablation. I might also update the archive addendum through a reply, and that''s fine. I could propose setting a rank score filter to check the scoreboard, but it might not be necessary. I need to ensure to limit tags to six and then move to the Archive Room to submit. I''ll customize the head_hidden_map as well, so let’s get those commands written out!'
