parts:
- text: "Queued and monitoring. Submitting one more small optimizer probe to bracket clip strength while awaiting results.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Typed heads + optimizer tweak: clip=1.2 (AdamW default) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"optimization, gradient-clipping, dsconv, typed-heads\"\nabstract: \"Bracketing study: test global-norm clipping at 1.2 (vs 1.0 default and 0.8 which raised CRI-Off but hurt avg). Same SE-shared DSConv + mean↔LSE + BiGRU with typed heads.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_taskheads_typed import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n\
    \          'ds_dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'pre_norm': True,\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4,\n          'head_hidden_map': {\n              'regression': 160,\n              'multilabel_regression': 128,\n              'multilabel_classification': 128,\n              'multiclass_classification': 96\n          }\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.2),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{rank author}`\n`/execute_action{page_size 20}`"
thinking_content: "**Considering updates and tests**\n\nI should update the Archive addendum with the tri-seed result of 612 and the optimizer effect of 613. I’ve already written the typed_heads_results.md, so now I’m wondering if I should also conclude the typed heads SOTA gap, which remains about 0.011. Maybe I should shift focus to the DSConv channel width or dilation schedules, but that could be more complex. Testing another DSConv block or varying the dilation pattern seems like an option, even with the small sequence lengths. Positional encodings are another area for improvement.**Evaluating positional encoding and updates**\n\nImplementing positional encoding requires some code changes to DSConv. I could add a small sinusoidal adjustment to the input channels, which should be allowed by the system's submission functions. However, this new direction may lead to increased tokens and development time. Since there are already two ongoing experiments, it might be wise to update the Archive\
  \ and plan minor parameter changes after reviewing the results. I also need to keep track of results in the dual_expert_summary while considering submission cooldown periods between experiments.**Exploring token management and actions**\n\nThe last output from token management indicated a cooldown, meaning I can only perform another prune at tick 399. Since it's currently at tick 398, I won't prune just yet. I could create a Private Memory update, but that doesn’t seem necessary. Setting the page sort to author or score might help monitor submissions. I’ll also draft a plan document, \"next_moves.md,\" ensuring I adhere to YAML quoting rules. We need to keep actions concise, like going to the research counter and ranking authors based on submissions.**Updating summaries and planning next steps**\n\nI can write a new summary of tri-seed results and decisions in the \"noema/results/summary_tick398.md\" file. However, we just updated the typed_heads_results.md, and since tri-seed has concluded,\
  \ I'd note that the mean is 0.6754, proposing default adoption and mentioning the CRI-Off improvement with the optimizer. Since we've already included those details, I won't duplicate them. Instead, I can prepare a code change file to support the \"se_reduction\" parameter in the build_network, and propose trying out a clip of 1.1 later. For now, I can also check ranked scores and increase the page size to see more results.**Planning actions and submissions**\n\nI’m proposing to update the archive reply to include tri-seed results, but I believe that’s already done. Now, I want to keep actions minimal: monitoring the scoreboard and continuing after results. I should execute commands to rank authors and potentially update the results file regarding the tri-seed conclusion, though that’s already been done. \n\nI can create a Private Memory entry for the stop criteria, but I think monitoring is enough for now. I could propose to run an ablation with options like gradient clipping or adjusting\
  \ beta2. Submitting one additional ablation, like widening the regression head, might be too heavy right now. Instead, I’ll go for a submission of \"clip=1.2\" since that earlier adjustment improved CRI-Off. I’ll craft the submission, ensuring that the create_optimizer function returns the right setup and keeping tags within limits. Let's write that out!"
