parts:
- text: "Implementing a direct hybrid dual-path (DSConv mean+max + motif max) replication to target CRI-Off, then submitting a run.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Hybrid Dual-Path DSConv with Mean+Max pooling and a Conv-Motif specialized path.\n  - Shared DSConv backbone (5 dilated blocks, d_model=256)\n  - Main path: concat[global mean, global max] of DSConv features\n  - Specialized path: 1D Conv(k=5) + GELU + Dropout -> global max\n  - Fusion: concat(main_path, specialized_path) -> Dropout -> LayerNorm\n  - Task-specific heads: 128-dim MLP + dropout -> output\n  Universal across datasets; no dataset-specific logic.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n\
    \          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n      }\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          # Depthwise conv\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                      dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME',\n                      name='dw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          # Pointwise conv\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x =\
    \ nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class SharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Project input to d_model\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = x\n          for i, d in enumerate(self.dilations):\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, name=f'dsconv_{i}')(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n     \
    \     z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return z.squeeze(-1) if self.d_output == 1 else z\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class ClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class HybridDualPath(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = SharedBackbone(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          # Main path: mean + max\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          main_feat = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n          # Specialized motif path\n          m = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='motif_conv')(h)\n          m = nn.gelu(m)\n          m = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(m, deterministic=deterministic)\n          motif_feat = jnp.max(m, axis=1)\n          # Fuse\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_feat,\
    \ motif_feat], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm(name='fused_ln')(fused)\n          # Heads\n          if self.task_type == 'regression':\n              return RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression':\n              return MultiLabelRegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_classification':\n              return ClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == 'multiclass_classification':\n              return ClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f'Unknown\
    \ task_type: {self.task_type}')\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = HybridDualPath(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              d_model=int(hp.get('d_model', 256)),\n              num_blocks=int(hp.get('num_blocks', 5)),\n              dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              motif_kernel_size=int(hp.get('motif_kernel_size', 5)),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n\
    \          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Dual-Path (DSConv mean+max + motif max) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, mean-max, motif, dual-path, heads\"\nabstract: \"Shared DSConv backbone with hybrid pooling (mean+max) fused with a Conv-motif path (k=5, max-pool). LayerNorm before 128-d task heads. Unified\
    \ across datasets. Tests if this SOTA-aligned dual-path raises CRI-Off while maintaining average.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads import build_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n\
    `/execute_action{storage write noema/results/plan_next.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum (Tick 401): Direct Hybrid Dual-Path replication queued.\n  - Implemented DSConv mean+max main path + Conv-motif(k=5) specialized path with max pooling; LN before 128-d task heads.\n  - Submission: seed=42. Goal: approach CRI-Off ≥0.11 with avg ≥0.682.\n  Decision gates:\n  - If CRI-Off shows large gain with acceptable averages, tri-seed and integrate as alternative head in paper (with trade-offs vs BiGRU path and typed heads).\n  - Else, finalize typed heads as default (<1M params, strong CRI-On) and position hybrid as negative/partial result.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Determining next steps**\n\nI'm assessing our next actions based on the current context at tick 401. I’ve compared the SOTA evaluations, where a significant high was noted, and I'm looking into our typed heads SE with the DSConv approach, which has shown varying results. The optimizer settings have had mixed effects, and the small adjustments in SE haven’t yielded the expected improvements. To enhance CRI-Off, I'll consider proposing strategies based on the successful architecture I see in the Veritas II model.**Analyzing code differences**\n\nI’m delving into the code from evaluation 562 to spot differences. The architecture includes a Dual-Path Task Specific Head Network, featuring a common model dimension and shared blocks. It combines a hybrid pooling approach and a specialized convolutional motif detector. Notably, they don’t use BiGRU, focusing instead on a distinct motif path that seems crucial for CRI-Off performance. Our previous attempts with the motif path\
  \ didn’t boost CRI-Off, especially when combined with mean and max pooling. It appears we need to rethink our approach!**Assessing training parameters and architecture**\n\nThe SOTA achieved a CRI-Off score of 0.1365, but there were warnings about Spearman correlation being NaN at times. Their extended training up to 72 epochs likely helped because our process typically stops earlier after 14-31 epochs. While we're limited to certain functions, I wonder if we can adjust the architecture for depth and gating specific to the CRI-Off dataset without violating the unified approach. The SOTA’s motif path appears to enhance performance across tasks, taking advantage of specialized motifs that improve detection, which could be crucial for our model.**Exploring pairwise interactions**\n\nI’m considering the possibility of using pairwise interaction convolution across channels. This could involve integrating cross-channel multiplicative interactions or Toeplitz correlation features to resemble\
  \ mismatch alignments, while keeping it generalized for different tasks and not tied to a specific dataset. However, using depth-wise separable convolutions might not sufficiently capture base complement interactions. \n\nI could propose adding a \"pairwise k-mer co-occurrence\" path with 1x1 convolutions to enhance our feature set across channels, although that could complicate the shape.**Evaluating cross-correlation pooling and architecture differences**\n\nI'm exploring the idea of implementing a \"cross-correlation pooling\" path where one half of the sequence is convolved with the reversed second half. While this approach can be generalized, it might lean towards being dataset-specific. Previous attempts with bi-window pooling yielded unstable results, indicating the importance of hybrid pooling strategies seen in SOTA. \n\nAlso, I notice they used a specific architecture without BiGRU, and long training times seem essential for CRI-Off improvement. So, maybe adapting our dropout\
  \ and avoiding complexity in the architecture could bring better results, allowing for more epochs without overfitting. Finally, it might be necessary to replicate that successful motif path approach explicitly.**Planning architecture replication**\n\nI think the best path forward is to implement a \"head dropout schedule\" or \"weight decay\" to slow down training without altering the loop. I can adjust the learning rate globally to 0.001. Using a dropout rate of 0.15 or 0.2 could help regulate performance. Our previous attempts with mean+max pooling haven’t performed well on CRI-Off, so maybe I’ll adapt the architecture to replicate the SOTA model by focusing on their feature fusion method. \n\nI’ll aim to create our model file, ensuring it aligns with SOTA while being permissible for submission. Ultimately, this way we can explore achieving better results under our own framework!"
