tick: 402
role: model
parts:
- text: "Submitting a tri-expert variant that fuses DSConv pooled features, BiGRU, and a motif conv path via learnable scalar gating; then logging the plan while 625 runs.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/tri_expert_pool_gru_motif.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Tri-Expert RNA model:\n    - Shared DSConv backbone (5 dilated depthwise-separable conv blocks, d_model=256)\n    - Expert A (Pooling): learned mix(mean, LSE τ=0.25, length-normalized)\n    - Expert B (BiGRU): BiGRU(160) over per-base embeddings (Dense to GRU dim), final states concat\n    - Expert C (Motif): 1D Conv(k=5) + GELU + Dropout -> global max\n    - Fusion: learnable scalar gate over the 3 expert projections (softmax on logits); post-fusion LayerNorm\n    - Heads: task-specific 128-d MLP with dropout\n  Universal across datasets; no dataset-specific logic.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special\
    \ import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          # pooling\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n      }\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau: float, length_normalize: bool = True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          # Depthwise (grouped) conv with dilation\n     \
    \     x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                      dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME',\n                      name='dw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          # Pointwise\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class SharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Dense projection to hidden features\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = x\n          for i, d in enumerate(self.dilations):\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, name=f'ds_{i}')(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  class ExpertPooling(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      tau: float\n      length_normalize_lse: bool\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          lse_pool = _lse_pool(h, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          w = self.param('mix_w', lambda rng, shp: jnp.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=h.dtype), (2,))\n          w = jax.nn.softmax(w)\n          pooled = w[0] * mean_pool + w[1] * lse_pool\n          return pooled\n\n  class ExpertBiGRU(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # Project\
    \ to GRU dim\n          xin = nn.Dense(self.gru_dim, name='gru_in')(x)\n          f = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hf = f(xin)[:, -1, :]\n          b = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hb = b(jnp.flip(xin, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n          rep = jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)\n          rep = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim, name='gru_proj')(rep)\n          return rep\n\n  class ExpertMotif(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic=True):\n          m = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='motif_conv')(h)\n          m = nn.gelu(m)\n          m = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(m, deterministic=deterministic)\n          rep = jnp.max(m, axis=1)\n          rep = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim, name='motif_proj')(rep)\n          return rep\n\n  class HeadRegression(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n\
    \      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return out.squeeze(-1) if self.d_output == 1 else out\n\n  class HeadGeneric(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class TriExpertNetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      gru_dim: int = 160\n      tau:\
    \ float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = SharedBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          rep_a = ExpertPooling(self.hidden_dim, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          rep_b = ExpertBiGRU(self.gru_dim, self.hidden_dim)(x)\n          rep_c = ExpertMotif(self.hidden_dim, self.motif_kernel_size, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          # Projections (already projected to hidden_dim within experts)\n          # Fusion: learnable scalar gate over 3 experts\n          logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros((3,), dtype=rep_a.dtype), (3,))\n          w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n          fused = w[0] * rep_a + w[1] * rep_b + w[2] * rep_c\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6, name='post_ln')(fused)\n          #\
    \ Heads\n          if self.task_type == 'regression':\n              return HeadRegression(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression':\n              return HeadGeneric(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_classification':\n              return HeadGeneric(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == 'multiclass_classification':\n              return HeadGeneric(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f'Unknown task_type: {self.task_type}')\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = TriExpertNetwork(\n          \
    \    d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(hp.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              gru_dim=int(hp.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n              tau=float(hp.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(hp.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              motif_kernel_size=int(hp.get('motif_kernel_size', 5)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n\
    \          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Tri-expert gated: Pool(mean↔LSE τ=0.25) + BiGRU(160) + Motif(k=5) — scalar gate + post-LN — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, tri-expert, pooling, bigru, motif, gating\"\nabstract: \"Three complementary experts atop a shared DSConv backbone: learned mix(mean, length-normalized LSE τ=0.25), BiGRU(160), and Conv-motif(k=5) with max pooling; fused by learnable scalar gate and post-fusion LayerNorm.\
    \ Typed 128-d heads. Tests CRI-Off gains without sacrificing average.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from tri_expert_pool_gru_motif import build_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete]\
    \ {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/plan_next.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Plan update (Tick 402):\n  - Reviewed SOTA 562 (CRI-Off 0.1365) and baseline 369. Key delta vs our best appears to be a strong motif pathway fused with mean+max main path; we implemented two probes:\n    • 625: Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max + motif) — running.\n    • NEW: Tri-expert gated (pool mean↔LSE + BiGRU + motif) with scalar gating and post-LN — submitted (seed=42).\n  - Acceptance criteria: avg ≥0.676 with CRI-Off ≥0.085 (ideally ≥0.10) without major regressions; else document as negative and keep typed-heads default (~0.6754).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Managing compute tasks**\n\nI see that we can calculate parameter counts and training compute, but there's limited action allowed. I need to pay attention to token usage, which is currently 47%. The user seems to want us to take action and issue commands for research. I realize there's room for one more evaluation to run concurrently, so I could try \"SE reduction=8 seed=7\" or test something else, but recent tri-seeding hasn't shown significant improvements. I might replicate the typed heads with adjusted settings to enhance performance.**Exploring dropout parameters**\n\nI’m thinking about testing the parameter \"head_dropout_regression=0.05,\" but it seems the current code might not allow for per-task dropout. The file 'dual_expert_dsconv_shared_backbone_se_taskheads_typed.py' likely maps differently. We could propose a new submission code wrapper to introduce 'head_drop_map' for typed heads, but that’s not available right now. Instead, I might need to either create\
  \ a new file or adjust the existing one to accept dropout mapping properly. I'll have to think carefully about the internal structure needed for this!**Considering alternative strategies**\n\nI'm exploring an alternative approach that doesn't require modifying the module itself. I could set the 'dropout_rate' globally to 0.08, but I remember that reducing it previously impacted PRS negatively, though that was with a different setup. Another idea is to tweak the 'learning_rate' to 0.0008, but the effect of a smaller learning rate is uncertain. Given the tight timeline, I could propose running a \"Hybrid Dual-Path gating\" strategy to enhance CRI-Off, while also planning to submit the tri-seed once the current task completes.**Exploring improvements for CRI-Off**\n\nI’m considering that a smaller \"head_intermediate_dim,\" like 96, might help reduce overfitting and improve CRI-Off. However, with the current setup involving typed heads and dropout at 0.10, I remember we already adjusted the\
  \ width for the head in the concat path. Testing a \"regression head hidden 96\" could reduce capacity and may improve Spearman, but I'm not very optimistic about it. It might be better to run \"standard typed heads\" with stronger weight decay to help CRI-Off, though that could interact across tasks. It's important to log this run and prepare to finalize the paper while aiming for stability.**Planning gating and experiments**\n\nI want to attempt one more ablation, setting \"gate_temp=1.2\" to see if we can enhance performance. I could create a new file for typed heads, but I don’t have the existing code on hand. Instead, I can propose a simple integration for the scalar gate using softmax. With concurrency, I can submit a run for the gating temperature typed heads now as a second evaluation after the current one completes. \n\nAdditionally, I could consider incorporating a specialized motif path while keeping the changes manageable, like testing a tri-expert gating network for potential\
  \ gains.**Implementing tri-expert architecture**\n\nI need to ensure that our code compiles properly, and considering the heaviness of it, I’ll aim for moderate code. We're moving forward with implementing 'tri_expert_pool_gru_motif.py' and submitting a tri-expert gating model that utilizes pooling, BiGRU, and motif features.\n\nI’ll define the DSConv backbone using Flax and manage different tasks for the heads typed: regression, multilabel regression, multilabel classification, and multiclass classification. The input will be embedded using Dense layers, with pooling based on mean and LSE, followed by RNN and convolutional features. \n\nOnce the code is drafted, I'll store it and ensure everything is formatted correctly for submission!"
