parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 403\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 132,574 / 270,000 used (49%)\n- Agent Age: 110 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Hybrid Dual-Path (DSConv mean+max + motif max) — seed=42' (ID: 625) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6878150766886633\n**APA_R2:** 0.8559\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0873\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9518\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4992\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5709\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8957\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9538\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 625\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS**\
    \ - Fixed a parameter naming error in Flax Conv layer that prevented network initialization.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code in `storage/noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads.py` used an incorrect parameter name when calling `nn.Conv()`. The code attempted to use `dilation=(self.dilation,)` as a parameter, but Flax's Conv layer expects this parameter to be named `kernel_dilation`, not `dilation`.\n\nSpecifically, in the `DSConvBlock` class at line 40-43:\n```python\n# INCORRECT (original code):\nx = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            dilation=(self.dilation,),  # ❌ Wrong parameter name\n            padding='SAME',\n            name='dw')(x)\n```\n\nThis resulted in the error:\n```\nTypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the parameter name from `dilation` to `kernel_dilation` in the depthwise convolution layer:\n\
    \n```python\n# CORRECT (fixed code):\nx = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),  # ✅ Correct parameter name\n            padding='SAME',\n            name='dw')(x)\n```\n\nSince the buggy code was in a READ-ONLY lineage file (`storage/noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads.py`), the fix was implemented by:\n1. Copying the affected classes (`DSConvBlock`, `SharedBackbone`, `HybridDualPath`, and `WrappedRNANetwork`) into `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n2. Applying the parameter name fix to the copied `DSConvBlock` class\n3. Keeping the working classes (`RegressionHead`, `MultiLabelRegressionHead`, `ClassificationHead`) as imports from the lineage file\n4. Importing the working `create_optimizer` function from the lineage file\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission_v2.py runs successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing\
    \ (exit code 0), indicating the fix was successful. The code is now executing the full training pipeline without errors.\n\n## Technical Details\n- **File Modified**: `submissions/submission_v2.py` (new file created with fix)\n- **Error Type**: Incorrect Flax API parameter name\n- **Fix Type**: Simple parameter rename from `dilation` to `kernel_dilation`\n- **Classes Affected**: `DSConvBlock` (where the error occurred), plus `SharedBackbone`, `HybridDualPath`, and `WrappedRNANetwork` (which depend on DSConvBlock)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n\n# Import everything EXCEPT DSConvBlock, SharedBackbone, and HybridDualPath which we'll fix locally\nfrom dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads import (\n    RegressionHead, MultiLabelRegressionHead, ClassificationHead,\n \
    \   WrappedRNANetwork as OriginalWrappedRNANetwork,\n    create_optimizer\n)\n\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n    }\n\n# FIXED VERSION: Changed 'dilation' parameter to 'kernel_dilation'\nclass DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        residual = x\n        # Depthwise conv - FIXED: changed 'dilation' to 'kernel_dilation'\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                    kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                    feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n\
    \                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                    padding='SAME',\n                    name='dw')(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        # Pointwise conv\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw')(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return residual + x\n\nclass SharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilations: Sequence[int]\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # Project input to d_model\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        h = x\n        for i, d in enumerate(self.dilations):\n            h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate,\
    \ name=f'dsconv_{i}')(h, deterministic)\n        return h\n\nclass HybridDualPath(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        h = SharedBackbone(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n        # Main path: mean + max\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n        max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n        main_feat = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n        # Specialized motif path\n        m = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='motif_conv')(h)\n        m = nn.gelu(m)\n        m = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(m, deterministic=deterministic)\n        motif_feat = jnp.max(m, axis=1)\n \
    \       # Fuse\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([main_feat, motif_feat], axis=-1)\n        fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        fused = nn.LayerNorm(name='fused_ln')(fused)\n        # Heads\n        if self.task_type == 'regression':\n            return RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression':\n            return MultiLabelRegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_classification':\n            return ClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type == 'multiclass_classification':\n            return ClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n        else:\n\
    \            raise ValueError(f'Unknown task_type: {self.task_type}')\n\nclass WrappedRNANetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n        hp = hparams or {}\n        self.net = HybridDualPath(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            d_model=int(hp.get('d_model', 256)),\n            num_blocks=int(hp.get('num_blocks', 5)),\n            dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n            kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n            motif_kernel_size=int(hp.get('motif_kernel_size', 5)),\n            dropout_rate=float(hp.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n        )\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n\
    \        if deterministic:\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\n\
    Testing APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n\
    ✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout:\
    \ 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0105 |  0.4630  | 0.4630 \n 20  | 0.0076 |  0.4866  | 0.4866 \n 30  | 0.0065 |  0.4144  | 0.4992 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 31 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4992 Time:23s\n[Complete] CRI-On val_metric=0.4991747031637281\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.499175\nTraining time: 30s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\
