parts:
- text: "Great result: Hybrid Dual-Path hit 0.6878 with CRI-Off 0.0873. I’ll fix the DSConv dilation API locally to avoid debugger dependence and replicate across seeds. Then I’ll correct the tri-expert module for upcoming runs.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_fixed.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Hybrid Dual-Path DSConv with Mean+Max main path + Conv-Motif specialized path.\n  Fixed DSConv depthwise conv to use kernel_dilation (Flax API).\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n      }\n\n  class\
    \ DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          # Depthwise conv: use kernel_dilation (Flax API)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME',\n                      name='dw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          # Pointwise conv\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class SharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size:\
    \ int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = x\n          for i, d in enumerate(self.dilations):\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, name=f'dsconv_{i}')(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return z.squeeze(-1) if self.d_output == 1 else z\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class ClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class HybridDualPath(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n      dropout_rate:\
    \ float = 0.10\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = SharedBackbone(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          # Main path: mean + max\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          main_feat = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n          # Specialized motif path\n          m = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='motif_conv')(h)\n          m = nn.gelu(m)\n          m = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(m, deterministic=deterministic)\n          motif_feat = jnp.max(m, axis=1)\n          # Fuse\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_feat, motif_feat], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm(name='fused_ln')(fused)\n          # Heads\n          if self.task_type\
    \ == 'regression':\n              return RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression':\n              return MultiLabelRegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_classification':\n              return ClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == 'multiclass_classification':\n              return ClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f'Unknown task_type: {self.task_type}')\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = HybridDualPath(\n\
    \              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              d_model=int(hp.get('d_model', 256)),\n              num_blocks=int(hp.get('num_blocks', 5)),\n              dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              motif_kernel_size=int(hp.get('motif_kernel_size', 5)),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n        \
    \      return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n                         optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/tri_expert_pool_gru_motif_v2.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Tri-Expert gated model (Pooling mean↔LSE τ=0.25, BiGRU, Motif) — kernel_dilation fix.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n         \
    \ 'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'gru_dim': 160,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n      }\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau, length_normalize=True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME',\n                      name='dw')(x)\n\
    \          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class SharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = x\n          for i, d in enumerate(self.dilations):\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, name=f'ds_{i}')(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  class ExpertPooling(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      tau: float\n      length_normalize_lse:\
    \ bool\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          lse_pool = _lse_pool(h, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          w = self.param('mix_w', lambda rng, shp: jnp.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=h.dtype), (2,))\n          w = jax.nn.softmax(w)\n          return w[0] * mean_pool + w[1] * lse_pool\n\n  class ExpertBiGRU(nn.Module):\n      gru_dim: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          xin = nn.Dense(self.gru_dim, name='gru_in')(x)\n          f = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hf = f(xin)[:, -1, :]\n          b = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n          hb = b(jnp.flip(xin, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n          rep = jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)\n          rep = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim, name='gru_proj')(rep)\n          return\
    \ rep\n\n  class ExpertMotif(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic=True):\n          m = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='motif_conv')(h)\n          m = nn.gelu(m)\n          m = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(m, deterministic=deterministic)\n          rep = jnp.max(m, axis=1)\n          rep = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim, name='motif_proj')(rep)\n          return rep\n\n  class HeadMLP(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      squeeze_last: bool = False\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return out.squeeze(-1) if self.squeeze_last else out\n\n\
    \  class TriExpertNetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      gru_dim: int = 160\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = SharedBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          rep_a = ExpertPooling(self.hidden_dim, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          rep_b = ExpertBiGRU(self.gru_dim, self.hidden_dim)(x)\n          rep_c = ExpertMotif(self.hidden_dim, self.motif_kernel_size, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros((3,), dtype=rep_a.dtype), (3,))\n          w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n          fused = w[0]\
    \ * rep_a + w[1] * rep_b + w[2] * rep_c\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6, name='post_ln')(fused)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression':\n              return HeadMLP(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, squeeze_last=True)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type in ('multilabel_regression', 'multilabel_classification', 'multiclass_classification'):\n              return HeadMLP(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, squeeze_last=False)(fused, deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f'Unknown task_type: {self.task_type}')\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = TriExpertNetwork(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(hp.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size',\
    \ 7)),\n              dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              gru_dim=int(hp.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n              tau=float(hp.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(hp.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              motif_kernel_size=int(hp.get('motif_kernel_size', 5)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x,\
    \ deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n                         optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n```\n\nSubmitting a stability replicate for the Hybrid Dual-Path using the fixed module (seed=7).\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max + motif max) — seed=7 — fixed kernel_dilation\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, mean-max, motif, dual-path, stability\"\nabstract: \"Replication of the Hybrid Dual-Path that reached 0.6878 (seed=42), using a fixed module (kernel_dilation) to avoid debugger changes. Tests stability; target is avg ≥0.686 with CRI-Off ≥0.085.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_fixed\
    \ import build_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/plan_next.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (Tick 403) — Hybrid Dual-Path success and next steps\n  - 625 (seed=42): 0.6878 | CRI-Off 0.0873 | PRS 0.5709 | ncRNA\
    \ 0.9538 — near-SOTA avg; CRI-Off improved over typed-heads but below Veritas (0.1365).\n  - Submitted stability replicate: Hybrid Dual-Path seed=7 using fixed kernel_dilation implementation.\n  - Tri-expert gated (pool+BiGRU+motif) pending (628); fixed tri-expert module saved for future runs.\n\n  Next gates:\n  - If Hybrid tri-seed (42/7/123) averages ≥0.686 with CRI-Off ≥0.085, adopt as competitive variant and document trade-offs vs typed-heads (CRI-On ↑) and DSConv baselines.\n  - Then probe motif kernel k∈{3,7}, and optional main-path mean+max vs mean+LSE mix (keep params <1M).\n  - If tri-expert outperforms on CRI-Off without avg loss, replicate and consider defaulting to tri-expert.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning next steps**


  I’m looking to take action based on the previous results and ongoing evaluations. The Hybrid Dual-Path method shows promise with a score of 0.6878, but it’s just shy of the state-of-the-art benchmarks. I need to plan next steps for the Tri-expert variant while focusing on stabilizing the Tri-seed for score 625. Tuning gating or head size and considering LSE pooling are options I want to explore further in order to enhance our results and maintain compliance.**Updating code and archive**


  I need to update the archive and add results to the paper addendum. I’ll also fix the DSConv dilation parameter in the lineage code to improve stability and avoid future debugging. The current file can’t be modified because it’s read-only, but I can write to my own lineage storage path. To be cautious, I will save a corrected copy as ''noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_v2.py'' for future submissions and import from that file instead.**Updating tri-expert code**


  I noticed the tri-expert code is currently using the correct ''kernel_dilation'' in the DSConvBlock, but we previously had an error with the ''dilation'' parameter. In the tri_expert code, we need to ensure ''dilation'' is accurately referenced to prevent issues. Since the current configuration, 628, is already submitted, I can’t change that. So I’ll proactively correct both the tri_expert and hybrid modules for future runs. Also, I need to plan PR activities focusing on tri-seeds and consider adapting gating or head dropout strategies. I''ve got enough tokens available too!**Planning next steps**


  I’m set to write the corrected tri_expert file with ''kernel_dilation'' and do the same for the hybrid file. I need to submit tri-seed replication for 625 using seeds 7 and 123 while referencing the corrected module to avoid debugger issues. I’ll create a new file, ''dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_fixed.py,'' for this. Besides, I need to consider submitting tri-seed replicates for hybrid as well. I’ll also update the results summary and check the paper for mentioning our recent achievement. Lastly, I should manage tokens while being aware of the concurrency limit!**Submitting experiments and updates**


  Right now, only experiment 628 is running while 625 is finished. I believe we can submit up to one or possibly two new experiments. Given that guideline, I''ll assume we can submit one more and go ahead with a replication for seed=7. I need to write the corrected module ''dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_fixed.py'' and ensure it includes ''kernel_dilation.'' I’ll also update the tri_expert file and prepare a results log summarizing the improvements, making sure to follow the YAML quoting rules. Let’s carefully structure this!'
