parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 404\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 143,919 / 270,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 111 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Tri-expert gated: Pool(mean↔LSE τ=0.25) + BiGRU(160) + Motif(k=5) — scalar gate + post-LN — seed=42' (ID: 628) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6850457169390953\n**APA_R2:** 0.8573\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0841\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9512\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4963\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5644\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8974\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9446\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report\
    \ for Evaluation 628\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the Flax Conv parameter bug. The code is now running without crashing (300+ seconds execution confirmed).\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported `tri_expert_pool_gru_motif` from the agent's lineage directory (`storage/noema/submissions/`). This module contained a bug in the `DSConvBlock` class where it used the incorrect parameter name for Flax's `nn.Conv`:\n\n**Incorrect (line 55 in original):**\n```python\nx = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            dilation=(self.dilation,),  # WRONG PARAMETER NAME\n            padding='SAME',\n            name='dw')(x)\n```\n\n**Error:**\n```\nTypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'\n```\n\nFlax's `nn.Conv` expects `kernel_dilation` not `dilation` as the parameter name.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v3.py` with a complete standalone implementation\
    \ that includes the corrected parameter:\n\n**Correct:**\n```python\nx = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),  # FIXED\n            padding='SAME',\n            name='dw')(x)\n```\n\n### Why Complete Rewrite Was Necessary\nInitial attempt (v2) tried to override just the `DSConvBlock` class while still importing from the buggy module. This didn't work because:\n1. The submission imported `build_network` from the lineage module\n2. That module's internal references still used the buggy `DSConvBlock`\n3. Python imports are resolved at module load time, so the override had no effect\n\nThe solution was to create a completely standalone implementation with all classes defined locally, eliminating any dependency on the buggy lineage file.\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing (timeout threshold)\n- Exit code:\
    \ 0 (success)\n- The evaluation is still running (likely training the model), which is expected behavior\n- Original error (`TypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'`) no longer occurs\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Fixed File:** `submissions/submission_v3.py`\n- **Classes Copied:** All network components from `tri_expert_pool_gru_motif.py`\n- **Single Line Change:** `dilation=` → `kernel_dilation=` in `DSConvBlock.__call__`\n- **Verification Method:** 300-second timeout monitoring (standard success threshold)\n\n## Recommendation\nThe agent (Noema II) should update their lineage file `storage/noema/submissions/tri_expert_pool_gru_motif.py` with the correct parameter name to prevent future submissions from encountering this same error.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\n\"\"\"\nTri-Expert\
    \ RNA model with fixed DSConvBlock (kernel_dilation parameter fix)\nComplete standalone implementation without buggy imports.\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nfrom jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 256,\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n        'gru_dim': 160,\n        'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n        'tau': 0.25,\n        'length_normalize_lse': True,\n    }\n\ndef _lse_pool(h, tau: float, length_normalize: bool = True):\n    L = h.shape[1]\n    core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n    if length_normalize:\n        core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n    return tau * core\n\nclass DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation:\
    \ int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        residual = x\n        # Depthwise (grouped) conv with dilation - FIXED: kernel_dilation instead of dilation\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                    kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                    feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                    padding='SAME',\n                    name='dw')(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        # Pointwise\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw')(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return residual + x\n\nclass SharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilations: Sequence[int]\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self,\
    \ x, deterministic=True):\n        # Dense projection to hidden features\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        h = x\n        for i, d in enumerate(self.dilations):\n            h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, name=f'ds_{i}')(h, deterministic)\n        return h\n\nclass ExpertPooling(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    tau: float\n    length_normalize_lse: bool\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n        lse_pool = _lse_pool(h, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n        w = self.param('mix_w', lambda rng, shp: jnp.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=h.dtype), (2,))\n        w = jax.nn.softmax(w)\n        pooled = w[0] * mean_pool + w[1] * lse_pool\n   \
    \     return pooled\n\nclass ExpertBiGRU(nn.Module):\n    gru_dim: int\n    hidden_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # Project to GRU dim\n        xin = nn.Dense(self.gru_dim, name='gru_in')(x)\n        f = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n        hf = f(xin)[:, -1, :]\n        b = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_dim))\n        hb = b(jnp.flip(xin, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n        rep = jnp.concatenate([hf, hb], axis=-1)\n        rep = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim, name='gru_proj')(rep)\n        return rep\n\nclass ExpertMotif(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h, deterministic=True):\n        m = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='motif_conv')(h)\n        m = nn.gelu(m)\n        m = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(m, deterministic=deterministic)\n        rep = jnp.max(m, axis=1)\n        rep = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim,\
    \ name='motif_proj')(rep)\n        return rep\n\nclass HeadRegression(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    hidden: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n        return out.squeeze(-1) if self.d_output == 1 else out\n\nclass HeadGeneric(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    hidden: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\nclass TriExpertNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    hidden_dim: int = 256\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n    dropout_rate:\
    \ float = 0.10\n    gru_dim: int = 160\n    tau: float = 0.25\n    length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n    motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = SharedBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n        rep_a = ExpertPooling(self.hidden_dim, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n        rep_b = ExpertBiGRU(self.gru_dim, self.hidden_dim)(x)\n        rep_c = ExpertMotif(self.hidden_dim, self.motif_kernel_size, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n        # Projections (already projected to hidden_dim within experts)\n        # Fusion: learnable scalar gate over 3 experts\n        logits = self.param('fusion_logits', lambda rng, shp: jnp.zeros((3,), dtype=rep_a.dtype), (3,))\n        w = jax.nn.softmax(logits)\n        fused = w[0] * rep_a + w[1] * rep_b + w[2] * rep_c\n        fused = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6, name='post_ln')(fused)\n\
    \        # Heads\n        if self.task_type == 'regression':\n            return HeadRegression(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression':\n            return HeadGeneric(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_classification':\n            return HeadGeneric(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type == 'multiclass_classification':\n            return HeadGeneric(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f'Unknown task_type: {self.task_type}')\n\nclass WrappedRNANetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n        hp = hparams or {}\n        self.net = TriExpertNetwork(\n            d_output=d_output,\n\
    \            task_type=task_type,\n            hidden_dim=int(hp.get('hidden_dim', 256)),\n            kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n            dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n            dropout_rate=float(hp.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n            gru_dim=int(hp.get('gru_dim', 160)),\n            tau=float(hp.get('tau', 0.25)),\n            length_normalize_lse=bool(hp.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n            motif_kernel_size=int(hp.get('motif_kernel_size', 5)),\n        )\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n\
    \                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating\
