- text: "Submitting the hybrid dual-path tri-seed replicate (seed=123) using the fixed module, then logging results and next probes.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max + motif max) — seed=123 — fixed kernel_dilation\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, mean-max, motif, dual-path, stability\"\nabstract: \"Tri-seed replication of the Hybrid Dual-Path that reached 0.6878 (seed=42). Using the fixed kernel_dilation implementation to avoid debugger patches. Target: avg ≥0.686 with CRI-Off ≥0.085.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_fixed import build_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n\
    \      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/hybrid_dual_path_results.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max main + motif max) — Results (Tick 404)\n  - 625 (seed=42): 0.6878 | CRI-Off 0.0873 | PRS 0.5709 | MRL 0.8957 | ncRNA 0.9538 | APA 0.8559 | Modif 0.9518 | CRI-On 0.4992\n  - 628 (tri-expert gated): 0.6850 | CRI-Off 0.0841 | PRS 0.5644 | MRL 0.8974 | ncRNA 0.9446 | APA 0.8573 | Modif 0.9512 | CRI-On 0.4963\n  In-flight:\n  - 630 (seed=7, fixed kdilation) — stability replicate for Hybrid Dual-Path\n  - NEW: seed=123 (fixed kdilation) —\
    \ completes tri-seed for Hybrid Dual-Path\n\n  Notes:\n  - Hybrid Dual-Path reaches near-SOTA averages with improved CRI-Off vs typed heads; still below Veritas II CRI-Off (0.1365).\n  - Tri-expert adds motif + BiGRU + pooling; slight avg drop vs Hybrid DP but close, keeping CRI-Off ~0.084.\n\n  Next queued when slots free:\n  - Hybrid DP motif kernel sweep: k ∈ {3, 7} (compare vs k=5 baseline, seed=42).\n  - Optional: main-path aggregator swap (mean+LSE vs mean+max) to evaluate CRI-Off trade-offs under Hybrid DP.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning experiment submissions**\n\nI can submit two experiments now, which is great! I'll propose submitting the hybrid dual-path replicate with seed 123 using a fixed module (ID 631) and the hybrid dual-path variant with motif_kernel_size 7 and seed 42. \n\nI might compare motif k=3 versus k=7 with seed 42 to see how it stacks with the previous results. We have a concurrency limit, so I'll fill the slots effectively: hybrid fixed seed 123 and the hybrid variant focusing on the new path. Let's see how it goes!**Deciding on experiment submissions**\n\nI think I'll go with the motif k=7 variant, using seed 42 for comparability since seed 42 is set for the baseline. We could also consider updating our paper, given our near-SOTA results with fewer parameters. But for now, my focus is on utilizing the available slots. \n\nI need to fix the tri_expert module with kernel_dilation and refer to the new results log. So here’s the plan: I’ll submit the hybrid fixed module with\
  \ seed 123 and the hybrid variant with motif_kernel_size 7 using seed 42. Time to implement these actions!**Planning submission actions**\n\nI'm ready to submit my second action: a hybrid dual-path with motif k=7 using seed 42 and the fixed kernel_dilation. I need to adjust my hyperparameters to set 'motif_kernel_size' to 7. Additionally, I should commit the dual expert summary to storage and correct the older tri_expert module for future use. \n\nI have to watch the concurrency limit, which is currently safe because there’s only one evaluation running. However, if I submit two new experiments, it might exceed the concurrent limit of two pending evaluations. I need to be careful with this!**Reviewing submission limits**\n\nI’m considering the current situation: there’s the experiment 630 running, and if I try to submit two new evaluations, that would mean three concurrent, which exceeds the limit of two. I remember running into this issue before when submitting a third while two were active.\n\
  \nTo stay within safe limits, I should only submit one new evaluation for now, maintaining the total at two running experiments. The \"Running Experiments\" table confirms that only one is currently running, so submitting one more should keep us safe.**Finalizing submission actions**\n\nI’ve decided that we should only submit one additional job at a time. It makes sense to prioritize the seed=123 replicate to complete the tri-seed. After submitting that, I’ll wait until the next tick to submit the motif k=7 variant. I’ll also write this plan to our 'plan_next' document and consider updating the summary in 'hybrid_dual_path_results.md'. \n\nSo, here’s the plan: I’ll submit with seed=123, update the summary, and ensure proper YAML formatting for any titles. Let's get that response ready!"
