tick: 405
role: model
parts:
- text: "Resubmitting corrected seed=123 for Hybrid Dual-Path (alias fix), and probing motif kernel k=7.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max + motif max) — seed=123 — fixed alias\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, mean-max, motif, dual-path, stability\"\nabstract: \"Resubmission of the Hybrid Dual-Path tri-seed replicate with a fixed optimizer alias to avoid recursion. Target: avg ≥0.686 with CRI-Off ≥0.085.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_fixed import build_network, create_optimizer as create_optimizer_impl\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return\
    \ build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer_impl(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max + motif max, k=7) — seed=42 — kernel sweep\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, mean-max, motif, dual-path, ablation\"\nabstract: \"Motif kernel sweep for the Hybrid Dual-Path: increase motif kernel to k=7 (vs k=5 baseline). Tests PRS/CRI-Off gains while preserving avg near 0.686.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_fixed import build_network, create_optimizer as create_optimizer_impl\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return\
    \ {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 7,  # swept from 5 -> 7\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer_impl(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/hybrid_dual_path_results.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Hybrid Dual-Path — Running log (Tick 405)\n  Completed:\n  - 625 (seed=42): 0.6878 | CRI-Off 0.0873 | PRS 0.5709 | MRL 0.8957 | ncRNA 0.9538\n  - 630 (seed=7, fixed kdilation): 0.6853 | CRI-Off 0.0756 | PRS 0.5651\
    \ | MRL 0.8941 | ncRNA 0.9462\n  - 628 (tri-expert gated): 0.6850 | CRI-Off 0.0841 | PRS 0.5644 | MRL 0.8974 | ncRNA 0.9446\n\n  Issues:\n  - 633 (seed=123) failed due to optimizer name recursion; resubmitted with alias fix.\n\n  In-flight:\n  - Hybrid DP seed=123 (alias fix) — tri-seed completion.\n  - Hybrid DP motif kernel sweep: k=7 (seed=42).\n\n  Notes:\n  - Hybrid DP is near-SOTA avg with improved CRI-Off vs typed heads (~0.087 vs ~0.078), though below Veritas II CRI-Off 0.1365.\n  - Next: if tri-seed ≥0.686 and CRI-Off ≥0.085, consider adopting Hybrid DP; else document as competitive variant and proceed with motif k sweep and potential mean+LSE main-path swap.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning experiment adjustments**\n\nI need to address the failed seed=123 hybrid, while noting that we have 630 successful runs with seed=7 and 633 failures, but no active experiments currently. We can fix and resubmit the corrected seed=123. It’s also essential to propose a motif kernel sweep for k=3 and k=7, but I want to avoid excessive runs. For now, I think I’ll submit two: the correct 123 replicate and one motif at k=7. I'll ensure proper logging and follow YAML rules too. I must also set up an alias for the optimizer to prevent recursion issues.**Planning gating and submissions**\n\nI should think about gating: if the tri-seed passes, we’ll adopt it as a near-SOTA variant; otherwise, we’ll consider tri-expert. My plan includes submitting the corrected seed=123 replicate and using an alias import for that action. Then, I’ll submit the motif kernel sweep run using a motif size of 7 and the same seed 42, though k could also be 3. I’ll update the 'hybrid_dual_path_results.md'\
  \ for all corrections and consider updating 'plan_next.md' later. Ensuring the 'create_optimizer' alias is essential, and I’ll craft the necessary code accordingly.**Preparing motif run and commands**\n\nFor the motif run with k=7, I’ll import `build_network` and set `create_optimizer` as `make_opt`. In `_define_hyperparameters`, I'll add the motif kernel size of 7. The dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_fixed module is already set to return the optimizer chain. I need to prepare a log message, considering the possibility of including additional tri-expert seeds, but we're limited to two concurrent runs. I’ll ensure we are in Research Counter and that I only output commands and YAML with minimal commentary. \n\nLet’s submit the necessary commands and log updates for the corrected seed and motif kernel.**Documenting the resubmission**\n\nI should note in the document that the \"corrected seed=123 has been resubmitted\" and reference it as the alias \"fix.\" This is a straightforward way to keep\
