tick: 406
role: model
parts:
- text: "Solid progress: Hybrid Dual-Path is near-SOTA and stable; tri-expert is close. While runs 636/637 are pending, I’ll prep the main-path aggregator swap (mean+LSE vs mean+max) with length-normalized LSE τ and log next steps.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_agg_variants.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Hybrid Dual-Path DSConv with configurable main-path aggregator:\n    - Shared DSConv backbone (5 dilated depthwise-separable conv blocks, d_model=256)\n    - Main path: aggregator in {'mean_max', 'mean_lse'} -> concatenated stats\n        * mean_max: concat(global mean, global max)\n        * mean_lse: concat(global mean, length-normalized LSE(τ))\n    - Specialized motif path: Conv1D(k=motif_kernel_size) + GELU + Dropout -> global max\n    - Fusion: concat(main_path, motif_path) -> Dropout -> LayerNorm\n    - Heads: task-specific 128-d MLP + dropout\n  Flax Conv uses kernel_dilation (correct API).\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict,\
    \ Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',  # or 'mean_max'\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n      }\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau: float, length_normalize: bool = True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME',\n                      name='dw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class SharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n\
    \          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = x\n          for i, d in enumerate(self.dilations):\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, name=f'dsconv_{i}')(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def _main_path_features(h, aggregator: str, tau: float, length_normalize_lse: bool):\n      mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n      if aggregator == 'mean_max':\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          return jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n      elif aggregator == 'mean_lse':\n          lse_pooled = _lse_pool(h, tau, length_normalize_lse)\n          return jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, lse_pooled], axis=-1)\n      else:\n          raise ValueError(f'Unknown aggregator: {aggregator}')\n\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic:\
    \ bool = True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return z.squeeze(-1) if self.d_output == 1 else z\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class ClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return\
    \ nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class HybridDualPath(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      aggregator: str = 'mean_lse'\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = SharedBackbone(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          main_feat = _main_path_features(h, self.aggregator, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          m = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='motif_conv')(h)\n          m = nn.gelu(m)\n          m = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(m, deterministic=deterministic)\n          motif_feat = jnp.max(m, axis=1)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_feat,\
    \ motif_feat], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm(name='fused_ln')(fused)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression':\n              return RegressionHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression':\n              return MultiLabelRegressionHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type in ('multilabel_classification', 'multiclass_classification'):\n              return ClassificationHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f'Unknown task_type: {self.task_type}')\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net\
    \ = HybridDualPath(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              d_model=int(hp.get('d_model', 256)),\n              num_blocks=int(hp.get('num_blocks', 5)),\n              dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              motif_kernel_size=int(hp.get('motif_kernel_size', 5)),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              aggregator=str(hp.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse')),\n              tau=float(hp.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(hp.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n    \
    \      if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/hybrid_dual_path_results.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Hybrid Dual-Path — Status (Tick 406)\n  Completed:\n  - 625 (seed=42, k=5, mean+max): 0.6878 | CRI-Off 0.0873 | PRS 0.5709 | MRL 0.8957 | ncRNA 0.9538\n  - 630 (seed=7, k=5, mean+max, fixed): 0.6853 | CRI-Off 0.0756 | PRS 0.5651\
    \ | MRL 0.8941 | ncRNA 0.9462\n  - 628 (Tri-expert gated): 0.6850 | CRI-Off 0.0841 | PRS 0.5644 | MRL 0.8974 | ncRNA 0.9446\n\n  In-flight:\n  - 636 (seed=123, k=5, mean+max, alias fix) — tri-seed completion\n  - 637 (seed=42, k=7, mean+max) — motif kernel sweep\n\n  Prepared:\n  - dual_path_hybrid_agg_variants.py — supports main-path aggregator swap:\n    * mean_max: concat(mean, max)\n    * mean_lse: concat(mean, LSE(τ), length-normalized)\n\n  Next (after slots free):\n  - Submit Hybrid DP with main-path mean+LSE (τ=0.25, len-norm), k=5 (seed=42), then replicate (7/123).\n  - If tri-seed (k=5, mean+max) ≥ 0.686 avg and CRI-Off median ≥ 0.085, adopt Hybrid DP as competitive variant; else report as near-SOTA and proceed with aggregator swap analysis.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Composing dual path hybrid aggregate**\n\nI'm working on the dual_path_hybrid_agg_variants.py file. First, I’ll implement a DSConvBlock with kernel dilation fix and a SharedBackbone. For computing pooled_main, if the aggregator is 'mean_max', I’ll concatenate the mean and max values. For 'mean_lse', I need to decide between 'mixture' or 'concat'. I'll ensure the fusing from the main path keeps dimensions consistent. Finally, I’ll include pre-fusion dropout and layer normalization before organizing the file accordingly.**Updating tri-expert file and results**\n\nI'm considering making updates to the original tri_expert_pool_gru_motif.py file to set the kernel_dilation parameter and prevent future issues, but since we've already created version 2, it might not be necessary. I plan to update the hybrid_dual_path_results.md with details on tri-seed partial average and acceptance gating. \n\nI’ll write the code to noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_agg_variants.py, and append\
