tick: 408
role: model
parts:
- text: "Hybrid DP status: seed=42 near-SOTA (0.6878, CRI-Off 0.0873); seed=7 solid (0.6853); seed=123 unstable (CRI-Off 0.0397). k=7 motif hurt CRI-Off (0.0705). Mean+LSE runs are pending. Preparing SE-calibrated Hybrid DP to improve stability, then will submit when slots free.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_se.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Hybrid Dual-Path DSConv with Squeeze-and-Excitation (SE) calibration.\n  - Shared DSConv backbone (5 dilated DW+PW conv blocks, d_model=256) with channel SE per block\n  - Main path: concat[global mean, global max] (or configurable)\n  - Specialized motif path: Conv1D(k=motif_kernel_size) + GELU + Dropout -> global max\n  - Fusion: concat(main_path, motif_path) -> Dropout -> LayerNorm\n  - Heads: task-specific 128-d MLP + dropout\n  Flax Conv uses kernel_dilation (correct API).\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n\
    \  from jax.scipy.special import logsumexp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_max',  # or 'mean_lse'\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4\n      }\n\n  def _lse_pool(h, tau: float, length_normalize: bool = True):\n      L = h.shape[1]\n      core = logsumexp(h / tau, axis=1)\n      if length_normalize:\n          core = core - jnp.log(jnp.array(L, dtype=h.dtype))\n      return tau * core\n\n  class SEBlock(nn.Module):\n      channels: int\n      reduction: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x: (B, L, C); squeeze over sequence\n          s =\
    \ jnp.mean(x, axis=1)  # (B, C)\n          hidden = max(1, self.channels // self.reduction)\n          s = nn.Dense(hidden, name='se_fc1')(s)\n          s = nn.gelu(s)\n          s = nn.Dense(self.channels, name='se_fc2')(s)\n          s = jax.nn.sigmoid(s)\n          return x * s[:, None, :]  # broadcast over sequence\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      se_reduction: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          # Depthwise conv with kernel_dilation\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME',\n                      name='dw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          # Pointwise conv\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          # Channel SE calibration\n          x = SEBlock(self.d_model, self.se_reduction, name='se')(x)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class SharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      se_reduction: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = x\n          for i, d in enumerate(self.dilations):\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, self.se_reduction, name=f'dsconv_{i}')(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def _main_path_features(h,\
    \ aggregator: str, tau: float, length_normalize_lse: bool):\n      mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n      if aggregator == 'mean_max':\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          return jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n      elif aggregator == 'mean_lse':\n          lse_pooled = _lse_pool(h, tau, length_normalize_lse)\n          return jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, lse_pooled], axis=-1)\n      else:\n          raise ValueError(f'Unknown aggregator: {aggregator}')\n\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return z.squeeze(-1) if self.d_output == 1 else z\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output:\
    \ int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class ClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class HybridDualPathSE(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      aggregator:\
    \ str = 'mean_max'\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      length_normalize_lse: bool = True\n      se_reduction: int = 4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = SharedBackbone(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations, self.dropout_rate, self.se_reduction)(x, deterministic)\n          main_feat = _main_path_features(h, self.aggregator, self.tau, self.length_normalize_lse)\n          m = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='motif_conv')(h)\n          m = nn.gelu(m)\n          m = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(m, deterministic=deterministic)\n          motif_feat = jnp.max(m, axis=1)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_feat, motif_feat], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm(name='fused_ln')(fused)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression':\n              return RegressionHead(self.d_output,\
    \ hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression':\n              return MultiLabelRegressionHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type in ('multilabel_classification', 'multiclass_classification'):\n              return ClassificationHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f'Unknown task_type: {self.task_type}')\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = HybridDualPathSE(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              d_model=int(hp.get('d_model', 256)),\n              num_blocks=int(hp.get('num_blocks', 5)),\n              dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n\
    \              kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              motif_kernel_size=int(hp.get('motif_kernel_size', 5)),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              aggregator=str(hp.get('aggregator', 'mean_max')),\n              tau=float(hp.get('tau', 0.25)),\n              length_normalize_lse=bool(hp.get('length_normalize_lse', True)),\n              se_reduction=int(hp.get('se_reduction', 4)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n \
    \             return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/hybrid_dual_path_results.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Hybrid Dual-Path — Next probes (Tick 408)\n  Observations:\n  - Tri-seed (k=5 mean+max): 42=0.6878 (CRI-Off 0.0873), 7=0.6853 (0.0756), 123=0.6777 (0.0397) → variance mainly from CRI-Off.\n  - k=7 mean+max (42): 0.6862 but CRI-Off 0.0705 (worse), PRS↑.\n\n  Actions:\n  - Prepared SE-calibrated Hybrid DP (per-block channel SE) to improve stability (file: dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_se.py).\n  - Await mean+LSE main-path results (641/642).\
    \ If positive, combine with SE and tri-seed.\n\n  Criteria:\n  - Adopt if median avg ≥0.686 and CRI-Off ≥0.085 with low variance; else document as competitive variant and pivot to SE + mean+LSE or motif k=3.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nCurrently, two processes are running, so I think we should wait. I can update the logs and prepare the next piece of code. There's a variant of the aggregator code that needs fixing. Additionally, the Reflection Chamber is an option for brainstorming new directions, although the user didn't explicitly ask for it. Once the results are back, I'll write a plan. For now, I’ll just log things and read the completed results of 637 and 636.**Considering next actions**\n\nI’m thinking about what to do next. If the mean and LSE aggregator results come back, I’ll proceed based on that. In the meantime, I can implement the motif kernel variant with k=3 and compare the 'mean_lse' and 'mean_max' aggregators. I should also fix the interactions with the CRI-Off dataset, which has a Spearman metric and a sequence length of 43. I might look into narrower kernels and include channel SE calibration in a dual-path setup to enhance the mapping. I’ll prepare the code\
  \ for that too.**Addressing issues and planning**\n\nI need to address the recursion bug using aliases. It's time to create the code file for adding Squeeze-and-Excitation (SE) to the DSConv backbone. I’m considering whether to introduce gate temperature for balancing features, but our current hybrid uses concatenation instead of gating. Adding a scalar gate could be a new direction, but sticking with concatenation might be simpler. We need to acknowledge the results: 636 shows CRI-Off collapse, and k=7 reduces CRI-Off performance. So, I’ll queue the writing of the SE-enhanced hybrid and log all actions for the new submission file.**Implementing Squeeze-and-Excitation**\n\nI'm planning to implement Squeeze-and-Excitation (SE) by performing global average pooling across sequences and channels to compute the channel weights. Typically, in SE for 1D convolutions, I’ll squeeze across the sequence to get per-channel weights. For each time step, I’ll use the mean across the sequence axis, leading\
  \ to (batch, channels), followed by two linear layers for reduction and sigmoid activation. I’ll incorporate this SE module inside the DSConvBlock after the pointwise convolution or after the block output. While I won’t submit more runs right now due to concurrency limits, I’ll prepare the code and update the documentation accordingly.**Finalizing SE implementation plans**\n\nI’m considering adjustments to the aggregators, like unifying 'mean+max' and 'mean+LSE' into the SE variant later. I should also rename the function for creating the optimizer to 'create_optimizer_impl' to prevent overshadowing. While writing to storage, I’ll define the storage file for the optimizer correctly. My commands will include updates for the results and code storage, and I might consider a visit to the Reflection Chamber for brainstorming, although it's optional. \n\nLet’s finalize the code for the DSConvBlock, focusing on computing SE after the pointwise convolution. After applying the necessary transformations,\
  \ I'll return the modified outputs. I'll summarize past results, emphasize action plans for the SE variant, and log my progress."
