parts:
- text: "Submitting SE-calibrated Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max main, motif k=5) for stability, seeds 42 and 123; then logging.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Dual-Path + SE (mean+max main, motif k=5) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, mean-max, motif, dual-path\"\nabstract: \"SE-calibrated Hybrid Dual-Path: DSConv backbone with per-block SE (reduction=4), main path concat(mean,max), motif conv k=5. Tests stability and CRI-Off vs non-SE variant.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_se import build_network, create_optimizer as create_optimizer_impl\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n        \
    \  'aggregator': 'mean_max',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer_impl(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Dual-Path + SE (mean+max main, motif k=5) — seed=123\"\ntags: \"dsconv, squeeze-excitation, pooling, mean-max, motif, dual-path\"\nabstract: \"Replication (seed=123) of SE-calibrated Hybrid Dual-Path to assess stability and CRI-Off variance. Same config as seed=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_se import\
    \ build_network, create_optimizer as create_optimizer_impl\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_max',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'length_normalize_lse': True,\n          'se_reduction': 4\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer_impl(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/hybrid_dual_path_results.md}`\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Hybrid Dual-Path — SE calibration submissions (Tick 409)\n  Mean+LSE main-path hurt CRI-Off (641: 0.0428; 642: 0.0708). Motif k=7 (637) also reduced CRI-Off (0.0705).\n  Best so far: k=5 mean+max — 625 (seed=42): 0.6878 | CRI-Off 0.0873; 630 (seed=7): 0.6853 | 0.0756; 636 (seed=123): 0.6777 | 0.0397 (unstable).\n\n  New runs:\n  - SE-calibrated Hybrid DP (per-block SE reduction=4), main-path mean+max, motif k=5 — seeds {42,123} to test if SE improves CRI-Off stability without avg loss.\n\n  Next (if slots free after SE results):\n  - Motif kernel k=3 probe (expect potential CRI-Off increase).\n  - If SE stabilizes CRI-Off ≥0.085 median with avg ≥0.686, tri-seed and adopt; else report as competitive variant and finalize paper addendum.\n```"
