tick: 410
role: model
parts:
- text: "SE runs are pending. Preparing a regression-calibrated Hybrid DP variant to de-risk CRI-Off variance (task-type dropout + L2 feature norm for regression tasks), and logging the plan. No new submissions now to respect the 2-run concurrency.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max main + motif max, k=5) with regression calibration:\n    - Shared DSConv backbone (5 dilated DW+PW conv blocks, d_model=256), kernel_dilation fix\n    - Main path: concat(global mean, global max)\n    - Motif path: Conv1D(k=5) + GELU + Dropout -> global max\n    - Fusion: concat -> Dropout -> LayerNorm\n    - Regression calibration:\n        * Task-type-specific head dropout (regression heads use lower dropout, default 0.05)\n        * L2 normalization of fused features before regression head (stabilizes Spearman-heavy tasks)\n    - Heads: 128-d MLP + dropout\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any,\
    \ Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'reg_head_dropout': 0.05,   # lower dropout for regression tasks\n      }\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                    \
    \  padding='SAME',\n                      name='dw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class SharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = x\n          for i, d in enumerate(self.dilations):\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, name=f'dsconv_{i}')(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return z.squeeze(-1) if self.d_output == 1 else z\n\n  class GenericHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class HybridDualPathRegCal(nn.Module):\n   \
    \   d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      reg_head_dropout: float = 0.05\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = SharedBackbone(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          main_feat = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n          m = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='motif_conv')(h)\n          m = nn.gelu(m)\n          m = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(m, deterministic=deterministic)\n          motif_feat = jnp.max(m, axis=1)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_feat, motif_feat], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm(name='fused_ln')(fused)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression':\n              return RegressionHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.reg_head_dropout, l2_norm_input=True)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression':\n              return GenericHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type in ('multilabel_classification', 'multiclass_classification'):\n              return GenericHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f'Unknown task_type: {self.task_type}')\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = HybridDualPathRegCal(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n\
    \              d_model=int(hp.get('d_model', 256)),\n              num_blocks=int(hp.get('num_blocks', 5)),\n              dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              motif_kernel_size=int(hp.get('motif_kernel_size', 5)),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              reg_head_dropout=float(hp.get('reg_head_dropout', 0.05)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n     \
    \         return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/hybrid_dual_path_results.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Hybrid Dual-Path — Regression calibration prepared (Tick 410)\n  Findings:\n  - Mean+LSE main path (τ=0.25) degraded CRI-Off: 641 (42) 0.0428; 642 (123) 0.0708.\n  - Motif k=7 reduced CRI-Off vs k=5 (637: 0.0705).\n  - Best remains k=5 mean+max: 625 (42) 0.0873; 630 (7) 0.0756; 636 (123) 0.0397 (unstable).\n\n  Prepared (no submission until slots free):\n  - dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py: adds task-type regression calibration\n\
    \    • L2 feature normalization before regression heads\n    • Lower regression head dropout (0.05)\n  Goal: reduce CRI-Off variance (esp. seed=123) while preserving avg.\n\n  Next:\n  - After SE runs (646/647) finish, submit:\n    • RegCal Hybrid DP (k=5, mean+max), seeds {42,123}\n    • Motif k=3 ablation (k=3, mean+max), seed=42\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning improvements for CRI-Off**\n\nI need to figure out the next steps, like preparing a motif kernel with a variant for k=3 to improve CRI-Off, as the agent suggested. Seeing a drop in CRI-Off indicates a mapping issue, possibly in the dataset. I’m considering recalibrating components like head dropout or using pre-head layer normalization. We've previously added pre-head LN, which showed promise, but for hybrid dual paths, I wonder if widening the regression head would help. To avoid getting lost in hyper-parameter adjustments, I could focus on incorporating pairwise cross-correlation features.**Exploring pairwise features for CRI-Off**\n\nI'm considering the usual SOTA, which combines motif convolution and hybrid methods, but I've noticed that CRI-Off sometimes benefits from using pairwise mismatch features. The idea is to create a generic \"pairwise interaction\" channel through a 1D convolution over either element-wise multiplication or absolute differences.\
  \ However, this introduces the challenge of dataset specificity. Other datasets use single sequences, but we might generate cross-correlation features across all datasets. While this may seem meaningless for some tasks, it won’t cause harm. I’m also considering a position-wise self outer product to reduce dimensions through bilinear convolution.**Refining architectural rules for datasets**\n\nAccording to Station rules, the architecture must remain consistent across datasets, though I can tailor the final layers for different prediction types. I’m considering adding a dataset-agnostic \"interaction\" path that computes convolution over pairwise channel products, which could enhance CRI-Off without causing issues elsewhere. Another possibility is introducing a small depthwise convolution with a kernel size of 1 across the channels. I’m also pondering feature standardization for Spearman metric tasks, but noting that we can't change the loss function and must evaluate with Spearman while\
  \ training with MSE.**Addressing training instabilities in CRI-Off**\n\nI’m noticing some training instabilities, with an early stopping at epoch 15 for CRI-Off using seed 123. This might suggest head overfitting or insufficient correlation. I think tuning dropout could help — perhaps setting it to 0.05 specifically for regression tasks while keeping it at 0.1 for classification. The code supports task-type-specific adjustments in dropout within the heads, which could benefit CRI-Off. Adding LayerNorm or a unit-norm constraint on fused features for regression tasks might also stabilize things, even if I can’t change the training loop directly.**Implementing regression improvements**\n\nI’m considering a custom module for regression tasks, allowing for task-type-specific adaptations, like gradient clipping. We also found and fixed the seed alias recursion bug! Next up, I need to submit a motif k=3 variant for CRI-Off improvement and adjust the regression head dropout to 0.05 with L2 normalization\
  \ on features. I notice that we're limited to two concurrent submissions, so I'll prepare the code modules without submitting them yet. \n\nI'll create the dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py module and document the changes while updating logs and plans. I’ll ensure the code avoids naming conflicts, implement the required parameters, and efficiently store everything for future use."
