tick: 411
role: model
parts:
- text: "Submitting two focused probes: regression calibration to stabilize CRI-Off on the unstable seed, and motif kernel k=3 ablation to test CRI-Off gains.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max + motif max, k=5) + RegCal (L2, head_dropout=0.05) — seed=123\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, motif, dual-path, regression-calibration\"\nabstract: \"Regression-calibrated Hybrid Dual-Path: L2 normalization of fused features before regression heads and lower regression head dropout (0.05). Goal: reduce CRI-Off variance (esp. seed=123) while preserving near-SOTA average.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal import build_network, create_optimizer as create_optimizer_impl\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n\
    \          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'reg_head_dropout': 0.05\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer_impl(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max + motif max, k=3) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, mean-max, motif, dual-path, ablation\"\nabstract: \"Motif kernel ablation for Hybrid Dual-Path: k=3 (vs k=5 baseline). Hypothesis: shorter motifs may improve CRI-Off (short guide/target).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_fixed\
    \ import build_network, create_optimizer as create_optimizer_impl\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 3,  # ablation: 3 vs 5\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer_impl(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/hybrid_dual_path_results.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Hybrid Dual-Path — Targeted Probes (Tick 411)\n  New submissions:\n\
    \  - RegCal (L2 + reg head dropout=0.05) — seed=123: mitigate CRI-Off variance on unstable seed.\n  - Motif k=3 ablation — seed=42: test shorter motifs for CRI-Off uplift.\n\n  Recent findings:\n  - SE (per-block) reduced CRI-Off (646: 0.0464; 647: 0.0508) without avg gains.\n  - Mean+LSE main-path degraded CRI-Off (641: 0.0428; 642: 0.0708).\n  - Best remains non-SE, k=5 mean+max: 625 (seed=42) 0.6878 | CRI-Off 0.0873; 630 (seed=7) 0.6853 | 0.0756; 636 (seed=123) 0.6777 | 0.0397.\n\n  Next:\n  - If RegCal lifts seed=123 CRI-Off (≥0.070) with avg ≥0.683, replicate (seed=42) and report reduced variance.\n  - If k=3 improves CRI-Off ≥0.085 with avg ≥0.686, replicate and consider adopting.\n  - Otherwise finalize Hybrid DP as competitive variant and emphasize typed-heads (CRI-On gains) in paper addendum.\n```"
