tick: 415
role: model
parts:
- text: "Results received: RegCal stabilizes CRI-Off and lifts CRI-On; tri-seed mean ≈ 0.6850. Next, test learned scalar gating between main and motif paths on top of RegCal to push beyond 0.6878 while preserving stability.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP + RegCal + learned scalar gate (main↔motif), k=5 — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, mean-max, motif, gating, calibration, regression\"\nabstract: \"Hybrid Dual-Path with main mean+max and motif max (k=5), augmented with per-sample learned scalar gating between paths and regression calibration (L2 pre-norm + head dropout=0.05). Tests if adaptive fusion improves stability and average score over RegCal-only.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from hybrid_dual_path import build_network  # existing HDP backbone with main+motif\n  # Assumes hybrid_dual_path supports hparams: fusion ('avg'|'scalar_gate'), motif_kernel, regcal_l2, head_dropout\n\
    \n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          # backbone/experts\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'motif_kernel': 5,\n          'main_aggregator': 'mean_max',\n          # fusion + calibration\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',          # learned 2-way softmax gate (main vs motif)\n          'post_norm': True,\n          'regcal_l2': True,                # L2 normalization before regression head\n          'head_dropout': 0.05,             # regression head dropout\n          # optimization\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'grad_clip': 1.0\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds, vm = trial_data.get('dataset'), trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP + RegCal + learned scalar gate (main↔motif), k=5 — seed=123\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, mean-max, motif, gating, calibration, regression, stability\"\nabstract: \"Replication of the learned scalar gate HDP with RegCal at seed=123 to assess stability across seeds. Configuration identical to seed=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from hybrid_dual_path import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'motif_kernel': 5,\n          'main_aggregator': 'mean_max',\n          'fusion': 'scalar_gate',\n          'post_norm':\
    \ True,\n          'regcal_l2': True,\n          'head_dropout': 0.05,\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'grad_clip': 1.0\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds, vm = trial_data.get('dataset'), trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/hybrid_dual_path_results.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Hybrid Dual-Path (HDP) — RegCal + Gating Plan (Tick 415)\n\n  Current baselines:\n  - 625 (HDP mean+max main + motif k=5, seed=42): 0.6878 | CRI-Off 0.0873 | PRS 0.5709 | MRL 0.8957 | ncRNA 0.9538.\n  - RegCal (L2 + head_dropout=0.05):\n\
    \    • 652 (seed=123): 0.6854 | CRI-Off 0.0727 | CRI-On 0.5081\n    • 657 (seed=42):  0.6835 | CRI-Off 0.0870 | CRI-On 0.4790\n    • 658 (seed=7):   0.6860 | CRI-Off 0.0744 | CRI-On 0.5009\n    Tri-seed mean ≈ 0.6850. RegCal stabilizes CRI-Off and lifts CRI-On vs unstable 636 (0.0397).\n\n  Submitted now:\n  - Learned scalar gate between main(mean+max) and motif(max) paths + RegCal (clip=1.0), seeds {42,123}.\n    Goal: exceed 0.6878 while preserving CRI-Off ~0.08 and strong PRS/MRL.\n\n  Next if needed:\n  - Add seed=7 for gating.\n  - Tiny head LR-only warmup (200 steps) or head_dropout=0.06 for PRS polish, if average < 0.688.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Implementing submissions**\n\nI'm working on two submissions: the first one, eval A, is using 'HDP + scalar gate + RegCal (L2, head_dropout 0.05)' with a target to beat 0.6878. The second, eval B, will use 'HDP + scalar gate + RegCal' for stability with a different seed, 123. \n\nI need to execute the research command and submit the first evaluation. I'll wrap the YAML content and ensure the optimizer utilizes AdamW with proper clipping. I'll also update the results log accordingly.**Double-checking details**\n\nI'm reviewing some important details. It seems titles require quoting only if they contain colons or specific special characters. Plus signs appear to be acceptable. For example, in the title \"Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max + motif max, k=5) + RegCal (L2, head_dropout=0.05) — seed=42\", the only issue would be the equals sign, which seems fine.\n\nI’ll also log the tri-seed results, which are: 625 with 0.6878 (best single seed 42), 630 at 0.6853 (seed=7), and 636\
  \ at 0.6777 (seed=123).**Updating tri-seed results**\n\nI'm looking at the tri-seed results after RegCal, which are: 657 with 0.6835, 658 at 0.6860, and 652 with 0.6854, giving a mean of 0.6850. I want to update the 'hybrid_dual_path_results.md' file to reflect these results along with the gating plan.\n\nI need to ensure that the commands are clear and concise while remaining within the token limits. I’ll structure my commands accordingly for the research section and summary write. Also, I need to be cautious with YAML quoting for anything that includes colons, but it seems I'm on the right track!"
