thinking_content: "**Planning evaluation submission**\n\nI need to respond by submitting the third seed gating run again. We hit a limit error during an earlier attempt, but now that the previous seeds are finished, we can move on with seed=7 gating. I also want to document the results—it seems gating decreased CRI-Off values, but the averages might not have improved. If the average is below 0.688, we might need to explore head-only LR warmup or slight head_dropout changes.**Considering gating results**\n\nLooking at the results, gating seems worse. I think I should still complete the tri-seed gating for completeness but plan for the next improvements. A minor head-only LR warmup and tuning head_dropout to 0.06 might help. However, I want to keep things simple and stick to one configuration for a clean comparison. I can queue a second experiment, possibly testing head-only warmup on the HDP baseline. With 77k tokens used, we’re at 29% of our budget, so things look fine for now.**Managing\
  \ token budget and imports**\n\nEarlier, our token budget was high at 78% but has now dropped to 27%, which feels safe. I also need to ensure that module names match real file names to avoid debugger issues. For future submissions, using the correct import path is crucial to prevent auto-debugger overhead. The earlier correct import was “from storage.noema.submissions.dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_gated import build_network.” \n\nAdditionally, I have to align hyperparameter keys, ensuring everything matches properly for smooth processing.**Assessing regcal implementation**\n\nIt seems that regcal (L2 pre-norm and head dropout) might be in a separate file called 'dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py.' However, the gating version may not include the regcal L2 portion, and our gating results haven't recognized the regcal flag. This might mean our runs didn’t apply regcal L2 but did use head_dropout at 0.05. I need to verify if the file 'dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal_gated.py' exists\
  \ for submission, as the debug points to two files concerning gating.**Planning gating and RegCal experiments**\n\nWe definitely need to combine gating with regcal, but there might not be a single file to support both. I’m considering using 'dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py' for RegCal, though it may lack gating capabilities. Since results suggest gating isn't beneficial, I should focus on minimal changes to the baseline RegCal setup. \n\nMy plan includes submitting gating with seed=7 using the correct imports and parameters, and initiating a new experiment for HDP with adjustments like head_dropout set to 0.06. I'll keep track of results carefully while conserving compute resources.**Finalizing gating and results update**\n\nGiven the complexity, I’ve decided to submit only the gating run for seed=7. I’ll update the results file indicating that gating is underperforming, then plan to revert to the fixed average fusion and finalize the paper addendum. I noticed an issue with the\
  \ running experiments section not showing current runs, but once I submit seed=7, that should resolve itself. \n\nI also need to ensure proper import paths and summarize the gating results compared to the RegCal baseline, indicating that we should deprioritize gating moving forward unless a better combined file emerges."
