tick: 418
role: model
parts:
- text: "Gating underperforms; proceeding with a safer optimizer tweak on RegCal HDP to try a small lift.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP + RegCal (L2, head_dropout=0.06) + warmup-cosine LR — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, mean-max, motif, calibration, optimization\"\nabstract: \"Hybrid Dual-Path with mean+max main and motif max (k=5), RegCal head (L2 pre-norm) with slightly stronger head dropout (0.06). Uses global warmup-cosine schedule (200-step warmup) with AdamW+clip. Tests mild optimization polish over RegCal baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import optax\n  # Use verified RegCal implementation path\n  from storage.noema.submissions.dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_max',\n\
    \          'regcal_l2': True,\n          'head_dropout': 0.06,      # slightly stronger than 0.05\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'grad_clip': 1.0\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      # Global schedule: 200-step warmup to LR, cosine decay to 0.5*LR over 20k steps\n      sched = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n          init_value=0.0, peak_value=learning_rate,\n          warmup_steps=200, decay_steps=20000, end_value=learning_rate * 0.5\n      )\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=sched, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds, vm = trial_data.get('dataset'), trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write\
    \ noema/results/hybrid_dual_path_results.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # HDP — RegCal polish vs Gating (Tick 418)\n  Gating (scalar gate) underperformed RegCal:\n  - 659 (seed=42): 0.6814 | CRI-Off 0.0528 | PRS 0.5701 | MRL 0.8976\n  - 660 (seed=123): 0.6798 | CRI-Off 0.0704 | PRS 0.5666 | MRL 0.8983\n  - 662 (seed=7): running\n  RegCal baseline (L2 + head_dropout=0.05) tri-seed ≈ 0.6850 with stable CRI-Off (~0.08).\n\n  Submitted now (seed=42):\n  - RegCal + mild optimization polish: head_dropout=0.06, warmup-cosine LR (200-step warmup), AdamW+clip.\n  Goal: small average lift without harming CRI-Off/PRS/MRL.\n\n  Next:\n  - If neutral, freeze HDP-RegCal as default and conclude gating as negative result.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating module settings**


