- text: "Gating underperforms; focusing on a safer HDP-RegCal tweak (k=7 motif) while seed=123 polish runs.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP + RegCal (L2, head_dropout=0.05), motif k=7 — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, mean-max, motif, calibration\"\nabstract: \"Hybrid Dual-Path with mean+max main and motif max, increasing motif kernel to k=7 under RegCal (L2 pre-norm, head_dropout=0.05). Tests whether broader motif context recovers or exceeds the 0.6878 single-seed baseline while preserving CRI-Off stability.\"\ncontent: |\n  import optax\n  from storage.noema.submissions.dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 7,   # was 5; sweep to 7 under RegCal\n          'aggregator': 'mean_max',\n          'regcal_l2':\
    \ True,\n          'head_dropout': 0.05,\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'grad_clip': 1.0\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds, vm = trial_data.get('dataset'), trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/hybrid_dual_path_results.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # HDP — Current status (Tick 420)\n  - Best single-seed so far: 625 (HDP k=5, mean+max) = 0.6878.\n  - RegCal baseline (L2 + head_dropout=0.05) tri-seed ≈ 0.6850; stable CRI-Off ~0.08.\n  - Gating (scalar) tri-seed avg ≈ 0.6786; CRI-Off degraded → deprecated.\n\
    \  - RegCal polish (head_dropout=0.06 + warmup-cosine):\n    • 663 (seed=42): 0.6833 (neutral vs 657’s 0.6835).\n\n  Submitted now:\n  - RegCal with motif k=7 (seed=42) to test if broader motif context improves average without harming CRI-Off.\n\n  Pending:\n  - 666 (RegCal polish, seed=123) running.\n\n  If neutral:\n  - Freeze HDP-RegCal (k=5) as default; finalize archive addendum with negative gating result and stable near-SOTA performance.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning code adjustments**\n\nI’m thinking we should prepare a clean, minimal code template for HDP RegCal and adjust the aggregator naming to match the actual code used by the debugger. It looks like we should also consider scheduling an ablation for training time versus parameter count. The main tasks involve deprecating gating, freezing the default configuration, and documenting the next plan. It seems our score of 0.6878 slightly exceeds the known state of the art at 0.6866, which is exciting!**Evaluating seed configurations**\n\nI noticed that the top submitted evaluations in the past were around 0.6866. So, our score of 0.6878 might be close to the state of the art or even a new best! I'm considering whether we should run a tri-seed for the HDP baseline with k=5 to confirm this. Previously, seeds 7 and 123 showed varying results, but we improved seed 123 with RegCal. It might be a good idea to tweak the baseline configuration for stability and fairness, ensuring\
  \ we use the same setup across seeds.**Assessing tri-seed performance**\n\nWe’re analyzing the tri-seeds: 657 with 0.6835, 658 at 0.6860, and 652 at 0.6854, which averages to 0.6850, still below our target of 0.6866. I’m considering minor calibrations to improve CRI-Off without degrading its performance. Previous adjustments to CRI-On helped stabilize CRI-Off, while gating had a negative impact. It could be useful to customize head architecture for regression tasks without violating dataset-specific constraints. However, I need to tread carefully to maintain task-type specificity without overstepping.**Updating pooling strategies**\n\nI'm reviewing the \"Bi-Window pooling equal halves\" with seed 42 showing an outlier at 0.6788, which isn’t helpful. The “Even/Odd” approach feels neutral, while “Channel SE calibration” provided small gains with scores around 0.6756 to 0.6758, but they pertain to SE-shared DSConv, not HDP. It looks like the current default setup with HDP RegCal head dropout\
  \ at 0.05 is still the best. I’ll revert to that, finalize the tri-seed documentation, and update \"hybrid_dual_path_results.md\" before proceeding to the archive adjustments.**Planning next steps**\n\nToken usage looks fine, so let's summarize actions to take. First, I’ll write to storage about the negative impact of gating. I can update the archive with addendum content summarizing final conclusions and evaluation IDs. It might be useful to create a SOTA scoreboard to confirm ranks, but it's not necessary. \n\nI plan to submit a run for HDP RegCal with k=7 using seed 42, and I’ll also update \"hybrid_dual_path_results.md\" with this submission. Finally, I can set up to check the leaderboard if needed, keeping everything concise."
