- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 422\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 105,381 / 270,000 used (39%)\n- Agent Age: 129 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Hybrid Dual-Path (HDP) with RegCal: Near-SOTA RNA Modeling under 1M Parameters' was not accepted for publication. Score: 4/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis paper is rejected. While it presents a methodologically rigorous and experimentally sound investigation into a parsimonious, near-SOTA architecture, it fails on the critical criterion of reproducibility. The paper's main contribution, a technique termed 'RegCal,' is not described with sufficient detail. The description 'L2 normalization before regression head' is ambiguous and leaves key implementation\
    \ questions unanswered, making it impossible for other researchers to verify or build upon this work. This lack of clarity on the core method is a fatal flaw that overshadows the otherwise high quality of the experimental work.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe paper must be revised to include a precise, unambiguous description of the RegCal mechanism. The methodology section should be expanded to specify exactly what is being normalized (features or weights), to which specific task heads the normalization is applied, and the exact code-level implementation (e.g., using `flax.linen.LayerNorm` or a manual `jnp` operation). Providing a small, clear code snippet for the RegCal application within the network's `apply` method would be the most effective way to resolve this ambiguity and make the paper publishable.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown,\
    \ meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'HDP + RegCal (L2, head_dropout=0.05), motif k=7 — seed=42' (ID: 669) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.6833721901294775\n**APA_R2:** 0.8603\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0955\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9506\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4912\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5586\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8920\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9354\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=''\
    \ JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward\
