role: model
parts:
- text: "Acknowledged. I’ll resubmit with a precise RegCal specification, including exact code and task mapping to address reproducibility.\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Revised: HDP-RegCal — Precise Specification and Code for Reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"This addendum provides an exact, code-level specification of the RegCal mechanism used in our Hybrid Dual-Path (HDP) architecture. We clarify what is normalized, where it is applied in the forward pass, which task heads receive the normalization, and the exact Flax/JAX implementation. We also list the evaluation IDs demonstrating RegCal’s effect.\"\ncontent: |\n  Scope\n  - Architecture: Hybrid Dual-Path (HDP) = DSConv backbone (5 dilated blocks), main path pooling (mean+max), motif path (1D conv k∈{5,7} + global max), fused into shared features.\n  - Goal of RegCal: stabilize and improve regression-family tasks (APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL; PRS is multilabel regression) by normalizing the feature vector fed to regression\
    \ heads.\n\n  RegCal: Precise Definition\n  - What: Per-sample L2 normalization of the fused feature vector z ∈ R^{B×H} before the regression Dense head(s).\n    z_norm = z / (||z||_2 + ε), where ||z||_2 is over the last (feature) dimension.\n  - Where: Applied in the network forward pass immediately before the final regression head Dense layer(s).\n  - Which heads:\n    • Apply to regression and multilabel regression tasks: {APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL, PRS}.\n    • Do NOT apply to classification tasks: Modif (multilabel classification) and ncRNA (multiclass classification).\n  - Weights: No weight normalization or special constraints; Dense head weights are standard nn.Dense parameters. RegCal is feature-only.\n  - Dropout: A small head dropout is applied after RegCal for regression heads (default 0.05). Classification heads are unchanged from the non-RegCal baseline.\n\n  Exact Code (Flax/JAX)\n  - File reference in lineage storage: storage/noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py\n\
    \  - Minimal, self-contained snippet illustrating the apply() logic around heads:\n\n  ```\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  def l2_normalize(x, eps=1e-6):\n      # x: [B, H]\n      norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n      return x / (norm + eps)\n\n  class HDPHeads(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str                     # \"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\", \"multilabel_classification\", \"multiclass_classification\"\n      head_dropout: float = 0.05         # Used for regression-family heads\n      regcal_l2: bool = True             # Enable/disable RegCal L2 feature norm\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, fused, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # fused: [B, H] shared features after DSConv main+motif fusion\n          if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\"):\n              z = l2_normalize(fused, eps=1e-6) if self.regcal_l2 else fused\n              z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n              y = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)  # d_output=1 for APA/CRI-Off/CRI-On/MRL; d_output=3 for PRS\n              return y.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else y\n\n          elif self.task_type in (\"multilabel_classification\", \"multiclass_classification\"):\n              # Classification heads unchanged; no L2 feature normalization\n              z = fused\n              z = nn.Dropout(rate=0.10)(z, deterministic=deterministic)  # baseline classification dropout\n              y = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)  # d_output=12 (Modif) or 13 (ncRNA)\n              return y\n  ```\n\n  Notes on Integration\n  - The fused feature ‘fused’ is produced by:\n    1) Main path: global mean+max pooling of DSConv features → projection to H.\n    2) Motif path: Conv1D(k) + global max → projection to H.\n    3) Fusion: sum of projections (no gating in the RegCal default). The result is fused ∈ R^{B×H}.\n  - RegCal then\
    \ operates as above, within the head wrapper, only for regression-family tasks.\n\n  Hyperparameters (Reproducible Default)\n  - hidden_dim (H)=256; DSConv kernel=7; dilations=[1,2,4,8,16]\n  - Main pooling: mean+max\n  - Motif kernel: k=5 (k=7 optional, see ablation)\n  - RegCal: regcal_l2=True; head_dropout=0.05 (regression-family only)\n  - Optimizer: AdamW (lr=1e-3), global clip=1.0; batch size=64; early stopping (patience=10)\n  - No pretrained weights; no external data; same architecture across datasets with only heads adapted by task type.\n\n  Evidence and IDs\n  - Baseline HDP (no RegCal):\n    • 625 (seed=42): 0.6878 | CRI-Off 0.0873 | PRS 0.5709 | MRL 0.8957 | ncRNA 0.9538\n    • 630 (seed=7):  0.6853 | CRI-Off 0.0756\n    • 636 (seed=123):0.6777 | CRI-Off 0.0397  (unstable)\n    ⇒ Tri-seed mean ≈ 0.6836\n  - HDP + RegCal (regcal_l2=True, head_dropout=0.05, k=5):\n    • 657 (seed=42): 0.6835 | CRI-Off 0.0870 | PRS 0.5629 | MRL 0.8943\n    • 658 (seed=7):  0.6860 | CRI-Off\
    \ 0.0744 | PRS 0.5677 | MRL 0.8948\n    • 652 (seed=123):0.6854 | CRI-Off 0.0727 | PRS 0.5637 | MRL 0.8957\n    ⇒ Tri-seed mean ≈ 0.6850 with improved/stable CRI-Off (~0.07–0.09).\n  - RegCal polish (head_dropout=0.06 + warmup-cosine LR) was neutral:\n    • 663 (seed=42): 0.6833 | CRI-Off 0.0711\n    • 666 (seed=123):0.6851 | CRI-Off 0.0724\n\n  Negative Result (for completeness)\n  - Scalar gating between main/motif lowered average and degraded CRI-Off:\n    • 659 (seed=42): 0.6814 | CRI-Off 0.0528\n    • 660 (seed=123):0.6798 | CRI-Off 0.0704\n    • 662 (seed=7):  0.6746 | CRI-Off 0.0547\n  - We therefore deprecate gating and recommend RegCal.\n\n  Conclusion\n  - RegCal is a simple, explicit feature normalization inserted immediately before regression heads, improving stability and maintaining near-SOTA performance in a <1M parameter model. The provided code snippet and file reference make the method fully reproducible.\n```"
