parts:
- text: "Waiting for the z-norm capture run to finish; preparing aggregation utilities and checking for outputs.\n\n`/execute_action{storage list noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/tools/aggregate_norms.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import json, os, glob\n  import numpy as np\n\n  IN_DIR = \"storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms\"\n  OUT_MD = \"storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_summary.md\"\n\n  def load_all():\n      data = []\n      for fp in glob.glob(os.path.join(IN_DIR, \"*.json\")):\n          with open(fp, \"r\") as f:\n              j = json.load(f)\n          ds = j.get(\"dataset\")\n          s = j.get(\"summary\", {})\n          data.append((ds, s))\n      return sorted(data, key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n  def fmt_row(ds, s):\n      return f\"| {ds} | {s.get('n', 0)} | {s.get('mean', 0):.3f} | {s.get('std', 0):.3f} | {s.get('q05', 0):.3f} | {s.get('q25', 0):.3f} | {s.get('q50', 0):.3f} | {s.get('q75', 0):.3f} | {s.get('q95', 0):.3f} |\"\n\n\
    \  def main():\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT_MD), exist_ok=True)\n      rows = load_all()\n      if not rows:\n          with open(OUT_MD, \"w\") as f:\n              f.write(\"# HDP-RegCal — Pre-normalization z-norms\\nNo JSON summaries found yet.\\n\")\n          return\n      header = \"| Dataset | N | mean ||z||2 | std | q05 | q25 | q50 | q75 | q95 |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\\n\"\n      body = \"\\n\".join(fmt_row(ds, s) for ds, s in rows)\n      note = \"\\n\\nNote: Values reflect pre-normalization fused feature norms captured on the validation split.\"\n      with open(OUT_MD, \"w\") as f:\n          f.write(\"# HDP-RegCal — Pre-normalization z-norm distributions (validation)\\n\\n\")\n          f.write(header + body + note)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/README_norms.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  HDP-RegCal z-norm capture (validation) — How to interpret\n  - Each JSON in hdp_regcal_norms/{DATASET}.json\
    \ contains summary statistics of ||z||2 computed before RegCal on the fused features for that dataset’s validation set.\n  - Summaries include mean, std, and quantiles (q05..q95).\n  - After the capture run (Eval 677) finishes, run aggregate_norms.py locally or reproduce the table by reading the JSON files to compare scales across regression-family tasks {APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL, PRS}.\n  - Expected: distributions differ across tasks; RegCal (feature L2) aligns scales at the head input, which helps stability (notably CRI-Off).\n```"
thinking_content: '**Monitoring evaluation progress**


  I need to respond with some actions or commentary regarding the evaluation for HDP-RegCal. The evaluation is currently running after reading the train_single.py and defaults. I think waiting for the results is wise, and it could be helpful to draft a summary plan for storage. Once the results are in, I can update the archive. Meanwhile, I can prepare to read the results files and write analysis code to parse the JSON files saved after evaluation completion.**Planning token management and evaluations**


  I’m considering going to Token Management to prune unnecessary tokens, but token usage is at 116,974 out of 270,000, which is fine. I can also submit additional seeds for the z-norm capture to enhance distributions. Each submission runs parallel across seven datasets, but my code collects norms only for regression tasks in each trial while the complete() function operates on a single dataset. After the evaluation completes, I’ll read the JSON files, update the paper with a summary figure highlighting differences, and compute a table with the numbers.**Preparing JSON aggregation**


  My next step is to write a script that aggregates these JSON files. However, I can also do this manually by listing the files in storage, like using ''storage list noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms.'' After the evaluation finishes, I plan to read each file, compute a summary, and create an aggregated file, updating the archive with a new section on "Pre-normalization feature norm distribution differences." Even though I can''t trigger anything now while the evaluation is running, I can definitely set a reminder and work on the analysis aggregator script for later use.**Setting up aggregation plan**


  Given that we want to keep things concise, I’m outlining a plan with some actions. First, I''ll write an aggregator script to ''storage: noema/tools/aggregate_norms.py,'' which will read the JSON files and create a markdown summary with a table. After that, I can either continue with research or take a moment to document everything. I’ll also adjust the ''complete'' function to print "Saved ds z-norm summary." For now, I can attempt to list the contents of ''noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms,'' even if they aren’t present yet. Once EVAL 677 completes, I can manually aggregate the data from the JSONs.**Planning action steps**


  I realize that reading JSONs involves parsing and computing, which means I can manually handle it if the values are there. I’ll first attempt to ''storage list'' for ''noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms'' and then read the JSON files, but they probably aren''t there yet, so a brief wait might help. Additionally, I could create an email to myself or add a README in the results folder outlining the next steps. Although we might want to use a second seed for generalization, the reviewer suggested focusing on measuring across tasks instead. So, I’ll proceed with the following actions: check the storage list, write the aggregator script and a stub README, and optionally note everything in Private Memory while keeping token use to a minimum.'
