  At this point, the process is still running, but I can prepare to aggregate results once it''s finished. I’m considering suggesting token pruning for savings, though I need to think about the cooldown period. Previously, we had a 4-tick cooldown, and now we’re at tick 428; it seems we might be free to prune but may not need it yet since we''ve used only 135k out of 270k tokens. I could also check the storage directory for any existing JSON files, but I''ll wait until the evaluation finishes. Meanwhile, I can set up the aggregator and plan for the upcoming experiments, like norm analysis.**Deciding next steps**


  The next step involves waiting or tackling other tasks. I could initiate a more thorough tri-seed run of HDP-RegCal, but it''s not essential right now. I want to log housekeeping by creating a cross-task descriptive table with an existing script. However, it seems I can only run scripts through a submission''s code, which limits my options. Instead, I could manually compute the aggregated markdown after saving JSONs with my aggregator. I also have the option to add a code patch to include ''z_pre'' in heads, but that requires modifying stored code. During the evaluation, I used a filter to capture last 2D features, which isn''t precise but manageable.**Planning for results update**


  I want to add a plan for a small document update once the results arrive. First, I’ll check the storage list for the relevant files. If there aren’t any, I can prepare a helpful message confirming that we’re waiting. The actions will include checking the storage list at noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms and possibly reading one JSON if it exists. The final output will focus on executing station commands with minimal commentary, ensuring any strings with special characters are properly quoted in YAML. The aggregator script is already set up, which is great!**Planning for increased reliability**


  I want to propose scheduling a second seed capture to boost reliability, but the station only lets us run two concurrent tasks. Currently, we''re running 679, so we could potentially queue another task, but it would need a seed of 123. Each training trial is dataset-specific, with only one dataset''s JSON saving at a time. Once 679 finishes, I expect to see five JSON outputs. I can''t run the aggregator script, but I can manually create a summary from the JSONs. For now, I’ll check the storage list and if there are no files, we’ll wait. I''ll execute that storage list command.'
