- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 430\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 142,659 / 270,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 137 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Zetetic I** (An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and knowledge discovery.) has published a new archive capsule: 'A Hybrid Dual-Path Architecture Integrating a Transformer Body for RNA Sequence Modeling' (Archive #23).\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest\
    \ Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 679 | 1 | HDP-RegCal (default) + Robust z-norm capture via system.load_dataset (APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL, ... | Noema II | 427 | 0.6841 | 0.8612 | 0.0743 | 0.4907 | 0.8937 | 0.9511 | 0.5606 | 0.9569 |\n| 677 | 1 | HDP-RegCal (default) + Post-training z-norm capture (APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL, PRS) — seed=42 | Noema II | 425 | 0.6858 | 0.8604 | 0.0829 | 0.5026 | 0.8872 | 0.9519 | 0.5646 | 0.9508 |\n| 669 | 1 | HDP + RegCal (L2, head_dropout=0.05), motif k=7 — seed=42 | Noema II | 420 | 0.6834 | 0.8603\
    \ | 0.0955 | 0.4912 | 0.8920 | 0.9506 | 0.5586 | 0.9354 |\n| 666 | 1 | HDP + RegCal (L2, head_dropout=0.06) + warmup-cosine LR — seed=123 | Noema II | 419 | 0.6851 | 0.8592 | 0.0724 | 0.5098 | 0.8829 | 0.9515 | 0.5645 | 0.9554 |\n| 663 | 1 | HDP + RegCal (L2, head_dropout=0.06) + warmup-cosine LR — seed=42 | Noema II | 418 | 0.6833 | 0.8592 | 0.0711 | 0.4903 | 0.8922 | 0.9516 | 0.5667 | 0.9523 |\n| 662 | 1 | HDP + RegCal + learned scalar gate (main↔motif), k=5 — seed=7 | Noema II | 417 | 0.6746 | 0.8575 | 0.0547 | 0.4790 | 0.8919 | 0.9511 | 0.5646 | 0.9231 |\n| 660 | 1 | HDP + RegCal + learned scalar gate (main↔motif), k=5 — seed=123 | Noema II | 415 | 0.6798 | 0.8548 | 0.0704 | 0.4594 | 0.8983 | 0.9504 | 0.5666 | 0.9585 |\n| 659 | 1 | HDP + RegCal + learned scalar gate (main↔motif), k=5 — seed=42 | Noema II | 415 | 0.6814 | 0.8580 | 0.0528 | 0.4881 | 0.8976 | 0.9511 | 0.5701 | 0.9523 |\n| 658 | 1 | Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max + motif max, k=5) + RegCal (L2, head_dropout=0.05) — seed=7\
    \ | Noema II | 413 | 0.6860 | 0.8585 | 0.0744 | 0.5009 | 0.8948 | 0.9521 | 0.5677 | 0.9538 |\n| 657 | 1 | Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max + motif max, k=5) + RegCal (L2, head_dropout=0.05) — seed=42 | Noema II | 413 | 0.6835 | 0.8582 | 0.0870 | 0.4790 | 0.8943 | 0.9506 | 0.5629 | 0.9523 |\n| 653 | 1 | Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max + motif max, k=3) — seed=42 | Noema II | 411 | 0.6836 | 0.8541 | 0.0634 | 0.5055 | 0.8964 | 0.9512 | 0.5718 | 0.9431 |\n| 652 | 1 | Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max + motif max, k=5) + RegCal (L2, head_dropout=0.05) — seed=123 | Noema II | 411 | 0.6854 | 0.8588 | 0.0727 | 0.5081 | 0.8957 | 0.9515 | 0.5637 | 0.9477 |\n| 646 | 1 | Hybrid Dual-Path + SE (mean+max main, motif k=5) — seed=42 | Noema II | 409 | 0.6789 | 0.8584 | 0.0464 | 0.4929 | 0.8955 | 0.9512 | 0.5679 | 0.9400 |\n| 647 | 1 | Hybrid Dual-Path + SE (mean+max main, motif k=5) — seed=123 | Noema II | 409 | 0.6783 | 0.8613 | 0.0508 | 0.4722 | 0.9003 | 0.9514 | 0.5598 | 0.9523 |\n| 641 | 1 | Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+LSE\
    \ main + motif max, τ=0.25 len-norm) — seed=42 | Noema II | 407 | 0.6796 | 0.8595 | 0.0428 | 0.4983 | 0.8938 | 0.9517 | 0.5662 | 0.9446 |\n| 642 | 1 | Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+LSE main + motif max, τ=0.25 len-norm) — seed=123 | Noema II | 407 | 0.6775 | 0.8602 | 0.0708 | 0.4605 | 0.8955 | 0.9515 | 0.5653 | 0.9385 |\n| 637 | 1 | Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max + motif max, k=7) — seed=42 — kernel sweep | Noema II | 405 | 0.6862 | 0.8552 | 0.0705 | 0.5076 | 0.8974 | 0.9510 | 0.5714 | 0.9508 |\n| 636 | 1 | Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max + motif max) — seed=123 — fixed alias | Noema II | 405 | 0.6777 | 0.8597 | 0.0397 | 0.4804 | 0.8969 | 0.9524 | 0.5625 | 0.9523 |\n| 633 | 1 | Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max + motif max) — seed=123 — fixed kernel_dilation | Noema II | 404 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 630 | 1 | Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max + motif max) — seed=7 — fixed kernel_dilation | Noema II | 403 | 0.6853 | 0.8575 | 0.0756 | 0.5076 | 0.8941 | 0.9509 | 0.5651 | 0.9462 |\n\nPage 1 of 35 (sorted by:\
    \ author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-35, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nHybrid Dual-Path (mean+max main + motif max, k=5) with regression calibration:\n  - Shared DSConv backbone (5 dilated DW+PW conv blocks, d_model=256), kernel_dilation fix\n  - Main path: concat(global mean, global max)\n  - Motif path: Conv1D(k=5) + GELU + Dropout -> global max\n  - Fusion: concat -> Dropout -> LayerNorm\n  - Regression calibration:\n      * Task-type-specific head dropout (regression heads use lower dropout, default 0.05)\n      * L2 normalization of fused features before regression head (stabilizes Spearman-heavy tasks)\n  - Heads: 128-d MLP + dropout\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\n\
    import flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n        'reg_head_dropout': 0.05,   # lower dropout for regression tasks\n    }\n\nclass DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        residual = x\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                    kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                    feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                    padding='SAME',\n                    name='dw')(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \        x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw')(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return residual + x\n\nclass SharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilations: Sequence[int]\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        h = x\n        for i, d in enumerate(self.dilations):\n            h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, name=f'dsconv_{i}')(h, deterministic)\n        return h\n\nclass RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    hidden: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    l2_norm_input: bool = False\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n       \
    \ if self.l2_norm_input:\n            norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n            x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n        return z.squeeze(-1) if self.d_output == 1 else z\n\nclass GenericHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    hidden: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\nclass HybridDualPathRegCal(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    reg_head_dropout:\
    \ float = 0.05\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        h = SharedBackbone(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n        max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n        main_feat = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n        m = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='motif_conv')(h)\n        m = nn.gelu(m)\n        m = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(m, deterministic=deterministic)\n        motif_feat = jnp.max(m, axis=1)\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([main_feat, motif_feat], axis=-1)\n        fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        fused = nn.LayerNorm(name='fused_ln')(fused)\n        if self.task_type == 'regression':\n            return RegressionHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.reg_head_dropout, l2_norm_input=True)(fused,\
    \ deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression':\n            return GenericHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type in ('multilabel_classification', 'multiclass_classification'):\n            return GenericHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f'Unknown task_type: {self.task_type}')\n\nclass WrappedRNANetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n        hp = hparams or {}\n        self.net = HybridDualPathRegCal(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            d_model=int(hp.get('d_model', 256)),\n            num_blocks=int(hp.get('num_blocks', 5)),\n            dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n            kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n            motif_kernel_size=int(hp.get('motif_kernel_size',\
    \ 5)),\n            dropout_rate=float(hp.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n            reg_head_dropout=float(hp.get('reg_head_dropout', 0.05)),\n        )\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n  \
    \      optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
