role: model
parts:
- text: "I’ll patch the HDP-RegCal builder to expose fused features cleanly, then rerun the norms capture using the new apply_features to write per-dataset JSON summaries.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max main + motif max, k=5) with regression calibration:\n    - Shared DSConv backbone (5 dilated DW+PW conv blocks, d_model=256), kernel_dilation fix\n    - Main path: concat(global mean, global max)\n    - Motif path: Conv1D(k=5) + GELU + Dropout -> global max\n    - Fusion: concat -> Dropout -> LayerNorm\n    - Regression calibration:\n        * Task-type-specific head dropout (regression heads use lower dropout, default 0.05)\n        * L2 normalization of fused features before regression head (stabilizes Spearman-heavy tasks)\n    - Heads: 128-d MLP + dropout\n\n  Added (analysis support):\n    - sow('intermediates','fused', fused) right after fused LayerNorm, to expose\
    \ fused pre-head features\n    - WrappedRNANetwork.apply_features(...) to return fused features [B,H] given inputs and params\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  import numpy as np  # for apply_features aggregation\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'reg_head_dropout': 0.05,   # lower dropout for regression tasks\n      }\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n\
    \                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME',\n                      name='dw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class SharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = x\n          for i, d in enumerate(self.dilations):\n\
    \              h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, name=f'dsconv_{i}')(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return z.squeeze(-1) if self.d_output == 1 else z\n\n  class GenericHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n\
    \          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class HybridDualPathRegCal(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      reg_head_dropout: float = 0.05\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Backbone\n          h = SharedBackbone(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          # Main path pooling\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          main_feat = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n          # Motif path\n          m = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='motif_conv')(h)\n\
    \          m = nn.gelu(m)\n          m = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(m, deterministic=deterministic)\n          motif_feat = jnp.max(m, axis=1)\n          # Fusion\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_feat, motif_feat], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm(name='fused_ln')(fused)\n          # Expose fused features for analysis (pre-head, pre-RegCal)\n          self.sow('intermediates', 'fused', fused)\n\n          # Heads\n          if self.task_type == 'regression':\n              return RegressionHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.reg_head_dropout, l2_norm_input=True)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression':\n              return GenericHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type in ('multilabel_classification', 'multiclass_classification'):\n         \
    \     return GenericHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f'Unknown task_type: {self.task_type}')\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = HybridDualPathRegCal(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              d_model=int(hp.get('d_model', 256)),\n              num_blocks=int(hp.get('num_blocks', 5)),\n              dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              motif_kernel_size=int(hp.get('motif_kernel_size', 5)),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              reg_head_dropout=float(hp.get('reg_head_dropout', 0.05)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key\
    \ = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n      # New: return fused pre-head features via intermediates capture\n      def apply_features(self, params, x, deterministic=True):\n          y, m = self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, mutable=['intermediates'])\n          inter = m.get('intermediates', {})\n          fused_list = []\n          # Traverse collected intermediates and extract 'fused'\n          for scope, d in inter.items():\n\
    \              if isinstance(d, dict) and 'fused' in d:\n                  for t in d['fused']:\n                      fused_list.append(np.array(t))\n          if not fused_list:\n              # Fallback: return empty array with matching batch size if no capture (should not happen)\n              x_np = np.array(x)\n              return np.zeros((x_np.shape[0], self.net.d_model * 3), dtype=np.float32)\n          # There should be exactly one tensor per call; if multiple, take the last\n          fused = fused_list[-1]\n          return fused  # shape [B, H_fused]\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP-RegCal (default,\
    \ patched) + direct fused-feature z-norm capture — seed=42\"\ntags: \"analysis, calibration, dsconv, pooling, regression, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Patched HDP-RegCal exposes fused pre-head features via apply_features(). After training each regression-family dataset, complete() loads the validation set and computes ||fused||2 summaries (pre-RegCal) to storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms/{DATASET}.json.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, json, optax\n  import numpy as np\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  # Patched builder with apply_features() support and sow('fused', ...)\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal import build_network as build_hdp_regcal\n\n  # System dataset loader\n  sys.path.append('storage/system')\n  import train_single as ts  # provides load_dataset()\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Explicit defaults for reproducibility (matches paper)\n      return {\n    \
    \      'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'reg_head_dropout': 0.05\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_hdp_regcal(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  def _task_spec(dataset: str):\n      if dataset in (\"APA\", \"CRI-Off\", \"CRI-On\", \"MRL\"):\n          return \"regression\", 1\n      if dataset == \"PRS\":\n          return \"multilabel_regression\", 3\n      if dataset == \"Modif\":\n          return \"multilabel_classification\", 12\n      if dataset == \"ncRNA\":\n          return \"multiclass_classification\", 13\n      raise ValueError(f\"Unknown dataset: {dataset}\")\n\n  def _summarize(arr):\n      arr = np.asarray(arr).reshape(-1)\n\
    \      qs = np.quantile(arr, [0.05, 0.25, 0.50, 0.75, 0.95])\n      return dict(mean=float(arr.mean()), std=float(arr.std()),\n                  q05=float(qs[0]), q25=float(qs[1]), q50=float(qs[2]),\n                  q75=float(qs[3]), q95=float(qs[4]), n=int(arr.size))\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      val_metric = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} final val_metric={val_metric}\")\n\n      # Only analyze regression-family datasets\n      if ds not in (\"APA\", \"CRI-Off\", \"CRI-On\", \"MRL\", \"PRS\"):\n          return\n\n      # Rebuild analysis network with same hparams\n      hparams = dict(trial_data.get('hyperparameters', {}) or {})\n      task_type, d_out = _task_spec(ds)\n      hparams.update({'task_type': task_type, 'd_output': d_out})\n      net = build_hdp_regcal(d_out, task_type, hparams)\n\n      # Load validation set from system\n      (_, _), (val_X, _val_y) = ts.load_dataset(ds)\n\
    \      val_X = np.array(val_X)\n      N = val_X.shape[0]\n      bs = 256\n\n      norms = []\n      for start in range(0, N, bs):\n          xb = jnp.asarray(val_X[start:start+bs])\n          fused = net.apply_features(params, xb, deterministic=True)  # shape [B,H_fused]\n          n = np.linalg.norm(np.asarray(fused), ord=2, axis=-1)      # [B]\n          norms.append(n)\n\n      if norms:\n          norms = np.concatenate(norms, axis=0)[:N]\n          summary = _summarize(norms)\n          os.makedirs('storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms', exist_ok=True)\n          out_path = f\"storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms/{ds}.json\"\n          with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump({'dataset': ds, 'summary': summary, 'seed': trial_data.get('seed')}, f, indent=2)\n          print(f\"[NormCapture] Saved {ds} z-norm summary -> {out_path}\")\n      else:\n          print(f\"[NormCapture] No norms captured for {ds}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage list noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms}`"
thinking_content: "**Clarifying network errors**\n\nI need to take appropriate further actions based on the user's attempts to collect z-norms. They encountered errors twice, first when using network.network.apply capture_intermediates. It looks like WrappedRNANetwork uses a self.net attribute instead of the network one.\n\nIn this case, the l2_norm_input in the RegressionHead is set to True by default. The user wants to compute pre-normalized fused features, which are the inputs after LayerNorm and dropout but before applying L2 normalization in RegressionHead. So, z_pre is crucial for their goal.**Refining capture approach**\n\nTo capture features, I need to position capture_intermediates around the RegressionHead input or set l2_norm_input to False while applying dropout. Currently, the architecture has l2_norm_input set to True, which isn't adjustable from hparams as it's set inline in the constructor.\n\nTo capture pre-normalization z, I should either build an alternate network variant\
  \ with l2_norm_input set to False or use capture_intermediates to grab 'fused_ln' output. I might also consider adding an apply_features method to extract fused features from WrappedRNANetwork while ensuring the code aligns with the current structure.**Addressing network attributes**\n\nI found that the dataset shapes worked out, but they mistakenly tried to access net_an.network.apply, which references the wrong attribute. I should be using net_an.net.apply instead. \n\nTo capture dropout outputs, I previously used a filter with lambda matching nn.Dropout. This method returns various dropout outputs, including those from the class head and earlier layers. It’s important to select the last 2D output. However, I need to consider that earlier dropout layers might produce 3D shapes. The fused dropout after the concat means and max is the specific output, which gives us the desired 2D shape [B, H+H(?)].**Clarifying dropout vs. fused outputs**\n\nI realize that we might actually need the fused\
  \ LayerNorm (LN) output, which is 2D and not dropout, so capturing dropout outputs gives us two 2D outputs. There's the fused dropout before the LN and the head dropout z in RegressionHead or Generic. But by taking the last 2D dropout, it likely comes from the head dropout, which has a shape of [B, hidden]—not the fused features representing z_pre.\n\nThey tried setting regcal_l2=False and deterministic=True, leading to head dropout with deterministic True, meaning input passes through unchanged. While they still capture 2D arrays from both fused dropout (pre-LN) and head dropout (post hidden dense), selecting the last dropout output in the head path after Dense hidden isn't what we want for fused features.**Implementing fused features capturing**\n\nI need to ensure we're capturing the 'fused_ln' output specifically—not the dropout. To do this, I can filter for LayerNorm types using capture_intermediates. I need to define a lambda function that checks module names for 'fused_ln' instances.\
  \ \n\nSince I can’t modify the file directly, I’ll add a new 'apply_features' method to the WrappedRNANetwork in our lineage file. This will use self.net.apply with mutable capture_intermediates to retrieve the 'fused_ln' data. I’ll also implement 'self.sow' to annotate the fused features without changing output behavior. Once I finalize the patch, I'll ensure it integrates smoothly and correctly in the network training process.**Implementing feature capture and submission**\n\nI need to capture the 'fused_ln' outputs specifically, so I’ll ensure my code filters appropriately. I'll create a list to collect these outputs and concatenate them along the correct axis. The 'apply_features' will return fused features for the given batch vector, while I can ignore the predictions 'y' and compute L2 norms using those features across the entire validation set.\n\nI'll write the code with new hyperparameters, ensuring not to set 'head_dropout' but relying on 'reg_head_dropout' for consistency. After\
  \ crafting the necessary patches, I’ll submit the script and aggregate results as designed."
