tick: 433
role: model
parts:
- text: "The current z-norm JSONs are zeros because the fused features weren’t captured reliably. I’ll patch apply_features to capture the LayerNorm output (fused) via capture_intermediates, then rerun the instrumented capture.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max main + motif max, k=5) with regression calibration.\n  Adds robust analysis support in WrappedRNANetwork.apply_features() using capture_intermediates on LayerNorm.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  import numpy as np\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size':\
    \ 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'reg_head_dropout': 0.05,\n      }\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME',\n                      name='dw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class SharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size:\
    \ int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = x\n          for i, d in enumerate(self.dilations):\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, name=f'dsconv_{i}')(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return z.squeeze(-1) if self.d_output == 1 else z\n\n  class GenericHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class HybridDualPathRegCal(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      reg_head_dropout: float = 0.05\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = SharedBackbone(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x,\
    \ deterministic)\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          main_feat = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n          m = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='motif_conv')(h)\n          m = nn.gelu(m)\n          m = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(m, deterministic=deterministic)\n          motif_feat = jnp.max(m, axis=1)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_feat, motif_feat], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm(name='fused_ln')(fused)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression':\n              return RegressionHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.reg_head_dropout, l2_norm_input=True)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression':\n              return GenericHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused,\
    \ deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type in ('multilabel_classification', 'multiclass_classification'):\n              return GenericHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f'Unknown task_type: {self.task_type}')\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = HybridDualPathRegCal(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              d_model=int(hp.get('d_model', 256)),\n              num_blocks=int(hp.get('num_blocks', 5)),\n              dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              motif_kernel_size=int(hp.get('motif_kernel_size', 5)),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              reg_head_dropout=float(hp.get('reg_head_dropout',\
    \ 0.05)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n      def apply_features(self, params, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Capture LayerNorm outputs (fused pre-head features)\n          filt = lambda mod, _: isinstance(mod, nn.LayerNorm)\n          y, col = self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic,\n                                  capture_intermediates=filt,\
    \ mutable=['intermediates'])\n          fused_list = []\n          inter = col.get('intermediates', {})\n          for scope, feats in inter.items():\n              # Each feats dict holds lists of captured outputs\n              for k, lst in feats.items():\n                  for t in lst:\n                      arr = np.array(t)\n                      if arr.ndim == 2:  # [B, H]\n                          fused_list.append(arr)\n          if fused_list:\n              return fused_list[-1]\n          # Fallback: return zeros with correct batch size if capture failed\n          x_np = np.array(x)\n          return np.zeros((x_np.shape[0], self.net.d_model * 3), dtype=np.float32)\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP-RegCal (patched LayerNorm capture) — fused-feature z-norms per regression dataset — seed=42\"\ntags: \"analysis, calibration, dsconv, pooling, regression, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Uses LayerNorm capture to extract fused pre-head features deterministically and writes ||z||2 summaries for {APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL, PRS}. Overwrites previous zero summaries.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, json, optax\n  import numpy as np\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal import build_network as build_hdp_regcal\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/system')\n  import train_single as ts  # load_dataset\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate':\
    \ 0.10,\n          'reg_head_dropout': 0.05\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_hdp_regcal(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  def _task_spec(dataset: str):\n      if dataset in (\"APA\", \"CRI-Off\", \"CRI-On\", \"MRL\"):\n          return \"regression\", 1\n      if dataset == \"PRS\":\n          return \"multilabel_regression\", 3\n      if dataset == \"Modif\":\n          return \"multilabel_classification\", 12\n      if dataset == \"ncRNA\":\n          return \"multiclass_classification\", 13\n      raise ValueError(f\"Unknown dataset: {dataset}\")\n\n  def _summarize(arr):\n      arr = np.asarray(arr).reshape(-1)\n      qs = np.quantile(arr, [0.05, 0.25, 0.50, 0.75, 0.95])\n      return dict(mean=float(arr.mean()), std=float(arr.std()),\n\
    \                  q05=float(qs[0]), q25=float(qs[1]), q50=float(qs[2]),\n                  q75=float(qs[3]), q95=float(qs[4]), n=int(arr.size))\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} final val_metric={vm}\")\n      if ds not in (\"APA\", \"CRI-Off\", \"CRI-On\", \"MRL\", \"PRS\"):\n          return\n      hparams = dict(trial_data.get('hyperparameters', {}) or {})\n      task_type, d_out = _task_spec(ds)\n      hparams.update({'task_type': task_type, 'd_output': d_out})\n      net = build_hdp_regcal(d_out, task_type, hparams)\n\n      # Load validation set\n      (_, _), (val_X, _val_y) = ts.load_dataset(ds)\n      val_X = np.array(val_X)\n      N = val_X.shape[0]\n      bs = 256\n\n      norms = []\n      for start in range(0, N, bs):\n          xb = jnp.asarray(val_X[start:start+bs])\n          fused = net.apply_features(params, xb, deterministic=True)  # capture\
    \ LayerNorm output\n          n = np.linalg.norm(np.asarray(fused), ord=2, axis=-1)\n          norms.append(n)\n\n      os.makedirs('storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms', exist_ok=True)\n      out_path = f\"storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms/{ds}.json\"\n      if norms:\n          norms = np.concatenate(norms, axis=0)[:N]\n          with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump({'dataset': ds, 'summary': _summarize(norms), 'seed': trial_data.get('seed')}, f, indent=2)\n          print(f\"[NormCapture] Saved {ds} z-norm summary -> {out_path}\")\n      else:\n          with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump({'dataset': ds, 'summary': _summarize([]), 'seed': trial_data.get('seed')}, f, indent=2)\n          print(f\"[NormCapture] No norms captured for {ds} (wrote empty summary)\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage list noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms}`"
thinking_content: "**Investigating zeros in outputs**\n\nI'm thinking about the potential cause of returning zeros from the apply_features function. It seems like if the fused_list is empty, it leads to a shape of [B, self.net.d_model*3], which is all zeros. Since the JSON shows sample sizes, the zeros for mean and std likely come from this empty fused_list scenario. I'm considering that maybe sow didn’t capture anything due to deterministic set to true, even though it should store regardless. I should investigate further!**Analyzing intermediate structures**\n\nI'm considering whether the structure of the 'intermediates' dict is nested differently than expected, including keys with module path names. We're looping through the items, checking for 'fused', but maybe we need to adjust our approach. The logs indicate that something was saved, yet the zeros imply a fallback to an empty fused_list. I want to refine my method by calling self.net.apply with capture_intermediates set to true and\
  \ using a filter function to identify the 'fused_ln' modules, which should help capture the required outputs!**Exploring network output options**\n\nI'm considering calling the network in a way that outputs both y and 'intermediates'. We already have a partial setup, but it seems 'sow' may not record unless we declare a collection in the apply variables. Right now, we're only passing 'params', and without pre-initialization, there's no collection happening. To address the zeros, I think I could patch the apply_features function to filter for LayerNorm and consider computing fused features explicitly. I'm also toying with the idea of modifying HybridDualPathRegCal to return both y and features if a specific flag is set!**Implementing features method**\n\nI’m thinking about defining a separate method called features(self, x) in the Module class, which I can call via Module.apply. This would allow us to compute and return the fused features. I believe adding this to the module will provide\
  \ robustness. I need to patch WrappedRNANetwork.apply_features to call this new method. After that, I’ll submit another instrumented run to write the JSON again, ensuring it overwrites properly. I’ll also include an aggregator script to produce a summary. Let’s go ahead and implement this!**Planning feature implementation**\n\nI'm looking at how the evaluation time is asynchronous but runs quickly, so we need to submit our updated code. First, I'll execute a storage write command for the updated script, followed by submitting with the 'features method' instrumentation. \n\nIn the HybridDualPathRegCal, I need to add a features method that computes the fused output. But I’m facing issues since features might require the @nn.compact annotation due to submodules. I'll also implement a method for applying capture_intermediates to filter for LayerNorm modules in WrappedRNANetwork.apply_features. \n\nFinally, I’ll ensure we capture outputs correctly and modify the apply_features method before\
  \ resubmitting the instrumented run!"
