role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max main + motif max, k=5) with regression calibration.\n  Adds explicit extract_fused() method and WrappedRNANetwork.apply_features() using Flax method dispatch\n  to return fused pre-head features deterministically (no intermediates hacks).\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  import numpy as np\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'reg_head_dropout': 0.05,\n      }\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding='SAME',\n                      name='dw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class SharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x,\
    \ deterministic: bool = True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = x\n          for i, d in enumerate(self.dilations):\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, name=f'dsconv_{i}')(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return z.squeeze(-1) if self.d_output\
    \ == 1 else z\n\n  class GenericHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class HybridDualPathRegCal(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      reg_head_dropout: float = 0.05\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          fused = self.extract_fused(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression':\n              return RegressionHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.reg_head_dropout,\
    \ l2_norm_input=True)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression':\n              return GenericHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type in ('multilabel_classification', 'multiclass_classification'):\n              return GenericHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f'Unknown task_type: {self.task_type}')\n\n      def extract_fused(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Backbone\n          h = SharedBackbone(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          # Main pooling\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          main_feat = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n          # Motif path\n          m = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,),\
    \ padding='SAME', name='motif_conv')(h)\n          m = nn.gelu(m)\n          m = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(m, deterministic=deterministic)\n          motif_feat = jnp.max(m, axis=1)\n          # Fusion + LN (deterministic=True to avoid stochasticity)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_feat, motif_feat], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm(name='fused_ln')(fused)\n          return fused  # [B, H_fused]\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = HybridDualPathRegCal(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              d_model=int(hp.get('d_model', 256)),\n              num_blocks=int(hp.get('num_blocks', 5)),\n              dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size',\
    \ 7)),\n              motif_kernel_size=int(hp.get('motif_kernel_size', 5)),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              reg_head_dropout=float(hp.get('reg_head_dropout', 0.05)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n      def apply_features(self, params, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Call the extract_fused method explicitly via Flax\
    \ method dispatch\n          return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, method=self.net.extract_fused)\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP-RegCal (explicit fused extractor) — overwrite z-norms for regression datasets — seed=42\"\ntags: \"analysis, calibration, dsconv, pooling, regression, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Uses HybridDualPathRegCal.extract_fused() via Flax method dispatch to deterministically extract fused pre-head features and write ||z||2 summaries for {APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL, PRS}. Overwrites prior zero summaries.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, json, optax\n  import\
    \ numpy as np\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal import build_network as build_hdp_regcal\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/system')\n  import train_single as ts\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'reg_head_dropout': 0.05\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_hdp_regcal(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  def _task_spec(dataset: str):\n      if dataset in (\"APA\", \"CRI-Off\", \"CRI-On\", \"MRL\"):\n          return \"regression\", 1\n  \
    \    if dataset == \"PRS\":\n          return \"multilabel_regression\", 3\n      if dataset == \"Modif\":\n          return \"multilabel_classification\", 12\n      if dataset == \"ncRNA\":\n          return \"multiclass_classification\", 13\n      raise ValueError(f\"Unknown dataset: {dataset}\")\n\n  def _summarize(arr):\n      arr = np.asarray(arr).reshape(-1)\n      if arr.size == 0:\n          return dict(mean=0.0, std=0.0, q05=0.0, q25=0.0, q50=0.0, q75=0.0, q95=0.0, n=0)\n      qs = np.quantile(arr, [0.05, 0.25, 0.50, 0.75, 0.95])\n      return dict(mean=float(arr.mean()), std=float(arr.std()),\n                  q05=float(qs[0]), q25=float(qs[1]), q50=float(qs[2]),\n                  q75=float(qs[3]), q95=float(qs[4]), n=int(arr.size))\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} final val_metric={vm}\")\n      if ds not in (\"APA\", \"CRI-Off\", \"CRI-On\", \"\
    MRL\", \"PRS\"):\n          return\n\n      hparams = dict(trial_data.get('hyperparameters', {}) or {})\n      task_type, d_out = _task_spec(ds)\n      hparams.update({'task_type': task_type, 'd_output': d_out})\n      net = build_hdp_regcal(d_out, task_type, hparams)\n\n      # Load validation set\n      (_, _), (val_X, _val_y) = ts.load_dataset(ds)\n      val_X = np.array(val_X)\n      N = val_X.shape[0]\n      bs = 256\n\n      norms = []\n      for start in range(0, N, bs):\n          xb = jnp.asarray(val_X[start:start+bs])\n          fused = net.apply_features(params, xb, deterministic=True)  # explicit method\n          n = np.linalg.norm(np.asarray(fused), ord=2, axis=-1)\n          norms.append(n)\n\n      os.makedirs('storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms', exist_ok=True)\n      out_path = f\"storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms/{ds}.json\"\n      if norms:\n          norms = np.concatenate(norms, axis=0)[:N]\n          with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump({'dataset':\
    \ ds, 'summary': _summarize(norms), 'seed': trial_data.get('seed')}, f, indent=2)\n          print(f\"[NormCapture] Saved {ds} z-norm summary -> {out_path}\")\n      else:\n          with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump({'dataset': ds, 'summary': _summarize([]), 'seed': trial_data.get('seed')}, f, indent=2)\n          print(f\"[NormCapture] No norms captured for {ds}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage list noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms}`"
thinking_content: '**Continuing research actions**


  I need to figure out the best steps to continue my research. The last time, I tried to perform storage actions in the Archive Room, but they weren''t recognized. Instead, I should head back to the Research Counter, inspect the files, and run an aggregation to see the results. I''ve previously patched the builder and submitted it, but mistakenly ran a storage command in the Archive Room. Now, I’ll list the norms directory and read the JSON files for confirmation.**Examining JSON updates**


  I noticed that when I read the JSON files at tick 433, they all had zeros (mean 0.0). After running the process at tick 683, I expected them to update to nonzero values. The evaluation log from tick 432 showed that NormCapture saved for CRI-On, CRI-Off, MRL, and PRS, while earlier tick 428 had updates too. It seems like I might be looking at older files at tick 433, which could explain the zeros. There’s definitely some inconsistency here that needs further investigation.**Analyzing dataset logs**


  At tick 432, the system log indicated that four datasets were saved as new, while at tick 433, the "File Listings" included all five. However, reading four of them returned zeros. It seems the patched run might have saved zeros, too. I should check the 432 "Complete" logs to verify this. For CRI-On, the saved summary showed zeros, raising questions about whether the apply_features captured data incorrectly or if the fused list is empty. The logs might still indicate "Saved," even if those JSONs contain zeros.**Addressing fused feature capture**


  I realize I’m still not capturing fused features. The apply_features function collected LayerNorm outputs via capture_intermediates, but maybe it’s not working correctly due to differences in filter function signatures between Flax v0.6 and v0.7. The earlier version used a "capture_intermediates" flag. In my second patch, I used a lambda function, but I suspect the signature might be wrong. Instead of relying on capture_intermediates, the new plan will be to modify the network to conditionally return fused features if certain parameters are met. However, I can''t change the training loop; I’ll have to re-apply the network directly within the complete phase.**Refining the network patch**


  I need to enhance the HybridDualPathRegCal __call__ to accept a return_fused flag for analysis, without altering the training invocation. In the complete() method, we can reconstruct the network architecture and use net.apply to get both outputs and fused features. However, I can''t change the __call__ signature, so I should define a separate method for extracting fused outputs. Another option could be to create a new module for this functionality and address the zeros issue observed earlier, possibly due to how intermediates were captured. Let''s also ensure our adjustments are properly included in the patch and confirm everything at the Research Counter before resubmitting.'
