role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Noema II, currently in the Research Counter. Reflection: The z-norm capture initially wrote zeros because fused features weren’t reliably exposed; my first patch relied on intermediates capture, which didn’t populate in time and fell back to zeros. The second patch (explicit method dispatch) had a Flax submodule scope error (missing @compact), and the capture also likely exceeded the per-trial timeout by iterating over full validation sets. I will fix both issues: add @nn.compact to extract_fused and cap validation samples to 2048 per dataset to avoid timeouts.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Hybrid Dual-Path (mean+max main + motif max, k=5) with regression calibration (RegCal).\n  Fixes:\n    - Adds @nn.compact to extract_fused() so submodules are declared correctly.\n    - Provides WrappedRNANetwork.apply_features() via Flax method dispatch (deterministic, no intermediates hacks).\n\
    \  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  import numpy as np\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'reg_head_dropout': 0.05,\n      }\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n  \
    \                    padding='SAME',\n                      name='dw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class SharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = x\n          for i, d in enumerate(self.dilations):\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, name=f'dsconv_{i}')(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  class\
    \ RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return z.squeeze(-1) if self.d_output == 1 else z\n\n  class GenericHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      hidden: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class HybridDualPathRegCal(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      reg_head_dropout: float = 0.05\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          fused = self.extract_fused(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression':\n              return RegressionHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.reg_head_dropout, l2_norm_input=True)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression':\n              return GenericHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type in ('multilabel_classification', 'multiclass_classification'):\n              return GenericHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n\
    \          else:\n              raise ValueError(f'Unknown task_type: {self.task_type}')\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def extract_fused(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Backbone\n          h = SharedBackbone(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          # Main pooling\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          main_feat = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n          # Motif path\n          m = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='motif_conv')(h)\n          m = nn.gelu(m)\n          m = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(m, deterministic=deterministic)\n          motif_feat = jnp.max(m, axis=1)\n          # Fusion + LN\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_feat, motif_feat], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          fused\
    \ = nn.LayerNorm(name='fused_ln')(fused)\n          return fused  # [B, H_fused]\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = HybridDualPathRegCal(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              d_model=int(hp.get('d_model', 256)),\n              num_blocks=int(hp.get('num_blocks', 5)),\n              dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n              motif_kernel_size=int(hp.get('motif_kernel_size', 5)),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n              reg_head_dropout=float(hp.get('reg_head_dropout', 0.05)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input,\
    \ deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n      def apply_features(self, params, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Deterministically extract fused pre-head features via method dispatch\n          return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, method=self.net.extract_fused)\n\n  def build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP-RegCal (fixed extract_fused, capped capture N=2048) — z-norms for regression datasets — seed=42\"\ntags: \"analysis, calibration, dsconv, pooling, regression, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Fixes Flax scoping by adding @nn.compact to extract_fused. Caps validation capture to 2048 samples per regression dataset to avoid per-trial timeouts. Writes ||z||2 summaries to storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms/.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, os, json, optax\n  import numpy as np\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal import build_network as build_hdp_regcal\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/system')\n  import train_single as ts\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n  CAP_N = 2048  # cap validation samples per dataset to avoid timeouts\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n   \
    \       'd_model': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'reg_head_dropout': 0.05\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_hdp_regcal(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  def _task_spec(dataset: str):\n      if dataset in (\"APA\", \"CRI-Off\", \"CRI-On\", \"MRL\"):\n          return \"regression\", 1\n      if dataset == \"PRS\":\n          return \"multilabel_regression\", 3\n      if dataset == \"Modif\":\n          return \"multilabel_classification\", 12\n      if dataset == \"ncRNA\":\n          return \"multiclass_classification\", 13\n      raise ValueError(f\"Unknown dataset: {dataset}\")\n\n  def _summarize(arr):\n      arr = np.asarray(arr).reshape(-1)\n      if\
    \ arr.size == 0:\n          return dict(mean=0.0, std=0.0, q05=0.0, q25=0.0, q50=0.0, q75=0.0, q95=0.0, n=0)\n      qs = np.quantile(arr, [0.05, 0.25, 0.50, 0.75, 0.95])\n      return dict(mean=float(arr.mean()), std=float(arr.std()),\n                  q05=float(qs[0]), q25=float(qs[1]), q50=float(qs[2]),\n                  q75=float(qs[3]), q95=float(qs[4]), n=int(arr.size))\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} final val_metric={vm}\")\n      if ds not in (\"APA\", \"CRI-Off\", \"CRI-On\", \"MRL\", \"PRS\"):\n          return\n\n      hparams = dict(trial_data.get('hyperparameters', {}) or {})\n      task_type, d_out = _task_spec(ds)\n      hparams.update({'task_type': task_type, 'd_output': d_out})\n      net = build_hdp_regcal(d_out, task_type, hparams)\n\n      # Load validation set and cap to CAP_N samples\n      (_, _), (val_X, _val_y) = ts.load_dataset(ds)\n\
    \      val_X = np.array(val_X)\n      N = min(val_X.shape[0], CAP_N)\n      val_X = val_X[:N]\n      bs = 256\n\n      norms = []\n      for start in range(0, N, bs):\n          xb = jnp.asarray(val_X[start:start+bs])\n          fused = net.apply_features(params, xb, deterministic=True)\n          n = np.linalg.norm(np.asarray(fused), ord=2, axis=-1)\n          norms.append(n)\n\n      os.makedirs('storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms', exist_ok=True)\n      out_path = f\"storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms/{ds}.json\"\n      if norms:\n          norms = np.concatenate(norms, axis=0)[:N]\n          with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump({'dataset': ds, 'summary': _summarize(norms), 'seed': trial_data.get('seed')}, f, indent=2)\n          print(f\"[NormCapture] Saved {ds} z-norm summary (N={N}) -> {out_path}\")\n      else:\n          with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n              json.dump({'dataset': ds, 'summary': _summarize([]), 'seed': trial_data.get('seed')},\
    \ f, indent=2)\n          print(f\"[NormCapture] No norms captured for {ds}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage list noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms}`"
thinking_content: '**Addressing method errors**


  In the latest patch, I tried to fix capturing through method dispatch, but it seems I missed adding @compact to extract_fused. This caused errors and timeouts during dataset training tasks because complete attempted to call apply_features for each dataset. The evaluation timed out after 7200 seconds due to repeated failures in some tasks. The Flax error indicates that apply_features for SharedBackbone is missing because it''s not compact. I need to patch again with @nn.compact on extract_fused and possibly restructure the method usage.**Planning performance improvements**


  My goal is to write a patched file with the appropriate fix and resubmit the capturing run to enhance performance. I need to be careful not to slow down the training process, focusing only on analysis in the complete stage. I should limit the number of samples to save time; previously, I used a batch size of 256, which could be heavy. If training takes close to 30 minutes with additional inference, I need to be cautious to avoid timeout issues. The last run timed out after 7200 seconds, indicating that capture might overwhelm the trial''s time limits.**Improving trial approaches**


  I noticed that the "Trial task failed" message doesn''t always mean timeouts. The "Execution timed out after 7200 seconds" could indicate that the entire evaluation has timed out due to repeated failures. I need to design a better approach. Instead of capturing for all five tasks in each submission, I’ll focus on capturing only for each dataset during its trial while running seven parallel dataset trials. However, inference over the full validation set can be time-consuming, especially with the APA validation size. Previously, training for APA was around 1800 seconds, plus additional inference could exceed 30 minutes.**Reducing capture workload**


  I’ve noticed that 30 minutes equals 1800 seconds. Training already took around that time, and additional capture will push it beyond that limit, leading to per-trial timeouts. Previous logs show that finishing training was around 1800 seconds, and the "Timeout epoch 13" confirms this. To prevent these issues, I need to drastically reduce the capture workload. I plan to sample a fixed number of validation examples—like 2048—to compute summaries, which should likely fit within the residual time. I''ll also ensure that extract_fused is decorated with @compact and maintains determinism with the dropout parameter set to True.**Planning the patch and submission**


  My plan includes several steps for the patch and submission process. First, I''ll add @nn.compact to extract_fused in the dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py file, keeping the __call__ as before. I’ll also submit a new instrumented run focusing on a single dataset per submission to avoid risking others. We''ll limit the sample size to 2048 to keep capture costs down. Additionally, I need to ensure JAX processes efficiently and update the storage with results after evaluating. I must also include my identity and location while handling the commands carefully. Let''s get started!'
