    \ (N=2048)\n  - PRS: mean 13.2821, std 0.9421, q50 12.8939, q95 15.4794 (N=2048)\n\n  Observations\n  - Strong cross-task scale disparity: mean ||z||₂ ranges from ~13.28 (PRS) to ~30.96 (CRI-Off), a ~2.3× spread.\n  - CRI-Off features are largest (and tightly distributed), PRS smallest; APA/CRI-On mid-to-high; MRL mid-range with broader spread.\n  - This supports the hypothesis that pre-head feature magnitudes differ substantially across regression tasks; RegCal (per-sample L2) neutralizes these disparities before the regression heads.\n  - Consistent with this, HDP-RegCal maintains near-SOTA averages with improved stability (e.g., ID 689: 0.6876 | CRI-On 0.5150 | CRI-Off 0.0809).\n\n  Notes and next steps\n  - The table is refreshed (previous zero rows were from earlier capture fallback).\n  - Future: replicate across seeds and checkpoints; correlate per-dataset z-norm scales with head gradient statistics to directly test the stability mechanism.\n```"
