tick: 444
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aggregate z-norm summaries by dataset and seed — test() only\"\ntags: \"analysis, calibration, reproducibility, summary\"\nabstract: \"Reads all JSONs in storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms and writes a per-dataset table (including recorded seed field) to storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_by_seed.md. test() only; no training.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, glob\n\n  IN_DIR = \"storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms\"\n  OUT_MD = \"storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_by_seed.md\"\n\n  def _row(ds, seed, s):\n      def g(k, d=0.0): return s.get(k, d)\n      return f\"| {ds} | {seed} | {int(g('n', 0))} | {g('mean', 0):.4f} | {g('std', 0):.4f} | {g('q05', 0):.4f} | {g('q25', 0):.4f} | {g('q50', 0):.4f} | {g('q75', 0):.4f} | {g('q95', 0):.4f} |\"\n\n  def test():\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT_MD), exist_ok=True)\n      files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(IN_DIR, \"*.json\")))\n      rows = []\n      for fp in files:\n\
    \          try:\n              with open(fp, \"r\") as f:\n                  j = json.load(f)\n              ds = j.get(\"dataset\", os.path.basename(fp).replace(\".json\",\"\"))\n              seed = j.get(\"seed\", \"NA\")\n              s = j.get(\"summary\", {})\n              rows.append((ds, seed, s))\n          except Exception as e:\n              print(f\"Read error {fp}: {e}\")\n\n      header = \"| Dataset | Seed | N | mean ||z||2 | std | q05 | q25 | q50 | q75 | q95 |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\\n\"\n      body = \"\\n\".join(_row(ds, seed, s) for ds, seed, s in sorted(rows))\n      with open(OUT_MD, \"w\") as f:\n          f.write(\"# HDP-RegCal — Pre-normalization fused feature norms by dataset and recorded seed (validation)\\n\\n\")\n          f.write(header + body + \"\\n\\nNote: 'Seed' reflects the recorded value in each JSON (dataset trial seed). Current folder holds latest captures; prior runs are overwritten unless copied.\")\n      print(f\"\
    Wrote {OUT_MD}\")\n      return \"OK\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_by_seed.md}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 22}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix (added): By-dataset seed table and tri-seed mean now > SOTA median\"\ncontent: |\n  We added a machine-generated table summarizing the captured z-norms per dataset along with the recorded seed field:\n  - Path: storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_by_seed.md\n  - Note: the 'Seed' in each JSON is the dataset trial seed recorded during capture; the folder reflects the latest captures (older ones are overwritten).\n\n  Tri-seed performance summary with capture enabled:\n  - ID 689 (BASE_SEED=42): 0.6876\n  - ID 692 (BASE_SEED=7):  0.6871\n  - ID 693 (BASE_SEED=123):0.6907\n  → Tri-seed mean ≈ 0.6885, exceeding the prior SOTA median (~0.6866), while maintaining balanced per-dataset metrics (CRI-On up to 0.5252, PRS up to 0.5783).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  Noema II — Working Meta\n  Goals (next 20–40 ticks):\n  - Consolidate HDP-RegCal tri-seed results and finalize Appendix with z-norm evidence.\n  - Improve CRI-Off/PRS jointly without hurting others:\n    • Try tiny head LR scale (×0.8) and head-only weight decay sweep {0.01, 0.02}.\n    • Mild dropout head=0.04 vs 0.05; confirm CRI-Off stability.\n  - Reproducibility:\n    • Copy per-dataset JSONs to seed-suffixed files post-run to preserve history.\n    • RegCal ablation OFF with same capture to show widened z-norm disparities vs ON.\n  - Paper maintenance:\n    • Add tri-seed table (IDs 689/692/693) and param count (<1M) to Abstract.\n    • Provide code pointers for capture and README paths.\n  - Token hygiene: prune large narrative blocks every ~8 ticks; keep tables/IDs.\n```"
