tick: 447
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Snapshot OFF norms and build ON vs OFF comparison — test() only\"\ntags: \"analysis, calibration, reproducibility, norms\"\nabstract: \"Copies current z-norm JSONs as seed-suffixed OFF snapshots, then writes a per-dataset ON vs OFF comparison table (means, deltas, ratios) to storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_on_off.md. Test-only; no training.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, glob\n\n  IN_DIR = \"storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms\"\n  OUT_MD = os.path.join(IN_DIR, \"hdp_regcal_norms_on_off.md\")\n\n  def _read(fp):\n      with open(fp, \"r\") as f:\n          j = json.load(f)\n      return j\n\n  def _copy_off_snapshots():\n      # Copy current unsuffixed JSONs (latest capture) to *_seed{seed}_off.json\n      wrote = 0\n      for fp in sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(IN_DIR, \"*.json\"))):\n          base = os.path.basename(fp)\n          if \"_seed\" in base:\n              continue  # already a snapshot (on/off)\n        \
    \  j = _read(fp)\n          ds = j.get(\"dataset\", base.replace(\".json\", \"\"))\n          seed = j.get(\"seed\", \"NA\")\n          dst = os.path.join(IN_DIR, f\"{ds}_seed{seed}_off.json\")\n          with open(dst, \"w\") as f:\n              json.dump(j, f, indent=2)\n          wrote += 1\n      print(f\"[Snapshot] Wrote {wrote} OFF snapshots.\")\n      return wrote\n\n  def _load_snapshots(suffix):\n      snaps = {}\n      for fp in sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(IN_DIR, f\"*_{suffix}.json\"))):\n          j = _read(fp)\n          ds = j.get(\"dataset\", os.path.basename(fp).split(\"_seed\")[0])\n          snaps[ds] = j\n      return snaps\n\n  def test():\n      os.makedirs(IN_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      # 1) Snapshot OFF from current unsuffixed JSONs\n      _copy_off_snapshots()\n      # 2) Load ON/OFF snapshots\n      on = _load_snapshots(\"on.json\")\n      off = _load_snapshots(\"off.json\")\n      # 3) Build comparison table (use one snapshot per dataset if multiple present)\n\
    \      header = \"| Dataset | ON mean ||z||2 | OFF mean ||z||2 | Δ (OFF-ON) | Ratio (OFF/ON) | ON N | OFF N |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\\n\"\n      rows = []\n      datasets = sorted(set(on.keys()) | set(off.keys()))\n      for ds in datasets:\n          on_s = on.get(ds, {}).get(\"summary\", {})\n          off_s = off.get(ds, {}).get(\"summary\", {})\n          on_mean = float(on_s.get(\"mean\", 0.0))\n          off_mean = float(off_s.get(\"mean\", 0.0))\n          d = off_mean - on_mean if (on_mean or off_mean) else 0.0\n          r = (off_mean / on_mean) if on_mean not in (0, None) else 0.0\n          on_n = int(on_s.get(\"n\", 0))\n          off_n = int(off_s.get(\"n\", 0))\n          rows.append(f\"| {ds} | {on_mean:.4f} | {off_mean:.4f} | {d:.4f} | {r:.3f} | {on_n} | {off_n} |\")\n      body = \"\\n\".join(rows) if rows else \"_No snapshots found yet._\"\n      with open(OUT_MD, \"w\") as f:\n          f.write(\"# HDP-RegCal — ON vs OFF pre-head fused feature norms\
    \ (validation)\\n\\n\")\n          f.write(header + body + \"\\n\\nNotes:\\n- ON = RegCal enabled; OFF = RegCal disabled.\\n- Means computed from captured summaries; ON snapshots: *_seed*_on.json; OFF snapshots: *_seed*_off.json.\\n\")\n      print(f\"Wrote {OUT_MD}\")\n      return \"OK\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_on_off.md}`"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating test submissions**


  I''m noticing that we have 699 running, while 697 was just for testing and has completed. There aren''t any pending tasks, so I can submit a test-only aggregator quickly. However, even though it says we hit a limit of 2, I still have 699 running. My focus should be on keeping actions minimal but effective while updating the archive with ablation results. I need to ensure the JSONs are saved and updated correctly, reflecting the latest status.**Planning test submissions**


  I plan to run a test submission to copy z-norm JSONs to the seed-suffixed files for snapshot 698 OFF. After that, I’ll run an aggregator to create on/off datasets and compute delta ratios and variances. For the next experiments, I’m considering a small learning rate scale factor and a weight decay sweep to enhance CRI-Off and PRS. We only have two concurrent tasks, and since 699 is running, I should prioritize the test-only aggregator first. This will streamline our submission process.**Adjusting optimizer settings**


  I need to ensure that the `create_optimizer` function returns an optax chain. I wonder if we can set separate parameter groups, but the default training loop may not support that without specific code. I might approximate head learning rate scaling by adding a pre-head multiplier in the network. Alternatively, I could implement head dropout settings of 0.04 versus 0.05 using the `head_dropout` parameter. I will create runs for the head dropout and a global weight decay of 0.02, but I should wait until 699 completes to launch the modifications.**Planning concise actions**


  I''m thinking about how to be concise based on the instructions. First, I''ll copy OFF JSONs to seed-suffixed "off" files as a test submission. Then, I’ll aggregate the on/off comparisons into a new markdown document and update the README with a summary of the ablation results and tri-seeds. If we have enough free concurrency, I can submit a training run with `head_dropout=0.04` and a global weight decay of 0.02. Given that one run is already going, I should prioritize the aggregator test first.**Structuring aggregator tests**


  I need to be cautious since the system executes sequentially. The aggregator test will run quickly, but I can''t submit training yet since 699 is running. If I add a training run, I''ll exceed the concurrency limit. So, I’ll start with just the aggregator test.


  My main actions include copying the current JSONs to seed-suffixed "off" files and then running the aggregator to build a comparative table. I''ll ensure to build this as a single combined test to stay within limits. Afterward, I can update the archive based on results!'
