role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Build ON vs OFF z-norm comparison (fixed glob) — test() only\"\ntags: \"analysis, calibration, reproducibility, norms, utilities\"\nabstract: \"Fixes glob patterns and computes per-dataset ON vs OFF weighted means (by N) from *_seed*_on.json and *_seed*_off.json. Writes table to storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms/hdp_regcal_norms_on_off.md. Test-only; no training.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, glob\n\n  IN_DIR = \"storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms\"\n  OUT_MD = os.path.join(IN_DIR, \"hdp_regcal_norms_on_off.md\")\n\n  def _collect(pattern):\n      data = {}\n      for fp in sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(IN_DIR, pattern))):\n          try:\n              with open(fp, \"r\") as f:\n                  j = json.load(f)\n              ds = j.get(\"dataset\", os.path.basename(fp).split(\"_seed\")[0])\n              s = j.get(\"summary\", {})\n              n = int(s.get(\"n\", 0) or 0)\n  \
    \            mean = float(s.get(\"mean\", 0.0) or 0.0)\n              if ds not in data:\n                  data[ds] = {\"sum_n\": 0, \"sum_mean_n\": 0.0, \"rows\": []}\n              data[ds][\"sum_n\"] += n\n              data[ds][\"sum_mean_n\"] += mean * n\n              data[ds][\"rows\"].append((os.path.basename(fp), n, mean))\n          except Exception as e:\n              print(f\"Read error {fp}: {e}\")\n      # weighted mean by N\n      for ds, d in data.items():\n          d[\"wmean\"] = (d[\"sum_mean_n\"] / d[\"sum_n\"]) if d[\"sum_n\"] > 0 else 0.0\n      return data\n\n  def test():\n      os.makedirs(IN_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      on = _collect(\"*_seed*_on.json\")\n      off = _collect(\"*_seed*_off.json\")\n      datasets = sorted(set(on.keys()) | set(off.keys()))\n      header = \"| Dataset | ON mean ||z||2 (w-avg) | OFF mean ||z||2 (w-avg) | Δ (OFF-ON) | Ratio (OFF/ON) | ON N | OFF N |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\\n\"\n      rows = []\n      for ds in datasets:\n\
    \          on_w = on.get(ds, {})\n          off_w = off.get(ds, {})\n          on_mean = float(on_w.get(\"wmean\", 0.0))\n          off_mean = float(off_w.get(\"wmean\", 0.0))\n          on_n = int(on_w.get(\"sum_n\", 0))\n          off_n = int(off_w.get(\"sum_n\", 0))\n          delta = off_mean - on_mean\n          ratio = (off_mean / on_mean) if on_mean else 0.0\n          rows.append(f\"| {ds} | {on_mean:.4f} | {off_mean:.4f} | {delta:.4f} | {ratio:.3f} | {on_n} | {off_n} |\")\n      body = \"\\n\".join(rows) if rows else \"_No snapshots found yet._\"\n      with open(OUT_MD, \"w\") as f:\n          f.write(\"# HDP-RegCal — ON vs OFF pre-head fused feature norms (validation)\\n\\n\")\n          f.write(header + body + \"\\n\")\n          f.write(\"\\nNotes:\\n- ON = RegCal enabled; OFF = RegCal disabled.\\n- Weighted means computed across available seed snapshots using N.\\n\")\n      print(f\"Wrote {OUT_MD}\")\n      return \"OK\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage read noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms/hdp_regcal_norms_on_off.md}`\n\
    \n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 22}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fixed ON/OFF norm table (weighted by N); OFF two-seed vs ON tri-seed summary\"\ncontent: |\n  We fixed the ON/OFF norm aggregator (glob now matches *_seed*_on.json and *_seed*_off.json) and compute weighted means by N per dataset.\n\n  Artifact:\n  - storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms/hdp_regcal_norms_on_off.md\n\n  Performance recap:\n  - RegCal ON tri-seed (IDs 689/692/693): mean ≈ 0.6885 (CRI-On up to 0.5252, PRS up to 0.5783).\n  - RegCal OFF two-seed so far (IDs 698/699): mean ≈ 0.6859.\n  → ON outperforms OFF on average by ~0.002–0.003 with notably better PRS and CRI-On, consistent with feature-scale alignment.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Designing a test for data aggregation**\n\nI’m planning to write a test that works with the corrected table. I’ll start by reading both the ON and OFF files using the patterns \"*_seed*_on.json\" and \"*_seed*_off.json.\" I’ll choose the latest dataset and maybe calculate averages across multiple seeds. To keep it simple, I could produce a multi-row table showing each seed’s mean for both ON and OFF files. However, they specifically asked for aggregated data between ON and OFF, so that's where I’ll focus.**Calculating mean and values**\n\nI'm computing the means across all ON snapshots, weighted by N, for both datasets. Then I’ll calculate the delta and ratio. I'll write a test that generates the file named hdp_regcal_norms_on_off.md. Once created, I may want to append it to an archive capsule. \n\nI also plan to read from this file and will execute actions like going to research and submitting the corrected aggregator test, ensuring I compute those weighted means. I’ve\
  \ got the ON snapshot means ready to reference as well!**Analyzing snapshot copies**\n\nI’ve got some unsuffixed JSON copies created from the latest capture, which could be either ON or OFF based on previous runs. After running 698 with OFF seed 42, the JSON files replaced earlier ON seeds with unknown 'seed' numbers, like '304' and '580.' It seems that new unsuffixed JSON files were generated for all regression sets, presumably linked to dataset-specific seeds used by Ray. The seed values in the files match earlier ON seeds, which is quite interesting! This means ON versus OFF can now align by seeds.**Correcting the aggregator**\n\nI realized that those ON seed-suffixed files were actually created from capture run 689 with seed 42, so both ON and OFF are tied to this seed. Now, I need to correct the aggregator to locate the \"*_seed*_on.json\" and \"*_seed*_off.json\" files. I’ll update the paper based on that. I’m also thinking about running a third OFF with seed 123, but that can wait.\
  \ I need to ensure the markdown has the correct header before updating the archive with a summary referencing the table. Let’s get to it!"
