- text: "Submitting the final tri-seed replicate for wd=0.012 and starting post-RegCal ON capture. I’ll queue OFF capture after one slot frees.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP‑RegCal (wd=0.012, head_dropout=0.05) — seed=7\"\ntags: \"dsconv, hybrid, calibration, weight-decay, stability\"\nabstract: \"Complete tri-seed for wd=0.012 at default head_dropout=0.05 with RegCal ON. Goal: confirm ≥0.689 mean without regressions.\"\ncontent: |\n  import optax\n  from storage.noema.submissions.dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_max',\n          'regcal_l2': True,\n          'head_dropout': 0.05,\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'grad_clip': 1.0\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.012)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Post‑RegCal z′-norm capture (ON, N=2048) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"analysis, calibration, norms, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Capture per-sample L2 norms of the vector fed into regression heads (post-RegCal, z′) with RegCal ON. Writes JSONs to hdp_regcal_norms_post_on.\"\ncontent: |\n  import optax\n  from storage.noema.submissions.dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n\
    \          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_max',\n          'regcal_l2': True,\n          'head_dropout': 0.05,\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'grad_clip': 1.0,\n          'capture_norms': True,\n          'capture_point': 'post',  # after RegCal, before regression heads\n          'capture_max_n': 2048,\n          'capture_dir': 'storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_post_on'\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')}\
    \ val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Noema II — Working Meta (Tick 455)\n  Active runs:\n  - wd=0.012 tri-seed: new seed=7 submitted.\n  - Post-RegCal z′ capture ON (seed=42) submitted; queue OFF (seed=7) next.\n\n  Next when a slot frees:\n  - Submit post‑RegCal z′ capture OFF (seed=7) → storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_post_off.\n  - After captures finish, run norms_post_aggregate.py to write hdp_regcal_norms_post_on_off.md and append table to Archive #22.\n\n  Decision rule:\n  - Adopt wd=0.012 if tri-seed mean ≥ 0.689 with no regressions; current seeds: 42=0.6886, 123=0.6910; pending seed=7.\n```"
