  \ the SOTA scoreboard later and confirm that the meta prompt is set as needed. My plan is outlined clearly!**Summarizing and managing results**\n\nI need to create a \"FINAL.md\" to summarize key results, including tri-seed means for base RegCal ON with wd=0.01 (0.6885) and wd=0.012 (0.6880), plus the normative results from the post-RegCal derived table. \n\nNext, I’ll go to the archive and respond to capsule 22, summarizing the closure, deleting the incorrect placeholder ON JSONs, and managing my token management tasks. Pruning ticks 450-459 is necessary, but I must supply the appropriate YAML and carefully document any changes to avoid fabricating data. I’ll be sure to note the removals!**Planning actions for tasks**\n\nI’m outlining the actions I need to take. First, I’ll execute moves to research and delete specific JSON files in the noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_post_on/ directory. I’ll update the README_norms.md with a note on the derived method, overwriting the existing file, and\
  \ create a FINAL.md for summarizing everything.\n\nNext, I’ll go to the archive to note the deletion of placeholder ON JSONs, adopt the derived table, and report final metrics. For token management, I need to prune ticks 450-459 but confirm that some were pruned earlier, so I'll focus on the correct ticks!**Summary preparation**\n\nI need to prepare a summary that covers several evaluations. First, I’ll include evaluations 707 and 708 for head_dropout values of 0.04 and 0.04 + wd 0.012 results. The WD 0.012 tri-seed mean for 713/714/717 is 0.6880, and I’ve decided to keep wd=0.01.\n\nNext, I’ll address that post-RegCal evaluations 718 and 719 didn't write files. On evaluations, we achieved an off result of 0.6897 and generated a derived ON/OFF table from earlier data. I'll also mention tools created, including norms_post_aggregate.py and norms_post_from_prehead.py, while ensuring we note the removal of placeholder ON JSONs for integrity. Finally, I need to quote YAML correctly and organize\
  \ my actions neatly. Alright, let's move forward!"
