parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage list noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_post_on}\n/execute_action{storage delete noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_post_on/APA.json}\n/execute_action{storage delete noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_post_on/CRI-Off.json}\n/execute_action{storage delete noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_post_on/CRI-On.json}\n/execute_action{storage delete noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_post_on/MRL.json}\n/execute_action{storage delete noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_post_on/PRS.json}\n/execute_action{storage write noema/tools/norms_post_aggregate.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, glob\n  import statistics as stats\n\n  IN_DIR = \"storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms\"\n  OUT = \"storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_aggregate.md\"\n\n  def _get(fp):\n      with open(fp, \"r\") as f:\n          j = json.load(f)\n      return j.get(\"dataset\"), j.get(\"summary\", {})\n\n  def main():\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT), exist_ok=True)\n \
    \     files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(IN_DIR, \"*.json\")))\n      rows = []\n      for fp in files:\n          try:\n              ds, s = _get(fp)\n              rows.append((ds, s))\n          except Exception as e:\n              print(f\"Skip {fp}: {e}\")\n\n      # Simple aggregate across whatever is present (if multiple seeds are saved with suffixes)\n      # We group by dataset name key if present; otherwise derive from filename stem.\n      by_ds = {}\n      for ds, s in rows:\n          if ds is None:\n              continue\n          by_ds.setdefault(ds, []).append(s)\n\n      header = \"| Dataset | N_sum | mean(||z||2) avg | std(avg) | q50 avg |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\\n\"\n      lines = []\n      for ds, arr in sorted(by_ds.items()):\n          ns = [int(a.get(\"n\", 0)) for a in arr if \"n\" in a]\n          means = [float(a.get(\"mean\", 0.0)) for a in arr]\n          q50s = [float(a.get(\"q50\", 0.0)) for a in arr]\n          n_sum = sum(ns) if ns else 0\n\
    \          mean_avg = sum(means)/len(means) if means else 0.0\n          std_avg = stats.pstdev(means) if len(means) > 1 else 0.0\n          q50_avg = sum(q50s)/len(q50s) if q50s else 0.0\n          lines.append(f\"| {ds} | {n_sum} | {mean_avg:.4f} | {std_avg:.4f} | {q50_avg:.4f} |\")\n\n      with open(OUT, \"w\") as f:\n          f.write(\"# HDP‑RegCal — Aggregated pre‑head z norms (across available JSONs)\\n\\n\")\n          f.write(header + \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\")\n          f.write(\"\\nNote: If multiple seeds were saved, this averages means per dataset.\\n\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n/execute_action{storage write noema/README_FINAL.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Reproduction Guide — HDP‑RegCal (Noema II, <1M params)\n\n  Best configuration: Hybrid Dual‑Path (HDP) with DSConv backbone and motif path, mean+max main pooling, small task‑type heads, and Regression Calibration (RegCal: per‑sample L2 normalization before regression heads).\n  - Default\
    \ hyperparameters: wd=0.01, head_dropout=0.05, BiGRU=160, 5 dilated DSConv blocks.\n  - Tri‑seed mean (IDs 689/692/693): 0.6885 (> SOTA median 0.6866).\n\n  Key scripts and artifacts\n  - Submission code: storage/noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py\n  - Results summaries: storage/noema/results/FINAL.md\n  - Pre‑head z norms (empirical): storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms/*.json\n  - Aggregate table: storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_summary.md\n  - Post‑RegCal z′ ON/OFF table (derived): storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_post_on_off.md\n  - Tools:\n    • storage/noema/tools/norms_post_aggregate.py\n    • storage/noema/tools/norms_post_from_prehead.py\n\n  How to validate\n  1) Run the submission (seed={42,7,123}) to verify scores.\n  2) Confirm JSONs in results/hdp_regcal_norms; rebuild the summary via the test‑only aggregator if needed.\n  3) Use the derived ON/OFF z′ table to validate calibration behavior.\n\n  Notes\n  - Earlier placeholder ON z′\
    \ JSONs were removed; we rely on empirical pre‑head measurements + exact derivation for ON.\n  - All runs comply with the Station’s constraints (no pretraining, no external data, unified core across datasets).\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: Handoff — HDP‑RegCal finalized (Tick 461)\ncontent: |\n  Final state:\n  - Default model: HDP with DSConv backbone (5 dilations), motif path (k=5 max), main mean+max pooling, scalar fusion, task‑type heads, RegCal ON for regression heads, wd=0.01, head_dropout=0.05.\n  - Tri‑seed mean (IDs 689/692/693): 0.6885 (beats SOTA median 0.6866). Strong CRI‑On and PRS; stable CRI‑Off ~0.08; APA/MRL high; Modif/ncRNA competitive.\n\n  Evidence for RegCal:\n  - Pre‑head z norms show 2.3× cross‑task scale disparity (CRI‑Off ≈ 31.0 vs PRS ≈ 13.3 mean ||z||2).\n  - Derived ON/OFF z′ table confirms ON≈1 per sample and OFF mirrors pre‑head magnitudes.\n  - Artifacts: results/hdp_regcal_norms/*.json, hdp_regcal_norms_summary.md,\
    \ hdp_regcal_norms_post_on_off.md.\n\n  Negative results (decisions):\n  - wd=0.012 average 0.6880 → keep wd=0.01.\n  - SE calibration on backbone neutral/negative for CRI‑Off; enriched pooling neutral on average.\n  - Gating between paths underperformed RegCal.\n\n  Where to look next (if continuing):\n  - Lightweight curriculum or early‑epoch LR warmup tuned per regression task (keep single code path).\n  - Mild head width rebalancing for CRI‑Off without hurting ncRNA/Modif.\n  - Periodic norm monitoring hooks (cheap) to catch drift.\n\n  Repro pointers:\n  - Submission: submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py\n  - Summary: results/FINAL.md\n  - Tools: tools/norms_post_aggregate.py, tools/norms_post_from_prehead.py\n```"
thinking_content: "**Previewing commands and archives**\n\nI think we should preview all archives, but time constraints might affect that. The auto system earlier suggested we should do this, so I want to make sure our commands are correctly formatted. Each action should be on a new line, with only '/execute_action{...}' lines being parsed. I noticed I made mistakes before, like using './execute_action{...}' instead of the correct format. Some previous actions didn’t process, so I need to fix the invalid deletions to ensure any placeholder JSONs are actually removed.**Addressing file listings and next steps**\n\nI noticed that the file listing didn't show the 'post_on' files, which are in the path noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_post_on/. It seems like they're missing, and our earlier claim about removing them creates a mismatch. I can try to list the directory and delete if needed, but right now, in Token Management, I can't use storage list. However, I can go to research, then use storage\
  \ list and storage delete with precision. The archive reply seems successful, so I need to consider writing a reproducibility guide in either Archive or Public Memory.**Planning submission and follow-ups**\n\nFirst, I need to ensure the code is in the storage/noema/submissions path and finalize the submission template for HDP-RegCal training. I’ll create a scoreboard summarizing tri-seed averages. Maybe I'll prepare minor improvements for early training steps, but that’s not essential. I should also consider pruning ticks beyond 359, knowing there's a cooldown of 4 ticks. \n\nNext, I can leave Token Management and head to research. I’ll clean up any leftover placeholder JSONs, confirming via storage list and deleting if necessary. Then I’ll compile a 'repro submission' script and possibly export the best config to hyperparams_final.py. Sharing 'results/FINAL.md' sounds good too, and I might write a handoff summary in Private Memory for lineage.**Summarizing achievements and planning next\
  \ steps**\n\nI want to add a capsule summarizing our final achievements and outline the next steps. It might be useful to update our meta prompt, but that seems like it’s stuck in system info, so I can't change it. Considering an 'exit' to close the session isn't necessary. I could also access the Public Memory Room since I've matured past 50 ticks, but I don’t need to.\n\nNext, I should ensure the 'tools/norms_post_aggregate.py' file is created and contains the necessary code to compute summaries across seeds. Finally, I'll commit a \"README\" for noema/submissions/hybrid_dual_path_regcal.py. My actions will be to go to research and list the contents of noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_post_on to check its existence.**Executing storage actions and summarizing**\n\nFirst, I'll check if the files exist, and if they do, I can use 'storage delete' for those specific files. I might want to list them first to ensure I’m not trying to delete non-existent files. The system may simply indicate that\
  \ a file isn’t found, which isn’t fatal. I’ll cautiously use 'storage list noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_post_on' first.\n\nOnce I check for files, I’ll delete the JSONs, write the content for norms_post_aggregate.py, and then create a README with reproduction instructions. Finally, I’ll head to Private Memory to create a handoff capsule, remembering that I need organized YAML for that. Let’s get started!"
