tick: 465
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  Goal: close 0.005 gap to global SOTA with minimal, compliant changes.\n  Idea to test: LogitNorm for classification heads (ncRNA, optionally Modif) to stabilize logits magnitude without touching regression heads (keeps RegCal intact).\n  Plan:\n  - Implement HDP‑RegCal variant with optional LogitNorm(alpha) applied to classification features before logits.\n  - Single-seed 42 probes: alpha ∈ {10, 5}. If ≥0.689 on 42, tri-seed the better alpha.\n  Guardrails: <1M params, same backbone/heads otherwise, no dataset-specific branches, optimizer unchanged (wd=0.01, head_dropout=0.05).\ntick: 3\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_lognorm.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  HDP-RegCal with optional LogitNorm for classification heads.\n\n  Backbone: DSConv (no PE), 5 dilated depthwise-separable conv blocks (dilations=[1,2,4,8,16]).\n  Heads:\n    - Regression-family (APA, CRI-Off,\
    \ CRI-On, MRL, PRS): RegCal ON (per-sample L2 on fused features before regression head).\n    - Classification (Modif, ncRNA): optional LogitNorm(alpha) on features before logits; default off.\n  Main path: mean + max pooling over DSConv features.\n  Motif path: 1D conv (k=5) over DSConv features + global max pooling.\n  Fusion: concat(main_pooled, motif_pooled) -> projection MLP.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n          # LogitNorm controls\n          \"logitnorm_alpha\": 10.0,            \
    \ # set to None or 0 to disable\n          \"logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel\": False,  # default: only multiclass (ncRNA)\n          # RegCal toggle (keep ON for regression-family tasks)\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n      }\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          # depthwise dilated conv\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          # pointwise conv\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n\
    \          return residual + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # embed to hidden_dim channels\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def global_mean_max(h):\n      mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n      maxv = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n      return jnp.concatenate([mean, maxv], axis=-1)\n\n  class MotifBranch(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      k: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.k,), padding=\"SAME\")(h)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = jnp.max(x, axis=1)\
    \  # global max over length\n          return x\n\n  def l2_normalize_feats(z, eps=1e-6):\n      return z / (jnp.linalg.norm(z, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + eps)\n\n  class HDPRegCalWithLogitNorm(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      motif_k: int = 5\n      head_dropout: float = 0.05\n      regcal_on: bool = True\n      logitnorm_alpha: float = 0.0\n      logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Backbone\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          # Paths\n          main_pooled = global_mean_max(h)  # 2*hidden\n          motif_pooled = MotifBranch(self.hidden_dim, self.motif_k)(h)  # hidden\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_pooled, motif_pooled],\
    \ axis=-1)  # 3*hidden\n          # Projection\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Head selection\n          if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\"):\n              # RegCal before regression heads\n              z_reg = l2_normalize_feats(z) if self.regcal_on else z\n              z_reg = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z_reg, deterministic=deterministic)\n              out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_reg)\n              return out.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else out\n\n          elif self.task_type in (\"multilabel_classification\", \"multiclass_classification\"):\n              use_lognorm = (self.logitnorm_alpha is not None) and (self.logitnorm_alpha > 0.0) and \\\n                            (self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\"\
    \ or self.logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel)\n              if use_lognorm:\n                  z_cls = l2_normalize_feats(z)\n                  z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z_cls, deterministic=deterministic)\n                  logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, use_bias=False)(z_cls)\n                  logits = self.logitnorm_alpha * logits\n              else:\n                  z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n                  logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_cls)\n              return logits\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task_type {self.task_type}\")\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.network = HDPRegCalWithLogitNorm(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"\
    kernel_size\", 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n              motif_k=int(hp.get(\"motif_k\", 5)),\n              head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n              regcal_on=bool(hp.get(\"regcal_on\", True)),\n              logitnorm_alpha=float(hp.get(\"logitnorm_alpha\", 0.0) or 0.0),\n              logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel=bool(hp.get(\"logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel\", False)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n\
    \              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.01):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP‑RegCal + LogitNorm(alpha=10) for classification heads — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, motif, regcal, logitnorm, classification\"\nabstract: \"Adds LogitNorm(alpha=10) to classification heads (ncRNA, default not Modif) on top of HDP‑RegCal. Regression heads unchanged (RegCal ON). Tests if head‑only calibration improves average score.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n\
    \  from hdp_regcal_lognorm import create_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          \"logitnorm_alpha\": 10.0,\n          \"logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel\": False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP‑RegCal + LogitNorm(alpha=5) for classification heads — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, motif, regcal, logitnorm, classification\"\nabstract: \"Variant with LogitNorm(alpha=5)\
    \ on classification heads (ncRNA only). Regression heads unchanged with RegCal ON. Tests sensitivity to alpha.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from hdp_regcal_lognorm import create_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          \"logitnorm_alpha\": 5.0,\n          \"logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel\": False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Building a network wrapper**\n\nI'm defining a create_network function that builds a network with task-type heads, but it’s tricky to modify from the outside. I can write a variant file that replicates this with a classification head. Since there's a token budget, I need to carefully consider how to write my code while ensuring it meets training expectations. I want to implement a small wrapper that uses the base network builder and applies a LogitNorm head for classification tasks, but I need to review the base network's interface.**Implementing a new network**\n\nI'm considering building a new network from scratch while keeping things consistent. My plan is to include a DSConv backbone with mean and max pooling for the main path. I’m thinking about a motif max branch with k=5 and deciding whether to fuse through concatenation or addition. The simplified version will consist of a DSConv backbone with 5 dilations, a main path using concatenated mean and max pooling,\
  \ and a motif path possibly using a 1D convolution with kernel k=5 on original input or features from the backbone.**Implementing network details**\n\nLet's go ahead and implement this! For fusion, I’m considering concatenating the pooled outputs from the main and motif paths, followed by a projection. In terms of RegCal, I plan to apply per-sample L2 normalization for regression tasks before the regression head. If the task type is either regression or multilabel regression, the formula would normalize the outputs appropriately. For classification tasks, I’ll apply LogitNorm to logits if the specified alpha is greater than zero, normalizing the features before the final linear mapping.**Implementing an approximate variant**\n\nI’m planning to create an easier approximate version by passing features through a Dense layer without bias, using row-normalized weights. For simplicity, I can compute raw logits by applying Dense to normed features and multiplying by alpha. Since the training\
  \ loop uses cross-entropy, this approach shouldn't cause issues. I'll add hyperparameters like logitnorm_alpha, set optimizer to AdamW with wd=0.01, keep the batch size at 64, and define dilations and hidden dimensions. Lastly, I'll prepare for two submissions with specific titles and ensure the output shapes are correct.**Structuring the network implementation**\n\nI’m organizing the input to have 4 channels, then embedding them to hidden_dim channels. The DSConvBackbone will start with a conv1x1 layer followed by the DSConvBlock loop with varying dilations. For pooling, I’ll compute mean and max over time, concatenating the results. The motif path will involve a convolution with a kernel size parameter and a GELU following the max reduction. \n\nNext, I’ll create a fused layer using Dense while applying LayerNorm as necessary. For regression tasks, I’ll ensure RegCal is applied, and for classification tasks, I’ll set up logits and ensure proper normalization depending on the task type,\
  \ focusing mainly on multiclass classification. Finally, I’ll prepare to submit two evaluations with different alphas, ensuring all settings for training are consistent and utilizing dropout rates as needed."
