tick: 466
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{rank author}\n/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_lognorm_v2.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  HDP‑RegCal with LogitNorm option for classification heads and configurable ordering:\n  - logitnorm_order: 'dropout_then_norm' (default) or 'norm_then_dropout'\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          # LogitNorm controls (classification heads)\n          \"logitnorm_alpha\": 10.0,                # set <=0 to disable\n\
    \          \"logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel\": False, # default: only ncRNA (multiclass)\n          \"logitnorm_order\": \"dropout_then_norm\", # or \"norm_then_dropout\"\n      }\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n     \
    \ kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def global_mean_max(h):\n      mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n      maxv = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n      return jnp.concatenate([mean, maxv], axis=-1)\n\n  class MotifBranch(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      k: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.k,), padding=\"SAME\")(h)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n\n  def l2_normalize_feats(z, eps=1e-6):\n      return z / (jnp.linalg.norm(z, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + eps)\n\n  class HDPRegCalLogitNormV2(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      motif_k: int = 5\n      head_dropout: float = 0.05\n      regcal_on: bool = True\n      logitnorm_alpha: float = 0.0\n      logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel: bool = False\n      logitnorm_order: str = \"dropout_then_norm\"\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Backbone + paths\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          main_pooled = global_mean_max(h)\n          motif_pooled = MotifBranch(self.hidden_dim, self.motif_k)(h)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_pooled, motif_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n          # Projection\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\"):\n              z_reg = l2_normalize_feats(z) if self.regcal_on else z\n              z_reg = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z_reg, deterministic=deterministic)\n              out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_reg)\n              return out.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else out\n\n          elif self.task_type in (\"multilabel_classification\", \"multiclass_classification\"):\n              use_lognorm = (self.logitnorm_alpha is not None) and (self.logitnorm_alpha > 0.0) and \\\n                            (self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\" or self.logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel)\n              if use_lognorm:\n                  # Option A: dropout then normalize (preserves unit-norm at input to classifier)\n                  if self.logitnorm_order == \"dropout_then_norm\":\n                      z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n                      z_cls = l2_normalize_feats(z_cls)\n                  else:  # \"norm_then_dropout\"\n                      z_cls = l2_normalize_feats(z)\n                      z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z_cls, deterministic=deterministic)\n                  # ncRNA: no bias; Modif (if enabled): keep bias due to class priors\n                  use_bias = False if self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\" else True\n                  logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, use_bias=use_bias)(z_cls)\n                  logits = self.logitnorm_alpha * logits\n              else:\n                  z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n                  logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_cls)\n              return logits\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task_type {self.task_type}\")\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\"\
    , hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.network = HDPRegCalLogitNormV2(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n              motif_k=int(hp.get(\"motif_k\", 5)),\n              head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n              regcal_on=bool(hp.get(\"regcal_on\", True)),\n              logitnorm_alpha=float(hp.get(\"logitnorm_alpha\", 0.0) or 0.0),\n              logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel=bool(hp.get(\"logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel\", False)),\n              logitnorm_order=str(hp.get(\"logitnorm_order\", \"dropout_then_norm\")),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n\
    \          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.01):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning next steps**


  I need to respond based on the current context in the Research Counter. I''ve submitted two evaluations, 738 and 739, with LogitNorm at alpha 10 and 5 for the classification heads, and they''re currently running. I''ve reflected on low risk, so now I should decide whether to wait for the results. It might be useful to work on documentation or prepare code for a fallback variant ordering change. I can also consider an alternate version of the classification head if the results aren''t favorable, but I''ll be mindful of not running too many experiments concurrently.**Considering available actions**


  I’m reflecting on the actions available in the research counter, like submitting code, writing to storage, and updating documentation. I don’t think we need to add anything extensive right now, just minimal updates will do. I could also create a small test function to ensure our LogitNorm path doesn’t break shape, but we’ve already submitted and run those. Checking the archive for global SOTA gives a claim of 0.6935. It seems our goal is to close the 0.005 gap, so I should keep responses concise for the user.**Planning coding steps**


  I’m considering whether to ask to rank the author in the research counter for our runs, but they already seem to be visible. I could call for a preview of our last results after finishing, but that’s not available yet. It makes sense to write a small log entry in storage to note that we''re probing LogitNorm. We also have 36% tokens used, so I should manage those. I’m thinking of implementing the dropout-L2 variant code, but I’ll hold off on submission until the results come in. Let’s code the changes to set the classification order properly.**Revising the dropout order**


  I realized our previous setup was: z = LN, gelu, dropout, with the classification branch using L2 normalization after dropout. Now I''m reflecting that we should do dropout first, then normalize features, followed by the Dense layer with no bias and scaling with alpha. I''ll prepare that variant while ensuring dropout is applied correctly in training with deterministic set to False. I should implement this in the code file but hold off on submitting for now. Also, we can add logitnorm support with bias, and I might adjust the dropout location only in the classification branch.**Drafting code and actions**


  I’m planning to draft the code to include a parameter for `logitnorm_order`, with a default of ''dropout_then_norm'' and an alternative ''norm_then_dropout''. I want to ensure this doesn’t conflict with the current run, so I won''t submit yet. I’ll update a small document summarizing the plan and prepare to monitor our runs. I''ll implement a few actions, such as writing the variant code, and include logic for the classification branch based on `logitnorm_order`. The goal is to keep code minimal while still functional, so I''ll reuse earlier definitions where possible. Time to put this into action!'
