tick: 467
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 467\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema II — Working Meta (Tick 457)\nStatus:\n- wd=0.012 tri-seed mean = 0.6880 → keep wd=0.01 default.\n- Post‑RegCal z′: ON files materialized (property: per‑sample L2=1); OFF capture running (ID 719).\n\nNext:\n- After 719 completes, re-run norms_post_aggregate.py and append ON/OFF z′ table to Archive #22.\n- Close the analysis loop; no further head tuning planned.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 111,760 / 270,000 used (41%)\n- Agent Age: 174 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'HDP‑RegCal + LogitNorm(alpha=5) for classification heads — seed=42' (ID: 739) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6816156458989989\n**APA_R2:** 0.8483\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:**\
    \ 0.0754\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9515\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5039\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5674\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8817\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9431\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 739\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission code which had two critical bugs preventing execution. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Causes\n\n### Bug #1: Infinite Recursion (Original Submission)\nThe original submission defined wrapper functions that called themselves recursively:\n\n```python\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return create_network(hparams)  # ❌ Calls itself!\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return create_optimizer(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)  # ❌ Calls itself!\n```\n\nThese functions shadowed the imported functions from the lineage module, causing `RecursionError: maximum recursion depth exceeded`.\n\n### Bug #2: Incorrect Flax Conv Parameter (Lineage\
    \ Module)\nThe lineage helper file `storage/noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_lognorm.py` had a bug in the `DSConvBlock` class at line 51:\n\n```python\nx = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n            dilation=(self.dilation,),  # ❌ Wrong parameter name!\n            padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n```\n\nIn Flax linen, the correct parameter is `kernel_dilation`, not `dilation`. This caused:\n`TypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'`\n\n## Fix Applied (submission_v4.py)\n\nSince the lineage file `storage/noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_lognorm.py` is READ-ONLY and contains the bug, I created a **complete standalone implementation** in `submission_v4.py` with the following corrections:\n\n1. **Removed the recursive wrapper functions** - No longer needed since we're not importing from the buggy lineage file\n2. **Fixed the Conv parameter** - Changed `dilation=` to `kernel_dilation=`\
    \ in the `DSConvBlock` class\n3. **Copied all necessary classes** from the lineage file:\n   - `DSConvBlock` (with fix)\n   - `DSConvBackbone`\n   - `HDPRegCalWithLogitNorm`\n   - `WrappedRNANetwork`\n   - Helper functions: `global_mean_max`, `l2_normalize_feats`\n   - `MotifBranch`\n4. **Preserved the intended configuration** - `logitnorm_alpha=5.0` for classification heads as originally intended\n\n## Technical Details\n\nThe fix required copying the entire neural network architecture from the lineage module because:\n- Python module imports are immutable - can't modify imported classes\n- The bug was in a fundamental building block (`DSConvBlock`) used throughout the network\n- All dependent classes needed to reference the fixed version\n\nThe corrected `DSConvBlock` now properly uses Flax's `kernel_dilation` parameter:\n```python\nx = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\
    \  # ✅ Correct parameter!\n            padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n```\n\n## Result\n\nThe submission now:\n- ✅ Loads without recursion errors\n- ✅ Creates network instances successfully\n- ✅ Initializes parameters without crashes\n- ✅ Runs the evaluation pipeline (confirmed by 300+ seconds of execution)\n\nThe code is running successfully and will complete the full evaluation on its own.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\n\"\"\"\nHDP-RegCal with optional LogitNorm for classification heads.\nFixed version with corrected 'dilation' -> 'kernel_dilation' parameter.\n\nBackbone: DSConv (no PE), 5 dilated depthwise-separable conv blocks (dilations=[1,2,4,8,16]).\nHeads:\n  - Regression-family (APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, MRL, PRS): RegCal ON (per-sample L2 on fused features before regression head).\n  - Classification (Modif, ncRNA):\
    \ optional LogitNorm(alpha) on features before logits; default off.\nMain path: mean + max pooling over DSConv features.\nMotif path: 1D conv (k=5) over DSConv features + global max pooling.\nFusion: concat(main_pooled, motif_pooled) -> projection MLP.\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n        \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n        \"kernel_size\": 7,\n        \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n        \"ds_dilations\": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        \"motif_k\": 5,\n        \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n        \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n        # LogitNorm controls\n        \"logitnorm_alpha\": 5.0,             # set to None or 0 to disable\n        \"logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel\": False,  # default: only multiclass (ncRNA)\n        # RegCal toggle (keep ON for regression-family tasks)\n\
    \        \"regcal_on\": True,\n    }\n\nclass DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        residual = x\n        # depthwise dilated conv - FIXED: dilation -> kernel_dilation\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                    kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                    feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                    padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        # pointwise conv\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n        return residual + x\n\nclass DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilations: Sequence[int]\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n\
    \    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # embed to hidden_dim channels\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n        for d in self.dilations:\n            h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n        return h\n\ndef global_mean_max(h):\n    mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n    maxv = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n    return jnp.concatenate([mean, maxv], axis=-1)\n\nclass MotifBranch(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    k: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h):\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.k,), padding=\"SAME\")(h)\n        x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n        x = jnp.max(x, axis=1)  # global max over length\n        return x\n\ndef l2_normalize_feats(z, eps=1e-6):\n    return z / (jnp.linalg.norm(z, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + eps)\n\nclass HDPRegCalWithLogitNorm(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type:\
    \ str\n    hidden_dim: int = 256\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    motif_k: int = 5\n    head_dropout: float = 0.05\n    regcal_on: bool = True\n    logitnorm_alpha: float = 0.0\n    logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # Backbone\n        h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n        # Paths\n        main_pooled = global_mean_max(h)  # 2*hidden\n        motif_pooled = MotifBranch(self.hidden_dim, self.motif_k)(h)  # hidden\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([main_pooled, motif_pooled], axis=-1)  # 3*hidden\n        # Projection\n        z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)\n        z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n        z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Head selection\n\
    \        if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\"):\n            # RegCal before regression heads\n            z_reg = l2_normalize_feats(z) if self.regcal_on else z\n            z_reg = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z_reg, deterministic=deterministic)\n            out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_reg)\n            return out.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else out\n\n        elif self.task_type in (\"multilabel_classification\", \"multiclass_classification\"):\n            use_lognorm = (self.logitnorm_alpha is not None) and (self.logitnorm_alpha > 0.0) and \\\n                          (self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\" or self.logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel)\n            if use_lognorm:\n                z_cls = l2_normalize_feats(z)\n                z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z_cls, deterministic=deterministic)\n                logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, use_bias=False)(z_cls)\n\
    \                logits = self.logitnorm_alpha * logits\n            else:\n                z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n                logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_cls)\n            return logits\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task_type {self.task_type}\")\n\nclass WrappedRNANetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n        hp = hparams or {}\n        self.network = HDPRegCalWithLogitNorm(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n            kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n            ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n            dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n            motif_k=int(hp.get(\"motif_k\", 5)),\n            head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n            regcal_on=bool(hp.get(\"\
    regcal_on\", True)),\n            logitnorm_alpha=float(hp.get(\"logitnorm_alpha\", 0.0) or 0.0),\n            logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel=bool(hp.get(\"logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel\", False)),\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\
    \ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.01):\n    return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output\
    \ shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n\
