    \ Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 738\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code and it is now running without crashing. The evaluation has been executing for over 600 seconds, confirming the fix resolved all critical errors.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had **two distinct bugs**:\n\n### Bug 1: Infinite Recursion (Original Submission)\nThe original code imported `create_network` and `create_optimizer` from the lineage module, but then **redefined them with the same names**, causing infinite recursion:\n\n```python\nfrom hdp_regcal_lognorm import create_network, create_optimizer\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return create_network(hparams)  # ← Calls itself infinitely!\n```\n\n**Error**: `RecursionError: maximum recursion depth exceeded`\n\n### Bug 2: Incorrect Parameter Name in Lineage Module\nAfter fixing the recursion, v2 revealed a bug in the imported `hdp_regcal_lognorm.py` file. The `DSConvBlock` class\
    \ used an incorrect parameter name for Flax's `nn.Conv`:\n\n```python\n# WRONG (line 51 of hdp_regcal_lognorm.py):\nx = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n            dilation=(self.dilation,),  # ← Invalid parameter!\n            padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n```\n\n**Error**: `TypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'`\n\nThe correct parameter name in Flax is `kernel_dilation`, not `dilation`.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (v2): Fixed Infinite Recursion\nRemoved the redundant function redefinitions and kept only the imports and hyperparameters:\n\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nfrom hdp_regcal_lognorm import create_network, create_optimizer\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n        \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n        # ... other hyperparameters\
    \ ...\n    }\n```\n\n**Result**: Fixed the recursion error, but exposed the underlying bug in the lineage module.\n\n### Version 3 (v3): Fixed Parameter Name Bug\nSince the lineage directory is READ-ONLY, I copied only the buggy components (`DSConvBlock`, `DSConvBackbone`, `HDPRegCalWithLogitNorm`, `WrappedRNANetwork`, `create_network`) into the submission and fixed the parameter name:\n\n```python\n# Fixed version:\nx = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),  # ← Corrected!\n            padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n```\n\n**Key Strategy**:\n- Imported working helper functions (`create_optimizer`, `MotifBranch`, `l2_normalize_feats`, `global_mean_max`) that had no bugs\n- Copied and fixed only the buggy classes\n- Maintained all original functionality while correcting the Flax API usage\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success after running\
    \ for 607+ seconds without crashing. The code is executing the full training pipeline successfully.\n\n## Technical Notes\n- The Flax `nn.Conv` API uses `kernel_dilation` not `dilation` for dilated convolutions\n- This was verified by examining other working submissions in the lineage (e.g., `dsconv_pool_variants.py:24`)\n- The fix maintains all original architecture features: DSConv backbone with dilations [1,2,4,8,16], RegCal for regression heads, and LogitNorm(alpha=10) for classification heads\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n\n# Import working components from the lineage module\nfrom hdp_regcal_lognorm import (\n    create_optimizer,\n    DSConvBackbone,\n    MotifBranch,\n    l2_normalize_feats,\n    HDPRegCalWithLogitNorm,\n    WrappedRNANetwork,\n \
    \   global_mean_max\n)\n\n# Fix the buggy DSConvBlock - corrected parameter name from 'dilation' to 'kernel_dilation'\nfrom typing import Sequence\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nclass DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        residual = x\n        # depthwise dilated conv - FIXED: changed 'dilation' to 'kernel_dilation'\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                    kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                    feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                    padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        # pointwise conv\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n\
    \        return residual + x\n\n# Now override DSConvBackbone to use our fixed DSConvBlock\nclass DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilations: Sequence[int]\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # embed to hidden_dim channels\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n        for d in self.dilations:\n            h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n        return h\n\n# Now we need to recreate the network class with our fixed backbone\nclass HDPRegCalWithLogitNorm(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    hidden_dim: int = 256\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    motif_k: int = 5\n    head_dropout: float = 0.05\n    regcal_on: bool = True\n    logitnorm_alpha: float\
    \ = 0.0\n    logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # Backbone - now uses our fixed DSConvBackbone\n        h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n        # Paths\n        main_pooled = global_mean_max(h)  # 2*hidden\n        motif_pooled = MotifBranch(self.hidden_dim, self.motif_k)(h)  # hidden\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([main_pooled, motif_pooled], axis=-1)  # 3*hidden\n        # Projection\n        z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)\n        z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n        z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Head selection\n        if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\"):\n            # RegCal before regression heads\n            z_reg = l2_normalize_feats(z) if self.regcal_on else z\n            z_reg =\
    \ nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z_reg, deterministic=deterministic)\n            out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_reg)\n            return out.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else out\n\n        elif self.task_type in (\"multilabel_classification\", \"multiclass_classification\"):\n            use_lognorm = (self.logitnorm_alpha is not None) and (self.logitnorm_alpha > 0.0) and \\\n                          (self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\" or self.logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel)\n            if use_lognorm:\n                z_cls = l2_normalize_feats(z)\n                z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z_cls, deterministic=deterministic)\n                logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, use_bias=False)(z_cls)\n                logits = self.logitnorm_alpha * logits\n            else:\n                z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n                logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_cls)\n\
    \            return logits\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task_type {self.task_type}\")\n\n# Import the wrapper but we need to recreate it with our fixed network class\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\nfrom jax import random\n\nclass WrappedRNANetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n        hp = hparams or {}\n        self.network = HDPRegCalWithLogitNorm(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n            kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n            ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n            dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n            motif_k=int(hp.get(\"motif_k\", 5)),\n            head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n            regcal_on=bool(hp.get(\"regcal_on\", True)),\n            logitnorm_alpha=float(hp.get(\"logitnorm_alpha\"\
    , 0.0) or 0.0),\n            logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel=bool(hp.get(\"logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel\", False)),\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n        \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n        \"kernel_size\": 7,\n        \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n        \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n        \"motif_k\": 5,\n        \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n        \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n        \"regcal_on\": True,\n        \"logitnorm_alpha\": 10.0,\n        \"logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel\": False\n    }\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif\
