parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_lognorm_v2.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  HDP‑RegCal with LogitNorm option for classification heads.\n  Fixes:\n    - Use kernel_dilation in DSConvBlock.\n    - Add configurable ordering for LogitNorm: 'dropout_then_norm' (default) or 'norm_then_dropout'.\n    - Optional bias toggle for multiclass head under LogitNorm.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          # LogitNorm controls (classification\
    \ heads)\n          \"logitnorm_alpha\": 10.0,                # <=0 to disable\n          \"logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel\": False, # default: only ncRNA (multiclass)\n          \"logitnorm_order\": \"dropout_then_norm\", # or \"norm_then_dropout\"\n          \"logitnorm_bias_multiclass\": False,     # allow bias with LogitNorm for multiclass if True\n      }\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.hidden_dim,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              padding=\"SAME\"\n          )(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\
    \ kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def global_mean_max(h):\n      mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n      maxv = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n      return jnp.concatenate([mean, maxv], axis=-1)\n\n  class MotifBranch(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      k: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.k,), padding=\"SAME\")(h)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n\
    \          return jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n\n  def l2_normalize_feats(z, eps=1e-6):\n      return z / (jnp.linalg.norm(z, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + eps)\n\n  class HDPRegCalLogitNormV2(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      motif_k: int = 5\n      head_dropout: float = 0.05\n      regcal_on: bool = True\n      logitnorm_alpha: float = 0.0\n      logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel: bool = False\n      logitnorm_order: str = \"dropout_then_norm\"\n      logitnorm_bias_multiclass: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          main_pooled = global_mean_max(h)\n          motif_pooled = MotifBranch(self.hidden_dim, self.motif_k)(h)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_pooled,\
    \ motif_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\"):\n              z_reg = l2_normalize_feats(z) if self.regcal_on else z\n              z_reg = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z_reg, deterministic=deterministic)\n              out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_reg)\n              return out.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else out\n\n          elif self.task_type in (\"multilabel_classification\", \"multiclass_classification\"):\n              use_lognorm = (self.logitnorm_alpha is not None) and (self.logitnorm_alpha > 0.0) and \\\n                            (self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\" or self.logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel)\n              if use_lognorm:\n        \
    \          if self.logitnorm_order == \"dropout_then_norm\":\n                      z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n                      z_cls = l2_normalize_feats(z_cls)\n                  else:\n                      z_cls = l2_normalize_feats(z)\n                      z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z_cls, deterministic=deterministic)\n                  if self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n                      use_bias = bool(self.logitnorm_bias_multiclass)\n                  else:\n                      use_bias = True  # keep bias for multilabel if enabled\n                  logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, use_bias=use_bias)(z_cls)\n                  logits = self.logitnorm_alpha * logits\n              else:\n                  z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n                  logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_cls)\n              return logits\n          else:\n\
    \              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task_type {self.task_type}\")\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.network = HDPRegCalLogitNormV2(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n              motif_k=int(hp.get(\"motif_k\", 5)),\n              head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n              regcal_on=bool(hp.get(\"regcal_on\", True)),\n              logitnorm_alpha=float(hp.get(\"logitnorm_alpha\", 0.0) or 0.0),\n              logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel=bool(hp.get(\"logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel\", False)),\n              logitnorm_order=str(hp.get(\"\
    logitnorm_order\", \"dropout_then_norm\")),\n              logitnorm_bias_multiclass=bool(hp.get(\"logitnorm_bias_multiclass\", False)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:\
    \ float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.01):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP‑RegCal + LogitNorm v2 (alpha=10, order=dropout→norm, bias=False) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, motif, regcal, logitnorm, classification\"\nabstract: \"Re-test LogitNorm with corrected kernel_dilation and improved ordering (Dropout→L2→Dense) for ncRNA only; bias disabled. Regression heads unchanged with RegCal ON.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from hdp_regcal_lognorm_v2 import create_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"\
    weight_decay\": 0.01,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          \"logitnorm_alpha\": 10.0,\n          \"logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel\": False,\n          \"logitnorm_order\": \"dropout_then_norm\",\n          \"logitnorm_bias_multiclass\": False\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP‑RegCal + LogitNorm v2 (alpha=10, order=dropout→norm, bias=True) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, motif, regcal, logitnorm, classification\"\nabstract: \"Same as v2 but allow bias in the multiclass (ncRNA) classifier under LogitNorm; tests if bias restores priors and accuracy.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from hdp_regcal_lognorm_v2 import create_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n\
    \          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          \"logitnorm_alpha\": 10.0,\n          \"logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel\": False,\n          \"logitnorm_order\": \"dropout_then_norm\",\n          \"logitnorm_bias_multiclass\": True\n      }\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning response actions**


  I need to outline the logical steps forward. We''ve tried modifying the LogitNorm classification head on seed 42, but the score dropped compared to our baseline, showing no improvement. I had intended to adjust the dropout ordering, so we created a new script with configurable order. The next steps are to run seed 42 using the dropout followed by normalization and potentially use alpha=10, which performed better before. I also need to ensure that our submission wrapper correctly imports functions without redefining them.**Correcting code parameters**


  I need to make sure our v2 code uses the correct Flax conv dilation property. Earlier, we mistakenly used ''dilation'' instead of ''kernel_dilation'' in the DSConvBlock code. I need to review that since in the v2 implementation, we still wrote `nn.Conv(..., dilation=(self.dilation,), ...)` instead of correcting it. This is identified as a bug. Before submitting v2 for evaluation, I should fix it to use ''kernel_dilation'' and set the default ordering to ''dropout_then_norm'' to improve results.**Ensuring correct function imports**


  In the previous debug-run, we mistakenly used legacy code, placing `z_cls = l2_normalize_feats(z)` before the dropout, which isn''t the desired order. Testing v2 will help confirm the improved sequence. I must also ensure that the submission doesn''t have a recursion bug by importing `create_network` and `create_optimizer` from the `hdp_regcal_lognorm_v2` module. To avoid conflicts, I can import them as `build` and `makeopt`, while wrapping them with different names to prevent recursion issues. I’ll stick to importing without redefining.**Finalizing submission details**


  When importing `create_network`, I must keep in mind that it exists in the module''s global namespace, which means I shouldn''t redefine functions with the same name when preparing for submission. I need to pass hyperparameters, including setting `logitnorm_order` to ''dropout_then_norm'', `logitnorm_alpha` potentially at 10.0, and ensuring `logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel` is set to False. I might adjust `logitnorm_alpha` to 7.5, but I plan to submit a new evaluation using alpha=10. Additionally, testing `use_bias` for ncRNA could yield better results, as previous runs with it off showed lower performance.**Implementing v2 code updates**


  In our v2 setup, we''ve chosen `use_bias` as False for multiclass, but we could toggle this with a new parameter, `logitnorm_bias_multiclass`. I need to make adjustments to the code without excessive editing, focusing instead on the `logitnorm_order` and ensuring `logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel` is False. I''ll implement a patch to v2 for kernel_dilation and the bias toggle. After that, I’ll submit two runs to test both with and without bias. I''ll also ensure `create_optimizer` is defined and prep for our storage write with corrected code. Then it’s time to update our FINAL.md with notes on results.'
