role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_motif_stodepth.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  HDP‑RegCal with optional motif-branch stochastic depth (p_stodepth) and (optional) LogitNorm for classification heads.\n  Parsimonious tweak aimed at stabilizing early training for CRI-* via tiny stochastic gating of the motif path.\n  Default keeps LogitNorm disabled; RegCal remains ON for regression-family heads.\n\n  Notes:\n  - Stochastic depth gates the entire motif path representation per sample during training:\n      motif = (gate / p_keep) * motif, gate ~ Bernoulli(p_keep), p_keep = 1 - p_stodepth\n    At eval (deterministic=True), gate is 1 (no scaling).\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\"\
    : 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          # Stochastic depth (motif path only)\n          \"p_stodepth_motif\": 0.05,     # set 0.0 to disable; small like 0.05 recommended\n          # LogitNorm (classification heads) — disabled by default\n          \"logitnorm_alpha\": 0.0,       # <=0 to disable\n          \"logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel\": False,\n          \"logitnorm_order\": \"dropout_then_norm\",\n          \"logitnorm_bias_multiclass\": False,\n      }\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.hidden_dim,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n\
    \              feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              padding=\"SAME\"\n          )(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def global_mean_max(h):\n      mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n      maxv = jnp.max(h,\
    \ axis=1)\n      return jnp.concatenate([mean, maxv], axis=-1)\n\n  class MotifBranch(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      k: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.k,), padding=\"SAME\")(h)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return jnp.max(x, axis=1)  # (batch, hidden)\n\n  def l2_normalize_feats(z, eps=1e-6):\n      return z / (jnp.linalg.norm(z, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + eps)\n\n  class HDPRegCalMotifStoDepth(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      motif_k: int = 5\n      head_dropout: float = 0.05\n      regcal_on: bool = True\n      p_stodepth_motif: float = 0.0\n      logitnorm_alpha: float = 0.0\n      logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel: bool = False\n      logitnorm_order: str = \"dropout_then_norm\"\n      logitnorm_bias_multiclass:\
    \ bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Backbone\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          # Paths\n          main_pooled = global_mean_max(h)  # (batch, 2*hidden)\n          motif_pooled = MotifBranch(self.hidden_dim, self.motif_k)(h)  # (batch, hidden)\n\n          # Stochastic depth on motif path (training only)\n          if not deterministic and self.p_stodepth_motif > 0.0:\n              rng = self.make_rng(\"dropout\")\n              p_keep = 1.0 - self.p_stodepth_motif\n              gate = random.bernoulli(rng, p_keep, (motif_pooled.shape[0], 1))\n              motif_pooled = (gate * motif_pooled) / p_keep\n\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_pooled, motif_pooled], axis=-1)  # (batch, 3*hidden)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n\
    \          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\"):\n              z_reg = l2_normalize_feats(z) if self.regcal_on else z\n              z_reg = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z_reg, deterministic=deterministic)\n              out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_reg)\n              return out.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else out\n\n          elif self.task_type in (\"multilabel_classification\", \"multiclass_classification\"):\n              use_lognorm = (self.logitnorm_alpha is not None) and (self.logitnorm_alpha > 0.0) and \\\n                            (self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\" or self.logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel)\n              if use_lognorm:\n                  if self.logitnorm_order == \"dropout_then_norm\":\n                      z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \                      z_cls = l2_normalize_feats(z_cls)\n                  else:\n                      z_cls = l2_normalize_feats(z)\n                      z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z_cls, deterministic=deterministic)\n                  use_bias = self.logitnorm_bias_multiclass if self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\" else True\n                  logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, use_bias=use_bias)(z_cls)\n                  logits = self.logitnorm_alpha * logits\n              else:\n                  z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n                  logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_cls)\n              return logits\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task_type {self.task_type}\")\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.network = HDPRegCalMotifStoDepth(\n \
    \             d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n              motif_k=int(hp.get(\"motif_k\", 5)),\n              head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n              regcal_on=bool(hp.get(\"regcal_on\", True)),\n              p_stodepth_motif=float(hp.get(\"p_stodepth_motif\", 0.0)),\n              logitnorm_alpha=float(hp.get(\"logitnorm_alpha\", 0.0) or 0.0),\n              logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel=bool(hp.get(\"logitnorm_apply_to_multilabel\", False)),\n              logitnorm_order=str(hp.get(\"logitnorm_order\", \"dropout_then_norm\")),\n              logitnorm_bias_multiclass=bool(hp.get(\"logitnorm_bias_multiclass\", False)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n\
    \          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.01):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write noema/results/logitnorm_ablation.md}\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # LogitNorm Head Ablation — HDP‑RegCal (seed=42)\n\n  Motivation: stabilize classification logits by feature L2-normalization + alpha scale; regression heads unchanged (RegCal ON).\n\n  Results:\n  - alpha=5 (ID 739): 0.6816 | APA 0.8483 | CRI-Off 0.0754 | Modif 0.9515 | CRI-On 0.5039 | PRS 0.5674 | MRL 0.8817 | ncRNA 0.9431\n  - alpha=10 (ID 738): 0.6829 | APA 0.8549 | CRI-Off 0.0751 | Modif 0.9517 | CRI-On 0.5096 | PRS 0.5677 | MRL 0.8811 | ncRNA 0.9400\n\n  Takeaway: Both variants underperform the baseline (≈0.6885 tri-seed mean). ncRNA accuracy dropped ~0.004–0.008 vs. baseline ~0.947–0.949. Modif AUC stable.\n\n  Action: Prepared v2 with corrected kernel_dilation and improved ordering (Dropout→Norm→Dense) and bias toggle; IDs 744/745 running. If still neutral/negative, pivot to motif-path stochastic depth p=0.05 (code ready).\n```\n\n/execute_action{rank author}"
thinking_content: "**Pruning conversation tokens and actions**\n\nI should consider pruning conversation tokens as their usage is increasing, but it seems there’s still plenty of space at 129k. Next, I can take appropriate actions regarding code updates, like correcting `hdp_regcal_lognorm.py` to ensure it uses `kernel_dilation` and prevents wrapper recursion issues. I also want to fix the dropout ordering for classification. Additionally, once results are back, I could create a note in `results/FINAL.md`, but that can wait for now. I’ll keep an eye on ongoing experiments too.**Preparing for motif stochastic depth**\n\nI could just continue with the project. First, we might compute whether both values are less than 0.688 and pivot toward motif-branch stochastic depth. \n\nI’ll get the code ready in `submissions/hdp_regcal_stodepth.py`, using a probability of 0.05 that only applies to the motif branch, toggled through a dropout-like gating with Bernoulli during training. JAX Flax dropout\
  \ integration can use `nn.Dropout` with a keep probability of 1-p. However, since classic dropout scales differently, we need to ensure the gating works well on the motif output. It seems sensible to wait for v2 results before submitting anything, but preparing the code is a good idea.**Updating code files and plans**\n\nI should update `hdp_regcal_lognorm_v2.py`, which I've already done. Next, I'm thinking of creating a new file called `hdp_regcal_motif_stodepth.py`, but I won't submit it just yet. Alternatively, I could add support for the `motif_stodepth_p` parameter in the existing file, which would reduce code duplication. Instead, I might create a new file, `hdp_regcal_extras.py`, for modular gating methods.\n\nI plan to write `hdp_regcal_motif_stoch.py`, including RegCal, with optional LogitNorm and motif stochastic depth p. Once experiments 744 and 745 are complete, we can quickly submit a seed 42 test, but maybe we can submit concurrently since there are no current restrictions.**Managing\
  \ submissions and updates**\n\nThe Research Counter has both tasks running, and while I can still submit, there seems to be a submission cooldown period. It’s not explicitly stated, but since I've already submitted two at tick 467, I think I should hold off on new submissions for now until the cooldown resets. Instead, I can work on preparing the storage file and fixing lineage. I’ll write the new file, add a note to Private Memory, and possibly create a summary and plan. I'll also cross-check results in `FINAL.md` and update the meta prompt as needed. There's no API for direct updates, so I'll document changes in `README_FINAL.md`.**Planning code updates and managing submissions**\n\nI’m considering a few updates. We can perform some pruning if needed, but right now, it appears unnecessary with 129k tokens used. To start, I'll fix the stored `hdp_regcal_lognorm.py` for kernel_dilation and wrapper recursion by renaming functions accordingly. \n\nI’ll also modify `hdp_regcal_lognorm.py`\
  \ to incorporate LogitNorm improvements but will maintain `hdp_regcal_lognorm_v2.py` as the main file. Next, I'll write to `noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_motif_stodepth.py` to implement motif path gating. \n\nLastly, I’ll create the results files, noting the negative outcomes of LogitNorm. However, I’ll wait for v2 results to finalize before any further submissions."
