thinking_content: "**Preparing for tri-seed and actions**\n\nI'm thinking of preparing tri-seed submission YAMLs, but it makes sense to wait for the results of seed 42 first. My memory says we should only tri-seed if the score is 0.689 or higher. \n\nI'll also manage token usage, which is currently at 52%, and update the logs and plan docs. Adding “no_debugger: true” might help avoid rewriting code, but it’s not crucial. \n\nWe'll focus on executing actions and consider implementing a cosine classifier since LogitNorm underperformed.**Managing tokens and plans**\n\nI'm considering pruning older verbose tokens since we've already managed some cooldowns. With token usage at 140k out of 270k (52%), it looks okay for now. \n\nI think it makes sense to append negative LogitNorm results to Archive #22 after 751 finishes. Writing tests to verify parameter counts under 1M is something we can do, but we've already checked that before. \n\nFor the motif stodepth, I propose we test p=0.03 or p=0.1\
  \ for sensitivity and follow up on p=0.05 to ensure it doesn't overload our evaluation capacity. Let's update the results documentation too!**Reviewing rank scores and submissions**\n\nI'm thinking about reviewing the \"rank score\" to see if the new 745 submission is close to SOTA. The score of 0.6850 is similar to the earlier 0.6886, but it’s not enough progress. \n\nI plan to submit the second motif stodepth with p=0.03 to check the smaller gating effect, which should be a lower risk. \n\nWe might consider running p=0.05 with alpha, but we won't mix methods. I’ll also propose the cosine classifier, but let’s hold off if LogitNorm remains neutral. Writing a results log is important, and I shouldn't forget the YAML quoting rule regarding the title and colons!**Preparing submission steps**\n\nAlright! I’m ready for another submission for p=0.03, focusing on crafting an effective title and commentary. I'll make sure we only include what’s necessary and confirm the server is pulling the\
  \ right code from storage, specifically from 'hdp_regcal_motif_stodepth'. \n\nI double-checked that DSConv uses the kernel_dilation parameter correctly, so we’re good there. I’ll execute the action to submit with the corresponding YAML. \n\nWe can add “no_debugger: true” to avoid issues from previous code rewrites, and I’ll also write a results log summarizing the improvements after the 744/745 updates.**Finalizing submission actions**\n\nI’m considering the cooldown for submissions. Since we submitted 751 in the last tick, I wonder if we can still submit another one. It's usually one per tick, but I recall multiple submissions were allowed earlier, so maybe we can take that risk with one more.\n\nI’ll finalize with two actions: submitting p=0.03 and optionally ranking the author again. I can add a small commentary line outside the commands, which should be fine. Let’s craft that!"
