- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stochastic_depth_ablation.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Motif-Branch Stochastic Depth Ablation — HDP‑RegCal (seed=42)\n\n  Hypothesis: tiny stochastic depth on the motif branch (p) smooths early training, modestly improving CRI‑On/Off without harming others.\n\n  Config: HDP‑RegCal default (<1M params), RegCal ON for regression heads, no LogitNorm. Only motif path is stochastically gated during training with keep-prob 1-p (inference: no gating).\n\n  Results\n  - p = 0.05 — ID 751: 0.6841 | APA 0.8563 | CRI‑Off 0.0709 | Modif 0.9523 | CRI‑On 0.5111 | PRS 0.5664 | MRL 0.8931 | ncRNA 0.9385\n  - p = 0.03 — ID 755: 0.6842 | APA 0.8533 | CRI‑Off 0.0778 | Modif 0.9503 | CRI‑On 0.5194 | PRS 0.5585 | MRL 0.8886 | ncRNA 0.9415\n\n  Takeaway\n  - Both p=0.05 and p=0.03 are neutral/negative on the aggregate and below the default tri‑seed mean ≈ 0.6885.\n  - We will keep the motif path deterministic by default and\
    \ close this line of inquiry.\n```\n/execute_action{storage write noema/results/FINAL.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # HDP‑RegCal — Final Summary (Updated Tick 472)\n\n  Default (primary): HDP‑RegCal (<1M params) with deterministic motif path, mean+max main pooling, task‑type heads, and RegCal ON for regression heads; wd=0.01, head_dropout=0.05.\n  - Tri‑seed mean (IDs 689/692/693): 0.6885 (> SOTA median 0.6866). Strong CRI‑On/PRS; robust APA/MRL/Modif/ncRNA.\n\n  Negative/neutral probes (documented):\n  - LogitNorm for ncRNA:\n    • alpha=5 → ID 739: 0.6816; alpha=10 → ID 738: 0.6829.\n    • Corrected ordering + bias toggle: ID 744: 0.6838; ID 745: 0.6850.\n    ⇒ No average gain; revert to default classifier.\n  - Motif stochastic depth (training only):\n    • p=0.05 → ID 751: 0.6841; p=0.03 → ID 755: 0.6842.\n    ⇒ Neutral/negative; keep motif path deterministic.\n\n  Calibration evidence:\n  - Pre‑head fused feature norms show ~2.3× cross‑task disparity (CRI‑Off ≈ 31.0 vs PRS ≈ 13.3\
    \ mean ||z||₂).\n  - RegCal aligns scales at regression heads; stability retained.\n\n  Decision:\n  - Maintain the published default configuration as primary; minor head/motif perturbations did not close the remaining ~0.005 gap.\n  - All artifacts and ablation summaries are in storage/noema/results/.\n```\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 22}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Closure of minor probes: motif stochastic depth results and default reaffirmed\"\ncontent: |\n  We completed the stochastic‑depth sensitivity on the motif path:\n  - p=0.05 (ID 751): 0.6841\n  - p=0.03 (ID 755): 0.6842\n  Both are neutral/negative vs. the default tri‑seed mean (~0.6885). Together with the LogitNorm runs (IDs 739/738/744/745), these head/motif tweaks did not improve the aggregate.\n\n  Actions:\n  - Reaffirm the default HDP‑RegCal (<1M params) with deterministic motif path and RegCal ON for regression heads as the primary configuration.\n  - Logged details:\n    • LogitNorm ablation: storage/noema/results/logitnorm_ablation.md\n\
    \    • Stochastic‑depth ablation: storage/noema/results/stochastic_depth_ablation.md\n    • Final summary: storage/noema/results/FINAL.md\n\n  We’re closing this line and preserving the artifacts for reproducibility. Further gains likely require qualitatively different ideas beyond head‑only or minor motif perturbations.\n```"
