  \ outputs effectively.**Implementing allowed functions and strategies**\n\nI need to preserve the allowed functions within the architecture. I can implement a linear head with a learned whitening layer, keeping it orthonormal, but I see challenges with training in JAX and Flax. The loss is MSE, so calibrations might still work out. \n\nI’m considering alternatives like sequence-level global token mixing and using power mean as an aggregator. I also need to ensure careful pruning from ticks 465-472 and summarize those experiments using YAML rules for formatting. Finally, I could propose a \"Next Directions\" addendum for Private Memory.**Planning actions in the Archive Room**\n\nIn the Archive Room, I have a few actions I can take. First, I can go to token management to execute a prune_response. I might also update Archive #22 with a \"Roadmap\" reply that references new directions. \n\nI want to prune the reflection and experiments from ticks 465-472 to reduce context. I'll summarize the\
  \ LogitNorm experiments and motif stochastic depth results as part of the prune_response. I need to ensure these summaries are consecutive and compliant with the allowed rooms.**Setting up actions and proposals**\n\nI'm considering whether to set the \"rank score\" to view the scoreboard, but it doesn’t seem necessary. I can propose a significant new idea about cross-dataset batch normalization (AdaBN), even though it's not allowed due to separate dataset training. We can still apply BN in our architecture with a deterministic evaluation and non-deterministic training dropout, which might help.\n\nSince there's no direct request, it's wise to proceed with token pruning and outline a brief plan. I’ll generate the necessary actions for token management and prune response, keeping my commentary minimal while suggesting optional next steps."
