tick: 477
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{preview all}\n\n/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  Stagnation Protocol I — Baseline and three new ideas (not in Archive)\n  Baseline: Simple DSConv + mean+max pooling (no motif, no RegCal), <1M params.\n  New ideas:\n  1) Reverse-invariant dual-view averaging (RevAvg): pass both x and reversed x through the same backbone; average features, then mean+max pool. Hypothesis: improves robustness and CRI-* stability with zero parameter increase.\n  2) Power-mean pooling (P-mean): replace max with a learned power mean p≥1 (mean((ReLU(h))^p)^(1/p)), reparameterized p=softplus(u)+1 for stability. Hypothesis: interpolates between mean and max more smoothly than LSE τ, possibly improving ncRNA/APA while keeping CRI-* stable.\n  3) Stochastic Position Dropout (SPD): training-only random positional masking (prob p on sequence axis) before the backbone; identity at eval. Hypothesis: regularizes sequence locality, improving generalization without changing loss/loop.\n\
    \  Guardrails: Single DSConv backbone, same head, no dataset-specific branches, optimizer unchanged. Single-seed 42 first; if one ≥ baseline, tri-seed and then synthesize with HDP-RegCal.\ntick: 3\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_minibase_expts.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Minimal DSConv + pooling baseline and three probes:\n    - reverse_avg: process x and reversed x with shared backbone; average features\n    - use_powermean: replace max with learned power mean (mean + p-mean)\n    - token_drop_p: training-only positional masking before backbone\n\n  Heads: single hidden MLP (128) per task_type, no RegCal, no motif. <1M params.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n\
    \          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          # Probes\n          \"reverse_avg\": False,\n          \"use_powermean\": False,\n          \"p_init\": 2.0,\n          \"token_drop_p\": 0.0,\n      }\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,),\
    \ padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def global_mean_max(h):\n      mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n      maxv = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n      return jnp.concatenate([mean, maxv], axis=-1)\n\n  class PowerMean(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Learned power-mean on ReLU(h) across length.\"\"\"\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n          u = self.param(\"p_raw\", nn.initializers.zeros, (1,))\n          p = jax.nn.softplus(u) + 1.0\n          hp\
    \ = jax.nn.relu(h)\n          # avoid nan when hp==0: add eps\n          eps = 1e-6\n          m = jnp.mean(jnp.power(hp + eps, p), axis=1)\n          return jnp.power(m + eps, 1.0 / p)\n\n  class MiniDSConvNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      head_hidden: int = 128\n      head_dropout: float = 0.05\n      reverse_avg: bool = False\n      use_powermean: bool = False\n      token_drop_p: float = 0.0\n\n      def _token_drop(self, x, *, deterministic: bool):\n          if deterministic or self.token_drop_p <= 0.0:\n              return x\n          rng = self.make_rng(\"dropout\")\n          keep = random.bernoulli(rng, p=1.0 - self.token_drop_p, shape=(x.shape[0], x.shape[1], 1))\n          return x * keep\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Optional positional masking\n\
    \          x = self._token_drop(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          # Shared backbone\n          backbone = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate, name=\"backbone\")\n          h = backbone(x, deterministic)\n          if self.reverse_avg:\n              h_rev = backbone(jnp.flip(x, axis=1), deterministic)  # shared params\n              h = 0.5 * (h + h_rev)\n\n          # Pooling\n          if self.use_powermean:\n              pmean = PowerMean(name=\"pmean\")(h)\n              mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n              pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean, pmean], axis=-1)\n          else:\n              pooled = global_mean_max(h)\n\n          # Head (single hidden)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(pooled)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type\
    \ == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return out.squeeze(-1)\n          return out\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = MiniDSConvNet(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n              head_hidden=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden\", 128)),\n              head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n              reverse_avg=bool(hp.get(\"reverse_avg\", False)),\n              use_powermean=bool(hp.get(\"use_powermean\", False)),\n              token_drop_p=float(hp.get(\"token_drop_p\", 0.0)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key,\
    \ dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MINI-Baseline: DSConv (5 dilations)\
    \ + mean+max pooling — no motif, no RegCal — seed=42\"\ntags: \"baseline, dsconv, pooling, meanmax\"\nabstract: \"Simple DSConv backbone with dilations [1,2,4,8,16] and global mean+max pooling. Single hidden head; no motif path and no regression calibration. Reproduces a reasonable baseline under Stagnation Protocol.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_minibase_expts import create_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"reverse_avg\": False,\n          \"use_powermean\": False,\n          \"token_drop_p\": 0.0,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return create_network(hparams)\n\n  def\
    \ create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Idea 1 — RevAvg: reverse-invariant dual-view averaging + mean+max — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, invariance, reverse, robustness\"\nabstract: \"Process x and reversed x through the same DSConv backbone; average features before global pooling (mean+max). Hypothesis: reverse invariance improves robustness and CRI-* stability with no extra parameters.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_minibase_expts import create_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n      \
    \    \"reverse_avg\": True,\n          \"use_powermean\": False,\n          \"token_drop_p\": 0.0,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Idea 2 — P-mean: mean + learned power-mean pooling (p≥1) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, power-mean, adaptive\"\nabstract: \"Replace max with a learned power-mean (on ReLUed features) reparameterized as p=softplus(u)+1; concatenate with mean. Hypothesis: smoother interpolation between mean and max improves stability vs. LSE τ.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_minibase_expts import create_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\"\
    : 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"reverse_avg\": False,\n          \"use_powermean\": True,\n          \"p_init\": 2.0,\n          \"token_drop_p\": 0.0,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Idea 3 — SPD: training-only Stochastic Position Dropout (p=0.05) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, regularization, augmentation\"\nabstract: \"Apply training-only positional masking before the backbone (prob=0.05 per position), identity at eval. Hypothesis: regularizes locality and improves generalization without changing the loss or loop.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_minibase_expts import create_network, create_optimizer\n\
    \n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"reverse_avg\": False,\n          \"use_powermean\": False,\n          \"token_drop_p\": 0.05,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Choosing a baseline thoughtfully**\n\nI need to select a baseline like \"DSConv mean+max,\" but maybe it's worth considering a simpler option like 1D Conv with Global mean+max pooling since my current baseline is pretty low. The alternative \"DSConv mean+max\" shows better potential. The instructions suggest using a simple baseline with a reasonable score, so I should probably go with \"DSConv mean+max, no motif, no RegCal.\" I also need to generate three new ideas that differ from past archives, which will be a challenge.**Generating unique ideas**\n\nI need to come up with truly different ideas. One possibility is a position-free token drop augmentation using Random Nucleotide Masking with a consistency regularization method similar to R-Drop. This could help improve CRI-Off stability while maintaining invariance to noise. However, I can't modify the training loop, particularly train_single.py. Instead, I could implement a stochastic token masking within the network\
  \ while ensuring it applies only when deterministic is false—though I have to be cautious not to violate any guidelines.**Exploring innovative ideas**\n\nI’m brainstorming ideas for architecture. One option, Idea B, is adaptive power-mean pooling with gradient-safe reparameterization, which could be a novel alternative to LSE, especially since we haven't addressed it in the archive. However, we need to ensure it doesn't overlap with previously learned parameters.\n\nFor Idea C, I’m considering antisense reverse-complement equivariance. While RNA tasks might have strand-specific characteristics, it's essential to be cautious about using external knowledge that could lead to incorrect assumptions regarding reverse complement symmetry.**Proposing new ideas**\n\nI'm considering implementing \"reverse-invariant pooling,\" where I average the representation of a sequence and its reversed version processed through a shared backbone. This method would involve weight-sharing for original and reversed\
  \ inputs, allowing for averaging features before they reach the head. While it does double the computation, I think it could be a novel approach, even though it seems like data augmentation.\n\nFor Idea D, I’m thinking about \"phase-shifted dilations\" in a multi-grid setup. Then, for Idea E, we could center features per batch before pooling, similar to BatchNorm but using Layer Normalization. Lastly, for Idea F, there's the \"ordinal regression head for PRS\" tailored to multi-label regression.**Planning the experimentation**\n\nI can't change the loss function since it’s mean squared error (MSE), but I could use bounded outputs through a tanh for reducing outliers, though this could affect predictions. We need to come up with three new ideas that are implementable with the allowed functions. I’m thinking of using a baseline of DSConv mean+max without motif or RegCal. I’ll also implement ideas like reverse-invariant pooling, power-mean pooling with learned parameters, and a TokenDrop\
  \ layer for some interesting variations. I’ll establish a plan for submission steps to keep everything organized and compliant.**Implementing the code**\n\nI'm planning to write separate files for the dsconv_common backbone functions to minimize code duplication. To save tokens, I can implement both the baseline and its variants in a single file controlled by hyperparameters. \n\nI'll create a script called `dsconv_minibase_expts.py` where I can toggle options like reverse averaging, power mean, and token drop. It's essential to ensure that functions like `_define_hyperparameters`, `create_network`, and `create_optimizer` are implemented correctly. I’ll also focus on ensuring functionality for the token drop and reverse averaging processes. Finally, I’ll organize submissions for each idea with specific hyperparameter settings."
