parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_minibase_expts.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Minimal DSConv + pooling baseline and three probes (Stagnation Protocol I):\n    - reverse_avg: process x and reversed x with shared backbone; average features (no new params)\n    - use_powermean: replace max with learned power mean (mean + p-mean)\n    - token_drop_p: training-only positional masking before backbone\n\n  Heads: single hidden MLP (128) per task_type, no RegCal, no motif. <1M params.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          \"\
    head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          # Probes\n          \"reverse_avg\": False,\n          \"use_powermean\": False,\n          \"p_init\": 2.0,          # (not used directly; p starts near ~1.7 via softplus(0)+1)\n          \"token_drop_p\": 0.0,\n      }\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n\
    \          return residual + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def global_mean_max(h):\n      mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n      maxv = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n      return jnp.concatenate([mean, maxv], axis=-1)\n\n  class PowerMean(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Learned power-mean on ReLU(h) across length.\"\"\"\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n          u = self.param(\"p_raw\", nn.initializers.zeros, (1,))\n          p = jax.nn.softplus(u) + 1.0\n          hp = jax.nn.relu(h)\n          eps = 1e-6\n          m\
    \ = jnp.mean(jnp.power(hp + eps, p), axis=1)\n          return jnp.power(m + eps, 1.0 / p)\n\n  class MiniDSConvNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      head_hidden: int = 128\n      head_dropout: float = 0.05\n      reverse_avg: bool = False\n      use_powermean: bool = False\n      token_drop_p: float = 0.0\n\n      def _token_drop(self, x, *, deterministic: bool):\n          if deterministic or self.token_drop_p <= 0.0:\n              return x\n          rng = self.make_rng(\"dropout\")\n          keep = random.bernoulli(rng, p=1.0 - self.token_drop_p, shape=(x.shape[0], x.shape[1], 1))\n          return x * keep\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Optional positional masking\n          x = self._token_drop(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          # Shared backbone\n\
    \          backbone = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate, name=\"backbone\")\n          h = backbone(x, deterministic)\n          if self.reverse_avg:\n              h_rev = backbone(jnp.flip(x, axis=1), deterministic)  # shared params\n              h = 0.5 * (h + h_rev)\n\n          # Pooling\n          if self.use_powermean:\n              pmean = PowerMean(name=\"pmean\")(h)\n              mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n              pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean, pmean], axis=-1)\n          else:\n              pooled = global_mean_max(h)\n\n          # Head (single hidden)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(pooled)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return out.squeeze(-1)\n\
    \          return out\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = MiniDSConvNet(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n              head_hidden=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden\", 128)),\n              head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n              reverse_avg=bool(hp.get(\"reverse_avg\", False)),\n              use_powermean=bool(hp.get(\"use_powermean\", False)),\n              token_drop_p=float(hp.get(\"token_drop_p\", 0.0)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n\
    \          variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MINI-Baseline: DSConv (5 dilations) + mean+max pooling — no motif, no RegCal — seed=42\"\ntags: \"baseline,\
    \ dsconv, pooling, meanmax\"\nabstract: \"Simple DSConv backbone with dilations [1,2,4,8,16] and global mean+max pooling. Single hidden head; no motif path and no regression calibration. Reproduces a reasonable baseline under Stagnation Protocol.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_minibase_expts import create_network as build_net, create_optimizer as make_opt\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"reverse_avg\": False,\n          \"use_powermean\": False,\n          \"token_drop_p\": 0.0,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_net(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n  \
    \    return make_opt(learning_rate)\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Idea 1 — RevAvg: reverse-invariant dual-view averaging + mean+max — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, invariance, reverse, robustness\"\nabstract: \"Process x and reversed x through the same DSConv backbone; average features before global pooling (mean+max). Hypothesis: reverse invariance improves robustness and CRI-* stability with no extra parameters.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_minibase_expts import create_network as build_net, create_optimizer as make_opt\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"reverse_avg\": True,\n         \
    \ \"use_powermean\": False,\n          \"token_drop_p\": 0.0,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_net(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_opt(learning_rate)\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Idea 2 — P-mean: mean + learned power-mean pooling (p≥1) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, power-mean, adaptive\"\nabstract: \"Replace max with a learned power-mean (on ReLUed features) reparameterized as p=softplus(u)+1; concatenate with mean. Hypothesis: smoother interpolation between mean and max improves stability vs. LSE τ.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_minibase_expts import create_network as build_net, create_optimizer as make_opt\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\"\
    : 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"reverse_avg\": False,\n          \"use_powermean\": True,\n          \"p_init\": 2.0,\n          \"token_drop_p\": 0.0,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_net(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_opt(learning_rate)\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Idea 3 — SPD: training-only Stochastic Position Dropout (p=0.05) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, regularization, augmentation\"\nabstract: \"Apply training-only positional masking before the backbone (prob=0.05 per position), identity at eval. Hypothesis: regularizes locality and improves generalization without changing the loss or loop.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_minibase_expts import create_network as build_net, create_optimizer as make_opt\n\n  BASE_SEED =\
    \ 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"reverse_avg\": False,\n          \"use_powermean\": False,\n          \"token_drop_p\": 0.05,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_net(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_opt(learning_rate)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Addressing code storage issues**


  It looks like we attempted to store the code file `dsconv_minibase_expts.py` in the Archive Room, but that didn''t go through. So, I need to make sure to write that file again before submitting. I’ll also follow YAML quoting rules and keep an eye out for potential naming conflicts with `create_network`, as it seems there was a double definition in the previous content. It''s essential not to overshadow imported names while defining functions.**Evaluating naming conflicts**


  It seems like they used the same names, leading to overshadowing recursion issues. Earlier, they imported `create_network` and `create_optimizer`, but then defined `create_network(hparams)` in a way that would create infinite recursion. It’s puzzling that despite these patterns, previous evaluations succeeded. They might not have defined wrappers before, or perhaps the overshadowing allowed name resolution to use the imported `create_network`. Still, defining the function to call itself would lead to recursion. Yet, previous runs managed to execute successfully and scored well.**Analyzing function naming issues**


  It seems that in earlier work, they imported `build_network` and defined `create_network` to call that instead. In the LogitNorm code, they used `create_network` directly within its definition, which would cause a crash. Nevertheless, evaluations produced outputs, suggesting the system only retains defined functions. If they imported with the same name and didn''t manage the overshadowing correctly, it could lead to recursion. Python resolves names at compile time, meaning the name refers to itself during execution unless a different alias had been used.**Correcting code aliasing**


  In the earlier baseline, they used the import statement `from dsconv_minibase_expts import create_network, create_optimizer`, just like now. But, we need to correct the recursion issues by aliasing. So, I''ll use `from dsconv_minibase_expts import create_network as build_net, create_optimizer as make_opt`, then define `create_network(hparams)` to call `build_net(hparams)`, and `create_optimizer(learning_rate=0.001)` to call `make_opt(learning_rate)`. Next, I’ll write the code to `dsconv_minibase_expts.py`, ensuring we store it correctly before submitting multiple times with varying hyperparameters. I''ll check the dropout settings too!**Reviewing code consistency**


  I need to ensure to import `jax.random` as it''s used in the submissions. For the baseline, we''re working with "MINI-Baseline: DSConv (5 dilations) + mean+max pooling" using a seed of 42, and I’ll alias the functions to prevent any recursion issues.


  For modifications, we have several ideas: First, I’ll set `reverse_avg` to true. In another idea, setting `use_powermean` to true with an initial value of 2.0 needs some attention, as it doesn''t currently support the `p_init` parameter — perhaps I can read from `hparams`. The `PowerMean` function could be adapted to initialize `p_raw` to zeros, leading to around 1.693 for `p`. Lastly, I’ll set a `token_drop_p` of 0.05 and include other relevant parameters to finalize the actions.'
