parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 480\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema II — Working Meta (Tick 457)\nStatus:\n- wd=0.012 tri-seed mean = 0.6880 → keep wd=0.01 default.\n- Post‑RegCal z′: ON files materialized (property: per‑sample L2=1); OFF capture running (ID 719).\n\nNext:\n- After 719 completes, re-run norms_post_aggregate.py and append ON/OFF z′ table to Archive #22.\n- Close the analysis loop; no further head tuning planned.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 131,111 / 270,000 used (49%)\n- Agent Age: 187 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'MINI-Baseline: DSConv (5 dilations) + mean+max pooling — no motif, no RegCal — seed=42' (ID: 767) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6744577676558402\n**APA_R2:**\
    \ 0.8491\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0978\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9515\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4684\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5554\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8666\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9323\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 767\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code successfully. The submission now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported a function from the agent's lineage directory (`storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_minibase_expts.py`) that contained a bug. Specifically, the `DSConvBlock` class was using an incorrect parameter name for dilated convolutions in Flax.\n\n**The Bug:**\n```python\nx = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n            dilation=(self.dilation,),  # WRONG - parameter doesn't exist\n            padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n```\n\n**Error Message:**\n```\nTypeError: Conv.__init__()\
    \ got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'\n```\n\nIn Flax's `nn.Conv` layer, the parameter for dilation is called `kernel_dilation`, not `dilation`.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\nCreated `submission_v3.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Removed the import** from the buggy lineage file:\n   - Deleted: `from dsconv_minibase_expts import create_network as build_net, create_optimizer as make_opt`\n\n2. **Copied the complete network implementation** into the submission file to avoid using the buggy lineage code\n\n3. **Fixed the parameter name** in the `DSConvBlock` class (line 40):\n   ```python\n   x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n               kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n               feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n               kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),  # FIXED: changed 'dilation' to 'kernel_dilation'\n               padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n   ```\n\n## Verification\n\nThe monitor script confirmed success:\n- **Version 3** was created and executed\n- Code\
    \ ran for **300+ seconds** without crashing (timeout period)\n- Exit code: **0 (success)**\n- Status: Code is running successfully\n\nThe evaluation is still processing (likely running the full training pipeline across multiple datasets), but the critical issue has been resolved - the code no longer crashes on initialization.\n\n## Technical Details\n\n- **Issue Location:** `storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_minibase_expts.py`, line 43\n- **Fix Location:** `submissions/submission_v3.py`, line 40\n- **Root Cause:** API parameter name mismatch between intended usage and Flax library interface\n- **Solution:** Updated parameter name from `dilation` to `kernel_dilation` to match Flax API\n\n## Note on Earlier Attempts\n\nVersion 2 failed because it still imported from the lineage file even though it defined a local `DSConvBlock`. The `create_network` function called `build_net` from the import, which used the buggy lineage version instead of the fixed local version. Version 3 resolved this\
    \ by providing a complete standalone implementation.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\n\"\"\"\nFixed version - changed 'dilation' to 'kernel_dilation' in nn.Conv\n\nComplete implementation without imports from lineage file.\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n        \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n        \"kernel_size\": 7,\n        \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n        \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n        \"head_hidden\": 128,\n        \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n        \"reverse_avg\": False,\n        \"use_powermean\": False,\n        \"token_drop_p\": 0.0,\n    }\n\n# FIXED: Changed 'dilation' parameter\
    \ to 'kernel_dilation'\nclass DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        residual = x\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                    kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                    feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),  # FIXED: was 'dilation'\n                    padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n        return residual + x\n\nclass DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilations: Sequence[int]\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\
    \ kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n        for d in self.dilations:\n            h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n        return h\n\ndef global_mean_max(h):\n    mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n    maxv = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n    return jnp.concatenate([mean, maxv], axis=-1)\n\nclass PowerMean(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Learned power-mean on ReLU(h) across length.\"\"\"\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h):\n        u = self.param(\"p_raw\", nn.initializers.zeros, (1,))\n        p = jax.nn.softplus(u) + 1.0\n        hp = jax.nn.relu(h)\n        eps = 1e-6\n        m = jnp.mean(jnp.power(hp + eps, p), axis=1)\n        return jnp.power(m + eps, 1.0 / p)\n\nclass MiniDSConvNet(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    hidden_dim: int = 256\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    head_hidden: int = 128\n    head_dropout:\
    \ float = 0.05\n    reverse_avg: bool = False\n    use_powermean: bool = False\n    token_drop_p: float = 0.0\n\n    def _token_drop(self, x, *, deterministic: bool):\n        if deterministic or self.token_drop_p <= 0.0:\n            return x\n        rng = self.make_rng(\"dropout\")\n        keep = random.bernoulli(rng, p=1.0 - self.token_drop_p, shape=(x.shape[0], x.shape[1], 1))\n        return x * keep\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # Optional positional masking\n        x = self._token_drop(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        # Shared backbone\n        backbone = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate, name=\"backbone\")\n        h = backbone(x, deterministic)\n        if self.reverse_avg:\n            h_rev = backbone(jnp.flip(x, axis=1), deterministic)  # shared params\n            h = 0.5 * (h + h_rev)\n\n        # Pooling\n        if self.use_powermean:\n            pmean\
    \ = PowerMean(name=\"pmean\")(h)\n            mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n            pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean, pmean], axis=-1)\n        else:\n            pooled = global_mean_max(h)\n\n        # Head (single hidden)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(pooled)\n        z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n        z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n            return out.squeeze(-1)\n        return out\n\nclass WrappedRNANetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n        hp = hparams or {}\n        self.net = MiniDSConvNet(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n            kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n            ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"\
    ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n            dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n            head_hidden=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden\", 128)),\n            head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n            reverse_avg=bool(hp.get(\"reverse_avg\", False)),\n            use_powermean=bool(hp.get(\"use_powermean\", False)),\n            token_drop_p=float(hp.get(\"token_drop_p\", 0.0)),\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params},\
    \ x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward\
