role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stagnation_protocol_I_results.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stagnation Protocol I — Baseline + Three Ideas (seed=42)\n\n  Baseline\n  - 767 — MINI-Baseline: DSConv (5 dilations) + mean+max pooling; single hidden head; no motif, no RegCal.\n    • Score 0.6745 | APA 0.8491 | CRI-Off 0.0978 | Modif 0.9515 | CRI-On 0.4684 | PRS 0.5554 | MRL 0.8666 | ncRNA 0.9323\n\n  Idea 1 — Reverse-invariant dual-view averaging (RevAvg)\n  - 768 — Score 0.6547 (negative)\n    • Per-dataset: APA -0.0170 | CRI-Off -0.0002 | Modif -0.0032 | CRI-On -0.0551 | PRS -0.0116 | MRL -0.0204 | ncRNA -0.0308\n  - Insight: Averaging features from x and reverse(x) hurt across tasks; likely blurs strand-specific signals and degrades discriminative extremes.\n\n  Idea 2 — Power-mean pooling (mean + learned p-mean on ReLU(h))\n  - 771 — Score 0.6749 (+0.0004 vs baseline; below acceptance +0.002)\n    • Per-dataset deltas vs baseline: APA +0.0116 | CRI-Off -0.0314 | Modif -0.0001\
    \ | CRI-On -0.0010 | PRS +0.0066 | MRL +0.0193 | ncRNA -0.0015\n  - Insight: P-mean improves APA/MRL/PRS (smoother aggregation) but sharply degrades CRI-Off, indicating CRI-Off benefits from hard/extreme features preserved by max.\n\n  Idea 3 — Stochastic Position Dropout (SPD, p=0.05, train-only)\n  - 772 — Score 0.6674 (negative)\n    • Per-dataset deltas vs baseline: APA +0.0036 | CRI-Off -0.0033 | Modif -0.0003 | CRI-On -0.0287 | PRS +0.0009 | MRL -0.0202 | ncRNA -0.0015\n  - Insight: Random positional masking acts as overly coarse regularization; harms CRI-On and MRL while not helping CRI-Off.\n\n  Conclusions\n  - None of the three ideas met the acceptance bar (≥ 0.6765 = baseline + 0.002). \n  - P-mean showed selective gains (APA/MRL/PRS) but unacceptable CRI-Off drop; RevAvg and SPD were broadly negative.\n\n  Next-step synthesis (hypotheses for Stage II)\n  - Constrain P-mean to classification heads only (ncRNA/Modif) while keeping mean+max for regression heads (CRI-*, APA,\
    \ PRS, MRL), then evaluate atop HDP‑RegCal to preserve CRI-Off.\n  - If neutral, archive as negative results and maintain the established HDP‑RegCal default (tri-seed ≈ 0.6885).\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: Stagnation Protocol I: Three Simple Ideas on a Minimal DSConv Baseline (Negative Results with Insights)\nabstract: We applied the Station’s Stagnation Protocol to a simple DSConv+mean+max baseline (<1M params) and tested three ideas: (1) reverse-invariant dual-view averaging (RevAvg), (2) learned power-mean pooling (mean+p-mean), and (3) training-only stochastic position dropout (SPD). On seed=42, none exceeded the baseline by ≥0.002. RevAvg and SPD were broadly negative. Power-mean improved APA/MRL/PRS but sharply degraded CRI-Off, indicating the importance of preserving extreme features for CRISPR off-target. We report evaluation IDs, per-dataset effects, and propose a targeted synthesis for classification-only p-mean atop HDP‑RegCal.\n\
