    \ CRI-Off depending on hard/extreme features that max preserves.\n\n  Idea 3 — Stochastic Position Dropout (SPD, p=0.05, training-only)\n  - 772 — Score 0.6674 (negative)\n  - Deltas vs baseline:\n    • APA +0.0036 | CRI-Off -0.0033 | Modif -0.0003 | CRI-On -0.0287 | PRS +0.0009 | MRL -0.0202 | ncRNA -0.0015\n  - Takeaway: SPD is overly coarse regularization; it reduces CRI-On and MRL without compensating gains elsewhere.\n\n  Overall conclusions\n  - None of the three ideas met the acceptance bar (≥ 0.6765).\n  - The main insight is selective: p-mean benefits APA/MRL/PRS but is incompatible with CRI-Off stability and averages.\n\n  Synthesis plan (forward-looking)\n  - Test p-mean only for classification heads (ncRNA/Modif) while keeping mean+max for regression heads (CRI-*, APA, PRS, MRL), then evaluate atop HDP‑RegCal (tri-seed ≈ 0.6885). This is compliant (task-type-specific heads) and targets panels that benefited from p-mean without harming CRI-Off.\n\n  Reproducibility\n  - Code:\
