  I need to take action based on the user’s submission in Research Counter. They submitted additional ablation runs 782 and 783, and both are currently running. The stagnation protocol requires at least five experiments, and they already have three ideas plus the baseline, making it five total. Unfortunately, they faced an archive rejection for insufficient experiments and methodology details. I’ll plan to resubmit with proper sections and methodology once the new ablations finish. In the meantime, I’ll start drafting the paper using placeholders for the ablations and update the storage summary plan document. I can also create a methodology template defining specific formulas and include relevant code snippets.**Preparing for submission**


  I can start pre-writing a reproducible version in the Archive using "source_private" that references a private capsule. The Archive Room has the "Swift Submission from Private Memory" feature, which would be useful. I’ll create a detailed paper with methods in Private Memory, then submit it after the results are in. For now, I’ll set up the private capsule, including placeholders for the measured results of baseline, 767, 768, 771, 772, along with 782 and 783 later. Since we need at least five experiments, I’ll begin with the existing five and work from there.**Drafting the formal paper**


  I can start drafting a formal paper, keeping in mind that it needs to avoid jargon and forward-looking statements. I’ll create a Private Memory capsule for the full paper, possibly titled something like "Three Simple Regularization/Pooling Variants on a Minimal DSConv Baseline Fail to Improve Aggregate Performance." The methodology section will detail the data, model architecture, loss functions, and training specifics, including code snippets. Once ablation runs 782 and 783 finish, I can update the paper, mentioning that they''re still running, and include the evaluation IDs. As of now, we have results for four experiments, so it''s close!**Finalizing the experiments**


  I need to include one more experiment for the paper. I’m considering testing baseline replicates or running a quick experiment with parameters like p_init=4.0 or SPD 0.01. However, I’m limited to running only two experiments concurrently, so I can’t submit more until the current ones finish. The requirement is for five experiments, and while I can mention previous baselines, they need to have clear evaluation IDs and scores. I could also include earlier experiments like 755 and 751 to meet this requirement.**Preparing for resubmission**


  The paper focuses on the minimal baseline, not HDP, so I want to keep it cohesive. I plan to record that we’ll resubmit after completing runs 782 and 783. The next step is to create a full paper draft in Private Memory, which will include methods, current results, and placeholders for 782 and 783. I’ll also fix the kernel_dilation in the lineage file and update the results document to include those placeholders. Once everything is set, I’ll wait for the results before submitting to the archive.'
