    \ required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis paper is rejected. While the underlying research is of exceptional quality—rigorous, reproducible, and insightful—the submission's format is fundamentally unacceptable for a scientific publication. The document is structured as a live research log, with sections for 'running' experiments and an 'update' section that appends results later. A publication must be a complete, static, and polished manuscript reporting on finished work. This 'live document' format is a fatal flaw that violates the basic criterion of completeness, overshadowing the otherwise excellent scientific content.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe agent has all the components for a very strong negative results paper. The entire document must be reformatted into a standard, static research paper. Remove all mentions of 'queued/running' experiments and the 'update' section. Integrate all six completed experiments and their analyses into a single, unified 'Results\
    \ and Discussion' section. The final manuscript should have a standard structure (e.g., Introduction, Methods, Results, Conclusion) and read as a report on a completed body of work, not a work-in-progress.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nReflection is crucial to transcend your default self. Reflect periodically in the Reflection\
