parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_cls_pmean.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  HDP‑RegCal with task-type-specific pooling:\n    - Regression-family heads (APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, PRS, MRL): main pooling = mean+max; RegCal ON (per-sample L2) before head.\n    - Classification heads (Modif, ncRNA): main pooling = mean + learned Power-Mean (P-mean) on ReLU(h), p = softplus(u)+1 (p_init∈{2,3}).\n  Backbone and motif path shared across all tasks; only head pooling differs by task_type (compliant).\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import math\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n\
    \          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          # classification pooling\n          \"cls_pmean_init\": 2.0,   # try 2.0 or 3.0\n      }\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),  # correct API\n                      padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual\
    \ + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def global_mean_max(h):\n      mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n      maxv = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n      return jnp.concatenate([mean, maxv], axis=-1)\n\n  def _softplus_inv(y: float) -> float:\n      # inverse softplus for y>0: x = log(exp(y)-1)\n      return math.log(math.expm1(y)) if y > 0.0 else -20.0\n\n  class PowerMean(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Learned power-mean on ReLU(h) across length.\"\"\"\n      p_init: float = 2.0\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n          target\
    \ = max(1.0, float(self.p_init)) - 1.0\n          u0 = _softplus_inv(target)\n          def init_fn(rng, shape):\n              return jnp.full(shape, u0, dtype=h.dtype)\n          u = self.param(\"p_raw\", init_fn, (1,))\n          p = jax.nn.softplus(u) + 1.0\n          hp = jax.nn.relu(h)\n          eps = 1e-6\n          m = jnp.mean(jnp.power(hp + eps, p), axis=1)\n          return jnp.power(m + eps, 1.0 / p)\n\n  class MotifBranch(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      k: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.k,), padding=\"SAME\")(h)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n          return x\n\n  def l2_normalize_feats(z, eps=1e-6):\n      return z / (jnp.linalg.norm(z, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + eps)\n\n  class HDPRegCalTaskTypePooling(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int]\
    \ = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      motif_k: int = 5\n      head_dropout: float = 0.05\n      regcal_on: bool = True\n      cls_pmean_init: float = 2.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Backbone\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          # Task-type specific main pooling\n          if self.task_type in (\"multilabel_classification\", \"multiclass_classification\"):\n              pmean = PowerMean(self.cls_pmean_init, name=\"cls_pmean\")(h)\n              mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n              main_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean, pmean], axis=-1)\n          else:\n              main_pooled = global_mean_max(h)\n          # Motif path\n          motif_pooled = MotifBranch(self.hidden_dim, self.motif_k)(h)\n          # Fuse and project\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_pooled, motif_pooled], axis=-1)  # 3*hidden\n\
    \          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\"):\n              z_reg = l2_normalize_feats(z) if self.regcal_on else z\n              z_reg = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z_reg, deterministic=deterministic)\n              out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_reg)\n              return out.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else out\n          else:\n              z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n              logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_cls)\n              return logits\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.network = HDPRegCalTaskTypePooling(\n\
    \              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n              motif_k=int(hp.get(\"motif_k\", 5)),\n              head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n              regcal_on=bool(hp.get(\"regcal_on\", True)),\n              cls_pmean_init=float(hp.get(\"cls_pmean_init\", 2.0)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params':\
    \ params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.01):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP‑RegCal (task-type pooling): regression mean+max+RegCal; classification mean+P-mean (p_init=2.0) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, regcal, task-type, pmean, motif\"\nabstract: \"Implements task-type-specific pooling: regression-family heads use mean+max with RegCal; classification heads use mean+learned Power-Mean (p=softplus(u)+1, p_init=2.0). Backbone/motif\
    \ shared across tasks; heads differ by prediction type (compliant). Tests if classification-only smoothing recovers gains without hurting CRI-Off.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from hdp_regcal_cls_pmean import create_network as build_net, create_optimizer as make_opt\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          \"cls_pmean_init\": 2.0\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_net(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_opt(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle:\
    \ \"HDP‑RegCal (task-type pooling): regression mean+max+RegCal; classification mean+P-mean (p_init=3.0) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, pooling, regcal, task-type, pmean, motif, ablation\"\nabstract: \"Same as task-type pooling model but with stronger initial sharpness for classification P-mean (p_init=3.0). Ablation to test sensitivity and trade-offs across panels.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from hdp_regcal_cls_pmean import create_network as build_net, create_optimizer as make_opt\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          \"cls_pmean_init\": 3.0\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      return build_net(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_opt(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n/execute_action{storage write noema/results/HDP_task_type_pooling_plan.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Plan: Task-type pooling atop HDP‑RegCal\n  - Model: regression heads = mean+max + RegCal; classification heads = mean+P-mean (p_init∈{2,3}); shared DSConv backbone (5 dilations) and motif branch k=5.\n  - Submissions: IDs (pending) — p_init=2.0 and p_init=3.0, seed=42.\n  - Acceptance: ≥0.689 on seed 42 with CRI-Off ≥ baseline (≈0.08) and no major regressions; then tri-seed {7,123}.\n  - If neutral: retain default HDP‑RegCal; document negative results as an addendum to Archive #25.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating pooling strategies**


  I’m thinking about how using different pooling methods would change the representation dimension. Both options generate vectors of the same dimension, so they match. The P-mean produces a hidden_dim vector, similar to max pooling, which is fine. I need to implement the network to compute pooling based on the task type: classification gets P-mean, while others use max. It''s essential to ensure the model parameters include the P-mean block and that final layers can differ while following the core architecture guidelines.**Planning the network structure**


  I’m considering how to frame the head pooling as “task-type-specific head pooling” while keeping the backbone consistent. Tailoring the head pooling to prediction types seems acceptable. I need to implement the create_network function with hparams and aggregator class. Key elements include using kernel_dilation in the DSConvBlock and having pooling functions like mean and max, as well as a P-mean module. I’ll also determine how to handle classification and regression tasks, ensuring appropriate features and normalization methods!**Adjusting hyperparameters for submissions**


  I’m planning to keep the previously effective hyperparameters like hidden_dim 256, kernel size 7, motif_k 5, and various dropout rates. The evaluation title will be HDP-RegCal, with regression using mean and max pooling while classification uses mean and p-mean (p_init=2.0). Since previous evaluations just finished, it looks like I can submit two in one go: p_init set at 2.0 and 3.0 with seed 42, occupying the 2 available concurrency slots. I''ll also log the plan update file and focus on producing the necessary commands!'
