parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write noema/results/HDP_task_type_pooling_results.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  HDP‑RegCal with Task-Type Pooling (Regression: mean+max+RegCal; Classification: mean+P-mean)\n  Summary (seed=42)\n\n  Baseline reference (default HDP‑RegCal tri-seed ≈ 0.6885; seed‑42 ≈ 0.6886 from ID 713). Acceptance bar: ≥ 0.689 with CRI‑Off ≥ 0.08, no major regressions.\n\n  Results:\n  - 787 — cls P‑mean p_init=2.0: 0.6815\n    APA 0.8463 | CRI‑Off 0.0859 | Modif 0.9514 | CRI‑On 0.4962 | PRS 0.5668 | MRL 0.8807 | ncRNA 0.9431\n    Notes: Preserves CRI‑Off ≥ 0.08 and improves CRI‑On/PRS vs many prior runs, but avg < 0.689 target.\n\n  - 788 — cls P‑mean p_init=3.0: 0.6767\n    APA 0.8602 | CRI‑Off 0.0797 | Modif 0.9515 | CRI‑On 0.4580 | PRS 0.5693 | MRL 0.8842 | ncRNA 0.9338\n    Notes: Slight CRI‑Off dip (<0.08) and weaker CRI‑On; higher p sharpened classification pooling but did not raise avg.\n\n  Interpretation:\n  - Classification‑only P‑mean recovers some gains (PRS/CR\
    \ I‑On) while largely preserving CRI‑Off at p_init=2.0, but does not meet the target average. Stronger p (3.0) drops CRI‑Off below 0.08 and lowers average.\n  - Conclusion: Do not adopt; retain default HDP‑RegCal. Record as negative results in Archive #25.\n```\n\n/execute_action{reply 25}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Task-Type Pooling (mean+max+RegCal for regression; mean+P-mean for classification)\"\ncontent: |\n  We implemented the reviewer’s suggestion to test task-type-specific pooling atop HDP‑RegCal:\n  - Regression-family heads (APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, PRS, MRL): mean+max pooling + RegCal (unchanged).\n  - Classification heads (Modif, ncRNA): mean + learned Power-Mean (p=softplus(u)+1), with p_init∈{2.0, 3.0}.\n  - Shared DSConv backbone (5 dilations) and motif branch; only pooling differs by task_type (compliant).\n\n  Results (seed=42):\n  - ID 787 (p_init=2.0): 0.6815 | APA 0.8463 | CRI-Off 0.0859 | Modif 0.9514 | CRI-On 0.4962 | PRS 0.5668 | MRL 0.8807 | ncRNA 0.9431\n  - ID\
    \ 788 (p_init=3.0): 0.6767 | APA 0.8602 | CRI-Off 0.0797 | Modif 0.9515 | CRI-On 0.4580 | PRS 0.5693 | MRL 0.8842 | ncRNA 0.9338\n\n  Conclusion:\n  - Classification-only P-mean improves PRS and often CRI-On while keeping CRI-Off ≥ 0.08 at p_init=2.0, but the overall average did not exceed the HDP‑RegCal baseline (tri-seed ≈ 0.6885). Stronger p_init=3.0 lowered CRI-Off (<0.08) and the average.\n  - We therefore do not adopt task-type P-mean and retain the default HDP‑RegCal configuration.\n\n  Reproducibility:\n  - Code: storage/noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_cls_pmean.py\n  - IDs: 787 (p_init=2.0), 788 (p_init=3.0)\n  - Summary: storage/noema/results/HDP_task_type_pooling_plan.md, storage/noema/results/HDP_task_type_pooling_results.md\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning task updates**


  I’m thinking about how to use a reply for an addendum that keeps the previous text while summarizing the results. I want to confirm that while a tri-seed isn''t necessary since the acceptance criteria weren''t met, I’ll still include specific code pointers to certain evaluation IDs. I should be concise and focus on two main actions: crafting a results document and replying to archive #25 with an appropriate title and summary. Let''s move forward with this!**Reflecting on results**


  I’m noticing that the CRI-Off is preserved for p=2.0 at 0.0859, but there’s a slight drop for p=3.0 to 0.0797. The averages are 0.6815 and 0.6767, not exceeding 0.689, which suggests tri-seeding isn’t necessary. I’m also thinking that the classification-only P-mean didn’t yield an overall improvement, but it wasn''t negative either. Since 0.6815 is less than 0.6885, I propose to stick with the default and document this negative outcome. Now, let’s produce the final results!'
