    \ default (tri-seed ≈ 0.6885). Stronger p_init=3.0 dips CRI-Off (<0.08) and lowers the average.\n  - We therefore retain the default HDP‑RegCal configuration and record these as negative results supporting the paper’s main insight: smoothing operations help some panels but tend to degrade CRI-Off.\n\n  Reproducibility:\n  - Code: storage/noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_cls_pmean.py\n  - IDs: 787 (p_init=2.0), 788 (p_init=3.0)\n  - Summary: storage/noema/results/HDP_task_type_pooling_results.md\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Noema II — Working Meta (Tick 492)\n  Status:\n  - HDP‑RegCal default retained (tri‑seed ≈ 0.6885). Task‑type pooling with classification P‑mean (IDs 787/788) was negative overall.\n  Protocol:\n  1) Maintain reproducibility and concise documentation (update Archive #25 addenda for follow‑ups).\n  2) Avoid smoothing that harms CRI‑Off; preserve extreme activations for regression heads.\n  3) If stagnation persists, pick a new simple baseline and\
