tick: 493
role: model
parts:
- text: "Reflection Tick 1\n\nFeasibility and design details\n\nA) Regression-head WeightNorm (WN)\n- Layer form (per-output row weightnorm on final Dense):\n  - Params: v ∈ R^{d_in×d_out}, g ∈ R^{d_out}, b ∈ R^{d_out}\n  - Compute: w_i = (g_i / ||v_i||) · v_i (row-wise norm over d_in); y = z_reg · W + b\n- Why with RegCal: z_reg is per-sample unit-norm, so output scale is governed by g; removes residual scale coupling and may steady CRI-Off/PRS.\n- Implementation notes:\n  - Init v ~ N(0, σ); set g = 1.0 (or ||v_i|| at init for identity scaling); keep bias b.\n  - Apply only to regression-family heads (APA, CRI-* , PRS, MRL); leave classification heads unchanged.\n- Risks/mitigations: too-strong g growth → add mild weight decay (already have); WN sometimes slows early learning—accept small patience.\n\nB) Cosine classifier (feature+weight norm) for classification heads\n- Logits: ẑ = z_cls / ||z_cls||; Ŵ = W / ||W|| (row- or column-wise consistent); logits = α · ẑ · Ŵ (+ b for Modif\
    \ only).\n  - ncRNA (multiclass): typically no bias; α learned scalar (init 10).\n  - Modif (multilabel): keep per-class bias b to capture priors; α learned scalar (init 5–10).\n- Differences vs LogitNorm: also normalizes weights (not just features), removing classifier weight scale as a confound.\n- Risks: too-small α under-confident logits—use learned α with sensible init; BCE can tolerate, bias handles priors.\n\nC) Head rebalancing (capacity shift)\n- After fused projection, use hidden widths:\n  - Regression head hidden = 160 (from 128)\n  - Classification head hidden = 96 (from 128)\n- Rationale: slight capacity boost where RegCal helps (regression), small reduction where capacity is less critical; preserves <1M params.\n- Risks: classification small drop—acceptable if avg ≥0.689 and CRI-Off stable.\n\nAcceptance and diagnostics\n- Gate: seed-42 avg ≥ 0.689 and CRI-Off ≥ 0.08, no major regressions; else negative result.\n- Inspect: CRI-Off/Spearman stability; PRS R²; ncRNA accuracy;\
    \ Modif AUC; watch for α explosions (cap α if needed, e.g., softplus(α_raw)+1)."
