tick: 494
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_head_probes.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  HDP‑RegCal head probes (low-complexity, compliant):\n    - Backbone: DSConv (5 dilations), shared; motif branch k=5; mean+max main pooling for all tasks.\n    - Regression heads: RegCal (per-sample L2 on fused features); optional WeightNorm on final Dense.\n    - Classification heads: standard Dense; optional Cosine classifier (feature+weight norm) with learnable alpha.\n    - Optional head width rebalancing (reg_hidden, cls_hidden).\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\"\
    : [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          # Probes\n          \"use_reg_head_weightnorm\": True,   # A\n          \"use_cls_cosine\": False,           # B\n          \"reg_head_hidden\": 128,            # C (set 160 to test rebalancing)\n          \"cls_head_hidden\": 128,            # C (set 96 to test rebalancing)\n          \"alpha_init\": 10.0                 # for cosine classifier (ncRNA ~10, Modif 5-10)\n      }\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n      \
    \                padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def global_mean_max(h):\n      mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n      maxv = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n      return jnp.concatenate([mean, maxv], axis=-1)\n\n  class MotifBranch(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim:\
    \ int\n      k: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.k,), padding=\"SAME\")(h)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n          return x\n\n  def l2_normalize(x, eps=1e-6):\n      return x / (jnp.linalg.norm(x, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + eps)\n\n  class DenseWN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      use_bias: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          in_dim = x.shape[-1]\n          v = self.param(\"v\", nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (in_dim, self.features))\n          g = self.param(\"g\", nn.initializers.ones, (self.features,))\n          w = v / (jnp.linalg.norm(v, axis=0) + 1e-6) * g  # column (output) normalized\n          y = jnp.dot(x, w)\n          if self.use_bias:\n              b = self.param(\"bias\", nn.initializers.zeros, (self.features,))\n              y = y + b\n          return y\n\n  class CosineDense(nn.Module):\n      features:\
    \ int\n      alpha_init: float = 10.0\n      use_bias: bool = False  # bias only for multilabel (Modif); pass a bias Dense outside if needed\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, add_bias: bool = False):\n          # x: [B, D]\n          in_dim = x.shape[-1]\n          v = self.param(\"v\", nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (in_dim, self.features))\n          alpha = self.param(\"alpha\", lambda rng, shp: jnp.full(shp, self.alpha_init), (1,))\n          x_hat = l2_normalize(x)\n          w_hat = v / (jnp.linalg.norm(v, axis=0) + 1e-6)\n          y = jnp.dot(x_hat, w_hat) * alpha\n          if add_bias:\n              b = self.param(\"bias\", nn.initializers.zeros, (self.features,))\n              y = y + b\n          return y\n\n  class HDPRegCalHeadProbes(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      motif_k: int = 5\n \
    \     head_dropout: float = 0.05\n      regcal_on: bool = True\n      use_reg_head_weightnorm: bool = False\n      use_cls_cosine: bool = False\n      reg_head_hidden: int = 128\n      cls_head_hidden: int = 128\n      alpha_init: float = 10.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Backbone + pooling + motif\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          main = global_mean_max(h)\n          motif = MotifBranch(self.hidden_dim, self.motif_k)(h)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main, motif], axis=-1)  # 3*hidden\n          # Projection\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(fused)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\"):\n              # Regression heads:\
    \ RegCal + optional WeightNorm final Dense\n              z_reg = l2_normalize(z) if self.regcal_on else z\n              z_reg = nn.Dense(self.reg_head_hidden)(z_reg)\n              z_reg = jax.nn.gelu(z_reg)\n              z_reg = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z_reg, deterministic=deterministic)\n              if self.use_reg_head_weightnorm:\n                  y = DenseWN(self.d_output, use_bias=True)(z_reg)\n              else:\n                  y = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_reg)\n              return y.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else y\n\n          elif self.task_type in (\"multilabel_classification\", \"multiclass_classification\"):\n              z_cls = nn.Dense(self.cls_head_hidden)(z)\n              z_cls = jax.nn.gelu(z_cls)\n              z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z_cls, deterministic=deterministic)\n              if self.use_cls_cosine:\n                  add_bias = (self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\"\
    )\n                  logits = CosineDense(self.d_output, alpha_init=self.alpha_init)(z_cls, add_bias=add_bias)\n              else:\n                  logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_cls)\n              return logits\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task_type {self.task_type}\")\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = HDPRegCalHeadProbes(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n              motif_k=int(hp.get(\"motif_k\", 5)),\n              head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n              regcal_on=bool(hp.get(\"\
    regcal_on\", True)),\n              use_reg_head_weightnorm=bool(hp.get(\"use_reg_head_weightnorm\", False)),\n              use_cls_cosine=bool(hp.get(\"use_cls_cosine\", False)),\n              reg_head_hidden=int(hp.get(\"reg_head_hidden\", 128)),\n              cls_head_hidden=int(hp.get(\"cls_head_hidden\", 128)),\n              alpha_init=float(hp.get(\"alpha_init\", 10.0)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x,\
    \ deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.01):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP‑RegCal + Regression-Head WeightNorm (WN) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, regcal, weightnorm, regression-heads, motif, pooling\"\nabstract: \"Regression heads only: apply WeightNorm to the final Dense atop RegCal unit-norm features. Hypothesis: removes residual scale confounds and stabilizes CRI-Off/PRS without changing classification heads.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from hdp_regcal_head_probes import create_network as build_net, create_optimizer as make_opt\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n \
    \ def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          \"use_reg_head_weightnorm\": True,\n          \"use_cls_cosine\": False,\n          \"reg_head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"cls_head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"alpha_init\": 10.0\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_net(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_opt(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP‑RegCal + Cosine Classifier (classification heads only) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"dsconv, classification, cosine, normalization, regcal, motif\"\nabstract: \"Classification heads only: cosine classifier\
    \ (feature+weight norm) with learnable alpha; Modif keeps bias, ncRNA bias-free. Regression heads unchanged (RegCal + standard Dense). Tests calibration gains without affecting CRI-Off.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from hdp_regcal_head_probes import create_network as build_net, create_optimizer as make_opt\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          \"use_reg_head_weightnorm\": False,\n          \"use_cls_cosine\": True,\n          \"reg_head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"cls_head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"alpha_init\": 10.0\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return\
    \ build_net(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_opt(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning implementation actions**


  The system uses a single function for one dataset at a time, which seems efficient. I’m planning to maintain the training schedule and maybe update the documentation, especially since tokens are over 75%. I think we should prune some data. However, the user’s question appears to be a reflection tick, and although I previously noted that, I can now proceed with the code actions. I''ll focus on implementing toggles and submitting ideas for HDP-RegCal.**Setting up model configurations**


  I''m considering using the DSConv backbone with a motif branch and pooling that combines both mean and max for all tasks, particularly since the classification p-mean isn''t being utilized. It looks like I’ll stick with the RegCal specifically for regression tasks, as it fits better there. Now, I''m ready to generate the necessary configurations or components for implementation. This should streamline the process effectively!'
