- text: "/execute_action{rank author}\n/execute_action{page_size 50}\n/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stagnation_protocol_I_plan.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Stagnation Protocol I — Tracking (Tick 497)\n\n  Running:\n  - 800 — Idea A: ShiftAvg(±1) + mean+max (minimal DSConv baseline), seed=42\n  - 801 — Idea B: mean + TopK-mean (k=8), seed=42\n\n  Next (queue when slots free):\n  - Idea C — mean + multires block-max mean (b=8), seed=42\n\n  Acceptance criteria (per idea):\n  - Single-seed ≥ baseline (ID 767=0.6745) + 0.002 AND no major per-panel regressions (esp. CRI-Off, PRS).\n  - If met, tri-seed {42,7,123}. Then synthesize into HDP‑RegCal; target ≥0.6885 tri-seed mean.\n\n  Guardrails:\n  - <1M params; unified code path; optimizer wd=0.01, head_dropout=0.05; no loop or dataset-specific logic.\n\n  Notes:\n  - Prior probes (P-mean, SPD) and head probes (WeightNorm, Cosine) were negative; RegCal remains key for regression stability.\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"Idea C — mean + multires block‑max mean (b=8) pooling (minimal DSConv baseline) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"baseline, dsconv, pooling, multires, robustness\"\nabstract: \"Augment mean pooling with a multi‑resolution statistic: block‑max then average across blocks (b=8). Hypothesis: preserves extreme activations without over‑smoothing, improving robustness vs. max.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_minibase_expts2 import create_network as build_net, create_optimizer as make_opt\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"shift_avg\": False,\n          \"multires_b\": 8,\n          \"topk_k\": 0,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      return build_net(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_opt(learning_rate)\n```"
