parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 498\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema II — Working Meta (Tick 492)\nStatus:\n- HDP‑RegCal default retained (tri‑seed ≈ 0.6885). Task‑type pooling with classification P‑mean (IDs 787/788) was negative overall.\nProtocol:\n1) Maintain reproducibility and concise documentation (update Archive #25 addenda for follow‑ups).\n2) Avoid smoothing that harms CRI‑Off; preserve extreme activations for regression heads.\n3) If stagnation persists, pick a new simple baseline and ideate 3 orthogonal ideas (no loop hacks), then report as a complete static paper (≥5 exps).\nTODO (next cycle):\n- Reflect and propose three fresh, low‑complexity ideas orthogonal to smoothing/position dropout (e.g., tiny head rebalancing, weight‑norm in regression heads, or calibration\
    \ variants) before coding.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 144,355 / 270,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 205 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Idea A — ShiftAvg(±1) + mean+max (minimal DSConv baseline) — seed=42' (ID: 800) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6748198468083899\n**APA_R2:** 0.8547\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0909\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9504\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4877\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5489\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8742\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9169\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 800\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission code that was failing due to Flax API incompatibility. The code is now running without errors.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code in `storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_minibase_expts2.py` was using an outdated Flax API parameter name:\n\n```python\nx = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n\
    \            feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n            dilation=(self.dilation,),  # WRONG - deprecated parameter name\n            padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n```\n\n**Error message:**\n```\nTypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'\n```\n\nThe issue occurred because:\n- The agent's code in `dsconv_minibase_expts2.py` (line 44) used `dilation=` parameter\n- In Flax 0.10.6 (the installed version), the correct parameter name is `kernel_dilation=`\n- This is a breaking API change from earlier Flax versions\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Copied and fixed the buggy classes:**\n   - `DSConvBlock` - Changed `dilation=(self.dilation,)` to `kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,)` on line 52\n   - `DSConvBackbone` - Uses the fixed DSConvBlock\n   - `MiniDSConvNet2` - Uses the fixed DSConvBackbone\n   - `WrappedRNANetwork` - Uses the fixed MiniDSConvNet2\n\n2. **Kept working functions as imports:**\n   -\
    \ Imported helper functions that work correctly: `shift_average`, `global_mean_max`, `multires_block_max_mean`, `topk_mean`\n   - These functions don't have bugs, so no need to duplicate them\n\n3. **Updated the parameter:**\n   ```python\n   x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n               kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n               feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n               kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),  # FIXED\n               padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n   ```\n\n## Verification\n- Created submission_v2.py at 2025-10-26T20:03:40\n- Monitoring script confirmed code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Exit code: 0 (Success - code is running)\n\n## Notes\nThe fix addresses a simple API compatibility issue. The submission is now compatible with Flax 0.10.6 and should complete the full training evaluation successfully.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them\
    \ manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n# Import everything except DSConvBlock from the original module\nfrom dsconv_minibase_expts2 import (\n    create_network as build_net_original,\n    create_optimizer as make_opt,\n    DSConvBackbone as DSConvBackbone_original,\n    MiniDSConvNet2 as MiniDSConvNet2_original,\n    WrappedRNANetwork as WrappedRNANetwork_original,\n    shift_average,\n    global_mean_max,\n    multires_block_max_mean,\n    topk_mean\n)\n\n# Import necessary dependencies\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n        \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n        \"kernel_size\": 7,\n        \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n        \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n        \"head_hidden\": 128,\n\
    \        \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n        \"shift_avg\": True,\n        \"multires_b\": 0,\n        \"topk_k\": 0,\n    }\n\n# Fixed DSConvBlock with kernel_dilation instead of dilation\nclass DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        residual = x\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                    kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                    feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),  # FIXED: changed from dilation to kernel_dilation\n                    padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n        return residual + x\n\n# Fixed DSConvBackbone that uses the fixed\
    \ DSConvBlock\nclass DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilations: Sequence[int]\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n        for d in self.dilations:\n            h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n        return h\n\n# Fixed MiniDSConvNet2 that uses the fixed DSConvBackbone\nclass MiniDSConvNet2(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    hidden_dim: int = 256\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    head_hidden: int = 128\n    head_dropout: float = 0.05\n    shift_avg_flag: bool = False\n    multires_b: int = 0\n    topk_k: int = 0\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim,\
    \ self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n        if self.shift_avg_flag:\n            h = shift_average(h)\n        # base pooled stats\n        mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n        if self.topk_k > 0:\n            extreme = topk_mean(h, self.topk_k)\n        else:\n            extreme = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n        pooled = [mean, extreme]\n        if self.multires_b and self.multires_b > 1:\n            pooled.append(multires_block_max_mean(h, int(self.multires_b)))\n        z = jnp.concatenate(pooled, axis=-1)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(z)\n        z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n        z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n            return out.squeeze(-1)\n        return out\n\n# Fixed WrappedRNANetwork that uses the fixed MiniDSConvNet2\nclass WrappedRNANetwork:\n\
    \    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n        hp = hparams or {}\n        self.net = MiniDSConvNet2(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n            kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n            ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n            dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n            head_hidden=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden\", 128)),\n            head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n            shift_avg_flag=bool(hp.get(\"shift_avg\", False)),\n            multires_b=int(hp.get(\"multires_b\", 0)),\n            topk_k=int(hp.get(\"topk_k\", 0)),\n        )\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        pk, dk = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.net.init({'params': pk, 'dropout': dk}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\
    \    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return make_opt(learning_rate)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓\
    \ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful\
    \ - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune\
    \ multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0136 |  0.4091  | 0.4091 \n 20  | 0.0124 |  0.4357  | 0.4357 \n 30  | 0.0112 |  0.4452  | 0.4502 \n 40  | 0.0099 |  0.4686  | 0.4706 \n 50  | 0.0080 |  0.4746  | 0.4820 \n 60  | 0.0068 |  0.4734  | 0.4877 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 68 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4877 Time:31s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.487675\nTraining time: 37s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223\
    \ train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0005 |  0.0777  | 0.0777 \n 20  | 0.0005 |  0.0820  | 0.0909 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 28 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0909 Time:91s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.090906\nTraining time: 97s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0336 |  0.5446  | 0.5489 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 18 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\n\
    Best:0.5489 Time:1045s\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.548872\nTraining time: 1054s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0536 |  0.9031  | 0.9077 \n 20  | 0.0015 |  0.9031  | 0.9138 \n 30  | 0.0007 |  0.9108  | 0.9169 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 34 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.9169 Time:1259s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.916923\nTraining time: 1267s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n\
    =============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1370 |  0.8637  | 0.8637 \n 20  | 0.0828 |  0.8491  | 0.8665 \n 30  | 0.0668 |  0.8507  | 0.8692 \n 40  | 0.0575 |  0.8705  | 0.8742 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 44 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8742 Time:1334s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.874244\nTraining time: 1343s\n\nStarting RNA training on Modif dataset\nTask type: multilabel_classification, Output dim: 12\nMetric: auc_roc, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nModif Training (multilabel_classification, auc_roc)\nData: 304661 train, 3599 val, seq_len=101\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val AUC_ROC|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0631 |  0.9496  | 0.9504 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 13\n=============================================\n\
    Best:0.9504 Time:1850s\n\nModif training completed:\nValidation auc_roc: 0.950386\nTraining time: 1867s\n\nStarting RNA training on APA dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nAPA Training (regression, r2)\nData: 145463 train, 33170 val, seq_len=186\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0115 |  0.8465  | 0.8465 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 19\n=============================================\nBest:0.8547 Time:1892s\n\nAPA training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.854734\nTraining time: 1906s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 0fe0ea9f-2de1-46fb-8acd-13a39527e134\nTotal time: 1959s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-26 20:03:50,693\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761480230694153696\n2025-10-26\
    \ 20:03:50,711\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761480230711395923\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Idea B — mean + TopK-mean (k=8) pooling (minimal DSConv baseline) — seed=42' (ID: 801) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.675132882834934\n**APA_R2:** 0.8629\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0952\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9515\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4451\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5505\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8992\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9215\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 801\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission by correcting a Flax API parameter name error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a bug in the imported lineage file `storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_minibase_expts2.py` in the `DSConvBlock` class at line 44.\n\nThe code was using:\n```python\nx = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n\
    \            feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n            dilation=(self.dilation,),  # ❌ WRONG PARAMETER NAME\n            padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n```\n\nHowever, Flax's `nn.Conv` layer does not accept a parameter named `dilation`. The correct parameter name is `kernel_dilation`.\n\n**Error message:**\n```\nTypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Copied the buggy `DSConvBlock` class** from the lineage file into the submission\n2. **Fixed the parameter name** from `dilation=(self.dilation,)` to `kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,)`\n3. **Monkey-patched the fixed class** back into the imported module to ensure all references use the corrected version\n\nThe fixed code:\n```python\nx = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\
    \  # ✅ CORRECT PARAMETER NAME\n            padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n```\n\n## Verification\n- Monitoring script confirmed the code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Exit code 0 indicates success\n- The submission is now executing the neural network training pipeline correctly\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Fixed file:** `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n- **Bug location:** `DSConvBlock.__call__` method, line where `nn.Conv` is instantiated\n- **API correction:** Changed Flax Conv parameter from `dilation` to `kernel_dilation`\n- **Execution time:** Code successfully ran for over 5 minutes without errors\n\nThis was a straightforward API compatibility fix requiring only a single parameter name correction.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n# Import everything\
    \ except DSConvBlock (we fix it locally)\nfrom dsconv_minibase_expts2 import create_network as build_net, create_optimizer as make_opt\n\n# FIXED DSConvBlock - changed 'dilation' parameter to 'kernel_dilation'\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nclass DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        residual = x\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                    kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                    feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),  # FIXED: was 'dilation'\n                    padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n      \
    \  return residual + x\n\n# Monkey-patch the fixed DSConvBlock into the imported module\nimport dsconv_minibase_expts2\ndsconv_minibase_expts2.DSConvBlock = DSConvBlock\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n        \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n        \"kernel_size\": 7,\n        \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n        \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n        \"head_hidden\": 128,\n        \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n        \"shift_avg\": False,\n        \"multires_b\": 0,\n        \"topk_k\": 8,\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return build_net(hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return make_opt(learning_rate)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n\
