- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Idea C — mean + multires block‑max mean (b=8) pooling (minimal DSConv baseline) — seed=42 [patched]\"\ntags: \"baseline, dsconv, pooling, multires, robustness\"\nabstract: \"Augment global mean with a multi‑resolution statistic: block‑max (size b=8) then average across blocks. Patched DSConvBlock to use kernel_dilation for Flax 0.10.6. Tests preserving extremes without over‑smoothing.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  import jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  # Import baseline module\n  import dsconv_minibase_expts2\n  from dsconv_minibase_expts2 import create_network as build_net, create_optimizer as make_opt\n\n  # Patch DSConvBlock to use kernel_dilation (Flax 0.10.6)\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n\
    \          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual + x\n  dsconv_minibase_expts2.DSConvBlock = DSConvBlock\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"shift_avg\": False,\n          \"multires_b\"\
    : 8,   # enable block‑max mean with block size 8\n          \"topk_k\": 0,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_net(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_opt(learning_rate)\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write noema/results/minibase_shift_topk_summary.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Minimal DSConv baseline — new probes (seed=42)\n\n  Baseline:\n  - 767 — DSConv + mean+max (no motif, no RegCal): 0.6745 | APA 0.8491 | CRI-Off 0.0978 | CRI-On 0.4684 | PRS 0.5554 | MRL 0.8666 | Modif 0.9515 | ncRNA 0.9323\n\n  New ideas:\n  - 800 — ShiftAvg(±1) + mean+max: 0.6748 | CRI-Off 0.0909 | CRI-On 0.4877 | MRL 0.8742 | APA 0.8547 | ncRNA 0.9169\n  - 801 — mean + TopK-mean (k=8): 0.6751 | CRI-Off 0.0952 | CRI-On 0.4451 | MRL 0.8992 | APA 0.8629 | ncRNA 0.9215\n\n  Takeaways:\n  - Both are ≈baseline but below acceptance (+0.002). TopK-mean improves APA/MRL but reduces CRI-Off and CRI-On; ShiftAvg improves CRI-On moderately but lowers\
    \ CRI-Off and ncRNA.\n  - Proceeding to Idea C (mean + multires block‑max mean, b=8) to test multi‑resolution extremes without LSE‑style smoothing.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 25}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum 2: ShiftAvg and Top‑K pooling on minimal DSConv — Results and next step\"\ncontent: |\n  Extending the minimal DSConv baseline study:\n  - 800 — ShiftAvg(±1) + mean+max: 0.6748 (CRI-On ↑ to 0.4877; CRI-Off ↓ to 0.0909; ncRNA ↓ to 0.9169).\n  - 801 — mean + TopK-mean (k=8): 0.6751 (APA/MRL ↑ to 0.8629/0.8992; CRI-Off ↓ to 0.0952; CRI-On ↓ to 0.4451).\n  Neither exceeded the baseline by the +0.002 threshold. This reinforces that CRI-Off prefers preserving true maxima without smoothing/averaging. Next queued: Idea C — mean + multires block‑max mean (b=8), targeting multi‑resolution extremes without LSE‑like smoothing. Summary: storage/noema/results/minibase_shift_topk_summary.md.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating ideas and submissions**


  With our new A/B results in hand, I’m realizing that Idea C wasn’t submitted earlier due to a concurrent limit. We tried submitting it at tick 497 but encountered a failure because two others were running. Now that those are finished, I can submit Idea C. I also need to update our minimal baseline plan file and consider summarizing the new results for Archive #25, with thoughts on possibly halting exploration or moving to synthesis. However, since none passed the acceptance threshold, synthesis may not be warranted right now.**Planning submission and updates**


  It''s time to resubmit Idea C since it failed before due to two other ideas running simultaneously. I''ll go ahead and submit Idea C now. Additionally, I''ll write a summary of the results in markdown and update Archive #25 to include an addendum summarizing the results of Ideas A and B. Since we''ve already covered "head probes," I might add one more message about scheduling Idea C. I should also consider next steps, like finishing the Stagnation Protocol and drafting a new paper summarizing our experiments.**Updating experiments and code**


  Since Archive #25 was accepted with negative results for RevAvg, P-mean, and SPD, I can now update it with shiftAvg and topK as extended experiments. It seems we don’t need a new paper right now. I also want to fix the code by updating dsconv_minibase_expts2.py to use kernel_dilation. This will prevent future issues with the debugger. I''ll write a new content file to correct the parameters for future runs, although it may be a bit heavy in text. I''ll make sure to keep token usage minimal while including the necessary code block.**Planning Idea C with patches**


  I noticed we already wrote dsconv_minibase_expts2.py, but modifying it requires handling the entire content. To keep it simple, I might create a smaller "patch note" file to address the change. Instead, I could write a new file named dsconv_minibase_expts2_fixed.py for Idea C. To avoid issues, I''ll include a monkey-patched version of DSConvBlock within the submission, referencing dsconv_minibase_expts2. This way, I can ensure the correct parameters are included proactively without needing the debugger later.**Preparing for Idea C resubmission**


  Earlier, when we submitted Idea C, we built it based on dsconv_minibase_expts2 without including the necessary patch. This led to a "Submission failed due to concurrent pending" error. Now, resubmitting new code with the patch will help avoid that. I’ll execute the submission by writing code to import and monkey-patch DSConvBlock to use kernel_dilation while setting the multires_b param.


  After Idea C completes, I plan to finalize Stagnation Protocol Step 6, summarizing the three new ideas, and potentially updating Archive #25 with results for shiftAvg and topK, or creating an "Addendum 2." I’ll ensure to keep my commentary concise as we move forward!'
