role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_minibase_expts2.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Minimal DSConv + pooling baseline with three probes (fixed for Flax 0.10.6):\n    - shift_avg: weight-tied shift averaging h, (h + roll±1)/3 (no new params)\n    - multires_b: multi-resolution pooling via block max mean (additive pooled stat)\n    - topk_k: mean + top-k mean pooling (per-channel)\n  Heads: single hidden MLP (128); no motif; no RegCal. <1M params.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n        \
    \  # probes\n          \"shift_avg\": False,\n          \"multires_b\": 0,   # e.g., 8 for blocks of 8\n          \"topk_k\": 0        # e.g., 8 for mean of top-8 per channel\n      }\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),  # FIXED param name\n                      padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n\
    \      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def global_mean_max(h):\n      return jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(h, axis=1), jnp.max(h, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n\n  def shift_average(h):\n      return (h + jnp.roll(h, 1, axis=1) + jnp.roll(h, -1, axis=1)) / 3.0\n\n  def multires_block_max_mean(h, b: int):\n      if b <= 1:\n          return jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n      B, L, C = h.shape\n      pad = (b - (L % b)) % b\n      if pad > 0:\n          pad_width = ((0,0),(0,pad),(0,0))\n          h_pad = jnp.pad(h, pad_width, mode='constant', constant_values=0.0)\n          Lp = L + pad\n\
    \      else:\n          h_pad = h\n          Lp = L\n      hb = h_pad.reshape(B, Lp//b, b, C)\n      block_max = hb.max(axis=2)         # (B, nblocks, C)\n      return block_max.mean(axis=1)      # (B, C)\n\n  def topk_mean(h, k: int):\n      if k <= 0 or k > h.shape[1]:\n          return jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n      x = jnp.swapaxes(h, 1, 2)       # (B, C, L)\n      vals, _ = lax.top_k(x, k)       # top-k along L\n      return vals.mean(axis=-1)       # (B, C)\n\n  class MiniDSConvNet2(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      head_hidden: int = 128\n      head_dropout: float = 0.05\n      shift_avg_flag: bool = False\n      multires_b: int = 0\n      topk_k: int = 0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations,\
    \ self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          if self.shift_avg_flag:\n              h = shift_average(h)\n          mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          extreme = topk_mean(h, self.topk_k) if self.topk_k > 0 else jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          pooled = [mean, extreme]\n          if self.multires_b and self.multires_b > 1:\n              pooled.append(multires_block_max_mean(h, int(self.multires_b)))\n          z = jnp.concatenate(pooled, axis=-1)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(z)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return out.squeeze(-1)\n          return out\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n      \
    \    self.net = MiniDSConvNet2(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n              head_hidden=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden\", 128)),\n              head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n              shift_avg_flag=bool(hp.get(\"shift_avg\", False)),\n              multires_b=int(hp.get(\"multires_b\", 0)),\n              topk_k=int(hp.get(\"topk_k\", 0)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          pk, dk = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': pk, 'dropout': dk}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n\
    \              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_minibase_expts.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Minimal DSConv + pooling baseline (fixed kernel_dilation for Flax 0.10.6) and probes:\n    - reverse_avg\n    - use_powermean\n    - token_drop_p\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\
    \  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"reverse_avg\": False,\n          \"use_powermean\": False,\n          \"p_init\": 2.0,\n          \"token_drop_p\": 0.0,\n      }\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),  # FIXED\n                      padding=\"SAME\"\
    )(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def global_mean_max(h):\n      mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n      maxv = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n      return jnp.concatenate([mean, maxv], axis=-1)\n\n  class MotifBranch(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      k: int\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, h):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.k,), padding=\"SAME\")(h)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n          return x\n\n  def l2_normalize_feats(z, eps=1e-6):\n      return z / (jnp.linalg.norm(z, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + eps)\n\n  class MiniDSConvNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      head_hidden: int = 128\n      head_dropout: float = 0.05\n      reverse_avg: bool = False\n      use_powermean: bool = False\n      token_drop_p: float = 0.0\n\n      def _token_drop(self, x, *, deterministic: bool):\n          if deterministic or self.token_drop_p <= 0.0:\n              return x\n          rng = self.make_rng(\"dropout\")\n          keep = random.bernoulli(rng, p=1.0 - self.token_drop_p, shape=(x.shape[0], x.shape[1], 1))\n      \
    \    return x * keep\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          x = self._token_drop(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          backbone = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate, name=\"backbone\")\n          h = backbone(x, deterministic)\n          if self.reverse_avg:\n              h_rev = backbone(jnp.flip(x, axis=1), deterministic)\n              h = 0.5 * (h + h_rev)\n          if self.use_powermean:\n              # simple p-mean variant (kept for completeness)\n              u = self.param(\"p_raw\", nn.initializers.zeros, (1,))\n              p = jax.nn.softplus(u) + 1.0\n              hp = jax.nn.relu(h) + 1e-6\n              pmean = jnp.power(jnp.mean(hp ** p, axis=1), 1.0 / p)\n              pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(h, axis=1), pmean], axis=-1)\n          else:\n              pooled = global_mean_max(h)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(pooled)\n          z =\
    \ nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return out.squeeze(-1)\n          return out\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = MiniDSConvNet(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n              head_hidden=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden\", 128)),\n              head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n              reverse_avg=bool(hp.get(\"\
    reverse_avg\", False)),\n              use_powermean=bool(hp.get(\"use_powermean\", False)),\n              token_drop_p=float(hp.get(\"token_drop_p\", 0.0)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:\
    \ float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write noema/results/minibase_shift_topk_summary.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Minimal DSConv baseline — probes (seed=42) — Update with Idea C\n\n  Baseline:\n  - 767 — DSConv + mean+max (no motif, no RegCal): 0.6745 | APA 0.8491 | CRI-Off 0.0978 | CRI-On 0.4684 | PRS 0.5554 | MRL 0.8666 | Modif 0.9515 | ncRNA 0.9323\n\n  Probes:\n  - 800 — ShiftAvg(±1) + mean+max: 0.6748 | CRI-Off 0.0909 | CRI-On 0.4877 | MRL 0.8742 | APA 0.8547 | ncRNA 0.9169\n  - 801 — mean + TopK-mean (k=8): 0.6751 | CRI-Off 0.0952 | CRI-On 0.4451 | MRL 0.8992 | APA 0.8629 | ncRNA 0.9215\n  - 804 — mean + multires block‑max mean (b=8): 0.6717 | CRI-Off 0.0979 | CRI-On 0.4467 | MRL 0.8726 | APA 0.8500 | ncRNA 0.9292\n\n  Takeaways:\n  - No probe exceeded baseline by +0.002. TopK-mean improved APA/MRL but hurt CRI-On; ShiftAvg helped CRI-On but reduced ncRNA; multires block‑max underperformed average.\n\
    \  - Reinforces: preserving literal maxima (mean+max) is robust on the minimal DSConv baseline; smoothing/averaging variants tend to harm CRI-*.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 25}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum 3: Multi‑resolution block‑max pooling — negative result\"\ncontent: |\n  Final probe on the minimal DSConv baseline:\n  - 804 — mean + multires block‑max mean (b=8): 0.6717 | CRI‑Off 0.0979 | CRI‑On 0.4467 | MRL 0.8726 | APA 0.8500 | Modif 0.9515 | ncRNA 0.9292.\n  Compared to the baseline (767: 0.6745), this underperforms the average and provides no clear advantage over mean+max. Together with ShiftAvg and TopK‑mean, this concludes Stagnation Protocol I: simple, parameter‑free tweaks around pooling did not improve the minimal baseline. We therefore recommend retaining mean+max for DSConv baselines and focusing future work on regression‑head calibration (RegCal) and backbone/feature‑level innovations rather than additional pooling statistics. Summary:\
    \ storage/noema/results/minibase_shift_topk_summary.md.\n```"
