tick: 502
role: model
parts:
- text: "Reflection Tick 1\n\nSharpening the three ideas with concrete specs, safeguards, and success checks\n\n1) Learned per-channel mean↔max mixing (no smoothing)\n- Form: for each channel c, αc = σ(wc + b0); pooledc = αc·meanc + (1−αc)·maxc.\n- Rationale: adds a bounded, monotone nonlinearity before the head; the linear head alone can reweight mean/max but cannot enforce bounded convex mixing per channel.\n- Safeguards:\n  - Init bias b0 to favor max to protect CRI-Off (e.g., α0 ≈ 0.35 → b0 ≈ log(α0/(1−α0)) ≈ −0.62).\n  - Regularize w with small L2 (implicit via AdamW) and optionally clamp α to [0.05,0.95] to avoid collapse.\n  - Preserve head dimension: optionally concatenate [pooled, max] to keep 2C width if reducing to C hurts; run both “mix-only (C)” and “mix+max (C+C)” variants.\n- Ablations:\n  - Init α0 ∈ {0.35, 0.5, 0.65}.\n  - With vs without “mix+max” concat.\n- Success: +0.002 over baseline on seed 42, CRI-Off ≥ baseline, PRS stable.\n\n2) RMSNorm pre-head (swap LayerNorm)\n\
    - Form: z → RMSNorm(z) (scale only, γ learnable; no mean subtraction), then GELU, Dropout, Dense_out.\n- Rationale: reduces sensitivity to feature-scale drift without biasing means; orthogonal to RegCal.\n- Implementation:\n  - If flax.nn.RMSNorm unavailable, implement RMSNorm: z / sqrt(mean(z^2)+eps) * γ (per feature).\n  - Keep ε=1e-6; init γ=1.0.\n- Tests:\n  - Minimal baseline (seed 42).\n  - HDP‑RegCal main model (seed 42).\n- Success: ≥ +0.002 on minimal baseline; ≥0.689 on HDP‑RegCal with CRI-Off ≥ 0.08.\n\n3) Head capacity rebalancing (task-type)\n- Form (allowed as task-type specialization): regression head hidden=160, classification head hidden=96; shared elsewhere.\n- Rationale: allocate parameters toward regression panels (APA, CRI-*, PRS, MRL) which drive average; classification already strong.\n- Guardrails: <1M params overall; no other changes.\n- Success: HDP‑RegCal seed 42 ≥0.689 and CRI-Off ≥0.08; no big drops in Modif/ncRNA.\n\nGeneral checks and pitfalls\n- Protect\
    \ CRI-Off: any pooling change should not reduce literal max contribution (favor α toward max at init or include max in concat).\n- Keep Flax API consistent (kernel_dilation).\n- Report per-dataset deltas; accept small APA/MRL gains only if CRI-Off/PRS are not harmed."
thinking_content: '**Exploring parameter handling**


  I’m thinking about balancing parameter count without drastically changing head capacity. Mixing to produce a weighted sum and projecting with Linear might help. With C dimensions seen by the head versus a baseline of 2C, this could alter the parameter count, though it should remain under 1M. If I keep both and learn gating weights, I can concatenate them for mean and max. Using a linear layer after concatenation could enhance stability and reduce overfitting.**Identifying architectural considerations**


  I’m considering some potential pitfalls with per-channel gating affecting output dimensions across tasks. It''s important for the gating to remain dataset-invariant and shared across tasks. I’ll need to check if RMSNorm is available in JAX/Flax, especially as a replacement for LayerNorm''s epsilon. If not, I could implement it easily by calculating the mean of squares per feature dimension. For head capacity rebalancing, I can''t have dataset-specific methods but can keep a unified core architecture while tailoring final layers for different predictions.**Crafting parameter adjustments**


  I’m looking into adjusting head hidden size based on task type, making sure to keep total parameters under 1M. For metrics, meaningful gains would be a minimal baseline of +0.002 and around +0.0015 to +0.003 for HDP-RegCal. One concern is that mixing gating might affect CRI-Off, so I’ll need to bias initialization towards equal weighting or favoring max. Maybe I can set bias around -0.5 to lean toward max? I''ll propose an ablation grid to test this effectively while ensuring minimal classification drop for ncRNA.'
