tick: 502
role: model
parts:
- text: "Reflection Tick 2\n\nConcrete implementation plans, sanity checks, and evaluation matrix\n\nIdea 1 — Per-channel learned mix of mean and max\n- Code sketch (in pooling):\n  - Compute mean_c, max_c per channel from DSConv features h (shape B×L×C).\n  - α = sigmoid(w + b0), w∈R^C (params), b0 is scalar init bias shared or per-channel (start toward max).\n  - pooled_c = α_c·mean_c + (1−α_c)·max_c.\n  - Safety variant: concat [pooled, max] to retain explicit maxima (2C features).\n- Inits and variants:\n  - Bias choices: α0 ∈ {0.35, 0.5, 0.65} → b0 ≈ {−0.62, 0.0, +0.62}.\n  - Two heads: Mix-only (C-dim) vs Mix+Max (2C-dim).\n- Overhead: +C or +2C scalars (negligible); preserves literal max path (especially Mix+Max).\n- Risks/mitigations:\n  - If CRI-Off dips, try α0 smaller (favor max) and/or Mix+Max concat.\n  - Keep optimizer unchanged; AdamW provides light L2 on w.\n- Eval:\n  - Minimal baseline, seed=42: grid (α0∈{0.35,0.5} × {Mix-only, Mix+Max}).\n  - Accept if ≥ 0.6765 (≈ 0.6745\
    \ + 0.002) with CRI-Off ≥ 0.097 and PRS not worse (>0.553).\n  - If positive, port same pooling to HDP‑RegCal main path and test seed 42.\n\nIdea 2 — RMSNorm pre-head (swap LayerNorm)\n- Code sketch:\n  - RMSNorm(z) = z / sqrt(mean(z^2) + eps) ⊙ γ (γ learnable, per-feature), no mean subtraction; eps=1e-6; init γ=1.\n  - Insert: pooled → Dense(head_hidden) → RMSNorm → GELU → Dropout → Dense_out.\n- Rationale: scale-only normalization may stabilize head optimization while preserving mean shifts that LN removes; orthogonal to RegCal (which acts on regression features earlier).\n- Overhead: same params as LN (γ), possibly fewer stats.\n- Risks:\n  - If feature norms are already stable (RegCal path), effect could be neutral; classification could be sensitive—watch Modif/ncRNA.\n- Eval:\n  - Minimal baseline, seed=42: LN→RMSNorm swap.\n  - HDP‑RegCal, seed=42: swap in both classification and regression heads (RegCal unchanged).\n  - Accept if minimal baseline ≥ +0.002; HDP‑RegCal ≥ 0.689 and\
    \ CRI-Off ≥ 0.08.\n\nIdea 3 — Head capacity rebalancing (task-type)\n- Spec:\n  - Regression heads: hidden=160 (↑ from 128).\n  - Classification heads: hidden=96 (↓ from 128).\n  - Keep everything else identical; ensure total params <1M (HDP‑RegCal comfortably under before; this shift trades a bit toward regression).\n- Rationale: aggregate score dominated by regression panels; classification already saturated.\n- Risks:\n  - Over-reduction could hurt ncRNA/Modif; monitor ncRNA ≥ 0.934 and Modif AUC ≥ 0.950.\n- Eval:\n  - HDP‑RegCal, seed=42.\n  - Accept if overall ≥ 0.689, CRI-Off ≥ 0.08, and no significant drop on classification.\n\nSynthesis and decision tree\n- If Idea 1 works on the minimal baseline, immediately port Mix+Max variant to HDP‑RegCal main path (replacing fixed mean+max) and test seed 42; if ≥ 0.689 with CRI-Off ≥ 0.08, tri-seed.\n- If RMSNorm helps, adopt universally (both minimal baseline and HDP‑RegCal); it’s a safe, low-variance change.\n- If head rebalancing helps,\
    \ keep it as a separate ablation line in HDP‑RegCal and combine with RMSNorm (no interaction expected).\n- Otherwise, document negatives (Archive #25 addendum), reaffirm mean+max for DSConv baselines, and retain HDP‑RegCal defaults."
thinking_content: '**Evaluating RMSNorm and head capacity**


  I''m thinking for RMSNorm, if it''s positive, I should swap Layer Normalization in both minimal and HDP-RegCal. If head capacity is positive, I plan to keep it as is. I need to justify and document any negative results. To make this clearer, I''ll organize my thoughts into bullet points for better clarity. It feels like a good approach to keep everything structured and easy to follow!'
