tick: 502
role: model
parts:
- text: "Reflection Tick 3\n\nFinalize experiment specs, acceptance gates, and rollout plan\n\nTargets and gates\n- Minimal DSConv baseline (ID 767 ≈ 0.6745): accept change if score ≥ 0.6765 (≥ +0.002) with CRI-Off ≥ 0.097 and PRS ≥ 0.553; no large drops on ncRNA/Modif.\n- HDP‑RegCal (tri-seed ≈ 0.6885): accept change if seed=42 ≥ 0.689 and CRI-Off ≥ 0.080; no regressions ≥ 0.01 on Modif/ncRNA.\n\nIdea 1 — Per-channel learned mean↔max mix (no smoothing)\n- Pooling spec (h: B×L×C):\n  - mean = mean(h, axis=1), max = max(h, axis=1)\n  - α = sigmoid(w + b0), w∈R^C; b0 sets α0 ∈ {0.35, 0.5}; start α0=0.35 to favor max (protect CRI-Off)\n  - pooled = α⊙mean + (1−α)⊙max\n  - Safety variant: concat [pooled, max] (retain explicit maxima)\n- Eval matrix (minimal baseline, seed=42):\n  - α0 ∈ {0.35, 0.5} × variant ∈ {Mix-only (C), Mix+Max (2C)}\n- If any cell passes gate, port same pooling to HDP‑RegCal main path and test seed=42 (then tri-seed if ≥ gate)\n\nIdea 2 — RMSNorm pre-head (swap LayerNorm)\n\
    - RMSNorm(z) = z / sqrt(mean(z^2)+ε) ⊙ γ (γ learnable), ε=1e-6; insert right after Dense(head_hidden) and before GELU\n- Tests:\n  - Minimal baseline (seed=42): LN→RMSNorm swap\n  - HDP‑RegCal (seed=42): LN→RMSNorm swap in both regression and classification heads (RegCal unchanged)\n- Expectation: small stability gain; if neutral, record as negative and revert\n\nIdea 3 — Head capacity rebalancing (task-type)\n- HDP‑RegCal only (seed=42):\n  - Regression head hidden=160; Classification head hidden=96\n  - Keep total params <1M; optimizer unchanged\n- Rationale: shift capacity toward regression panels that dominate the average; classification already strong\n\nRisk controls and logging\n- CRI-Off protection: for Idea 1, bias α0 toward max and prefer Mix+Max variant if Mix-only hurts CRI-Off\n- API guards: all depthwise convs use kernel_dilation\n- Record per-dataset deltas and pooled-stat diagnostics; if a change helps only APA/MRL but hurts CRI-* or PRS, reject\n\nRollout and reporting\n\
    - Run minimal baseline: Idea 1 grid (2×2) and Idea 2; adopt best candidate if passes gate, else document negatives\n- Run HDP‑RegCal: Idea 2 (RMSNorm) and Idea 3 (head rebalance) independently; if either passes gate, tri-seed; if both pass, combine and re-test\n- Documentation: update results/*.md and append concise addenda to Archive #25; if all negative, publish the complete static report (≥5 exps) for Cycle II with insights on why literal max remains robust and where capacity reallocation fails to move the needle"
thinking_content: '**Planning for experiment outcomes**


  I need to consider what to do if there are no gains. I think we should publish a negative results paper summarizing three ideas and at least five experiments. It’ll be important to provide a plan to tri-seed the best ones as well. I can compute the expected parameter count impact to keep it under 1M, but I don''t need to be too exact. Also, I propose avoiding smoothing and keeping the literal maximum path while suggesting an initial α0 bias to preserve CRI-Off. Let''s document these ideas!'
