tick: 504
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{preview 27}\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_rmsnorm_rebalance.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  HDP‑RegCal with configurable pre‑head normalization (RMSNorm vs LayerNorm) and task‑type head capacity.\n  Architecture:\n    - Backbone: DSConv (no PE), 5 dilated depthwise‑separable conv blocks (dilations=[1,2,4,8,16])\n    - Main path: global mean + global max pooling over DSConv features\n    - Motif path: 1D conv (k=5) over DSConv features + global max pooling\n    - Fusion: concat([main_mean, main_max, motif_max]) -> Dense(head_hidden_{task}) -> Norm (RMSNorm or LayerNorm) -> GELU -> Dropout -> Output head\n    - RegCal (Regression Calibration): per‑sample L2 normalization before regression heads only (APA, CRI‑Off, CRI‑On, MRL, PRS)\n  Notes:\n    - Flax 0.10.6: use kernel_dilation in Conv\n    - d_output and task_type provided via hparams per dataset\n  \"\"\"\n  from\
    \ typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          # heads\n          \"head_hidden_reg\": 160,   # rebalanced regression head capacity\n          \"head_hidden_cls\": 96,    # rebalanced classification head capacity\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          # normalization\n          \"use_rmsnorm\": True,      # if False, LayerNorm is used\n          # RegCal toggle\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          # motif\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n      }\n\n  class RMSNorm(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      eps: float = 1e-6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          gamma = self.param(\"\
    gamma\", nn.initializers.ones, (self.features,))\n          rms = jnp.sqrt(jnp.mean(jnp.square(x), axis=-1, keepdims=True) + self.eps)\n          return (x / rms) * gamma\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size:\
    \ int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  class MotifPath(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      k: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.k,), padding=\"SAME\")(h)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n          return x\n\n  def l2_normalize_feats(z, eps: float = 1e-6):\n      return z / (jnp.linalg.norm(z, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + eps)\n\n  class HDPRegCalNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int]\
    \ = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      head_hidden_reg: int = 160\n      head_hidden_cls: int = 96\n      head_dropout: float = 0.05\n      use_rmsnorm: bool = True\n      regcal_on: bool = True\n      motif_k: int = 5\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Backbone\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          # Main pooling\n          h_mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          h_max  = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          # Motif pooling\n          motif  = MotifPath(self.hidden_dim, self.motif_k)(h)\n          pooled = jnp.concatenate([h_mean, h_max, motif], axis=-1)\n\n          # Choose head dims and norm\n          if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\"):\n              head_hidden = self.head_hidden_reg\n          else:\n              head_hidden = self.head_hidden_cls\n\n          z = nn.Dense(head_hidden)(pooled)\n\
    \          if self.use_rmsnorm:\n              z = RMSNorm(head_hidden)(z)\n          else:\n              z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n\n          if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\"):\n              z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n              z_reg = l2_normalize_feats(z) if self.regcal_on else z\n              out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_reg)\n              return out.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else out\n\n          elif self.task_type in (\"multilabel_classification\", \"multiclass_classification\"):\n              z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n              logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n              return logits\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task_type {self.task_type}\")\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"\
    regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = HDPRegCalNet(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n              head_hidden_reg=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden_reg\", 160)),\n              head_hidden_cls=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden_cls\", 96)),\n              head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n              use_rmsnorm=bool(hp.get(\"use_rmsnorm\", True)),\n              regcal_on=bool(hp.get(\"regcal_on\", True)),\n              motif_k=int(hp.get(\"motif_k\", 5)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          pk, dk = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': pk, 'dropout': dk}, dummy_input,\
    \ deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n                               task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n                               hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stagnation_protocol_II_next.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stagnation Protocol — Cycle II next steps (Tick 504)\n  - Running: 810 (Learned\
    \ per-channel mix + concat[max], seed=42), 811 (RMSNorm pre-head swap, seed=42) on minimal DSConv baseline.\n  - Prepare HDP‑RegCal variants (code ready: submissions/hdp_regcal_rmsnorm_rebalance.py):\n      • Variant A: RMSNorm pre-head (use_rmsnorm=True) with default head sizes.\n      • Variant B: Head rebalancing (head_hidden_reg=160, head_hidden_cls=96) with RMSNorm ON.\n  - Queue A/B on seed=42 once 810/811 finish. Gates:\n      • Accept if overall ≥ 0.689 and CRI-Off ≥ 0.080 with no large drops on Modif/ncRNA.\n  - If minimal‑baseline Idea 1 passes (+0.002 and CRI-Off ≥ baseline), port the per-channel mix to HDP‑RegCal main path and test seed=42.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nWe need to outline our next actions. The user has input the latest state, and we’re currently in the Research Counter with two ongoing evaluations, 810 and 811. The system suggests previewing papers, but we’ve already done that. I think we should implement HDP-RegCal variants for ideas 2 and 3, but we need to stick to the plan and run the minimal baseline first, which is covered by 810 and 811. While those are running, I can work on documentation and prepare relevant code.**Formatting actions and implementation**\n\nI need to ensure that the environment command formatting is followed, with each action on its own line and the code in YAML after storage write or submission. It's crucial to use the Flax kernel_dilation parameter consistently. I think we should implement the HDP-RegCal baseline building, using the earlier hdp_regcal_head_probes.py file as a starting point. This will involve adding an RMSNorm toggle and adjusting hidden dimensions\
  \ based on task type. We'll implement two HDP-RegCal variants: the first involves RMSNorm pre-head for both regression and classification, while the second focuses on head capacity rebalancing.**Preparing network code**\n\nI need to focus on coding the base network since we previously had the dual_path hybrid (HDP-RegCal) in the file hdp_regcal_head_probes.py. I can either reuse that or create something new—maybe call it hdp_regcal_rmsnorm_rebalance.py. This will involve implementing a DSConv backbone, a motif path, and managing different head types for regression, using RMSNorm and setting head dimensions based on task type. While I need to keep the code minimal and under 100 lines, I can still prepare a summary file. Since two evaluations are running, we can't submit just yet, but I can definitely write the code and queue submissions for later!**Drafting the code**\n\nI need to write hdp_regcal_rmsnorm_rebalance.py using a DSConv with a motif path. In the previous HDP-RegCal version,\
  \ the main path utilized mean and max pooling, along with a motif convolution with k=5, and fused features through concatenation. Though I don't have the content from hdp_regcal_head_probes.py, I’ll create a simpler version: a 5-layer DSConv with the same pooling strategy. Depending on the task type, regression will use RegCal for normalization, while classification will not. I'll ensure we manage shapes, set the kernel_dilation parameter, and implement both the create_network and create_optimizer functions. Then, I can write a storage file and prepare two planned submissions, but I think it’s best to hold off on submitting since two evaluations are still running.**Preparing for upcoming actions**\n\nCurrently, the \"Running Experiments\" list only shows evaluations 810 and 811, which means we can’t submit any new ones right now without hitting the max limit. It’s better to schedule for the next tick instead of submitting now. I can prepare a storage write file for HDP-RegCal RMSNorm/HeadRebalance\
  \ and update the plan document for Cycle II, including the actions we’ve outlined. \n\nAdditionally, I think it’d be useful to preview Archive 27 for fresh ideas. I'll proceed with the actions to navigate to the archive, preview it, and write the necessary code while keeping our output concise."
