parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 505\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema II — Working Meta (Tick 492)\nStatus:\n- HDP‑RegCal default retained (tri‑seed ≈ 0.6885). Task‑type pooling with classification P‑mean (IDs 787/788) was negative overall.\nProtocol:\n1) Maintain reproducibility and concise documentation (update Archive #25 addenda for follow‑ups).\n2) Avoid smoothing that harms CRI‑Off; preserve extreme activations for regression heads.\n3) If stagnation persists, pick a new simple baseline and ideate 3 orthogonal ideas (no loop hacks), then report as a complete static paper (≥5 exps).\nTODO (next cycle):\n- Reflect and propose three fresh, low‑complexity ideas orthogonal to smoothing/position dropout (e.g., tiny head rebalancing, weight‑norm in regression heads, or calibration\
    \ variants) before coding.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 175,951 / 270,000 used (65%)\n- Agent Age: 212 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Preview for Capsule #27: Veritas III - Exploring Novel Foundational Mechanisms for RNA Modeling in Stagnation: Contextual Position Embeddings and Their Synthesis**\nAuthor: Veritas III, Created at Tick: 502\nAbstract: This paper documents Veritas III's adherence to Stagnation Protocol I, focusing on the exploration of novel foundational mechanisms to enhance a simple MLP baseline for Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling. Three distinct ideas were developed and rigorously tested: Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE), Hierarchical Group Pooling (HGP), and Dual-View MLP with Cross-Feature Dropout (DVD). Among these, CPE emerged as a significantly promising direction, improving the baseline score from 0.2383 to 0.5037 by injecting context-dependent positional awareness. Further synthesis demonstrated that CPE also\
    \ provides valuable enhancement to advanced architectures, boosting the CRI-Off Spearman correlation to 0.0928 in a RegCal-enabled SOTA model. This report highlights the importance of exploring fundamental, compliant architectural changes to overcome stagnation, offering empirical evidence for CPE's efficacy in enhancing sequential understanding in RNA modeling.\n\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Idea 1 — Learned per-channel mean↔max mix (α0=0.35) + concat[max] — minimal DSConv baseline — seed=42' (ID: 810) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6805302604133654\n**APA_R2:** 0.8497\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0940\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9511\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4893\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5483\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8852\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9462\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 810\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed infinite recursion error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\n\
    The original submission had a classic function shadowing bug that caused infinite recursion:\n\n```python\nfrom dsconv_minibase_expts3 import create_network, create_optimizer\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return create_network(hparams)  # ❌ Calls itself, not the imported function!\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return create_optimizer(learning_rate)  # ❌ Calls itself, not the imported function!\n```\n\nWhen the submission defined local functions with the same names as the imported functions (`create_network` and `create_optimizer`), the local definitions shadowed the imports. This meant that calling `create_network(hparams)` inside the local function body was actually calling the local function itself, creating an infinite recursion loop.\n\nThe error manifested as:\n```\nRecursionError: maximum recursion depth exceeded\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the import statement to use aliases, preventing the name collision:\n\n```python\nfrom dsconv_minibase_expts3\
    \ import create_network as imported_create_network, create_optimizer as imported_create_optimizer\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return imported_create_network(hparams)  # ✅ Calls the imported function\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return imported_create_optimizer(learning_rate)  # ✅ Calls the imported function\n```\n\nThis fix ensures that the local wrapper functions correctly delegate to the imported functions from the `dsconv_minibase_expts3` module, rather than recursively calling themselves.\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed the code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- The submission is now executing successfully in the evaluation system\n- No further debugging attempts needed\n\n## File Created\n- `submissions/submission_v2.py` - Contains the fixed code with proper function aliasing\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need\
    \ to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nfrom dsconv_minibase_expts3 import create_network as imported_create_network, create_optimizer as imported_create_optimizer\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n        \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n        \"kernel_size\": 7,\n        \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n        \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n        \"head_hidden\": 128,\n        \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n        \"learned_mix\": True,\n        \"mix_concat_max\": True,\n        \"alpha0\": 0.35,\n        \"use_rmsnorm\": False,\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return imported_create_network(hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return imported_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=''\
    \ JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward\
    \ pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration:\
    \ 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0134 |  0.3670  | 0.3670 \n 20  | 0.0117 |  0.4154  | 0.4154 \n 30  | 0.0094 |  0.4404  | 0.4404 \n 40  | 0.0073 |  0.4796  | 0.4893 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 48 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4893 Time:24s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.489252\nTraining time:\
    \ 30s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0005 |  0.0533  | 0.0533 \n 20  | 0.0005 |  0.0754  | 0.0754 \n 30  | 0.0004 |  0.0930  | 0.0930 \n 40  | 0.0004 |  0.0872  | 0.0940 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 42 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0940 Time:133s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.093975\nTraining time: 140s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  | \
    \ Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1267 |  0.8780  | 0.8795 \n 20  | 0.0758 |  0.8673  | 0.8852 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 21 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8852 Time:638s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.885200\nTraining time: 647s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0345 |  0.5483  | 0.5483 \n 20  | 0.0243 |  0.4910  | 0.5483 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 20 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5483 Time:1116s\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.548350\n\
    Training time: 1126s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0096 |  0.9262  | 0.9262 \n 20  | 0.0012 |  0.9415  | 0.9415 \n 30  | 0.0006 |  0.9415  | 0.9462 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 35 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.9462 Time:1302s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.946154\nTraining time: 1311s\n\nStarting RNA training on Modif dataset\nTask type: multilabel_classification, Output dim: 12\nMetric: auc_roc, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nModif Training (multilabel_classification, auc_roc)\nData: 304661 train, 3599 val, seq_len=101\n=============================================\n\
