parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP‑RegCal + RMSNorm pre‑head (no capacity change) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"hdp-regcal, rmsnorm, normalization, calibration\"\nabstract: \"Swap LayerNorm→RMSNorm (scale-only) before both regression and classification heads in HDP‑RegCal; keep head sizes unchanged (128). Tests whether RMSNorm improves stability without capacity changes.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from hdp_regcal_rmsnorm_rebalance import create_network as _create_net, create_optimizer as _create_opt\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          \"head_hidden_reg\": 128,   # no capacity change vs baseline\n          \"head_hidden_cls\": 128,   # no capacity change vs baseline\n          \"\
    head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"use_rmsnorm\": True,      # LN -> RMSNorm\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return _create_net(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return _create_opt(learning_rate)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP‑RegCal + RMSNorm + head rebalancing (reg=160, cls=96) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"hdp-regcal, rmsnorm, capacity, calibration\"\nabstract: \"Combine RMSNorm pre‑head with task‑type head capacity rebalancing (regression=160, classification=96) within <1M params. Hypothesis: allocate capacity to regression panels while keeping classification stable.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from hdp_regcal_rmsnorm_rebalance import create_network as _create_net, create_optimizer as _create_opt\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"\
    learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          \"head_hidden_reg\": 160,   # rebalanced toward regression\n          \"head_hidden_cls\": 96,    # slightly reduced classification\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"use_rmsnorm\": True,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return _create_net(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return _create_opt(learning_rate)\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stagnation_protocol_II_results.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stagnation Protocol — Cycle II (partial results, seed=42)\n\n  Minimal DSConv baseline (ID 767 ≈ 0.6745):\n  - 810 — Per-channel learned mean↔max mix (α0=0.35) + concat[max]: 0.6805\n      • APA 0.8497 | CRI-Off 0.0940 | CRI-On 0.4893 | PRS 0.5483 | MRL 0.8852 | Modif 0.9511\
    \ | ncRNA 0.9462\n      • Passes avg (+0.006), but misses gate (CRI-Off < 0.097; PRS < 0.553). Insight: improves ncRNA/CRI-On, but harms PRS and slightly CRI-Off.\n  - 811 — RMSNorm pre-head (swap LN): 0.6745\n      • APA 0.8526 | CRI-Off 0.0957 | CRI-On 0.4808 | PRS 0.5473 | MRL 0.8644 | Modif 0.9511 | ncRNA 0.9292\n      • Neutral overall vs baseline; slight CRI-Off ↑, PRS ↓.\n\n  Decision:\n  - Do not port per-channel mix to HDP‑RegCal due to CRI-Off/PRS gate failures.\n  - Proceed with HDP‑RegCal RMSNorm tests (with and without head rebalancing). Submissions queued: RMSNorm only; RMSNorm + (reg=160, cls=96).\n```"
