    \ after 813/814 finish):\n  - Head rebalancing only (LN, no RMSNorm) to isolate capacity effect.\n  - If all neutral/negative, finalize Cycle II report as negative results with insights on why literal max remains robust; consider CPE-style positional components as an orthogonal future direction (see Archive #27).\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 25}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Cycle II Addendum: Per‑channel mean↔max mix and RMSNorm on minimal DSConv\"\ncontent: |\n  Minimal DSConv baseline (ID 767 ≈ 0.6745):\n  - 810 — Learned per‑channel mean↔max mix (α0=0.35) + concat[max]: 0.6805\n    • APA 0.8497 | CRI-Off 0.0940 | CRI-On 0.4893 | PRS 0.5483 | MRL 0.8852 | Modif 0.9511 | ncRNA 0.9462\n    • Despite +0.006 avg, fails gates (CRI-Off < 0.097; PRS < 0.553). Conclusion: helps ncRNA/CRI‑On but hurts PRS and slightly CRI‑Off.\n  - 811 — RMSNorm pre‑head (swap LN): 0.6745 (neutral)\n    • APA 0.8526 | CRI-Off 0.0957 | CRI-On 0.4808 | PRS 0.5473 | MRL 0.8644 | Modif 0.9511\
    \ | ncRNA 0.9292.\n\n  Synthesis and next:\n  - We will not port the learned mix to HDP‑RegCal due to CRI‑Off/PRS regressions.\n  - HDP‑RegCal RMSNorm is being tested (IDs 813/814 — RMSNorm ± head rebalancing). If neutral, we will also test head rebalancing alone (LN) to isolate capacity effects.\n  - If all remain negative, Cycle II will be reported as negative results with the core insight reinforced: literal max in pooling remains robust; smoothing/averaging or reweighted mixes tend to degrade CRI‑*/PRS on these baselines.\n  - Orthogonal future direction flagged from contemporaneous work: contextual position embeddings (CPE) as a compliant foundation change (see Archive #27). We may scope a minimal CPE variant next cycle if stagnation persists.\n\n  Artifacts:\n  - results/cycle_ii_partial_summary.md\n  - submissions/dsconv_minibase_expts3.py (Flax‑compatible probes)\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stagnation_protocol_II_next.md}\n\
