parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stagnation_protocol_II_results.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stagnation Protocol — Cycle II (finalized, seed=42 unless noted)\n\n  Baselines:\n  - Minimal DSConv mean+max (ID 767): 0.6745\n  - HDP‑RegCal (seed‑42 reference, ID 713): 0.6886 (tri‑seed ≈ 0.6885)\n\n  Minimal DSConv ideas:\n  - 810 — Per‑channel mean↔max mix (α0=0.35) + concat[max]: 0.6805\n      • APA 0.8497 | CRI-Off 0.0940 | CRI-On 0.4893 | PRS 0.5483 | MRL 0.8852 | Modif 0.9511 | ncRNA 0.9462\n      • ↑avg (+0.006) but fails gates (CRI‑Off < 0.097; PRS < 0.553). Not ported.\n  - 811 — RMSNorm pre‑head (swap LN): 0.6745\n      • Neutral overall; slight CRI‑Off ↑, PRS ↓.\n\n  HDP‑RegCal ideas:\n  - 813 — RMSNorm pre‑head (no capacity change): 0.6838\n      • APA 0.8513 | CRI-Off 0.0875 | CRI-On 0.5046 | PRS 0.5574 | MRL 0.8850 | Modif 0.9502 | ncRNA 0.9508\n      • Neutral/negative vs baseline; CRI‑Off slightly low.\n  - 814 — RMSNorm + head rebalancing (reg=160, cls=96):\
    \ 0.6800\n      • Negative; capacity shift did not help.\n  - 816 — Head rebalancing only (LN; reg=160, cls=96): 0.6813\n      • APA 0.8541 | CRI-Off 0.0755 | CRI-On 0.4880 | PRS 0.5682 | MRL 0.8875 | Modif 0.9508 | ncRNA 0.9446\n      • Negative due to CRI‑Off < 0.08 and lower avg vs baseline.\n\n  Conclusions:\n  - Literal max in pooling remains robust on these baselines; reweighted mean↔max improves some panels (ncRNA/CRI‑On) but harms PRS and slightly CRI‑Off.\n  - RMSNorm pre‑head is neutral/negative under HDP‑RegCal; head capacity rebalancing is ineffective and can depress CRI‑Off.\n  - HDP‑RegCal defaults remain preferred (tri‑seed ≈ 0.6885).\n\n  Next:\n  - Close Cycle II as negative results with analysis.\n  - Scope Cycle III: minimal, compliant Contextual Positional Encoding (CPE) variants for both minimal DSConv and HDP‑RegCal, inspired by Archive #27/#28.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol Cycle II: Negative\
    \ Results on Mean–Max Reweighting, RMSNorm, and Head Rebalancing\"\nabstract: \"We investigated three low-complexity ideas on a minimal DSConv baseline and on HDP‑RegCal: per‑channel mean↔max reweighting (no smoothing), RMSNorm pre‑head, and head capacity rebalancing. While the minimal baseline saw a +0.006 avg gain with mean↔max mixing, it failed CRI‑Off/PRS gates. RMSNorm and capacity rebalancing were neutral/negative on HDP‑RegCal. We conclude literal max remains robust; reweighting and head-level tweaks do not break stagnation here.\"\ntags: stagnation, baseline, pooling, normalization, capacity\ncontent: |\n  Summary\n  We executed Stagnation Protocol Cycle II with a minimal DSConv mean+max baseline (ID 767: 0.6745) and our strong HDP‑RegCal reference (seed‑42 ~0.6886; tri‑seed ≈0.6885). We tested:\n  1) Per‑channel mean↔max mixing (convex, no smoothing of maxima)\n  2) RMSNorm (scale‑only) pre‑head\n  3) Head capacity rebalancing by task type\n\n  Experiments (seed=42 unless stated)\n\
    \  Minimal DSConv mean+max baseline (ID 767: 0.6745):\n  - 810 — Per‑channel mean↔max mix (α0=0.35) + concat[max]: 0.6805\n    • APA 0.8497 | CRI‑Off 0.0940 | CRI‑On 0.4893 | PRS 0.5483 | MRL 0.8852 | Modif 0.9511 | ncRNA 0.9462\n    • Average ↑ +0.006, but misses gates (CRI‑Off < 0.097; PRS < 0.553), so not ported.\n  - 811 — RMSNorm pre‑head (swap LN): 0.6745 (neutral)\n    • APA 0.8526 | CRI‑Off 0.0957 | CRI‑On 0.4808 | PRS 0.5473 | MRL 0.8644 | Modif 0.9511 | ncRNA 0.9292\n\n  HDP‑RegCal reference (seed‑42 ~0.6886; tri‑seed ≈0.6885):\n  - 813 — RMSNorm pre‑head (no capacity change): 0.6838\n    • APA 0.8513 | CRI‑Off 0.0875 | CRI‑On 0.5046 | PRS 0.5574 | MRL 0.8850 | Modif 0.9502 | ncRNA 0.9508\n    • Neutral/negative overall; CRI‑Off slightly low.\n  - 814 — RMSNorm + head rebalancing (reg=160, cls=96): 0.6800\n    • Negative; rebalancing did not help.\n  - 816 — Head rebalancing only (LayerNorm; reg=160, cls=96): 0.6813\n    • APA 0.8541 | CRI‑Off 0.0755 | CRI‑On 0.4880 | PRS 0.5682\
    \ | MRL 0.8875 | Modif 0.9508 | ncRNA 0.9446\n    • Negative: CRI‑Off < 0.08 and lower average.\n\n  Analysis and Insights\n  - Literal max pooling remains robust in DSConv pipelines: attempts to reweight mean vs. max can help ncRNA/CRI‑On yet tend to degrade PRS and slightly CRI‑Off.\n  - RMSNorm pre‑head did not surpass LayerNorm within HDP‑RegCal; small gains on CRI‑On/ncRNA were offset by CRI‑Off regression.\n  - Head capacity rebalancing (reg↑, cls↓) alone or with RMSNorm failed to improve the aggregate and depressed CRI‑Off.\n\n  Takeaways\n  - Retain the established HDP‑RegCal defaults (tri‑seed ≈0.6885).\n  - For DSConv baselines, keep literal mean+max pooling; avoid smoothing or convex mixing unless PRS/CRI‑Off are explicitly protected.\n\n  Reproducibility Artifacts\n  - Results: storage/noema/results/stagnation_protocol_II_results.md\n  - Minimal DSConv probes: storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_minibase_expts3.py\n  - HDP‑RegCal variants: storage/noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_rmsnorm_rebalance.py\n\
    \  - Evaluation IDs: 767, 810, 811, 813, 814, 816\n\n  Future Work (Cycle III)\n  - Explore minimal, compliant Contextual Positional Encoding (CPE) variants for both minimal DSConv and HDP‑RegCal, inspired by Archive #27 (Veritas III) and #28 (Quaero I).\n  - Objective: inject positional awareness without destabilizing CRI‑Off or harming PRS, and test synthesis with HDP‑RegCal.\n```"
