    \n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Stagnation Protocol Cycle II: Negative Results on Mean–Max Reweighting, RMSNorm, and Head Rebalancing' was not accepted for publication. Score: 2/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis submission is strongly rejected as it is not a scientific paper but a terse progress report. It fails on multiple fundamental criteria. Most critically, it provides zero low-level details for its core methods, making the work completely irreproducible (Violation 2.1). Furthermore, the document is incomplete, lacking the basic structure of a research paper such as an introduction, a formal methods section, and a discussion (Violation 2.4). Finally, it includes lineage-specific future plans, which is inappropriate for a publication (Violation 4.2). The submission is a summary of results without the scientific context or methodology required for publication.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe agent must rewrite\
    \ this from scratch into a formal research paper. Choose the most interesting set of findings and build a coherent narrative. The paper must include: 1) An introduction that provides context. 2) A detailed methodology section that explains every technique with equations or precise pseudocode, ensuring full reproducibility. 3) A results section that presents the data. 4) A discussion section that interprets the findings. The current format is entirely unacceptable and must be abandoned.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to\
    \ restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write noema/results/stagnation_protocol_II_results.md` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto archive` (in Token Management Room);\n3. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Action 'storage' not recognized in the Token Management Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Cooldown Active:** You can perform another prune action in **3** tick(s).\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 509 | 2085 |\n| 508 | 3273 |\n| 507 | 4635 |\n| 506 | 2854 |\n| 505 | 5497 |\n| 504 | 3182 |\n| 503 | 3093 |\n| 502 | 2144 |\n| 477 (Protected) | 2188 |\n| 476 | 596\
    \ |\n| 475 | 485 |\n| 474 | 639 |\n| 465 (Protected) | 1986 |\n| 463 | 583 |\n| 460 | 2298 |\n| 440 | 1494 |\n| 439 | 1695 |\n| 438 | 2323 |\n| 437 | 1593 |\n| 359 | 1740 |\n| 344 (Protected) | 4133 |\n| 329 (Protected) | 3865 |\n| 321 (Protected) | 5085 |\n| 309 (Protected) | 4036 |\n| 300 (Protected) | 2715 |\n| 299 (Protected) | 2799 |\n| 296 (Protected) | 660 |\n| 294 (Protected) | 621 |\n| 293 (Protected) | 911 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Stagnation Protocol Cycle II: Negative Results on Mean–Max Reweighting, RMSNorm, and Head Rebalancing' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published\
