  \ field doesn’t support tables. I also want to include evaluation IDs for experiments and clear gating criteria. Lastly, I'll provide analysis insights based on our findings.**Including pseudocode and equations**\n\nI need to add pseudocode and equations for the methodology. For the per-channel mix, I can define pooled_c using the sigmoid function and blending mean and max values, along with an initial bias for alpha. The RMSNorm equation should show the normalization process, specifying dimensions. Then for the DSConv block, I’ll include details about dilated convolution with dropout and residuals. I'll also clarify training hyperparameters like learning rate, optimizer, and batch size. Finally, I need to present results in a clear, replicable table summarizing numeric metrics.**Formatting discussion and future work**\n\nI should consider showing results as a code block with an ASCII table format. In the discussion, I'll interpret findings, noting that PRS is sensitive to smoothing while\
  \ CRI-Off benefits from extremes. I’ll mention that RMSNorm might interfere with RegCal and doesn't effectively address head scaling, and that capacity rebalancing has a mild effect. For limitations and future work, I'll suggest improvements like enhanced gating and dynamic pooling. I'll also ensure to provide storage paths for reproducibility, and craft the content with proper YAML quoting when necessary while keeping multiline format in mind.**Creating archive entry**\n\nI’ve got a title idea: \"Mean–Max Reweighting, RMSNorm, and Head Rebalancing in DSConv RNA Models: A Negative Results Study under Stagnation Protocol II.” \n\nThe abstract will be around 120-150 words since that’s required for the new archive. I’ll include tags like stagnation, negative results, and DSConv.\n\nI'll outline sections like Introduction, Related Work, Methods (including architectures and proposed changes), Results (with a summary table), Discussion, Reproducibility, and Conclusion. Then I’ll implement the\
