- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 511\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema II — Working Meta (Tick 508)\nStatus:\n- HDP‑RegCal baseline tri-seed ≈ 0.6885.\n- Cycle II: Minimal DSConv learned per‑channel mix ↑avg to 0.6805 but failed CRI‑Off/PRS gates; RMSNorm neutral; RMSNorm+rebalancing negative.\nRunning:\n- 816 HDP‑RegCal head rebalancing only (LN; reg=160, cls=96) — ablation to isolate capacity.\nNext:\n- If 816 negative, finalize Cycle II report (negatives) and scope Cycle III: minimal, compliant Contextual Positional Encoding (CPE) variant inspired by #27/#28 for both minimal DSConv and HDP‑RegCal.\n- Maintain tokens: prune recent verbose ticks after each batch of results.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 166,297 / 270,000 used (62%)\n- Agent Age: 218 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\
    \n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Mean–Max Reweighting, RMSNorm, and Head Rebalancing in DSConv RNA Models: A Negative Results Study under Stagnation Protocol II' has been accepted for publication! Score: 8/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis is an exemplary revision that successfully addresses all previous critical feedback. The paper has been transformed from an unacceptable progress report into a high-quality, professional, and fully reproducible negative results study. The methodology for the novel ideas is now exceptionally clear, with detailed formulas and pseudocode. The paper presents a coherent and compelling narrative, rigorously testing three ideas on two different baselines and providing valuable insights into why they failed. This is a solid and valuable contribution that will help other researchers avoid unpromising directions.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\n\
    The paper does an excellent job of documenting these negative results. The agent's plan to explore Contextual Positional Encodings (CPE) in the next cycle is well-motivated by recent publications (Veritas III, Archive #27). When pursuing this, the agent should pay close attention to the synthesis results from Veritas III, which showed that while CPE boosted CRI-Off, the overall aggregate score did not increase. A key contribution for the next cycle would be to not only replicate the CRI-Off improvement but to find a way to integrate CPE such that it also lifts the overall aggregate score, perhaps by exploring different fusion methods or by tuning the CPE parameters specifically for the DSConv backbone.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 29-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields:\
    \ title, abstract, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Mean–Max Reweighting, RMSNorm, and Head Rebalancing in DSConv RNA Models: A Negative Results Study under Stagnation Protocol II' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 29 | Mean–Max Reweighting, RMSNorm, and Head Rebalancing in DSConv RNA Models: A Negative Results Study under Stagnation Protocol II | Noema II | Tick 510 | 1382 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 28 | On the Architectural Dependence of Positional Encodings for RNA Sequence Modeling | Quaero I | Tick 506 | 860 | 2 | (2 unread)\
    \ |\n| 27 | Veritas III - Exploring Novel Foundational Mechanisms for RNA Modeling in Stagnation: Contextual Position Embeddings and Their Synthesis | Veritas III | Tick 502 | 2148 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 26 | An Independent Architectural Exploration for Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling | Orion I | Tick 489 | 721 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 25 | Negative Results on a Minimal DSConv Baseline: Reverse-Invariance, Power-Mean Pooling, and Position Dropout | Noema II | Tick 488 | 1582 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 24 | Stabilizing CRI-Off Performance in Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling through Regression Calibration | Veritas III | Tick 474 | 1548 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 23 | A Hybrid Dual-Path Architecture Integrating a Transformer Body for RNA Sequence Modeling | Zetetic I | Tick 429 | 444 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 22 | HDP-RegCal: Parsimonious Hybrid Dual-Path DSConv with Explicit Regression Calibration for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling (<1M Params) | Noema II | Tick 423 | 2487 | 16 | (All Read) |\n| 21 | Veritas\
    \ II - Global SOTA & Record CRI-Off: Leveraging Task-Specific Prediction Heads for Unified RNA Modeling | Veritas II | Tick 378 | 1575 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 20 | Paper: A DSConv Architecture Optimized via Enriched Pooling and Parameter Reduction | Logos II | Tick 364 | 713 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 511
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{update 29-1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Reviewer response and Cycle III plan (CPE)\n  We appreciate the feedback. As suggested, Cycle III will investigate Contextual Positional Encoding (CPE) variants that are minimal, compliant, and reproducible. We will focus on:\n  - A residual CPE block inserted before DSConv: x ↦ x + β·DWConv_k(x) + γ·PE_sin(L,C), with learnable β,γ scalars; DWConv_k is depthwise 1D conv (k∈{3,5}) and PE_sin is sinusoidal positional encoding sized to hidden_dim C. This injects contextual position awareness with negligible parameters.\n  - Two targets: (a) Minimal DSConv+mean–max baseline, (b) HDP‑RegCal (same backbone) to test synthesis.\n  Gates:\n  - Minimal DSConv: improve average ≥ +0.002 vs. baseline without CRI‑Off/PRS regressions.\n  - HDP‑RegCal: maintain or improve aggregate (≥ seed‑42 reference), and CRI‑Off ≥ 0.08.\n  We will release full code and IDs as in this paper.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write\
    \ noema/submissions/dsconv_cpe_minibase.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Minimal DSConv + mean+max baseline with optional Contextual Positional Encoding (CPE).\n  CPE: residual x -> x + beta*DWConv_k(x) + gamma*PE_sin(L,C) where beta,gamma are learnable scalars (init 0.5, 0.1),\n       DWConv_k is depthwise conv (k=3 by default), and PE_sin is sinusoidal positional encoding with C dims.\n\n  Heads: single hidden MLP (128) with LayerNorm → GELU → Dropout → Dense; no RegCal, no motif. <1M params.\n  Flax 0.10.6 compatible (uses kernel_dilation).\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n      \
    \    \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          # CPE controls\n          \"use_cpe\": True,\n          \"cpe_kernel\": 3,\n          \"cpe_beta_init\": 0.5,\n          \"cpe_gamma_init\": 0.1,\n      }\n\n  def sinusoidal_pe(L: int, C: int):\n      pos = jnp.arange(L)[:, None]          # (L,1)\n      i = jnp.arange(C)[None, :]            # (1,C)\n      # standard Transformer-style angles\n      div_term = jnp.power(10000.0, ( (i//2)*2 ) / jnp.maximum(1.0, float(C)))\n      ang = pos / div_term\n      pe = jnp.where((i % 2) == 0, jnp.sin(ang), jnp.cos(ang))  # (L,C)\n      return pe  # (L,C)\n\n  class CPE(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      k: int = 3\n      beta_init: float = 0.5\n      gamma_init: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x: (B,L,C)\n          B, L, C = x.shape\n          # Depthwise conv for contextual bias\n          dw = nn.Conv(features=C, kernel_size=(self.k,), feature_group_count=C, padding=\"SAME\"\
    )(x)\n          beta = self.param(\"beta\", lambda rng, shp: jnp.array(self.beta_init, dtype=x.dtype), ())\n          # Sinusoidal PE\n          pe = sinusoidal_pe(L, C)[None, :, :]  # (1,L,C)\n          gamma = self.param(\"gamma\", lambda rng, shp: jnp.array(self.gamma_init, dtype=x.dtype), ())\n          return x + beta * dw + gamma * pe\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\
    \ kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      use_cpe: bool = True\n      cpe_kernel: int = 3\n      cpe_beta_init: float = 0.5\n      cpe_gamma_init: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          if self.use_cpe:\n              h = CPE(self.hidden_dim, self.cpe_kernel, self.cpe_beta_init, self.cpe_gamma_init)(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def global_mean_max(h):\n      mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n      maxv = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n      return jnp.concatenate([mean, maxv], axis=-1)\n\
    \n  class MiniDSConvCPE(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      head_hidden: int = 128\n      head_dropout: float = 0.05\n      use_cpe: bool = True\n      cpe_kernel: int = 3\n      cpe_beta_init: float = 0.5\n      cpe_gamma_init: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate,\n                             self.use_cpe, self.cpe_kernel, self.cpe_beta_init, self.cpe_gamma_init)(x, deterministic)\n          pooled = global_mean_max(h)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(pooled)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\
    \          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return out.squeeze(-1)\n          return out\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = MiniDSConvCPE(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n              head_hidden=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden\", 128)),\n              head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n              use_cpe=bool(hp.get(\"use_cpe\", True)),\n              cpe_kernel=int(hp.get(\"cpe_kernel\", 3)),\n              cpe_beta_init=float(hp.get(\"cpe_beta_init\", 0.5)),\n              cpe_gamma_init=float(hp.get(\"\
    cpe_gamma_init\", 0.1)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          pk, dk = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': pk, 'dropout': dk}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          if rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CPE-Minimal: DSConv + mean+max\
    \ + residual CPE (DWConv3 + sinusoidal) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"baseline, dsconv, positional-encoding, cpe, meanmax\"\nabstract: \"Add a minimal Contextual Positional Encoding (CPE) before DSConv: x ↦ x + β·DWConv3(x) + γ·PE_sin(L,C), with learnable β,γ. Tests whether contextual POS info improves the minimal DSConv+mean–max baseline without harming CRI‑Off/PRS.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_cpe_minibase import create_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"use_cpe\": True,\n          \"cpe_kernel\": 3,\n          \"cpe_beta_init\": 0.5,\n          \"cpe_gamma_init\": 0.1,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      return create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_cpe.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  HDP‑RegCal with optional minimal Contextual Positional Encoding (CPE) before DSConv.\n  CPE: h0 = Conv1x1(x); h0 <- h0 + beta*DWConv_k(h0) + gamma*PE_sin(L,C); then DSConv dilated blocks.\n  Rest: main mean+max + motif max; fused -> Dense(H_task) -> LayerNorm -> GELU -> Dropout -> head; RegCal ON for regression-family tasks.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n\
    \          \"head_hidden_reg\": 128,\n          \"head_hidden_cls\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          # motif\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          # CPE controls\n          \"use_cpe\": True,\n          \"cpe_kernel\": 3,\n          \"cpe_beta_init\": 0.5,\n          \"cpe_gamma_init\": 0.1,\n      }\n\n  def sinusoidal_pe(L: int, C: int):\n      pos = jnp.arange(L)[:, None]\n      i = jnp.arange(C)[None, :]\n      div_term = jnp.power(10000.0, ((i//2)*2) / jnp.maximum(1.0, float(C)))\n      ang = pos / div_term\n      pe = jnp.where((i % 2) == 0, jnp.sin(ang), jnp.cos(ang))\n      return pe\n\n  class CPE(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      k: int = 3\n      beta_init: float = 0.5\n      gamma_init: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n          B,L,C = h.shape\n          dw = nn.Conv(features=C, kernel_size=(self.k,), feature_group_count=C, padding=\"SAME\")(h)\n          beta = self.param(\"beta\", lambda\
    \ rng, shp: jnp.array(self.beta_init, dtype=h.dtype), ())\n          pe = sinusoidal_pe(L, C)[None, :, :]\n          gamma = self.param(\"gamma\", lambda rng, shp: jnp.array(self.gamma_init, dtype=h.dtype), ())\n          return h + beta*dw + gamma*pe\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual\
    \ + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      use_cpe: bool = True\n      cpe_kernel: int = 3\n      cpe_beta_init: float = 0.5\n      cpe_gamma_init: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          if self.use_cpe:\n              h = CPE(self.hidden_dim, self.cpe_kernel, self.cpe_beta_init, self.cpe_gamma_init)(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def l2_normalize_feats(z, eps=1e-6):\n      return z / (jnp.linalg.norm(z, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + eps)\n\n  class MotifPath(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      k: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n      \
    \    x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.k,), padding=\"SAME\")(h)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n\n  class HDPRegCalCPE(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      head_hidden_reg: int = 128\n      head_hidden_cls: int = 128\n      head_dropout: float = 0.05\n      regcal_on: bool = True\n      motif_k: int = 5\n      use_cpe: bool = True\n      cpe_kernel: int = 3\n      cpe_beta_init: float = 0.5\n      cpe_gamma_init: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate,\n                             self.use_cpe, self.cpe_kernel, self.cpe_beta_init, self.cpe_gamma_init)(x, deterministic)\n          h_mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n\
    \          h_max  = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          motif  = MotifPath(self.hidden_dim, self.motif_k)(h)\n          pooled = jnp.concatenate([h_mean, h_max, motif], axis=-1)\n          H = self.head_hidden_reg if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\") else self.head_hidden_cls\n          z = nn.Dense(H)(pooled)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\"):\n              z_reg = l2_normalize_feats(z) if self.regcal_on else z\n              out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_reg)\n              return out.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else out\n          else:\n              logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n              return logits\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams:\
    \ Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = HDPRegCalCPE(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n              head_hidden_reg=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden_reg\", 128)),\n              head_hidden_cls=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden_cls\", 128)),\n              head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n              regcal_on=bool(hp.get(\"regcal_on\", True)),\n              motif_k=int(hp.get(\"motif_k\", 5)),\n              use_cpe=bool(hp.get(\"use_cpe\", True)),\n              cpe_kernel=int(hp.get(\"cpe_kernel\", 3)),\n              cpe_beta_init=float(hp.get(\"cpe_beta_init\", 0.5)),\n              cpe_gamma_init=float(hp.get(\"cpe_gamma_init\", 0.1)),\n \
    \         )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          pk, dk = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': pk, 'dropout': dk}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          if rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n                               task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n                               hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"HDP‑RegCal + minimal CPE (DWConv3 + sinusoidal residual) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"hdp-regcal, positional-encoding, cpe, dsconv, calibration\"\nabstract: \"Insert a minimal Contextual Positional Encoding (CPE) before DSConv within HDP‑RegCal: h0 ← h0 + β·DWConv3(h0) + γ·PE_sin(L,C). Tests synthesis of CPE with RegCal to lift CRI‑Off without reducing aggregate.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from hdp_regcal_cpe import create_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden_reg\": 128,\n          \"head_hidden_cls\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"use_cpe\": True,\n          \"cpe_kernel\"\
    : 3,\n          \"cpe_beta_init\": 0.5,\n          \"cpe_gamma_init\": 0.1,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to respond with our next actions after the system accepted paper #29 with a score of 8/10. It suggests exploring CPE, and I should plan to start Cycle III with minimal DSConv and HDP‑RegCal. I’ll implement the minimal CPE module, ensuring compliance without hacks. Testing on the initial seed will be important, and I may want to update the published capsule with a brief addendum regarding the review suggestion.**Defining action steps**\n\nI see that the environment only accepts /execute_action commands for parsing, and multiple actions can be included. I could update Archive #29 with an addendum to address reviewer suggestions, using the command '/execute_action{update 29-1}' for the first message. It seems like there might be two messages in that capsule, possibly including a reviewer comment. Additionally, I want to start implementing minimal CPE variant code in submissions, ensuring I stick to allowed functions like create_network.**Implementing\
  \ CPE in DSConvBackbone**\n\nI’m planning to write a new submission that integrates Contextual Positional Encoding (CPE) into the DSConvBackbone. The idea is to implement per-channel sinusoidal encoding that’s generalized with a small convolution mixing in sequence content context. I’m thinking about using a depthwise 1D convolution on the identity positional encoding, with learned scalar blending of sinusoidal PE. The goal is to keep the complexity minimal, under 1 million parameters, while ensuring the contextual positional information is properly mixed. I'll define the CPE module to achieve this.**Testing DSConv with CPE**\n\nI see that many believe adding Positional Encoding (PE) to DSConv can actually hinder performance, while simpler CNNs benefit. Given this, I’m considering keeping PE disabled by default for DSConv. Since time is limited, I propose starting with a minimal DSConv baseline. \n\nI'll implement a file called dsconv_cpe_minibase.py, adding an optional CPE module before\
  \ the first DSConv block. This will include a depthwise convolution that incorporates context and positional bias while also using a sinusoidal embedding. Alternatively, I could consider a 1D conv method with gating, though that might be too complex.**Implementing CPE and Preparing Submissions**\n\nI plan to implement Contextual Positional Encoding (CPE) in my minimal DSConv model. First, I'll compute the sinusoidal position encoding and add a content convolution for residual connections. This involves defining the CPE class to properly shape the inputs and include learnable parameters. \n\nNext, I’ll create the files for the baseline DSConv with CPE and for the HDP-RegCal variant, ensuring we have careful gating to maintain or improve aggregate performance. I'll also update Archive #29 with a brief response addressing the reviewer's suggestions. It's crucial to keep our token usage in check as I proceed."
