parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write noema/results/cpe_cycle_plan.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Cycle III — Minimal Contextual Positional Encoding (CPE) Plan (Tick 512)\n\n  Objective\n  - Inject minimal, compliant positional/context signals into DSConv backbones and test synthesis with RegCal.\n  - Improve CRI-Off without reducing aggregate score; avoid harming PRS.\n\n  CPE Definition (residual)\n  - h0 = Conv1x1(x)\n  - CPE(h0): h0 <- h0 + β·DWConv_k(h0) + γ·PE_sin(L,C), with learnable β,γ (init β=0.5, γ=0.1), k∈{3,5}.\n  - DSConv dilated blocks follow unchanged.\n  - No changes to training loop, losses, or dataset logic.\n\n  Baselines\n  - Minimal DSConv mean+max (ID 767 ≈ 0.6745).\n  - HDP‑RegCal (seed‑42 ref ID 713 ≈ 0.6886; tri‑seed mean ≈ 0.6885).\n\n  Acceptance Gates\n  - Minimal DSConv: avg ≥ baseline+0.002 (≥0.6765) AND no regressions on CRI-Off (<0.097) or PRS (<0.553).\n  - HDP‑RegCal: avg ≥ seed‑42 ref (≥0.6886) AND CRI-Off ≥ 0.08 (no large Modif/ncRNA drops).\n\n  Ablation\
    \ Matrix (initial)\n  - Minimal DSConv:\n    • A1: CPE (k=3, β_init=0.5, γ_init=0.1) — submitted (ID 822).\n    • A2: CPE γ-only (β_init=0.0, γ_init=0.1) — isolates sinusoidal PE.\n  - HDP‑RegCal:\n    • B1: CPE (k=3, β_init=0.5, γ_init=0.1) — submitted (ID 823).\n    • B2: CPE (k=5, β_init=0.5, γ_init=0.1) — tests broader context.\n\n  Reporting\n  - Results and deltas recorded in results/cpe_cycle_plan.md and results/CPE_RESULTS.md\n  - If positive, tri-seed and then explore fusion tweaks (e.g., small post-CPE norm) only if necessary.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CPE-Minimal ablation: γ-only positional (β=0.0) — DSConv + mean+max — seed=42\"\ntags: \"baseline, dsconv, positional-encoding, cpe, ablation\"\nabstract: \"Isolate sinusoidal positional component by setting β_init=0.0 (no DWConv) and γ_init=0.1. Tests whether pure PE improves the minimal DSConv+mean–max baseline without harming CRI‑Off/PRS.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n\
    \  from dsconv_cpe_minibase import create_network as _net, create_optimizer as _opt\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"use_cpe\": True,\n          \"cpe_kernel\": 3,\n          \"cpe_beta_init\": 0.0,   # γ-only\n          \"cpe_gamma_init\": 0.1,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return _net(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return _opt(learning_rate)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP‑RegCal + CPE (k=5) — DWConv5 + sinusoidal residual — seed=42\"\ntags: \"hdp-regcal, positional-encoding, cpe, dsconv, calibration, ablation\"\nabstract: \"CPE variant with broader context (k=5) before DSConv within HDP‑RegCal:\
    \ h0 ← h0 + β·DWConv5(h0) + γ·PE_sin. Tests whether increased contextual window boosts CRI‑Off while maintaining aggregate.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from hdp_regcal_cpe import create_network as _net, create_optimizer as _opt\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden_reg\": 128,\n          \"head_hidden_cls\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"use_cpe\": True,\n          \"cpe_kernel\": 5,     # broadened DWConv context\n          \"cpe_beta_init\": 0.5,\n          \"cpe_gamma_init\": 0.1,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return _net(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float =\
    \ 0.001):\n      return _opt(learning_rate)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Interpreting positional contributions**\n\nI'm considering ways to interpret contributions based on positional info versus context. I should create a results plan document and establish acceptance gates. Managing tokens is recommended for pruning after batch results, though it’s not necessary right now.\n\nThere’s the option to preview past content and possibly implement \"CPE ablations\" for easier code toggling. However, I see there’s a submission cooldown with the system allowing limited concurrent runs; I should cautiously schedule a couple more.**Planning for experiments**\n\nI’m thinking it’s best to keep to two submissions at a time. I can summarize our plan and acceptance gates in a storage document, although updating the archive is optional.\n\nI might perform a reflection tick for idea scoping on integration with CRI-Off. Right now, I have a couple of immediate tasks: First, write the \"cpe_cycle_plan.md\" in results. Then, I can submit two ablation runs focusing\
  \ on minimal DSConv and HDP-RegCal, while scheduling an additional minimal ablation to ensure balanced compute. This will give us a total of four runs.**Addressing a recursion bug**\n\nThere’s a concern about a recursion bug I encountered earlier due to function shadowing. The code for earlier CPE and minimal tasks used the same `create_network` function name, leading to mistakes when submissions defined a function with that name and called itself.\n\nTo prevent this, I should alias the imports or avoid redefining functions altogether. In previous debugging, I modified imports to alias them. So, I'll import with aliases, like `from module import create_network as net_create`, and then define `create_network` accordingly. This will help avoid recursion issues.**Planning new ablations**\n\nI need to avoid recursion issues like the earlier mistake where I had a function calling itself. So, for our new approach, I'm proposing two ablations:\n\nFirst, there’s the \"CPE-Minimal ablation\" with\
  \ a gamma-only positional setting (β=0). I’ll use a seed of 42 and set `use_cpe` to True, with cpe_beta_init at 0.0 and cpe_gamma_init at 0.1 for isolation.\n\nSecond, I’m suggesting \"HDP-RegCal + CPE\" using a kernel of 5 with the same seed. I’ll log this in the results, write the documentation for the ablation matrix, and check on token management later after submission.**Finalizing submission steps**\n\nI can update the accepted archive with a small note about the CPE plan since I already added \"reviewer response and Cycle III plan\" as update 29-1.\n\nI need to ensure proper YAML string quoting for colons and other special characters. I'll check that the base modules exist, as I created `dsconv_cpe_minibase.py` and `hdp_regcal_cpe.py` already. \n\nNow, I’ll implement the submission code. I'll import the necessary modules with aliases and define the hyperparameters. My final actions will be to write `cpe_cycle_plan.md`, submit the minimal gamma-only ablation, and submit the HDP-RegCal\
  \ with kernel=5. I'll remember to follow YAML rules for titles. Let's get this done!"
