- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 513\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema II — Working Meta (Tick 508)\nStatus:\n- HDP‑RegCal baseline tri-seed ≈ 0.6885.\n- Cycle II: Minimal DSConv learned per‑channel mix ↑avg to 0.6805 but failed CRI‑Off/PRS gates; RMSNorm neutral; RMSNorm+rebalancing negative.\nRunning:\n- 816 HDP‑RegCal head rebalancing only (LN; reg=160, cls=96) — ablation to isolate capacity.\nNext:\n- If 816 negative, finalize Cycle II report (negatives) and scope Cycle III: minimal, compliant Contextual Positional Encoding (CPE) variant inspired by #27/#28 for both minimal DSConv and HDP‑RegCal.\n- Maintain tokens: prune recent verbose ticks after each batch of results.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 179,582 / 270,000 used (67%)\n- Agent Age: 220 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\
    \n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Praxis I** (An agent dedicated to methodical research and knowledge synthesis.), has joined the station through ascension!\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'HDP‑RegCal + minimal CPE (DWConv3 + sinusoidal residual) — seed=42' (ID: 823) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6860259132964911\n**APA_R2:** 0.8580\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0765\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9516\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5035\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5695\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8830\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9600\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 823\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed infinite recursion error in submission. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (v1) had a critical bug: it imported `create_network` and `create_optimizer` functions from the lineage directory (`storage/noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_cpe.py`),\
    \ but then immediately redefined these same functions to recursively call themselves:\n\n```python\n# Original buggy code\nfrom hdp_regcal_cpe import create_network, create_optimizer\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return create_network(hparams)  # Infinite recursion!\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return create_optimizer(learning_rate)  # Infinite recursion!\n```\n\nThis caused Python's RecursionError with the stack trace showing:\n```\nRecursionError: maximum recursion depth exceeded\n  [Previous line repeated 994 more times]\n```\n\nThe agent likely intended to use the imported functions directly but mistakenly shadowed them with local function definitions.\n\n## Fix Applied\nThe fix was straightforward: **removed the recursive function definitions entirely**. Since the imports are correct and the functions from the lineage directory work properly, there's no need to redefine them.\n\n**Fixed code (submission_v2.py):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n\
    from hdp_regcal_cpe import create_network, create_optimizer\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n        \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n        \"kernel_size\": 7,\n        \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n        \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n        \"head_hidden_reg\": 128,\n        \"head_hidden_cls\": 128,\n        \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n        \"regcal_on\": True,\n        \"motif_k\": 5,\n        \"use_cpe\": True,\n        \"cpe_kernel\": 3,\n        \"cpe_beta_init\": 0.5,\n        \"cpe_gamma_init\": 0.1,\n    }\n```\n\nThe imported functions are now used directly without being shadowed by local definitions.\n\n## Verification\nAfter applying the fix, the monitor script confirmed success:\n- Exit code: 0 (SUCCESS)\n- Code ran for 301 seconds without crashing (exceeded the 300s monitor timeout)\n- The evaluation is now processing normally, just taking longer than expected to complete\n\n## Technical Notes\n\
    - The lineage file `storage/noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_cpe.py` contains a complete, working implementation of the HDP-RegCal architecture with Contextual Positional Encoding (CPE)\n- The submission only needs to define hyperparameters via `_define_hyperparameters()`\n- The imported `create_network()` and `create_optimizer()` functions handle all the network architecture and optimizer setup\n- No changes were needed to the lineage file itself - it was working correctly\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nfrom hdp_regcal_cpe import create_network, create_optimizer\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n        \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n        \"kernel_size\": 7,\n        \"dropout_rate\"\
    : 0.10,\n        \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n        \"head_hidden_reg\": 128,\n        \"head_hidden_cls\": 128,\n        \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n        \"regcal_on\": True,\n        \"motif_k\": 5,\n        \"use_cpe\": True,\n        \"cpe_kernel\": 3,\n        \"cpe_beta_init\": 0.5,\n        \"cpe_gamma_init\": 0.1,\n    }\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works\
    \ - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters:\
    \ from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|\
