    CRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.076536\nTraining time: 107s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0021 |  0.9554  | 0.9600 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 18 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.9600 Time:682s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.960000\nTraining time: 691s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n\
    =============================================\n 10  | 0.1024 |  0.8830  | 0.8830 \n 20  | 0.0525 |  0.8752  | 0.8830 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 20 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8830 Time:803s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.882952\nTraining time: 813s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0256 |  0.5111  | 0.5695 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 16 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5695 Time:971s\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.569539\nTraining time: 981s\n\nStarting RNA training\
    \ on APA dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nAPA Training (regression, r2)\nData: 145463 train, 33170 val, seq_len=186\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0087 |  0.8470  | 0.8580 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 13\n=============================================\nBest:0.8580 Time:1812s\n\nAPA training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.858042\nTraining time: 1826s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 7651f2dd-8d49-47dc-a2ab-390308017ffe\nTotal time: 1937s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-27 00:13:59,968\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761495239968819981\n2025-10-27 00:13:59,982\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761495239982821519\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYour\
    \ research submission 'CPE-Minimal: DSConv + mean+max + residual CPE (DWConv3 + sinusoidal) — seed=42' (ID: 822) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6776548396520662\n**APA_R2:** 0.8525\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0978\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9509\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4692\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5552\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8734\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9446\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 822\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed infinite recursion error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had a classic **infinite recursion bug**:\n\n```python\nfrom dsconv_cpe_minibase import create_network, create_optimizer\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return create_network(hparams)  # ❌ Calls itself infinitely!\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return create_optimizer(learning_rate)  # ❌ Calls itself infinitely!\n```\n\nThe submission imported `create_network`\
    \ and `create_optimizer` from the `dsconv_cpe_minibase` module, but then **redefined** functions with the same names. When the evaluation system called `create_network()`, it invoked the local function which recursively called itself, leading to:\n\n```\nRecursionError: maximum recursion depth exceeded\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Removed the redundant function definitions** entirely. The fixed `submission_v2.py`:\n\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nfrom dsconv_cpe_minibase import create_network, create_optimizer\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n        \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n        \"kernel_size\": 7,\n        \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n        \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n        \"head_hidden\": 128,\n        \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n        \"use_cpe\": True,\n        \"cpe_kernel\": 3,\n        \"cpe_beta_init\": 0.5,\n        \"cpe_gamma_init\": 0.1,\n    }\n\
    \n# The create_network and create_optimizer functions are imported from dsconv_cpe_minibase\n# No need to redefine them - they already exist and work correctly!\n```\n\n**Key changes:**\n1. Removed the `create_network()` function definition that was shadowing the import\n2. Removed the `create_optimizer()` function definition that was shadowing the import\n3. Kept only the necessary `_define_hyperparameters()` function and module-level constants\n4. The imported functions from `dsconv_cpe_minibase` now work as intended\n\n## Result\n✅ The submission now runs successfully without crashing\n✅ Code executed for over 300 seconds without errors\n✅ The evaluation is proceeding normally (may take longer to complete training)\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Error Type**: RecursionError (infinite recursion)\n- **Location**: Lines 13-14 and 24-25 in original submission\n- **Solution**: Simple deletion of redundant wrapper functions\n- **Verification**: Monitored for 300+ seconds with no crashes\n\
    \n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nfrom dsconv_cpe_minibase import create_network, create_optimizer\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n        \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n        \"kernel_size\": 7,\n        \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n        \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n        \"head_hidden\": 128,\n        \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n        \"use_cpe\": True,\n        \"cpe_kernel\": 3,\n        \"cpe_beta_init\": 0.5,\n        \"cpe_gamma_init\": 0.1,\n    }\n\n# The create_network and create_optimizer functions are imported from dsconv_cpe_minibase\n# No need to redefine them - they already exist and work correctly!\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\n\
    STDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n\
