- text: "/execute_action{storage write noema/results/CPE_RESULTS.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Cycle III — CPE initial results (seed=42)\n\n  Baselines:\n  - Minimal DSConv mean+max (ID 767): 0.6745\n  - HDP‑RegCal seed‑42 reference (ID 713): 0.6886 (tri‑seed ≈ 0.6885)\n\n  CPE (residual): h0 <- h0 + β·DWConv_k(h0) + γ·PE_sin(L,C)\n\n  Results:\n  - 822 — Minimal DSConv + CPE(k=3, β=0.5, γ=0.1): 0.6777\n      • APA 0.8525 | CRI-Off 0.0978 | CRI-On 0.4692 | PRS 0.5552 | MRL 0.8734 | Modif 0.9509 | ncRNA 0.9446\n      • Passes gates (avg ≥ 0.6765, CRI-Off ≥ 0.097, PRS ≥ 0.553). Plan: tri‑seed once HDP variants tested.\n\n  - 823 — HDP‑RegCal + CPE(k=3, β=0.5, γ=0.1): 0.6860\n      • APA 0.8580 | CRI-Off 0.0765 | CRI-On 0.5035 | PRS 0.5695 | MRL 0.8830 | Modif 0.9516 | ncRNA 0.9600\n      • Fails gates (avg < 0.6886 and CRI-Off < 0.08). Insight: CPE helps CRI‑On/PRS/ncRNA but depresses CRI‑Off.\n\n  Next ablations (to restore CRI‑Off while keeping gains):\n  - Reduce or remove DWConv influence\
    \ (β→0) and lower γ to 0.05.\n  - Broaden k to 5 only if CRI‑Off stabilizes.\n\n  Queue:\n  - HDP‑RegCal + CPE γ‑only (β=0, γ=0.05) — target: CRI‑Off ≥ 0.08, avg ≥ 0.6886.\n  - HDP‑RegCal + CPE (β=0.25, γ=0.05) — low‑influence blended CPE.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP‑RegCal + CPE γ‑only (β=0.0, γ=0.05) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"hdp-regcal, positional-encoding, cpe, calibration, ablation\"\nabstract: \"Ablation to restore CRI‑Off: remove DWConv component (β=0.0) and halve sinusoidal amplitude (γ=0.05) in the CPE residual before DSConv. Hypothesis: reduce positional interference that depressed CRI‑Off while preserving PRS/CRI‑On gains.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from hdp_regcal_cpe import create_network as _net, create_optimizer as _opt\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\"\
    : 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden_reg\": 128,\n          \"head_hidden_cls\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"use_cpe\": True,\n          \"cpe_kernel\": 3,\n          \"cpe_beta_init\": 0.0,   # γ-only\n          \"cpe_gamma_init\": 0.05, # reduced amplitude\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return _net(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return _opt(learning_rate)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP‑RegCal + CPE low‑influence (β=0.25, γ=0.05, k=3) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"hdp-regcal, positional-encoding, cpe, calibration, ablation\"\nabstract: \"Low‑influence CPE residual (β=0.25, γ=0.05) before DSConv to balance positional signal and contextual bias. Goal: recover CRI‑Off ≥ 0.08 while retaining PRS/CRI‑On/ncRNA lifts.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n\
    \  from hdp_regcal_cpe import create_network as _net, create_optimizer as _opt\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden_reg\": 128,\n          \"head_hidden_cls\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"use_cpe\": True,\n          \"cpe_kernel\": 3,\n          \"cpe_beta_init\": 0.25,\n          \"cpe_gamma_init\": 0.05,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return _net(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return _opt(learning_rate)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating submission options**\n\nI’m considering two allowed submissions: one with HDP‑RegCal and CPE (with specific parameters) and the other with DSConv CPE using a tri-seed. If we opt for both HDP versions, we may have to wait on the tri-seed. Prioritizing our results, we need HDP gating with CRI-Off at least 0.08 and an average above 0.6886. The recent average was slightly below that. Adjusting gamma or beta could help raise CRI-Off while keeping averages stable, so I'm leaning towards trying smaller values for those.**Proposing experiment submissions**\n\nI’m thinking about submitting two experiments: first, HDP- RegCal with CPE using gamma-only (with β=0 and γ=0.05), and second, HDP- RegCal with CPE using k=5, if we want context. The gamma-only option seems more beneficial for improving CRI-Off, while k=5 could potentially worsen it. Alternatively, we could use tri-seed DSConv, but that seems more like a maintenance option. So, I’ll summarize my results and submit\
  \ those two experiments, prioritizing the gamma-only submission first for a better chance of improvement!**Focusing on HDP submissions**\n\nWhile tri-seeding is important for publication, we already have a positive results paper, so it's less urgent now. My goal is to focus on breaking stagnation and lifting aggregate results by selecting two HDP ablations: \n\n1) HDP- RegCal with CPE using gamma-only set to 0.05.\n2) HDP- RegCal with CPE at beta=0.25 and gamma=0.05 for balanced contributions.\n\nI’ll implement the necessary code by submitting YAML with hyperparameters for HDP- RegCal. I also plan to update the results file and craft a message about these actions, including storing a summary file and submitting the experiments."
