parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_cpe_minibase_postln.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Minimal DSConv + mean+max baseline with optional Contextual Positional Encoding (CPE)\n  and optional post-CPE LayerNorm to stabilize feature distribution.\n\n  CPE residual: h <- h + beta*DWConv_k(h) + gamma*PE_sin(L,C)\n  Post-stabilization (optional): h <- LayerNorm(h) over channel dim\n\n  Heads: single hidden MLP (128) with LayerNorm → GELU → Dropout → Dense; no RegCal, no motif. <1M params.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"\
    head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          # CPE controls\n          \"use_cpe\": True,\n          \"cpe_kernel\": 3,\n          \"cpe_beta_init\": 0.25,   # low-influence default\n          \"cpe_gamma_init\": 0.05,\n          \"post_cpe_layernorm\": True,\n      }\n\n  def sinusoidal_pe(L: int, C: int):\n      pos = jnp.arange(L)[:, None]\n      i = jnp.arange(C)[None, :]\n      div_term = jnp.power(10000.0, ((i//2)*2)/max(1.0, float(C)))\n      ang = pos / div_term\n      pe = jnp.where((i % 2) == 0, jnp.sin(ang), jnp.cos(ang))\n      return pe  # (L,C)\n\n  class CPE(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      k: int = 3\n      beta_init: float = 0.25\n      gamma_init: float = 0.05\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n          B,L,C = h.shape\n          dw = nn.Conv(features=C, kernel_size=(self.k,), feature_group_count=C, padding=\"SAME\")(h)\n          beta = self.param(\"beta\", lambda rng, shp: jnp.array(self.beta_init, dtype=h.dtype), ())\n          pe = sinusoidal_pe(L,\
    \ C)[None, :, :]\n          gamma = self.param(\"gamma\", lambda rng, shp: jnp.array(self.gamma_init, dtype=h.dtype), ())\n          return h + beta*dw + gamma*pe\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size:\
    \ int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      use_cpe: bool = True\n      cpe_kernel: int = 3\n      cpe_beta_init: float = 0.25\n      cpe_gamma_init: float = 0.05\n      post_cpe_layernorm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          if self.use_cpe:\n              h = CPE(self.hidden_dim, self.cpe_kernel, self.cpe_beta_init, self.cpe_gamma_init)(h)\n              if self.post_cpe_layernorm:\n                  h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)  # per-position LN across channels\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def global_mean_max(h):\n      mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n      maxv = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n      return jnp.concatenate([mean, maxv], axis=-1)\n\n\
    \  class MiniDSConvCPEPostLN(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      head_hidden: int = 128\n      head_dropout: float = 0.05\n      use_cpe: bool = True\n      cpe_kernel: int = 3\n      cpe_beta_init: float = 0.25\n      cpe_gamma_init: float = 0.05\n      post_cpe_layernorm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate,\n                             self.use_cpe, self.cpe_kernel, self.cpe_beta_init, self.cpe_gamma_init,\n                             self.post_cpe_layernorm)(x, deterministic)\n          pooled = global_mean_max(h)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(pooled)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return out.squeeze(-1)\n          return out\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = MiniDSConvCPEPostLN(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n              head_hidden=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden\", 128)),\n              head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n              use_cpe=bool(hp.get(\"use_cpe\", True)),\n              cpe_kernel=int(hp.get(\"cpe_kernel\", 3)),\n              cpe_beta_init=float(hp.get(\"\
    cpe_beta_init\", 0.25)),\n              cpe_gamma_init=float(hp.get(\"cpe_gamma_init\", 0.05)),\n              post_cpe_layernorm=bool(hp.get(\"post_cpe_layernorm\", True)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          pk, dk = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': pk, 'dropout': dk}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          if rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n\
    \      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_cpe_postln.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  HDP‑RegCal with optional minimal CPE before DSConv and optional post‑CPE LayerNorm.\n\n  CPE residual on h0: h0 <- h0 + beta*DWConv_k(h0) + gamma*PE_sin(L,C)\n  Then (optional) h0 <- LayerNorm(h0) over channels to stabilize distribution.\n  DSConv blocks, mean+max main, motif max; heads with RegCal for regression tasks.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden_reg\": 128,\n          \"head_hidden_cls\"\
    : 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          # CPE\n          \"use_cpe\": True,\n          \"cpe_kernel\": 3,\n          \"cpe_beta_init\": 0.25,\n          \"cpe_gamma_init\": 0.05,\n          \"post_cpe_layernorm\": True,\n      }\n\n  def sinusoidal_pe(L: int, C: int):\n      pos = jnp.arange(L)[:, None]\n      i = jnp.arange(C)[None, :]\n      div_term = jnp.power(10000.0, ((i//2)*2)/max(1.0, float(C)))\n      ang = pos / div_term\n      return jnp.where((i % 2) == 0, jnp.sin(ang), jnp.cos(ang))\n\n  class CPE(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      k: int = 3\n      beta_init: float = 0.25\n      gamma_init: float = 0.05\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n          B,L,C = h.shape\n          dw = nn.Conv(features=C, kernel_size=(self.k,), feature_group_count=C, padding=\"SAME\")(h)\n          beta = self.param(\"beta\", lambda rng, shp: jnp.array(self.beta_init, dtype=h.dtype), ())\n          pe\
    \ = sinusoidal_pe(L, C)[None, :, :]\n          gamma = self.param(\"gamma\", lambda rng, shp: jnp.array(self.gamma_init, dtype=h.dtype), ())\n          return h + beta*dw + gamma*pe\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n\
    \      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      use_cpe: bool = True\n      cpe_kernel: int = 3\n      cpe_beta_init: float = 0.25\n      cpe_gamma_init: float = 0.05\n      post_cpe_layernorm: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          if self.use_cpe:\n              h = CPE(self.hidden_dim, self.cpe_kernel, self.cpe_beta_init, self.cpe_gamma_init)(h)\n              if self.post_cpe_layernorm:\n                  h = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def l2_normalize_feats(z, eps=1e-6):\n      return z / (jnp.linalg.norm(z, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + eps)\n\n  class MotifPath(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n\
    \      k: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.k,), padding=\"SAME\")(h)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n\n  class HDPRegCalCPEPostLN(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      head_hidden_reg: int = 128\n      head_hidden_cls: int = 128\n      head_dropout: float = 0.05\n      regcal_on: bool = True\n      motif_k: int = 5\n      use_cpe: bool = True\n      cpe_kernel: int = 3\n      cpe_beta_init: float = 0.25\n      cpe_gamma_init: float = 0.05\n      post_cpe_layernorm: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate,\n                             self.use_cpe, self.cpe_kernel,\
    \ self.cpe_beta_init, self.cpe_gamma_init,\n                             self.post_cpe_layernorm)(x, deterministic)\n          h_mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          h_max  = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          motif  = MotifPath(self.hidden_dim, self.motif_k)(h)\n          pooled = jnp.concatenate([h_mean, h_max, motif], axis=-1)\n          H = self.head_hidden_reg if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\") else self.head_hidden_cls\n          z = nn.Dense(H)(pooled)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\"):\n              z_reg = l2_normalize_feats(z) if self.regcal_on else z\n              out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_reg)\n              return out.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else out\n          else:\n              logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\
    \              return logits\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = HDPRegCalCPEPostLN(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n              head_hidden_reg=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden_reg\", 128)),\n              head_hidden_cls=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden_cls\", 128)),\n              head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n              regcal_on=bool(hp.get(\"regcal_on\", True)),\n              motif_k=int(hp.get(\"motif_k\", 5)),\n              use_cpe=bool(hp.get(\"use_cpe\", True)),\n              cpe_kernel=int(hp.get(\"cpe_kernel\", 3)),\n   \
    \           cpe_beta_init=float(hp.get(\"cpe_beta_init\", 0.25)),\n              cpe_gamma_init=float(hp.get(\"cpe_gamma_init\", 0.05)),\n              post_cpe_layernorm=bool(hp.get(\"post_cpe_layernorm\", True)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          pk, dk = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': pk, 'dropout': dk}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          if rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n                               task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n \
    \                              hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write noema/results/CPE_RESULTS.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  (Update) Post-CPE stabilization prep\n  - Implemented post-CPE LayerNorm (per-token, across channels) in both minimal DSConv and HDP‑RegCal CPE backbones:\n    • files: submissions/dsconv_cpe_minibase_postln.py, submissions/hdp_regcal_cpe_postln.py\n  - Rationale: reduce distribution shift introduced by the residual positional/context signal; aim to recover CRI‑Off while keeping PRS/CRI‑On gains.\n  - Planned configs (seed=42) after current tri-seeds finish:\n    • HDP‑RegCal + CPE (k=3, beta=0.25, gamma=0.05) + post‑CPE LN\n    • Minimal DSConv + CPE (k=3, beta=0.25, gamma=0.05) + post‑CPE LN (sanity)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating response strategy**\n\nI need to craft a response based on the results of the CPE variants. The scores for ID 826 and ID 827 show some promising figures, but they’re still below the average. I’m running tri-seeds for a minimal baseline with IDs 829 and 830. Next steps involve updating results and planning for stabilization, applying some adjustments like reducing the amplitude gamma. However, I can’t submit additional experiments until the current ones finish.**Planning next steps**\n\nI think we can write the code and results, possibly heading to the Archive to add some addendum. It feels like we should prepare a submission script for post-CPE LayerNorm and gather h0 after the residual. However, I realize I can't submit right now, but I can store the script. The token budget is at 58%, which seems fine, though I'm noticing some pruning issues. I need to create either a new script or modify the existing CPE module. Let's also propose the new change for post-CPE\
  \ LayerNorm!**Planning code updates**\n\nI'm considering how normalizing across features for each position could really help reduce distribution shift and restore CRI-Off while keeping PRS/CRI-On intact. I think we can implement a parameter for 'post_cpe_layernorm' in both modules and plan to submit after tri-seed finishes. In the meantime, I can write the code and update the Archive for capsule #29 or #22. I'll store the updates in the right files to avoid breaking imports. I also want to prepare submission wrappers, but I can't submit right now due to concurrency limits.**Preparing module variations**\n\nI'm thinking about planning additional variations with k=3 post-LN using beta 0.25 and gamma 0.03, perhaps focusing on gamma-only with LayerNorm. However, I need to be careful not to overwhelm the process with too many actions. I’ll stick to the station instructions about using /execute_action lines and YAML blocks with minimal commentary. \n\nI want to write the v2 modules while including\
  \ the 'post_cpe_layernorm' hyperparameter, update the results plan, and implement `dsconv_cpe_minibase_postln.py` with LayerNorm applied correctly.**Implementing module updates**\n\nI'm deciding where to apply the LayerNorm after the CPE, so h will be modified as `h = CPE(...)(h)` and conditioned on `post_cpe_ln` being true. The module should work within both DSConvBackbone classes, so I’ll code accordingly. I'll also write wrappers for the HDP with the post-CPE LayerNorm configuration.\n\nNext, I'll update the results document and prepare storage writes for the updated modules, but I can't submit right now due to two running experiments. I'll ensure consistent kernel_dilation usage and note the earlier debug flagging the recursion. Let’s go ahead and implement the necessary scripts!"
