    \          \"use_cpe\": True,\n          \"cpe_kernel\": 3,\n          \"cpe_beta_init\": 0.25,\n          \"cpe_gamma_init\": 0.05,\n          \"post_cpe_layernorm\": True,\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CPE-Minimal + post‑CPE LayerNorm — DSConv + mean+max — seed=42\"\ntags: \"baseline, dsconv, cpe, positional-encoding, layernorm, meanmax\"\nabstract: \"Add per-token LayerNorm right after the residual CPE (β=0.25, γ=0.05, k=3) before DSConv in the minimal DSConv+mean+max baseline. Sanity test for stabilizing positional/context signal without harming CRI‑Off/PRS.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_cpe_minibase_postln import create_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\"\
    : [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"use_cpe\": True,\n          \"cpe_kernel\": 3,\n          \"cpe_beta_init\": 0.25,\n          \"cpe_gamma_init\": 0.05,\n          \"post_cpe_layernorm\": True,\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write noema/results/CPE_RESULTS.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  (Update) Tri-seed outcomes and post‑CPE LayerNorm tests (Tick 517)\n\n  Minimal DSConv + CPE (k=3, β=0.5, γ=0.1)\n  - 822 (seed=42): 0.6777 | CRI-Off 0.0978 | PRS 0.5552\n  - 829 (seed=7):  0.6616 | CRI-Off 0.0156 | PRS 0.5478 (failure)\n  - 830 (seed=123):0.6835 | CRI-Off 0.0992 | PRS 0.5541\n  → Tri-seed mean ≈ 0.6743 vs baseline 0.6745; unstable (seed 7 collapse). Do not adopt.\n\n  HDP‑RegCal + CPE before DSConv\n  - 823 (β=0.5, γ=0.1): 0.6860 | CRI-Off 0.0765\n  - 826 (β=0.0, γ=0.05; γ‑only): 0.6830 | CRI-Off 0.0781\n  - 827 (β=0.25, γ=0.05): 0.6843 | CRI-Off 0.0883\n  → Lowering CPE strength restores CRI‑Off but aggregate remains\
    \ < 0.6886.\n\n  New submissions:\n  - HDP‑RegCal + CPE (β=0.25, γ=0.05, k=3) + post‑CPE LayerNorm — seed=42 (goal: ≥0.6886 and CRI‑Off ≥0.08)\n  - Minimal DSConv + CPE (β=0.25, γ=0.05) + post‑CPE LayerNorm — seed=42 (sanity check)\n\n  Decision rule:\n  - If post‑CPE LN fails to meet gates, deprecate CPE for HDP‑RegCal and close Cycle III with negative results; keep HDP‑RegCal default (tri‑seed ≈ 0.6885).\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating CPE plans**


  I’m considering writing an Archive addendum or negative paper for the CPE attempts. I''ll make a plan to discontinue CPE work on HDP-RegCal and maybe test a final post-CPE LN run. The code for post-LN is prepared, but currently, nothing is running. I think we could run a post-CPE-LN ablation for the HDP-RegCal seed 42 and see if the average recovers to 0.6886 or higher. Although we just created the code, it might be worth submitting one more evaluation.**Planning CPE actions**


  I need to prepare some actions for our CPE work. First, I want to write an update to CPE_RESULTS.md to summarize the tri-seed results and pivot towards the post-CPE LN test. If that doesn''t work out, we may need to exit the CPE direction.


  I''ll submit the HDP-RegCal + CPE post-LN seed=42 using the new module hdp_regcal_cpe_postln.py, setting the hyperparameters as needed. Additionally, I''ll submit the minimal DSConv CPE post-LN to analyze the effects. Once that''s done, we can write to CPE_RESULTS.md. I need to ensure proper imports to avoid any recursion issues.**Finalizing CPE submissions**


  I want to maintain Beta and Gamma as low-influence values (0.25 and 0.05) with post LN set to True, and I’ll use the same for minimal DSConv. The CPE minimal tri-seed indicates that seed 7 has a very low CRI-Off of 0.0156. I could plan to test gamma-only and low-influence seeds for minimal DSConv to isolate insensitivity, but postponing that might be wise for now. I''ll proceed with the two submissions and mention in the results that HDP-RegCal CPE low-influence produced a CRI-Off of 0.0883, close to the 0.08 gate. Time to craft that message!'
