role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_quad_head.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  HDP‑RegCal with Quadratic Head Calibration (QHC) for regression-family tasks.\n  Idea: augment the regression head with elementwise squared features after RegCal to capture simple\n  second-order effects with minimal parameters.\n\n  For regression and multilabel regression tasks:\n    z = Dense(H) -> LayerNorm -> GELU -> Dropout\n    z_reg = L2_normalize(z)                                  # RegCal (per-sample)\n    z2 = z_reg * z_reg                                       # elementwise square\n    z_cat = concat([z_reg, alpha * z2])                      # alpha is learnable scalar (init ~0.2)\n    y = Dense(d_output)(z_cat)\n\n  For classification tasks:\n    Use the standard linear head (no quadratic augmentation).\n\n  Backbone: DSConv (no CPE), 5 dilated depthwise-separable conv blocks with dilations [1,2,4,8,16].\n  Pooling: main mean + main max; motif path: Conv(k=5)\
    \ + global max; fused = concat(mean, max, motif).\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden_reg\": 128,\n          \"head_hidden_cls\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"quad_alpha_init\": 0.2,   # initial scale for squared features in regression heads\n      }\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x\
    \ = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n\
    \          return h\n\n  class MotifPath(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      k: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.k,), padding=\"SAME\")(h)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n\n  def l2_normalize_feats(z, eps=1e-6):\n      return z / (jnp.linalg.norm(z, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + eps)\n\n  class HDPRegCalQuadHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      head_hidden_reg: int = 128\n      head_hidden_cls: int = 128\n      head_dropout: float = 0.05\n      regcal_on: bool = True\n      motif_k: int = 5\n      quad_alpha_init: float = 0.2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Backbone\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations,\
    \ self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          h_mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          h_max  = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          motif  = MotifPath(self.hidden_dim, self.motif_k)(h)\n          pooled = jnp.concatenate([h_mean, h_max, motif], axis=-1)\n\n          # Shared MLP-in head\n          H_reg = self.head_hidden_reg\n          H_cls = self.head_hidden_cls\n          H = H_reg if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\") else H_cls\n\n          z = nn.Dense(H)(pooled)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\"):\n              z_reg = l2_normalize_feats(z) if self.regcal_on else z\n              alpha = self.param(\"quad_alpha\", lambda rng, shp: jnp.array(self.quad_alpha_init, dtype=z.dtype), ())\n              z2 = z_reg * z_reg\n              z_cat = jnp.concatenate([z_reg,\
    \ alpha * z2], axis=-1)\n              out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_cat)\n              if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n                  return out.squeeze(-1)\n              return out\n          else:\n              logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n              return logits\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = HDPRegCalQuadHead(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n              head_hidden_reg=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden_reg\", 128)),\n              head_hidden_cls=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden_cls\", 128)),\n          \
    \    head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n              regcal_on=bool(hp.get(\"regcal_on\", True)),\n              motif_k=int(hp.get(\"motif_k\", 5)),\n              quad_alpha_init=float(hp.get(\"quad_alpha_init\", 0.2)),\n          )\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          pk, dk = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': pk, 'dropout': dk}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          if rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n                               task_type=hparams.get('task_type',\
    \ 'regression'),\n                               hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP‑RegCal + Quadratic Head Calibration (QHC) for regression-family tasks — seed=42\"\ntags: \"hdp-regcal, calibration, quadratic, regression, prsoff, robustness\"\nabstract: \"Augment the regression-family heads with a minimal quadratic term after RegCal: concat[z, α·z^2] before the final Dense. This aims to capture simple second-order effects (e.g., interactions) without altering training loops or losses. Classification heads remain linear.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from hdp_regcal_quad_head import create_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n\
    \          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"head_hidden_reg\": 128,\n          \"head_hidden_cls\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"regcal_on\": True,\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"quad_alpha_init\": 0.2,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write noema/results/QHC_PLAN.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Quadratic Head Calibration (QHC) — Plan and Gate (Tick 520)\n\n  Rationale:\n  - CRI‑Off/PRS may benefit from simple interaction-like effects. With RegCal, z has unit norm; adding z^2 (elementwise) provides a cheap second-order feature basis without violating training constraints.\n\n  Method:\n  - For regression-family tasks only (APA, CRI‑Off, CRI‑On, PRS, MRL): y = W[ z ; α·z^2 ] + b, with α learnable (init\
    \ 0.2). Classification heads unchanged.\n\n  Acceptance gate:\n  - Seed‑42 ≥ 0.689 and CRI‑Off ≥ 0.08; if met, tri‑seed. If close but < 0.689, try α_init ∈ {0.1, 0.3}.\n```"
