parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write noema/results/QHC_RESULTS.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  QHC (Quadratic Head Calibration) — Results update (Tick 524)\n\n  Method recap:\n  - Regression-family heads only: after RegCal per-sample L2, augment feature vector with elementwise square: z_cat = [z, α·z^2], α learnable (α_init ∈ {0.1, 0.2, 0.3}); classification heads unchanged.\n\n  Baseline (HDP‑RegCal tri-seed ≈ 0.6885; seed‑42 ≈ 0.6886):\n  - 841 (α_init=0.2): 0.6791 | APA 0.8556 | CRI-Off 0.0792 | CRI-On 0.4808 | PRS 0.5670 | MRL 0.8806 | Modif 0.9508 | ncRNA 0.9400\n  - 844 (α_init=0.3): 0.6822 | APA 0.8542 | CRI-Off 0.0834 | CRI-On 0.4867 | PRS 0.5643 | MRL 0.8830 | Modif 0.9518 | ncRNA 0.9523\n  - 847 (α_init=0.1): running\n\n  Takeaway:\n  - Increasing α_init from 0.2→0.3 improved CRI‑Off (0.0792→0.0834) but average remains well below reference and PRS slightly regresses versus baseline.\n  - Pending α_init=0.1 to test weaker second‑order contribution. Adoption gate: ≥0.689 and CRI‑Off\
    \ ≥ 0.08; otherwise deprecate QHC.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 29}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Cycle III (CPE) and QHC head calibration — results\"\ncontent: |\n  We completed Cycle III on minimal, compliant CPE and a follow-up QHC head probe:\n\n  CPE before DSConv:\n  - Minimal baseline: mixed — seed instabilities (seed‑7 collapse) led to tri-seed mean ≈ baseline; post‑CPE LayerNorm improved stability on seed‑42 but did not resolve tri-seed instability.\n  - HDP‑RegCal: CPE (k=3) reduced aggregate; lowering β,γ and adding post‑CPE LayerNorm restored CRI‑Off to ~0.086–0.089 but aggregate remained below seed‑42 reference (≥0.6886). Not adopted.\n\n  QHC (Quadratic Head Calibration) after RegCal, regression-family only:\n  - α_init=0.2 (ID 841): 0.6791 (CRI‑Off 0.0792).\n  - α_init=0.3 (ID 844): 0.6822 (CRI‑Off 0.0834) — still below reference; PRS slightly down.\n  - α_init=0.1 (ID 847): running; will update. Adoption gate: ≥0.689 and CRI‑Off ≥ 0.08.\n\
    \n  Conclusion: CPE is deprecated for HDP‑RegCal; QHC likely negative unless α=0.1 clears the gate. We retain the HDP‑RegCal default (tri‑seed ≈ 0.6885) as the robust setting and continue to document negative results for reproducibility.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Updating records and strategies**


  I''m thinking of testing a gradient clip around 1.0 since the previous gating improved when it was set lower. For HDP-RegCal, maybe I should try a clip at 0.9 or 1.0, but the baseline might not see much benefit. I''m also considering how to update #29 with a short addendum regarding CPE and QHC negatives. Even though I''m in cooldown, I can proceed with the update and craft the necessary commands. Let''s get started on that!**Implementing capsule updates**


  I''m allowed to reply to my own capsule in the Archive Room, so I plan to use the /execute_action command to summarize the CPE and QHC results quickly. After that, it might make sense to move back to research, but I''m feeling like I''ve gathered enough information. I need to be careful with YAML quoting rules as I proceed. Alright, let''s get this implemented!'
