parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 525\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema II — Working Meta (Tick 508)\nStatus:\n- HDP‑RegCal baseline tri-seed ≈ 0.6885.\n- Cycle II: Minimal DSConv learned per‑channel mix ↑avg to 0.6805 but failed CRI‑Off/PRS gates; RMSNorm neutral; RMSNorm+rebalancing negative.\nRunning:\n- 816 HDP‑RegCal head rebalancing only (LN; reg=160, cls=96) — ablation to isolate capacity.\nNext:\n- If 816 negative, finalize Cycle II report (negatives) and scope Cycle III: minimal, compliant Contextual Positional Encoding (CPE) variant inspired by #27/#28 for both minimal DSConv and HDP‑RegCal.\n- Maintain tokens: prune recent verbose ticks after each batch of results.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 192,218 / 270,000 used (71%)\n- Agent Age: 232 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\
    \n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'HDP‑RegCal + QHC (quadratic term after RegCal) — alpha_init=0.1 — seed=42' (ID: 847) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6835273061953131\n**APA_R2:** 0.8562\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0783\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9511\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5142\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5602\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8908\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9338\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 847\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed recursion error by removing redundant function redefinitions.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission contained a classic infinite recursion bug:\n\n1. The code imported `create_network` and `create_optimizer` from `hdp_regcal_quad_head` module\n2. Then immediately redefined these same function names in the submission\n3. The redefined functions simply called `create_network(hparams)` - but due to name shadowing, they were calling **themselves**\
    \ instead of the imported functions\n4. This caused infinite recursion: `create_network` → `create_network` → `create_network` → ... (repeated 994+ times until Python's recursion limit)\n\nThe problematic code was:\n```python\nfrom hdp_regcal_quad_head import create_network, create_optimizer\n\n# ... other code ...\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return create_network(hparams)  # ← Calls itself, not the imported function!\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return create_optimizer(learning_rate)  # ← Same problem\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nRemoved the redundant function redefinitions entirely. The fix was straightforward:\n\n**Version 2 Changes:**\n- Kept the imports: `from hdp_regcal_quad_head import create_network, create_optimizer`\n- Removed the redundant function definitions\n- Added a clarifying comment explaining why the functions don't need to be redefined\n\nThe fixed code simply imports the functions and uses them directly, which is the correct approach\
    \ since the imported functions already provide the exact same functionality.\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed code ran successfully for 300+ seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- The recursion error is completely eliminated\n- The submission now correctly uses the imported network architecture and optimizer\n\n## Technical Notes\nThe imported `hdp_regcal_quad_head` module provides a complete implementation of:\n- HDP-RegCal network with Quadratic Head Calibration (QHC)\n- DSConv backbone with dilated convolutions\n- L2 normalization for regression calibration\n- Quadratic feature expansion (z_reg * z_reg)\n- Learnable alpha parameter for quadratic term weighting\n\nThe submission only needed to specify hyperparameters (like `quad_alpha_init: 0.1` instead of the default 0.2), not reimplement the factory functions.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\
    \n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nfrom hdp_regcal_quad_head import create_network, create_optimizer\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n        \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n        \"kernel_size\": 7,\n        \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n        \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n        \"head_hidden_reg\": 128,\n        \"head_hidden_cls\": 128,\n        \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n        \"regcal_on\": True,\n        \"motif_k\": 5,\n        \"quad_alpha_init\": 0.1,\n    }\n\n# No need to redefine create_network and create_optimizer - they're already imported above\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n\
    ✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass\
    \ works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min\
    \ total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0087 |  0.4950  | 0.5048 \n 20  | 0.0010 |  0.4659  | 0.5142 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 22 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5142 Time:16s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.514171\nTraining time: 23s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\n\
