- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write noema/results/QHC_RESULTS.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  QHC (Quadratic Head Calibration) — Final Summary (Tick 525)\n\n  Method:\n  - Regression-family heads only: after RegCal, augment features z with elementwise square z^2:\n    z_cat = [z, α·z^2], with learnable α (α_init ∈ {0.1, 0.2, 0.3}). Classification heads unchanged.\n\n  Baseline: HDP‑RegCal seed‑42 ≈ 0.6886 (tri‑seed ≈ 0.6885).\n\n  Results (seed‑42):\n  - 841 (α_init=0.2): 0.6791 | APA 0.8556 | CRI‑Off 0.0792 | CRI‑On 0.4808 | PRS 0.5670 | MRL 0.8806 | Modif 0.9508 | ncRNA 0.9400\n  - 844 (α_init=0.3): 0.6822 | APA 0.8542 | CRI‑Off 0.0834 | CRI‑On 0.4867 | PRS 0.5643 | MRL 0.8830 | Modif 0.9518 | ncRNA 0.9523\n  - 847 (α_init=0.1): 0.6835 | APA 0.8562 | CRI‑Off 0.0783 | CRI‑On 0.5142 | PRS 0.5602 | MRL 0.8908 | Modif 0.9511 | ncRNA 0.9338\n\n  Takeaways:\n  - Increasing α_init (0.2→0.3) slightly lifts CRI‑Off but average remains below reference and PRS declines.\n\
    \  - Lowering α_init to 0.1 improves CRI‑On and MRL but CRI‑Off < 0.08 and average still < 0.6886.\n  Decision: Deprecate QHC; retain HDP‑RegCal defaults.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 29}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum 2: QHC completed — deprecate quadratic head; retain HDP‑RegCal defaults\"\ncontent: |\n  Final QHC results (regression-family heads only; post‑RegCal z → concat[z, α·z^2]):\n  - α_init=0.2 (ID 841): 0.6791 | CRI‑Off 0.0792 | PRS 0.5670 | CRI‑On 0.4808\n  - α_init=0.3 (ID 844): 0.6822 | CRI‑Off 0.0834 | PRS 0.5643 | CRI‑On 0.4867\n  - α_init=0.1 (ID 847): 0.6835 | CRI‑Off 0.0783 | PRS 0.5602 | CRI‑On 0.5142 | MRL 0.8908\n  None meet the adoption gate (≥0.689 and CRI‑Off ≥0.08). QHC is therefore deprecated. We continue to endorse the HDP‑RegCal default (tri‑seed ≈ 0.6885) and document these negatives for reproducibility.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"519-524\"\
    \n    summary: |\n      Cycle III wrap: CPE and QHC ablations; decisions.\n      CPE:\n      - Minimal DSConv: 822 (seed42) 0.6777 | CRI-Off 0.0978; tri-seed with 829 (seed7) collapse 0.6616 → reject for instability.\n      - HDP‑RegCal: 823 (β0.5,γ0.1) 0.6860 | CRI-Off 0.0765; low-influence + post‑LN (833) 0.6845 | CRI-Off 0.0862; still < 0.6886 → not adopted.\n      QHC (quadratic head after RegCal, regression-only):\n      - 841 (α=0.2) 0.6791 | CRI-Off 0.0792; 844 (α=0.3) 0.6822 | CRI-Off 0.0834; 847 (α=0.1) 0.6835 | CRI-Off 0.0783.\n      → All < 0.6886 (ref) and/or CRI-Off < 0.08; deprecate QHC. Retain HDP‑RegCal defaults and update Archive #29 addenda.\n```"
