parts:
- text: "Reflection Tick 2\n\nImplementation details, safety knobs, and evaluation matrix\n\nShared guardrails for all three ideas\n- Do not shadow imported create_network/create_optimizer (past recursion bug).\n- Keep params minimal: one scalar per idea (λ, η, δ). Constrain nonnegativity via softplus.\n- Preserve literal max path: never replace max with soft extremes.\n- Where applicable, compute mean/max on ReLU(h) to align scales and avoid signed cancellations.\n\nIdea 1 — MPRP (main path)\n- Compute:\n  - h+ = ReLU(h); mean_pos = mean(h+, axis=1); max_pos = max(h+, axis=1).\n  - λ = softplus(wλ); pooled = max_pos + λ · mean_pos.\n- Fused features = concat(pooled, motif_max) (dimension stays 2C if motif_max is C).\n- Init: wλ = log(exp(λ0) − 1), λ0 ∈ {0.25 (primary), 0.10, 0.50}.\n- Expected effects:\n  - Small robustness lift (mean) without reducing extremes (max). Watch CRI-Off (≥0.08) and PRS.\n\nIdea 2 — Motif contribution calibration η\n- Compute: fused = concat(mean_pos, max_pos,\
    \ η · motif_max), η = exp(wη), init wη=0 (η0=1.0).\n- Optional ablation if underperforms: freeze η for 10 epochs then unfreeze (but prefer fully learnable for simplicity).\n- Expected: stabilize cross-dataset motif magnitude; avoid over/under-weighting in PRS/CRI-*.\n\nIdea 3 — AADC (main path pre-pooling)\n- Compute: h’ = h + δ · DWConv3(h), δ = c · softplus(wδ) with c=0.1 clamp; use depthwise Conv1D(k=3), padding=SAME, no dilation.\n- Then mean/max on ReLU(h’).\n- Expected: mild anti-aliasing; must keep δ small to avoid perturbing maxima. If CRI-Off dips, reduce c→0.05 or abort.\n\nEvaluation matrix (single-seed 42, HDP‑RegCal only)\n- MPRP(λ0=0.25). If ≥ gate, sweep λ0∈{0.10, 0.50}.\n- η(η0=1.0).\n- AADC(δ0=0.1). If CRI‑Off < 0.08, retry δ0=0.05; otherwise reject.\n- If two pass individually, test combo MPRP+η (keep δ off).\n\nAcceptance gates and handling\n- Gate: avg ≥ 0.689 and CRI‑Off ≥ 0.08 (no ≥0.01 drops on Modif/ncRNA; PRS not worse by ≥0.01).\n- If within 0.001 of avg gate\
    \ and panels good, tri-seed for stability check.\n- If all three fail, document negatives succinctly; prune tokens and park HDP‑RegCal as final default."
