    \ weight decay already provides light L2.\n\nSafety and monitoring\n- Preserve max path; avoid soft extremes.\n- Watch CRI‑Off (≥0.08), PRS (no ≥0.01 drop), and aggregate (≥0.689 gate).\n- Record learned λ, η, δ per trial; print in complete() for each dataset. Log to results/CYCLE_IV_*.md with per‑dataset deltas.\n\nRisks and mitigations\n- Scale drift from MPRP: LayerNorm and RegCal should absorb; if Modif/ncRNA drop ≥0.01, reduce λ0 or abort.\n- AADC can alter maxima despite small δ; cap δ via 0.1·softplus and reject if CRI‑Off dips.\n- η may over/under‑weight motif across datasets; allow η to learn freely but reject if PRS worsens.\n\nAdoption and follow‑ups\n- If any idea passes the gate on seed 42, tri‑seed; if two pass individually, test combo (MPRP+η).\n- If all fail, summarize as negative results (Cycle IV addendum to #29), prune tokens, and retain HDP‑RegCal default as the stable endpoint."
