role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 529\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema II — Working Meta (Tick 508)\nStatus:\n- HDP‑RegCal baseline tri-seed ≈ 0.6885.\n- Cycle II: Minimal DSConv learned per‑channel mix ↑avg to 0.6805 but failed CRI‑Off/PRS gates; RMSNorm neutral; RMSNorm+rebalancing negative.\nRunning:\n- 816 HDP‑RegCal head rebalancing only (LN; reg=160, cls=96) — ablation to isolate capacity.\nNext:\n- If 816 negative, finalize Cycle II report (negatives) and scope Cycle III: minimal, compliant Contextual Positional Encoding (CPE) variant inspired by #27/#28 for both minimal DSConv and HDP‑RegCal.\n- Maintain tokens: prune recent verbose ticks after each batch of results.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 208,554 / 270,000 used (77%)\n- Agent Age: 236 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\
    \n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'HDP‑RegCal + MPRP (max‑preserving residual pooling λ0=0.25) — seed=42' (ID: 853) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6792239846787131\n**APA_R2:** 0.8507\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0850\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9511\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4609\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5634\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8896\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9538\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 853\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed infinite recursion error in submission. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (v1) had a **naming collision** that caused infinite recursion:\n\n```python\nfrom hdp_regcal_cycle4 import create_network, create_optimizer\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return create_network(hparams)\
    \  # ❌ Calls itself infinitely!\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return create_optimizer(learning_rate)  # ❌ Calls itself infinitely!\n```\n\nWhen the submission defined functions with the same names as the imported functions, the local definitions shadowed the imports. This caused the functions to call themselves recursively instead of calling the imported implementations from `hdp_regcal_cycle4`.\n\nThe error manifested as:\n```\nRecursionError: maximum recursion depth exceeded\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v2.py` with proper import aliasing to avoid naming collisions:\n\n```python\nfrom hdp_regcal_cycle4 import create_network as create_network_impl, create_optimizer as create_optimizer_impl\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return create_network_impl(hparams)  # ✅ Calls imported function\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return create_optimizer_impl(learning_rate)  # ✅ Calls imported function\n```\n\nBy importing\
    \ the functions with aliases (`create_network_impl` and `create_optimizer_impl`), the wrapper functions can now properly delegate to the imported implementations without causing recursion.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed successful execution:\n- Code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Exit code 0 (success)\n- No runtime errors detected\n\nThe fix resolves the immediate crash issue and allows the training/evaluation to proceed as intended.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nfrom hdp_regcal_cycle4 import create_network as create_network_impl, create_optimizer as create_optimizer_impl\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n        \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n       \
    \ \"kernel_size\": 7,\n        \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n        \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n        \"head_hidden_reg\": 128,\n        \"head_hidden_cls\": 128,\n        \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n        \"regcal_on\": True,\n        \"motif_k\": 5,\n        \"use_mprp\": True,\n        \"mprp_lambda_init\": 0.25,\n        \"use_motif_eta\": False,\n        \"motif_eta_init\": 1.0,\n        \"use_aadc\": False,\n        \"aadc_delta_init\": 0.10,\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return create_network_impl(hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return create_optimizer_impl(learning_rate)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape:\
    \ (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful\
