parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 530\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema II — Working Meta (Tick 508)\nStatus:\n- HDP‑RegCal baseline tri-seed ≈ 0.6885.\n- Cycle II: Minimal DSConv learned per‑channel mix ↑avg to 0.6805 but failed CRI‑Off/PRS gates; RMSNorm neutral; RMSNorm+rebalancing negative.\nRunning:\n- 816 HDP‑RegCal head rebalancing only (LN; reg=160, cls=96) — ablation to isolate capacity.\nNext:\n- If 816 negative, finalize Cycle II report (negatives) and scope Cycle III: minimal, compliant Contextual Positional Encoding (CPE) variant inspired by #27/#28 for both minimal DSConv and HDP‑RegCal.\n- Maintain tokens: prune recent verbose ticks after each batch of results.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 217,209 / 270,000 used (80%)\n- Agent Age: 237 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\
    \n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'HDP‑RegCal + motif contribution calibration (η learnable; η0=1.0) — seed=42' (ID: 854) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6809538078121297\n**APA_R2:** 0.8543\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0797\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9518\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4816\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5726\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8821\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9446\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 854\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed infinite recursion error. The submission now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission code had a critical recursion bug. After importing `create_network` and `create_optimizer` from the `hdp_regcal_cycle4` module, the code incorrectly redefined these functions as wrapper functions that called\
    \ themselves:\n\n```python\nfrom hdp_regcal_cycle4 import create_network, create_optimizer\n\n# BUG: These functions call themselves infinitely!\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return create_network(hparams)  # Calls itself, not the imported version\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return create_optimizer(learning_rate)  # Calls itself, not the imported version\n```\n\nWhen the evaluation system called `create_network(test_hparams)`, Python would resolve the local function definition (not the imported one), causing the function to call itself recursively until hitting the maximum recursion depth (1000 calls).\n\n## Fix Applied\nRemoved the unnecessary and buggy wrapper functions entirely. The imported functions from `hdp_regcal_cycle4` work perfectly as-is and don't need any wrapping.\n\n**Changes in submission_v2.py:**\n- Deleted the `create_network` wrapper function (lines 29-30 in original)\n- Deleted the `create_optimizer` wrapper function (lines 31-32\
    \ in original)\n- Kept the imports and `_define_hyperparameters()` function unchanged\n\nThe fixed submission is clean and simple:\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nfrom hdp_regcal_cycle4 import create_network, create_optimizer\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        # ... hyperparameter configuration ...\n    }\n```\n\n## Verification\nAfter applying the fix, the code runs successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating that:\n1. The recursion error is completely resolved\n2. The network creation and initialization work correctly\n3. The evaluation system can proceed with training/validation\n\nThe submission is now executing properly with the intended hyperparameter configuration (motif calibration enabled with eta=1.0, MPRP disabled, AADC disabled).\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need\
    \ to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nfrom hdp_regcal_cycle4 import create_network, create_optimizer\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n        \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n        \"kernel_size\": 7,\n        \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n        \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n        \"head_hidden_reg\": 128,\n        \"head_hidden_cls\": 128,\n        \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n        \"regcal_on\": True,\n        \"motif_k\": 5,\n        # Cycle IV toggles\n        \"use_mprp\": False,           # keep baseline mean+max in main\n        \"mprp_lambda_init\": 0.25,\n        \"use_motif_eta\": True,       # enable motif calibration\n        \"motif_eta_init\": 1.0,\n        \"use_aadc\": False,\n        \"aadc_delta_init\": 0.10,\n    }\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting\
    \ command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network\
    \ creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET\
