- text: "/execute_action{storage write noema/results/CYCLE_IV_RESULTS.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Cycle IV — Results update 2 (Tick 530)\n\n  Experiments (seed‑42; HDP‑RegCal ref ≈ 0.6886)\n  - MPRP (λ0=0.25): ID 853 → 0.6792 | APA 0.8507 | CRI‑Off 0.0850 | CRI‑On 0.4609 | PRS 0.5634 | MRL 0.8896 | Modif 0.9511 | ncRNA 0.9538\n  - Motif η (η0=1.0): ID 854 → 0.6810 | APA 0.8543 | CRI‑Off 0.0797 | CRI‑On 0.4816 | PRS 0.5726 | MRL 0.8821 | Modif 0.9518 | ncRNA 0.9446\n  - AADC (δ0=0.10): ID 856 → running\n\n  Takeaways:\n  - MPRP preserves extremes (CRI‑Off ≥ 0.08) but lowers aggregate vs reference; not adopted.\n  - Motif η improves PRS but CRI‑Off < 0.08 and aggregate still low; not adopted.\n  - Await AADC; if CRI‑Off drops or avg remains < 0.689, deprecate.\n\n  Next:\n  - If AADC negative, close Cycle IV with a negative-results addendum to #29 and freeze HDP‑RegCal defaults.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write noema/tools/submission_wrapping_guidelines.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Preventing\
    \ recursion bugs in submissions\n\n  Problem:\n  - Defining local create_network/create_optimizer after importing from your module shadows the imports and causes infinite recursion.\n\n  Wrong:\n  from my_module import create_network, create_optimizer\n  def create_network(hparams): return create_network(hparams)       # Recursion!\n  def create_optimizer(lr=1e-3): return create_optimizer(lr)        # Recursion!\n\n  Two correct options:\n  1) Use imports directly (no wrappers):\n     from my_module import create_network, create_optimizer\n\n  2) Alias imports and forward:\n     from my_module import create_network as create_network_impl, create_optimizer as create_optimizer_impl\n     def create_network(hparams): return create_network_impl(hparams)\n     def create_optimizer(lr=1e-3): return create_optimizer_impl(lr)\n\n  Tip:\n  - Only define _define_hyperparameters() and constants (BASE_SEED, BATCH_SIZE) in the submission when possible.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n\
    /execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"519\"\n    summary: |\n      CPE post‑LN results and decisions:\n      - 834 (minimal DSConv + post‑CPE LN): 0.6796 | CRI‑Off 0.0995 | PRS 0.5552.\n      - 833 (HDP‑RegCal + CPE β=0.25, γ=0.05 + post‑LN): 0.6845 | CRI‑Off 0.0862.\n      Conclusion: CPE fails aggregate gate; prep QHC head probe.\n\n  - ticks: \"520\"\n    summary: |\n      QHC (Quadratic Head Calibration) set up:\n      - Implemented HDP‑RegCal + QHC (concat[z, α·z^2] after RegCal). Submitted α_init=0.2 (ID 841). Logged plan and gate.\n\n  - ticks: \"522-524\"\n    summary: |\n      QHC sensitivity + addendum:\n      - 844 (α=0.3): 0.6822 (CRI‑Off 0.0834) — still below ref.\n      - 847 (α=0.1): 0.6835 (CRI‑Off 0.0783) — borderline CRI‑Off.\n      - Archive #29 addendum posted summarizing CPE negatives and QHC status.\n\n  - ticks: \"526\"\n    summary: |\n      Logged QHC results; prepared Cycle IV ideation (max‑preserving MPRP, motif η, anti‑alias\
    \ DWConv residual). Set gates and execution plan.\n```"
