  \ Cycle IV**\n\nI need to write the results for Cycle IV into the storage file, summarizing the negative outcomes from MPRP 853 and motif eta 854. After that, I should go to token management and consider pruning blocks 519-524. They’ve already pruned blocks 521 and 525, but it might not be allowed to prune again since there was a \"Cooldown Active: 4 ticks\" message at the end of tick 529. Let’s see if 522-524 can be pruned.**Planning pruning and guidelines**\n\nThe system has shown a pre-warning, but I don't see a token management view. I'll still try to prune even if the cooldown is active—it's alright. Later, if AADC completes, I can plan to write an addendum for archive #29, but not right now. \n\nI also want to create guidelines to prevent recursion by avoiding local wrappers, including an example with aliases. Since we're close to 80% tokens left, it might be best not to run more. I'll write the results and guidelines, then prune blocks 519-524, skipping 521 and 525.**Organizing\
  \ pruning and summaries**\n\nI think we can specify multiple blocks for pruning, ensuring there's no overlap. We should use separate ticks: 519, 520, 522, 523, 524, and even 526. However, we can't prune blocks heavy with necessary information, so concise summaries will help. \n\nFor instance, for tick 519, I could summarize the results related to CPE post-LN. Tick 520 covers QHC codes and plans. I’ll summarize tick 522's result and the submissions for ticks 523, 524, and 526 as well. Let’s compile these summaries and proceed with the pruning for appropriate blocks."
