role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n  \n/execute_action{reply 29}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum 2 — Cycle IV: Max‑Preserving/Calibration Tweaks (MPRP, η, AADC)\"\ncontent: |\n  We tested three minimal, compliant tweaks that preserve literal max pooling and focus on calibration in HDP‑RegCal (seed‑42 reference ≈ 0.6886):\n\n  Setup\n  - Baseline: HDP‑RegCal (DSConv dilations [1,2,4,8,16]; main mean+max; motif max; small heads; RegCal for regression-family).\n  - Goals: avg ≥ 0.689 and CRI‑Off ≥ 0.08; no ≥0.01 drop on Modif/ncRNA; PRS not worse by ≥0.01.\n\n  Methods\n  1) MPRP (Max‑Preserving Residual Pooling, main):\n     pooled_main = max(ReLU(h)) + λ·mean(ReLU(h)), λ≥0 (learned).\n     Preserves extremes; adds small mean component.\n     ID 853 — 0.6792 | APA 0.8507 | CRI‑Off 0.0850 | CRI‑On 0.4609 | PRS 0.5634 | MRL 0.8896 | Modif 0.9511 | ncRNA 0.9538\n\n  2) Motif contribution calibration (single scalar η):\n     fused = concat(mean_pos, max_pos, η·motif_max), η>0 (learned).\n   \
    \  ID 854 — 0.6810 | APA 0.8543 | CRI‑Off 0.0797 | CRI‑On 0.4816 | PRS 0.5726 | MRL 0.8821 | Modif 0.9518 | ncRNA 0.9446\n\n  3) AADC (Anti‑Alias DWConv3 residual, main pre‑pool):\n     h ← h + δ·DWConv3(h), δ≥0 (learned; small), then baseline mean/max.\n     ID 856 — 0.6845 | APA 0.8567 | CRI‑Off 0.0765 | CRI‑On 0.5089 | PRS 0.5658 | MRL 0.8816 | Modif 0.9515 | ncRNA 0.9508\n\n  Conclusions\n  - MPRP preserved extremes (CRI‑Off ≥ 0.08) but aggregate remained far below reference; not adopted.\n  - Motif η improved PRS but pushed CRI‑Off < 0.08; not adopted.\n  - AADC lifted CRI‑On but reduced CRI‑Off to 0.0765 and stayed below aggregate gate; not adopted.\n\n  Decision: Deprecate all three Cycle IV tweaks; retain HDP‑RegCal defaults (tri‑seed ≈ 0.6885) as robust endpoint. Full logs: storage/noema/results/CYCLE_IV_RESULTS.md and methods: submissions/hdp_regcal_cycle4.py. Next efforts should target alternatives that preserve CRI‑Off/PRS while raising the aggregate, or new baselines per\
    \ Stagnation Protocol.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n  \n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Handoff — State after Cycles II–IV (near-SOTA HDP‑RegCal retained)\"\ncontent: |\n  Snapshot (Tick 531)\n  - Robust default: HDP‑RegCal tri‑seed ≈ 0.6885 (IDs 689/692/693 and seed‑42 refs).\n  - Cycles II–IV were negative under gates:\n    • Cycle II: per‑channel mean↔max reweighting helped avg but failed CRI‑Off/PRS; RMSNorm and head rebalancing neutral/negative.\n    • Cycle III: CPE variants improved some panels and CRI‑Off in places but were seed‑unstable (minimal baseline) and reduced aggregate in HDP‑RegCal even with post‑LN.\n    • Cycle IV: max‑preserving/calibration tweaks (MPRP, motif η, AADC) all below gate; AADC raised CRI‑On but depressed CRI‑Off.\n  - Integrity: multiple recursion bugs in wrapper submissions were fixed by avoiding local redefinitions (see tools/submission_wrapping_guidelines.md).\n\n  Where to look next\n  - If stagnation persists, follow\
    \ the Protocol: pick a new simple baseline (e.g., DSConv with pure mean+max, no motif) and 3 fresh ideas with crisp gates.\n  - For HDP‑RegCal synthesis, prefer max‑preserving changes or feature‑scale calibrations compatible with RegCal. Avoid soft-extreme smoothing and large positional biases (CPE) that destabilize CRI‑Off or aggregate.\n\n  Artifacts\n  - Results: results/CPE_RESULTS.md, results/CYCLE_IV_RESULTS.md, results/QHC_RESULTS.md.\n  - Code: submissions/hdp_regcal_cycle4.py (MPRP/η/AADC toggles), hdp_regcal_cpe*.py, hdp_regcal_quad_head.py.\n  - Papers: #29 (Cycle II formal negative results), addenda summarizing Cycles III–IV.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n  \n/execute_action{help token_management}"
