- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 536\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema II — Working Meta (Tick 533)\nStatus:\n- Near-SOTA HDP‑RegCal retained (tri-seed ≈ 0.6885). Cycles II–IV (mean–max reweighting, RMSNorm, head rebalancing, CPE, quadratic heads, max-preserving tweaks) were negative or unstable.\nProtocol:\n1) Maintain reproducibility: keep scripts/results up to date; no further head/backbone tweaks unless clearly max-preserving and low risk.\n2) Stagnation mode: prioritize documentation and concise negative-result reports; avoid marginal probes that risk CRI‑Off/PRS regressions.\n3) Token hygiene: prune in batches when >75%; keep private handoff current.\nNext:\n- If a clear, max-preserving top‑k pooling variant with strict CRI‑Off guard (k∈{2,3}) emerges from literature or\
    \ peers, run single seed on HDP‑RegCal; else hold.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 132,138 / 270,000 used (49%)\n- Agent Age: 243 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'HDP‑RegCal + max‑preserving top‑k pooling (k=3) in main path — seed=42' (ID: 865) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6812218572835304\n**APA_R2:** 0.8552\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0760\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9522\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4908\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5627\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8792\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9523\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 865\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed two critical bugs: infinite recursion and incompatible Flax API usage. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe original submission (evaluation 865) had two distinct bugs:\n\n### Bug 1: Infinite Recursion (submission_v1.py)\nThe submission defined wrapper functions that called\
    \ themselves infinitely:\n```python\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return create_network(hparams)  # Calls itself!\n```\n\nThis happened because the imported function had the same name as the wrapper function, causing Python to resolve the call to the local function instead of the imported one.\n\n### Bug 2: Incompatible Flax API (storage/noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_topk.py)\nThe imported code used an outdated Flax Conv parameter name:\n```python\nx = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n            dilation=(self.dilation,),  # Wrong parameter name!\n            padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n```\n\nThe `dilation` parameter has been renamed to `kernel_dilation` in current versions of Flax.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (submission_v2.py) - Fixed Bug 1\nChanged the import aliases to avoid name collision:\n```python\nfrom hdp_regcal_topk import create_network as _create_network, create_optimizer\
    \ as _create_optimizer\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return _create_network(hparams)  # Calls imported function\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return _create_optimizer(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\nThis fixed the infinite recursion but revealed the second bug in the lineage code.\n\n### Version 3 (submission_v3.py) - Fixed Bug 2\nSince the bug was in the imported lineage file (read-only), I:\n1. Copied only the buggy classes (`DSConvBlock`, `DSConvBackbone`, `HDPRegCalTopK`, `WrappedRNANetwork`) into the submission\n2. Fixed the parameter name from `dilation` to `kernel_dilation`\n3. Kept imports for working helper functions (`global_mean_max`, `topk_mean_relu`, `l2_normalize_feats`, `MotifBranch`)\n\nThe key fix in `DSConvBlock`:\n```python\nx = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),  #\
    \ Fixed!\n            padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n```\n\n## Verification\n\nThe monitor script confirmed success:\n- Exit code: 0\n- Runtime: 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Status: Code is running successfully (taking longer than expected to complete, but no errors)\n\n## Technical Notes\n\n- **Flax API Change**: The `dilation` parameter in `nn.Conv` was replaced with `kernel_dilation` in newer Flax versions\n- **Import Strategy**: Used selective copying - only buggy classes were copied, working utility functions kept as imports\n- **Submission Strategy**: Each version is a complete, working implementation (not incremental patches)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nfrom hdp_regcal_topk import create_optimizer as _create_optimizer, WrappedRNANetwork, DSConvBackbone,\
    \ MotifBranch, l2_normalize_feats, global_mean_max, topk_mean_relu\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n        \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n        \"kernel_size\": 7,\n        \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n        \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n        \"motif_k\": 5,\n        \"head_hidden\": 128,\n        \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n        \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n        \"k_top\": 3\n    }\n\n# Fixed DSConvBlock with correct parameter name\nclass DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        residual = x\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                    kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                    feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n\
    \                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),  # Changed from 'dilation' to 'kernel_dilation'\n                    padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n        return residual + x\n\n# Fixed DSConvBackbone using the fixed DSConvBlock\nclass DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilations: Sequence[int]\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n        for d in self.dilations:\n            h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n        return h\n\n# Fixed network class using the corrected backbone\nclass HDPRegCalTopK(nn.Module):\n\
    \    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    hidden_dim: int = 256\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    motif_k: int = 5\n    head_hidden: int = 128\n    head_dropout: float = 0.05\n    k_top: int = 2\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # Backbone\n        h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n        # Main pooling: mean, max, topk_mean(ReLU)\n        mean, maxv = global_mean_max(h)\n        tkm = topk_mean_relu(h, self.k_top)\n        main_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean, maxv, tkm], axis=-1)  # (B, 3C)\n        # Motif path\n        motif = MotifBranch(self.hidden_dim, self.motif_k)(h)      # (B, C)\n        pooled = jnp.concatenate([main_pooled, motif], axis=-1)    # (B, 4C)\n\n        # Head block\n        z = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(pooled)\n        z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n\
    \        z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\"):\n            z_reg = l2_normalize_feats(z)  # RegCal ON\n            z_reg = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z_reg, deterministic=deterministic)\n            out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_reg)\n            return out.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else out\n        elif self.task_type in (\"multilabel_classification\", \"multiclass_classification\"):\n            z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n            return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_cls)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task_type {self.task_type}\")\n\nclass WrappedRNANetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n        hp = hparams or {}\n        self.net = HDPRegCalTopK(\n\
    \            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n            kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n            ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n            dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n            motif_k=int(hp.get(\"motif_k\", 5)),\n            head_hidden=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden\", 128)),\n            head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n            k_top=int(hp.get(\"k_top\", 2)),\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n \
    \           if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return _create_optimizer(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output\
    \ shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray\
    \ cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\
    \nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0101 |  0.4476  | 0.4476 \n 20  | 0.0020 |  0.3451  | 0.4908 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 23 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4908 Time:18s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.490804\nTraining time: 27s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0701  | 0.0760 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 18 (no improvement for 10\
    \ epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0760 Time:64s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.076049\nTraining time: 71s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1083 |  0.8792  | 0.8792 \n 20  | 0.0518 |  0.8693  | 0.8792 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 20 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8792 Time:772s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.879216\nTraining time: 781s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n\
    =============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0277 |  0.5565  | 0.5627 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 16 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5627 Time:956s\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.562735\nTraining time: 966s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0026 |  0.9385  | 0.9415 \n 20  | 0.0008 |  0.9462  | 0.9477 \n 30  | 0.0003 |  0.9446  | 0.9523 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 32 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\n\
    Best:0.9523 Time:1204s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.952308\nTraining time: 1214s\n\nStarting RNA training on APA dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nAPA Training (regression, r2)\nData: 145463 train, 33170 val, seq_len=186\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0090 |  0.8479  | 0.8552 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 14 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8552 Time:1530s\n\nAPA training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.855239\nTraining time: 1544s\n\nStarting RNA training on Modif dataset\nTask type: multilabel_classification, Output dim: 12\nMetric: auc_roc, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nModif Training (multilabel_classification, auc_roc)\nData: 304661 train, 3599 val, seq_len=101\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val\
    \ AUC_ROC|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0581 |  0.9485  | 0.9522 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 12\n=============================================\nBest:0.9522 Time:1870s\n\nModif training completed:\nValidation auc_roc: 0.952201\nTraining time: 1886s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: ff3eb050-bb08-4fd8-99e6-6317a6902675\nTotal time: 1888s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-27 06:42:04,744\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761518524744748226\n2025-10-27 06:42:04,760\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761518524760388067\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'HDP‑RegCal + max‑preserving top‑k pooling (k=2) in main path — seed=42' (ID: 864) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6864339376268046\n**APA_R2:** 0.8516\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:**\
    \ 0.0787\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9501\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5041\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5692\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8914\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9600\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 864\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission in version v4. The code now runs without crashing and has been executing for over 300 seconds, indicating the errors have been resolved.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had **two critical bugs**:\n\n### Bug 1: Infinite Recursion (v1)\nThe original submission contained recursive function definitions that called themselves:\n```python\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return create_network(hparams)  # Calls itself infinitely!\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return create_optimizer(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\nThis caused a `RecursionError: maximum recursion depth exceeded` when the code tried to create the network.\n\n### Bug\
    \ 2: Incorrect Flax Parameter Name (v2, v3)\nAfter fixing the recursion issue, the code exposed a bug in the imported lineage file `storage/noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_topk.py`. The `DSConvBlock` class was using an incorrect parameter name for `nn.Conv`:\n\n```python\nx = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n            dilation=(self.dilation,),  # WRONG! Should be 'kernel_dilation'\n            padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n```\n\nThis caused: `TypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'`\n\nThe correct Flax parameter is `kernel_dilation`, not `dilation`.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version v2\nRemoved the recursive function definitions to use the imported versions from the lineage directory.\n\n### Version v3 (incomplete)\nAttempted to override just the `DSConvBlock` class, but this didn't work because the imported `create_network` function still used the lineage's version\
    \ of all classes.\n\n### Version v4 (successful)\nCopied the **entire module** from the lineage directory and fixed the parameter name:\n- Changed `dilation=(self.dilation,)` to `kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,)` in the `DSConvBlock` class\n- Included all necessary classes: `DSConvBlock`, `DSConvBackbone`, `MotifBranch`, `HDPRegCalTopK`, `WrappedRNANetwork`\n- Included all helper functions: `global_mean_max`, `topk_mean_relu`, `l2_normalize_feats`\n- Included both required functions: `create_network` and `create_optimizer`\n- Used correct imports: `jax`, `jax.numpy`, `flax.linen`, `optax`\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that v4 ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing, which satisfies the success criteria. The submission is now properly executing the RNA model training/evaluation task.\n\n## Technical Details\n- The bug was in a READ-ONLY lineage file that couldn't be modified directly\n- The solution required copying the entire module to the submission\
    \ file to properly override the buggy code\n- The Flax library's `nn.Conv` class uses `kernel_dilation` parameter, not `dilation`\n- This was verified by inspecting the function signature using Python's `inspect` module\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\n\"\"\"\nHDP-RegCal with max-preserving top-k pooling in the main path.\nFixed version with correct kernel_dilation parameter for nn.Conv.\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n        \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n        \"kernel_size\": 7,\n        \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n        \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n        \"motif_k\": 5,\n   \
    \     \"head_hidden\": 128,\n        \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n        \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n        \"k_top\": 2\n    }\n\n# FIXED: Changed 'dilation' parameter to 'kernel_dilation' in nn.Conv\nclass DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        residual = x\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim,\n                    kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                    feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),  # FIXED: was 'dilation'\n                    padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n        return residual + x\n\nclass DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n\
    \    kernel_size: int\n    dilations: Sequence[int]\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n        h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n        for d in self.dilations:\n            h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n        return h\n\ndef global_mean_max(h):\n    mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n    maxv = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n    return mean, maxv\n\ndef topk_mean_relu(h, k: int):\n    # h: (B, L, C); compute mean of top-k over length per (B,C) after ReLU\n    hp = jnp.maximum(h, 0.0)\n    B, L, C = hp.shape\n    x = hp.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape((B * C, L))  # (B*C, L)\n    vals, _ = lax.top_k(x, k)\n    m = jnp.mean(vals, axis=-1)                    # (B*C,)\n    return m.reshape((B, C))                       # (B, C)\n\nclass MotifBranch(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    k: int\n    @nn.compact\n\
    \    def __call__(self, h):\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.k,), padding=\"SAME\")(h)\n        x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n        return jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n\ndef l2_normalize_feats(z, eps=1e-6):\n    return z / (jnp.linalg.norm(z, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + eps)\n\nclass HDPRegCalTopK(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    hidden_dim: int = 256\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    motif_k: int = 5\n    head_hidden: int = 128\n    head_dropout: float = 0.05\n    k_top: int = 2\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # Backbone\n        h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n        # Main pooling: mean, max, topk_mean(ReLU)\n        mean, maxv = global_mean_max(h)\n        tkm = topk_mean_relu(h, self.k_top)\n        main_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean, maxv,\
    \ tkm], axis=-1)  # (B, 3C)\n        # Motif path\n        motif = MotifBranch(self.hidden_dim, self.motif_k)(h)      # (B, C)\n        pooled = jnp.concatenate([main_pooled, motif], axis=-1)    # (B, 4C)\n\n        # Head block\n        z = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(pooled)\n        z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n        z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\"):\n            z_reg = l2_normalize_feats(z)  # RegCal ON\n            z_reg = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z_reg, deterministic=deterministic)\n            out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_reg)\n            return out.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else out\n        elif self.task_type in (\"multilabel_classification\", \"multiclass_classification\"):\n            z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n   \
    \         return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_cls)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task_type {self.task_type}\")\n\nclass WrappedRNANetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n        hp = hparams or {}\n        self.net = HDPRegCalTopK(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n            kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n            ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n            dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n            motif_k=int(hp.get(\"motif_k\", 5)),\n            head_hidden=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden\", 128)),\n            head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n            k_top=int(hp.get(\"k_top\", 2)),\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.net.init({'params':\
    \ params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.01):\n    return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION\
