role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Noema II, currently in the Research Counter. Recap: I ran max-preserving top-k pooling on the HDP‑RegCal baseline. Results: k=2 (ID 864) scored 0.6864 with CRI-Off 0.0787; k=3 (ID 865) scored 0.6812 with CRI-Off 0.0760. Both fail the adoption gates (avg ≥ 0.689 and CRI-Off ≥ 0.080). Reflection: Literal mean+max plus RegCal remains robust; small top-k additions did not lift aggregate and slightly suppressed CRI-Off. I will: 1) patch the lineage module to use kernel_dilation to avoid relying on the debugger, 2) log the results, and 3) append a concise addendum to Archive #29 documenting these negative findings.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_topk.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  HDP-RegCal with max-preserving top-k pooling in the main path (corrected).\n  - Main pooled features: concat[mean, max, topk_mean(ReLU(h), k)]\n  - Motif path: Conv1D(k=5) + global max\n  - Regression heads: RegCal (per-sample L2) before output\n  Note: Uses kernel_dilation\
    \ (Flax API). This file supersedes earlier version that used 'dilation'.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n          \"k_top\": 2,  # try {2,3}\n      }\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.hidden_dim,\n          \
    \    kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.hidden_dim,\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              padding=\"SAME\"\n          )(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return residual + x\n\n  class DSConvBackbone(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(1,), padding=\"SAME\")(x)\n          h = jax.nn.silu(h)\n          for d in self.dilations:\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def global_mean_max(h):\n      mean = jnp.mean(h,\
    \ axis=1)\n      maxv = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n      return mean, maxv\n\n  def topk_mean_relu(h, k: int):\n      # h: (B, L, C) -> mean of top-k over length per (B,C) after ReLU\n      hp = jnp.maximum(h, 0.0)\n      B, L, C = hp.shape\n      x = hp.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape((B * C, L))  # (B*C, L)\n      vals, _ = lax.top_k(x, k)                      # top-k along length\n      m = jnp.mean(vals, axis=-1)                    # (B*C,)\n      return m.reshape((B, C))\n\n  class MotifBranch(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      k: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim, kernel_size=(self.k,), padding=\"SAME\")(h)\n          x = jax.nn.gelu(x)\n          return jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n\n  def l2_normalize_feats(z, eps=1e-6):\n      return z / (jnp.linalg.norm(z, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + eps)\n\n  class HDPRegCalTopK(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n\
    \      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n      motif_k: int = 5\n      head_hidden: int = 128\n      head_dropout: float = 0.05\n      k_top: int = 2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n          # Backbone\n          h = DSConvBackbone(self.hidden_dim, self.kernel_size, self.ds_dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n          # Main pooling (max preserved)\n          mean, maxv = global_mean_max(h)\n          tkm = topk_mean_relu(h, self.k_top)\n          main = jnp.concatenate([mean, maxv, tkm], axis=-1)  # (B, 3C)\n          # Motif path\n          motif = MotifBranch(self.hidden_dim, self.motif_k)(h)      # (B, C)\n          pooled = jnp.concatenate([main, motif], axis=-1)           # (B, 4C)\n\n          # Head\n          z = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(pooled)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-6)(z)\n          z = jax.nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          if self.task_type in (\"regression\", \"multilabel_regression\"):\n              z_reg = l2_normalize_feats(z)  # RegCal ON\n              z_reg = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z_reg, deterministic=deterministic)\n              out = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_reg)\n              return out.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1) else out\n          elif self.task_type in (\"multilabel_classification\", \"multiclass_classification\"):\n              z_cls = nn.Dropout(rate=self.head_dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n              return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z_cls)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task_type {self.task_type}\")\n\n  class WrappedRNANetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp = hparams or {}\n          self.net = HDPRegCalTopK(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n\
    \              hidden_dim=int(hp.get(\"hidden_dim\", 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get(\"kernel_size\", 7)),\n              ds_dilations=tuple(hp.get(\"ds_dilations\", [1,2,4,8,16])),\n              dropout_rate=float(hp.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.10)),\n              motif_k=int(hp.get(\"motif_k\", 5)),\n              head_hidden=int(hp.get(\"head_hidden\", 128)),\n              head_dropout=float(hp.get(\"head_dropout\", 0.05)),\n              k_top=int(hp.get(\"k_top\", 2)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n\
    \                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      # Wrapper exposes network to Station; avoid name collisions in submissions.\n      return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1), task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.01):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/topk_pooling_results.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Top‑k pooling on HDP‑RegCal (seed=42) — Results (Tick 536)\n  Baseline ref: ~0.6886 (ID 713), tri‑seed ≈ 0.6885.\n\n  - ID 864 (k=2): 0.6864 | APA 0.8516 | CRI‑Off 0.0787 | CRI‑On 0.5041 | PRS 0.5692 | MRL 0.8914 | Modif 0.9501 | ncRNA 0.9600\n  - ID 865 (k=3): 0.6812 | APA 0.8552 | CRI‑Off 0.0760 | CRI‑On 0.4908 | PRS\
    \ 0.5627 | MRL 0.8792 | Modif 0.9522 | ncRNA 0.9523\n\n  Conclusion: Both k=2 and k=3 fail the adoption gates (avg ≥ 0.689; CRI‑Off ≥ 0.080). k=2 is close on average but below CRI‑Off guard; k=3 is clearly worse. Retain HDP‑RegCal defaults.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 29}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Max‑Preserving Top‑k Pooling (negative)\"\ncontent: |\n  We tested max‑preserving top‑k pooling in the HDP‑RegCal main path, augmenting mean+max with topk_mean(ReLU(h), k) (k ∈ {2,3}). Regression heads retained RegCal; motif path unchanged. Rationale: keep literal maxima while adding a robust summary of top activations to reduce outlier noise.\n\n  Results (seed=42):\n  - ID 864 (k=2): 0.6864 | CRI‑Off 0.0787 | PRS 0.5692 | ncRNA 0.9600\n  - ID 865 (k=3): 0.6812 | CRI‑Off 0.0760 | PRS 0.5627\n  Reference: baseline ~0.6886 (ID 713), tri‑seed ≈ 0.6885.\n\n  Conclusion: Neither variant meets the adoption gates (avg ≥ 0.689; CRI‑Off ≥ 0.080). k=2 approaches\
    \ the average but misses the CRI‑Off guard; k=3 underperforms more broadly. We retain the HDP‑RegCal default and provide code and logs:\n  - Code (corrected): storage/noema/submissions/hdp_regcal_topk.py (kernel_dilation fix)\n  - Results: storage/noema/results/topk_pooling_results.md\n```\n\nReflection: With top‑k pooling negative and multiple cycles confirming that literal mean+max pooling plus RegCal is robust, the prudent course is to pause further pooling/head tweaks unless a clearly max-preserving idea with a strong theoretical motivation emerges. I will focus on documentation, reproducibility, and token hygiene; if a promising variant appears (e.g., tiny top‑k with learned gate under a strict CRI‑Off prior), I will run a single‑seed probe; otherwise, I’ll hold."
