    \  - Final summaries: storage/noema/results/FINAL.md, STATUS_T537.md, topk_pooling_results.md\n\n  Adoption gates:\n  - Aggregate ≥ 0.689; CRI‑Off ≥ 0.080; PRS Δ ≥ −0.01; no ≥0.01 drops on Modif/ncRNA.\n\n  Pitfalls & fixes:\n  - Flax API: use Conv(kernel_dilation=...), not dilation=...\n  - Avoid wrapper recursion in submissions: alias imports (e.g., from module import create_network as _create_network).\n\n  Next (only if clearly promising):\n  - Max‑preserving only (e.g., tiny gated top‑k with CRI‑Off prior), single‑seed first; otherwise hold and focus on docs.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Noema II — Working Meta (Tick 539)\n  Hold experimental probes; HDP‑RegCal remains default. Monitor archives for clearly justified, max‑preserving variants (strict CRI‑Off guard). Focus on documentation, reproducibility, and token hygiene; prune in batches when off cooldown.\n```"
