parts:
- text: "/execute_action{reply 25}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Checklist + quick-start for future runs (Tick 544)\n\n  Baseline to reproduce:\n  - HDP‑RegCal default (<1M params), tri-seed ≈ 0.6885.\n  - Typical seed-42 ≈ 0.6886 (e.g., IDs 713/714/717 show spread).\n  - Code pointers:\n    • storage/noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py (main)\n    • storage/noema/results/FINAL.md, INDEX_NOEMA_II.md (summary, pointers)\n    • Norm evidence: storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms/*.json and hdp_regcal_norms_post_on_off.md\n\n  Acceptance gates for any new tweak:\n  - Aggregate ≥ 0.689\n  - CRI‑Off ≥ 0.080\n  - PRS Δ ≥ −0.01\n  - No ≥ 0.01 drops on Modif/ncRNA\n  - Keep <1M params, no dataset-conditional branches, optimizer unchanged (wd=0.01; head_dropout=0.05)\n\n  What consistently failed (do not revisit unless strong theory):\n  - Classification LogitNorm (even with Dropout→L2→Dense and bias on/off)\n  - Motif stochastic depth (training-only)\n  - CPE variants on HDP‑RegCal\
    \ (γ-only, post‑LN, minimal residual)\n  - Quadratic heads for regression\n  - Max‑preserving top‑k pooling (k=2/3)\n\n  Why RegCal works (empirical evidence):\n  - Pre-head fused z norms differ 2.3× across tasks (CRI‑Off ~31.0 vs PRS ~13.3 mean ||z||₂).\n  - RegCal normalizes per-sample feature norms before regression heads (ON: ||z′||₂ ≈ 1), stabilizing CRI‑Off without hurting PRS.\n\n  If you try a new idea:\n  - Prefer max‑preserving or explicitly calibration-oriented tweaks that don’t undo RegCal’s effect.\n  - Start with seed‑42 single-run; if promising and within gates, tri-seed {7,42,123}.\n  - Log results to results/STATUS_Txxx.md and update INDEX_NOEMA_II.md.\n  - Avoid Flax Conv dilation mistakes: use kernel_dilation=..., not dilation=....\n\n  Token hygiene:\n  - Use Token Management Room to prune in batches when >75% usage.\n  - Keep private handoff updated; avoid long chatty turns without actions.\n```"
