role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n  \n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP‑RegCal + grad-clip=0.75 (optimizer sweep) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"regcal, optimization, gradient-clipping, hdprc, calibration\"\nabstract: \"Minimal, compliant optimizer change: reduce global-norm gradient clipping from 1.0 to 0.75 on the HDP‑RegCal baseline. Hypothesis: tighter clipping further stabilizes CRI‑Off without harming PRS; all architecture and heads unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal import build_network as build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Keep baseline HDP‑RegCal hyperparameters (architecture unchanged)\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n\
    \          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"regcal_on\": True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1), hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\"), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      # Tighter global-norm clipping\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(0.75),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"HDP‑RegCal + grad-clip=0.50 (optimizer sweep) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"regcal, optimization, gradient-clipping, hdprc, calibration\"\nabstract: \"Further optimizer ablation on HDP‑RegCal: global-norm gradient clipping set to 0.50 to suppress gradient spikes (esp. CRI‑Off) while preserving PRS. All other\
    \ hyperparameters unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal import build_network as build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n          \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"regcal_on\": True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1), hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\"), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(0.50),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n\
    \      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning gradient experiments**


  I''m considering the theoretical aspects here: lowering the clip might reduce gradient spikes for CRI-Off, especially with a small dataset, which could improve stability. We saw clip 1.0''s benefits before, but haven’t tested values beyond that. I propose running a small experiment with HDP-RegCal using grad_clip values of 0.75 and 0.5. A minor adjustment in head_dropout could be worth trying too, maybe around 0.055. It seems like one or two experiments would be sufficient to gather useful insights.**Implementing submissions**


  I need to implement two submissions: one for "HDP-RegCal + grad clip=0.75" and another for "grad clip=0.5," both using seed 42. The training system will return optax.adamw, and I plan to use optax.chain to include the gradient clipping. I’ll import the necessary HDP-RegCal network builder from the earlier dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py file. I should also confirm the baseline configuration, which I recall includes a motif of k=5, head_dropout=0.05, hidden_dim=256, and certain dilations.**Setting up submissions**


  I plan to set minimal values for certain fields, remembering that "grad_clip" isn’t used by the network but rather by the optimizer. I’ll implement a custom create_optimizer function that returns optax.chain with the clipping. It’s important to measure any dead code and ensure compliance with aggregator text tags while preparing for two submissions. I''ll also double-check that the YAML for clips at 0.75 and 0.5 is formatted correctly. Lastly, I’ll include the necessary imports and ensure concise responses to fit within token limits.**Defining build function**


  I’m unsure about the function name, so it’s safer to define my own build by importing the module and calling build_network. Previously, I used "dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py" for submitting code, where I imported build_network. I’ll replicate that but first confirm the function exists. I’ll set BATCH_SIZE to 64 and define _define_hyperparameters to return default hyperparameters. From the baseline, I remember the keys like ''gru_dim,'' ''motif_k,'' ''head_dropout,'' and ''ds_dilations.'' I''ll set ''head_dropout'' to 0.05 and enable ''regcal_on'' since it seems to be on by default.**Finalizing submissions**


  I need to make sure that the no_debugger option is set, although it doesn’t seem necessary right now. I’ll go ahead and prepare the two submissions as planned. Updating the index is an optional step I''m considering, but it seems like it’s not needed for this task, so I’ll just proceed with what I have. Let’s keep things straightforward and get those submissions ready!'
