tick: 549
role: model
parts:
- text: "Adopting gradient clipping 0.50 for HDP‑RegCal. Tri-seed results: mean ≈ 0.6893; CRI-Off per-seed = {0.0909, 0.0963, 0.0852} ≥ 0.080; Modif/ncRNA stable; PRS within gate.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/gradclip_ablation_results.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # HDP‑RegCal — Gradient Clipping Ablation Results (Tick 549) — Final\n\n  Single-seed (42):\n  - clip=0.75 → 0.6914 | APA 0.8572 | CRI-Off 0.0744 | CRI-On 0.5327 | PRS 0.5714 | MRL 0.8930 | Modif 0.9511 | ncRNA 0.9600\n    • Fails CRI-Off guard (≥0.080) despite highest avg.\n  - clip=0.50 → 0.6901 | APA 0.8593 | CRI-Off 0.0909 | CRI-On 0.5137 | PRS 0.5685 | MRL 0.8945 | Modif 0.9512 | ncRNA 0.9523\n    • Passes gates.\n\n  Tri-seed (clip=0.50):\n  - seed=42 (ID 877): 0.6901 | CRI-Off 0.0909\n  - seed=7  (ID 879): 0.6892 | CRI-Off 0.0963\n  - seed=123 (ID 880): 0.6886 | CRI-Off 0.0852\n  → Mean ≈ 0.6893; all CRI-Off ≥ 0.080; Modif/ncRNA stable; PRS ≈ 0.567–0.569.\n\n  Decision:\n  - ADOPT clip=0.50 as the default\
    \ optimizer setting for HDP‑RegCal.\n  - Do NOT adopt clip=0.75 (CRI-Off below guard).\n\n  Notes:\n  - Architecture unchanged; RegCal ON; AdamW wd=0.01.\n  - Rationale: clip=0.50 reduces gradient spikes and stabilizes CRI‑Off without harming PRS or classification panels.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/submit_hdprc_clip050.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  HDP‑RegCal submission template with adopted optimizer setting:\n  Global-norm gradient clipping = 0.50 (AdamW wd=0.01). Architecture unchanged.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys, optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal import build_network as build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n          \"hidden_dim\": 256,\n          \"kernel_size\": 7,\n          \"dropout_rate\": 0.10,\n          \"ds_dilations\": [1,2,4,8,16],\n          \"motif_k\": 5,\n     \
    \     \"head_hidden\": 128,\n          \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n          \"regcal_on\": True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1), hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\"), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(0.50),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/FINAL.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # HDP‑RegCal — Final Summary (updated Tick 549)\n\n  Default method:\n  - HDP‑RegCal (<1M params), RegCal ON for regression heads; AdamW wd=0.01; Global-norm gradient clipping = 0.50 (adopted).\n\n  Evidence:\n  - Prior baseline tri-seed ≈ 0.6885 (clip=1.0).\n  - clip=0.75: 0.6914\
    \ (seed 42) but CRI-Off 0.0744 → rejected.\n  - clip=0.50: tri-seed mean ≈ 0.6893 with CRI-Off {0.0909, 0.0963, 0.0852} (IDs 877/879/880) → adopted.\n  - Panels remained stable (PRS ~0.567–0.569; Modif/ncRNA unchanged).\n\n  Files:\n  - Submission template (clip=0.50): storage/noema/submissions/submit_hdprc_clip050.py\n  - Ablation logs: results/gradclip_ablation_results.md\n  - Norm evidence: results/hdp_regcal_norms/*.json and hdp_regcal_norms_post_on_off.md\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 22}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Optimizer Improvement — Adopting Global-Norm Gradient Clipping 0.50\"\ncontent: |\n  We ablated global-norm gradient clipping on HDP‑RegCal (architecture unchanged; AdamW wd=0.01; RegCal ON).\n  Results:\n  - clip=0.75 (ID 876): 0.6914 avg but CRI‑Off 0.0744 → fails guard.\n  - clip=0.50 (IDs 877/879/880): seed=42 0.6901 (CRI‑Off 0.0909); seed=7 0.6892 (CRI‑Off 0.0963); seed=123 0.6886 (CRI‑Off 0.0852); tri‑seed mean ≈ 0.6893.\n  Decision:\n\
    \  - Adopt clip=0.50 as default (improves CRI‑Off stability while maintaining PRS and overall average).\n  Artifacts:\n  - Submission template: storage/noema/submissions/submit_hdprc_clip050.py\n  - Results: storage/noema/results/gradclip_ablation_results.md and results/FINAL.md\n  Rationale:\n  - Paired with RegCal, tighter clipping reduces gradient spikes on CRI‑Off without harming other panels, aligning with our calibration framework.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Noema II — Working Meta (Tick 549)\n  - Adopted clip=0.50 for HDP‑RegCal; templates and docs updated; Archive addendum posted.\n  - Next: monitor for literature-backed, max-preserving ideas; otherwise maintain reproducibility and token hygiene.\n```"
