- text: "/execute_action{storage write noema/results/REPRO_CHECKLIST.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Reproducibility Checklist — HDP‑RegCal (clip=0.50) — Tick 552\n\n  Goal\n  - Reproduce the retained near‑SOTA baseline with global‑norm gradient clipping 0.50 and confirm stability on CRI‑Off and PRS.\n\n  1) Environment & Files\n  - Submission template: storage/noema/submissions/submit_hdprc_clip050.py\n  - Core code (family): storage/noema/submissions/*\n  - Known pitfalls:\n    • Flax Conv uses kernel_dilation, not dilation.\n    • Avoid wrapper recursion; alias imported create_network/create_optimizer if wrapping.\n\n  2) Runs (tri‑seed)\n  - Seeds: 42, 7, 123 (BASE_SEED in template)\n  - Expected results (± typical variance):\n    • Seed 42: ~0.6901 | CRI‑Off ~0.0909 | PRS ~0.5685  (ref: ID 877)\n    • Seed 7:  ~0.6892 | CRI‑Off ~0.0963 | PRS ~0.5668  (ref: ID 879)\n    • Seed 123:~0.6886 | CRI‑Off ~0.0852 | PRS ~0.5675  (ref: ID 880)\n  - Adoption gates (for future tweaks):\n    • Aggregate\
    \ ≥ 0.689\n    • CRI‑Off ≥ 0.080\n    • PRS Δ ≥ −0.01 vs. reference\n    • No ≥0.01 drops on Modif/ncRNA\n\n  3) Artifacts to verify\n  - Results index: storage/noema/results/INDEX_NOEMA_II.md\n  - Final summary: storage/noema/results/FINAL.md\n  - Status snapshot: storage/noema/results/STATUS_T550.md\n  - Grad‑clip ablation log: storage/noema/results/gradclip_ablation_results.md\n  - Calibration evidence:\n    • Pre‑head z‑norms (regression): storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms/*.json\n    • Derived post‑RegCal z′ ON/OFF table: storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_post_on_off.md\n    • Summary: storage/noema/results/hdp_regcal_norms_summary.md\n\n  4) What NOT to change (kept for stability)\n  - No CPE variants (neutral/unstable on DSConv/HDP‑RegCal).\n  - No LogitNorm or cosine classifier (classification): neutral/negative.\n  - No quadratic regression heads; no motif stochastic depth; no top‑k main‑path pooling.\n\n  5) Reporting\n  - If re‑runs deviate beyond expected variance,\
    \ log in results/STATUS_Txxxx.md and append a note to Archive #22.\n  - Maintain concise diffs and IDs in all addenda.\n```"
