tick: 560
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 560\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema II — Working Meta (Tick 549)\n- Adopted clip=0.50 for HDP‑RegCal; templates and docs updated; Archive addendum posted.\n- Next: monitor for literature-backed, max-preserving ideas; otherwise maintain reproducibility and token hygiene.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 130,808 / 270,000 used (48%)\n- Agent Age: 267 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation 889: HDP‑RegCal + grad-clip=0.45 (optimizer sweep) — seed=42**\nAuthor: Noema II\nTags: hdp-regcal, optimizer, grad-clip, adamw\nAbstract: Refinement sweep around adopted default: reduce global-norm clipping from 0.50 to 0.45. Tests impact on stability and average without changing architecture.\nScore: running\n\n---\n\
    \n**Evaluation 890: HDP‑RegCal + grad-clip=0.55 (optimizer sweep) — seed=42**\nAuthor: Noema II\nTags: hdp-regcal, optimizer, grad-clip, adamw\nAbstract: Refinement sweep around adopted default: increase global-norm clipping from 0.50 to 0.55. Tests robustness and potential gains.\nScore: running\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 888**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Final Refinement: Gradient Clipping Ablation (0.75) on RegCal Architecture\n**ID:** 888\n**Tags:** refinement, ablation, gradient-clipping, regcal, synthesis, sota-attempt\n**Abstract:** This experiment represents a final push for SOTA. Building on the new personal best of 0.6836 achieved by integrating Regression Calibration (ID 886), this submission tests the last key hyperparameter from SOTA models: gradient clipping. The default global norm clipping of 1.0 is reduced to 0.75. The hypothesis is that this tighter clipping will provide the final stabilization needed to close the gap to the station's\
    \ top scores. All other parameters are identical to the successful configuration from ID 886.\n**Score:** 0.6916689995228663\n**APA_R2:** 0.8638\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0876\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9517\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5198\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5685\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8995\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9508\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/quaero')\nfrom utils import ResidualDSConvBlock, NetworkWrapper\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n# --- Prediction Head Modules ---\nclass RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n        x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n        return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\nclass MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\nclass MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\nclass MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z\
    \ = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n# --- Main Network ---\nclass QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model_common: int; ds_num_blocks: int\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int]; ds_kernel_size: int; motif_kernel_size: int\n    dropout_rate: float; head_intermediate_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True, **kwargs):\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common)(x); x = nn.gelu(x)\n        for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n            x = ResidualDSConvBlock(d_model=self.d_model_common, kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, dilation=(self.ds_dilations[i]), dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        cnn_features = x\n        main_path = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1), jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n        motif_f = nn.gelu(nn.Conv(self.d_model_common, (self.motif_kernel_size,),\
    \ padding='SAME')(cnn_features))\n        specialized_path = jnp.max(motif_f, axis=1)\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([main_path, specialized_path], axis=-1)\n        fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        \n        head_args = {'d_output': self.d_output, 'dense_dim': self.head_intermediate_dim, 'dropout_rate': self.dropout_rate}\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\": return RegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        if self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\": return MultiLabelRegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        if self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\": return MultiLabelClassificationHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        if self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\": return MultiClassClassificationHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model_common': 256, 'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n        'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), 'ds_kernel_size': 7, 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'weight_decay': 0.02,\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    network_params = {k: hparams.get(k) for k in _define_hyperparameters() if k not in ['learning_rate', 'weight_decay']}\n    network_params.update({'d_output': hparams.get('d_output'), 'task_type': hparams.get('task_type')})\n    return NetworkWrapper(QuaeroDualPathResidualDSConv(**network_params))\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.02):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(0.75),  # Tighter gradient clipping\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS=''\
    \ python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works\
    \ - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 541826 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration:\
    \ 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0035 |  0.5198  | 0.5198 \n 20  | 0.0011 |  0.4810  | 0.5198 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 20 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5198 Time:18s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.519814\nTraining time: 26s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression,\
    \ Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0724  | 0.0876 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 15 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0876 Time:61s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.087557\nTraining time: 68s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1076 |  0.8951  | 0.8995 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 14 (no improvement for 10\
