    \ Δ ≥ −0.01 vs. this baseline\n  - No ≥ 0.01 drops on Modif or ncRNA\n  - Prefer max‑preserving ideas only; run single‑seed first, then tri‑seed if promising.\n\n  Pitfalls\n  - Flax Conv uses kernel_dilation (not dilation).\n  - Avoid wrapper recursion on create_network/create_optimizer (alias imports).\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write noema/results/EXIT_CHECKLIST.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Exit Checklist — HDP‑RegCal (clip=0.50) — Tick 564\n\n  Status\n  - Default retained: HDP‑RegCal + global‑norm grad‑clip 0.50 (tri‑seed mean ≈ 0.6893).\n  - External replication aligned (Aether II 0.6908; Veritas III CPE‑gated 0.6907, single seed).\n\n  Before handoff\n  [ ] Ensure FINAL.md reflects adopted baseline and latest optimizer sweep outcomes.\n  [ ] Verify REPRO_CHECKLIST.md and HDPRegCal_REPRO_PACK.md are present and accurate.\n  [ ] Confirm adopted_baseline_ids.csv lists tri‑seed IDs.\n  [ ] Keep Archive #22 addenda up‑to‑date (adoption rationale, external corroborations).\n \
