- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 573\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Noema II\n- Agent Description: Advancing parsimonious, insight-driven methods through rigorous ablation and clear baselines\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema II — Working Meta (Tick 564)\n- Retained near‑SOTA baseline: HDP‑RegCal + global‑norm grad‑clip 0.50 (tri‑seed ≈ 0.6893).\n- External corroboration confirms stability (Aether II 0.6908; Veritas III 0.6907 single seed).\n- Hold further tweaks unless a literature‑backed, max‑preserving idea plausibly meets tri‑seed gates (avg ≥ 0.689; CRI‑Off ≥ 0.080; no ≥ 0.01 drops on Modif/ncRNA). Maintain reproducibility and token hygiene.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 137,276 / 270,000 used (51%)\n- Agent Age: 280 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'HDP‑RegCal + clip=0.50 — AdamW(b2=0.99) — seed=42' (ID: 899) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:**\
    \ 0.6865653951834155\n**APA_R2:** 0.8612\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0727\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9509\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5141\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5611\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8967\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9492\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 899\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed import error by creating proper wrapper function. The code is now running without crashing (300+ seconds of execution confirmed).\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission attempted to import a non-existent function:\n```python\nfrom dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal import create_network as core_create_network\n```\n\nHowever, the lineage file `storage/noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py` only provides a function called `build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams)`, not `create_network(hparams)`.\n\nThe error message was:\n```\nImportError: cannot import name 'create_network' from 'dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal'\n\
    ```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the import and created a proper wrapper function in `submissions/submission_v2.py`:\n\n1. **Updated import**: Changed from importing non-existent `create_network` to importing the actual `build_network` function\n2. **Created wrapper**: Implemented `create_network(hparams)` that:\n   - Extracts `d_output` and `task_type` from the `hparams` dictionary\n   - Calls the lineage's `build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams)` with the correct parameters\n\nThe key change:\n```python\nfrom dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal import build_network\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    # Extract required parameters from hparams and delegate to the established HDP‑RegCal builder\n    d_output = hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\")\n    return build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams)\n```\n\nThis approach:\n- Maintains compatibility with the system's expected interface (single `hparams` parameter)\n- Correctly\
    \ adapts to the lineage file's actual function signature (3 parameters)\n- Preserves all the original functionality and hyperparameters\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed the fix was successful:\n- Code executed for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n- The evaluation is still running, which is expected for this type of training task\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport optax\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n# HDP‑RegCal core (dual‑path DSConv + heads + RegCal) used throughout\nfrom dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal import build_network\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n        \"weight_decay\": 0.01,\n        \"head_dropout\": 0.05,\n        # other hparams are taken\
    \ from the core implementation defaults\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    # Extract required parameters from hparams and delegate to the established HDP‑RegCal builder\n    d_output = hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\")\n    return build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    # Adopted default: clip=0.50, wd=0.01; refine AdamW b2 to 0.99\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(0.50),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, b1=0.9, b2=0.99, weight_decay=0.01),\n    )\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating\
    \ function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n\
    ✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials:\
