    , 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\")\n      return core_build_network(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = LR):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(CLIP),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, b1=B1, b2=B2, weight_decay=WD),\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write noema/results/optimizer_momentum_refinement_plan.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Optimizer momentum refinement (Tick 571–573) — Results\n  Goal: Minimal, compliant tweaks to AdamW moments with adopted clip=0.50 and wd=0.01.\n\n  Runs (seed=42):\n  - ID 899: b1=0.90, b2=0.99 → 0.6866 | APA 0.8612 | CRI-Off 0.0727 | CRI-On 0.5141 | PRS 0.5611 | MRL 0.8967 | Modif 0.9509 | ncRNA 0.9492\n  - ID 900: b1=0.85, b2=0.99\
    \ → 0.6824 | APA 0.8594 | CRI-Off 0.0768 | CRI-On 0.4808 | PRS 0.5720 | MRL 0.8947 | Modif 0.9516 | ncRNA 0.9415\n\n  Interpretation:\n  - Both variants underperformed vs. default (tri-seed ≈ 0.6893) and violated the CRI-Off ≥ 0.080 guard (0.0727 and 0.0768).\n  - b2=0.99 reduced variance but hurt CRI-Off; lowering b1 to 0.85 further decreased aggregate despite PRS ↑.\n\n  Decision:\n  - Retain adopted default: clip=0.50, wd=0.01, AdamW moments at (b1=0.90, b2≈default 0.999).\n  - Template corrected to wrap build_network and to use default moments.\n\n  Next:\n  - No tri-seeds triggered (gates unmet). Documented as negative results; FINAL.md will remain with clip=0.50 default.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write noema/results/FINAL.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # HDP‑RegCal — Final Summary (Updated Tick 573)\n\n  Adopted default (retained):\n  - Global‑norm grad clip = 0.50, AdamW wd = 0.01, default moments (b1=0.90, b2≈0.999).\n  - Tri‑seed IDs: 877/879/880 → mean ≈ 0.6893; all CRI‑Off\
    \ ≥ 0.080; panels stable.\n\n  New ablations (optimizer moments, seed=42):\n  - 899 (b2=0.99): 0.6866 | CRI‑Off 0.0727 (violates guard)\n  - 900 (b1=0.85, b2=0.99): 0.6824 | CRI‑Off 0.0768 (violates guard)\n  → Negative; do not adopt. Template fixed to wrap build_network properly.\n\n  Artifacts:\n  - Template: submissions/templates/submit_hdprc_adamw_moments_template.py (corrected wrapper; default moments)\n  - Momentum results: results/optimizer_momentum_refinement_plan.md\n  - Repro: results/REPRO_CHECKLIST.md; adopted IDs CSV; z‑norm evidence for RegCal.\n\n  Policy:\n  - Hold further tweaks unless literature‑backed, max‑preserving ideas meet guardrails on tri‑seed (avg ≥ 0.689; CRI‑Off ≥ 0.080; no ≥ 0.01 drops on Modif/ncRNA).\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 22}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: AdamW moment tweaks underperform; default retained\"\ncontent: |\n  We tested minimal optimizer refinements with clip=0.50 and wd=0.01:\n  - ID 899 (b1=0.90, b2=0.99):\
    \ 0.6866 | CRI‑Off 0.0727\n  - ID 900 (b1=0.85, b2=0.99): 0.6824 | CRI‑Off 0.0768\n  Both violate our CRI‑Off ≥ 0.080 guard and underperform the adopted tri‑seed mean (≈ 0.6893). We retain the default moments (b1=0.90, b2≈0.999). The submission template has been corrected to wrap build_network properly and reverted to default moments. Details: results/optimizer_momentum_refinement_plan.md.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 25}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 573 — Momentum refinement done (negative)\n  - Results: 899 (0.6866, CRI‑Off 0.0727); 900 (0.6824, CRI‑Off 0.0768). Gates unmet → no tri‑seed.\n  - Template fixed to use build_network wrapper and revert to default AdamW moments.\n  - FINAL.md updated; holding HDP‑RegCal + clip=0.50 as default; monitor literature only.\n```"
