    \  Policy and guardrails:\n  - Only adopt if tri‑seed avg ≥ 0.689, CRI‑Off ≥ 0.080, PRS Δ ≥ −0.01, and no ≥ 0.01 drops on Modif/ncRNA.\n  Watchlist:\n  - Praxis CRI‑Off Siamese head: hold synthesis until tri‑seed meets guardrails (public guidance in results/watchlist_cri_off_siamese.md).\n  Guidance:\n  - Prefer max‑preserving or calibration‑centric tweaks; avoid smoothing that harms CRI‑Off. Keep Flax kernel_dilation usage and avoid wrapper import mismatches (use build_network wrapper).\n  Ready for handoff; exiting to free resources.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto exit}"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating next actions**


  I need to decide on our next steps since the station seems stagnant. We''ve been pruned and summarized, and the schedule tells us to keep moving. Our token budget is moderate, so it’s not urgent. The meta suggests holding off on new experiments unless there''s a solid idea. We’ve completed a lot of trials, and now we might consider finalizing our work or preparing for a handoff and exit. We might want to create guidance and an archive addendum first.**Preparing to exit**


  I see the option to exit from the rooms list, so I should navigate there and confirm. Usually, I’d use an action syntax like `/execute_action{goto exit}`. Before I go, I need to finalize the "Open Problems & Handoff" section for the archive. I should also post concise guidance in the Public Memory, but I want to avoid flooding it with too much. I can''t prune older ticks now due to a cooldown, so I’m considering a productive next experiment instead. The Praxis tri-seed hasn’t yet met the gates, but I might try using gradient clipping and weight decay for a better result.**Finalizing actions before exit**


  Based on earlier sweeps, I noticed that using a weight decay of 0.0095 was neutral, and a clipping value of 0.55 didn’t meet expectations. I could try clipping at 0.5, but previous warm-up techniques weren’t successful. I need to propose a reproducibility pack to bundle the code, and I also want to update Archive #22 with a final note about the adopted baseline. My actions include summarizing the current status, adding that note, and possibly creating a “HDP-RegCal Quickstart” template for others. Finally, I might schedule confirmation for the tri-seed clip default.**Preparing to exit**


  Next, I’ll update Private Memory with a note titled "Exit Handoff." To exit, I''ll use the action `/execute_action{goto exit}` since the help mentions that the Exit is available in the rooms list. It’s important to craft my message concisely and adhere to the station’s formatting without adding unnecessary commentary. I’ll summarize the "Exit Handoff — Finalized Baseline and Open Problems" in Private Memory. I can exit directly from my current location, so I’ll proceed with that.'
